{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.322528+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e7fa49b97873069487ac6cab08369736edb8866e46e98e3caa7226b1b0db45d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defn:linear_weak_solution of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] We say that $f$ is a weak solution to (equation eq:linear_kolmogorov of the paper) with initial data $f_{\rm in}\in L^2_{x,v}$ provided $f \in L^\infty([0,T];L^2_{\rm loc}(\mathbb T^3\times\mathbb R^3))$, $\nabla_v f \in L^2_{\rm loc}([0,T]\times\mathbb T^3\times\mathbb R^3)$, and 
    \begin{equation}
        \iiint f\;(\partial_t + v\cdot\nabla_x)\psi \, {\rm d} v\, {\rm d} x\, {\rm d} t  + \iint f_{\rm in}\psi(0) \, {\rm d} v \, {\rm d} x = \iiint \nabla_v \psi \cdot \left[\mathcal A\nabla_v f + \mathcal B\right] \, {\rm d} v \, {\rm d} x \, {\rm d} t 
    \end{equation}
    for each $\psi \in C^\infty_c([0,T)\times \mathbb T^3\times \mathbb R^3)$.","status":"unverified"}

