	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.761270+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ea4a9024f55e20e0875a7e28bb53c59ef88406e64471a25352cd08b53269775","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop negvalue1 of arXiv:2609.02682, 'LDP for tensor forms'] Suppose $c=v=2$, $\int_0^1 W_\infty (., y) dy = 1$ $\lambda$-a.e., $W_\infty>0$ $\lambda$-a.e., $\mu(\{1\})=p_1=p\in(0,1)$, $\mu(\{2\})= p_2=1-p$, and $\boldsymbol{\alpha}=(\theta,-\theta) $ for some $\theta \in \mathbb{R}$. 
 \begin{itemize}
     \item[(i)] The maximizer of (equation eq:potts_unconstrained_opt of the paper) is $(\frac{p\exp({2\theta})}{1-p+p\exp({2\theta})},\frac{1-p}{1-p+p\exp({2\theta})})$ $\lambda$-a.e. and hence it is unique. 
     \item [(ii)] For $y\in(-1,1)$, the good rate function $I_{W_\infty,(1,-1)}(y)$ (see (equation eq:i2 of the paper)) can be simplified as 
     \[ \Big(\frac{y+1}{2}\Big)\log \Big(\frac{y+1}{2p}\Big)+\Big(\frac{1-y}{2}\Big)\log\Big(\frac{1-y}{2(1-p)}\Big).\]

\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.522218+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ea5ae5153bbac4e9e943569307b1025059ab4329b66058b293c12b1bf2d8095","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T3.1 of arXiv:2512.18990, '\bf Hybrid Stochastic Functional Differential Equations with Infinite Delay: Approximation'] Under Assumptions (A2.1 of the paper) and (A2.2 of the paper), for each integer $k\ge 1$ and each $0<T\leq k$, the
  truncated SFDE ((sfde2 of the paper)) has a unique global solution $x^k(t)$ on $t\in (-\8,T]$.  Moreover,  there is a positive constant $C_T$,
  which is the same as in Theorem (T2.3 of the paper), { such that}
{
\begin{align}
\sup_{0\le t\le T} \mathbb{E} W_1(x^k(t),t) \le  C_T, \ \ \forall~ 0<T\leq k,
