{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.747408+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f0c827feaec94b3eca48f67c9f61b7b63bf64ddbabd8fc0829db1aa3ab6e18d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:poisson of arXiv:2608.28169, 'characteristic polynomial of self-normalized random matrices'] Let $\big(N_{-,\ell}\big)_{\ell\geqslant 1}$ and $\big(N_{+,\ell}\big)_{\ell\geqslant 1}$ be two i.i.d.\ sequences of independent random variables  with $N_{-,\ell}$ following a Poisson $\mathcal{P}\big(\frac{1}{2\ell}\big)$ distribution. Define 
    \begin{equation*}
        Z_k^{(0)} = \sum_{\ell | k} \ell  (N_{+,\ell } + (-1)^{k/\ell } N_{-,\ell }) \,, \qquad k\geqslant 1\,.
    \end{equation*}
    For integers $k_1,\ldots, k_\ell\geqslant 1$, we then have the convergence of traces
        \begin{equation}
        \left(\operatorname{Tr} \left[ {\mathbf Y}^{k_1}_n \right], \dots, \operatorname{Tr} \left[ {\mathbf Y}^{k_\ell}_n \right] \right) \stackrel{\rm d}{\rightarrow} \left(Z_{k_1}^{(0)}, \dots, Z_{k_\ell}^{(0)} \right) \,,\qquad n\to\infty\,,
    \end{equation}
    and the following convergence in distribution  of characteristic polynomial $p_n$ for the topology of local uniform convergence in $\mathbb{D}$:
    \begin{equation*}
        p_n \stackrel{\rm d}{\rightarrow} F_0 \,, \qquad n\to\infty\,,
    \end{equation*}
    where $F_0$ is the random holomorphic function 
    \begin{equation}

        F_0(z) = \exp \left( - \sum_{k \geqslant 1} \frac{z^k}{k} Z_k^{(0)} \right) .
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

