{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.900372+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f1c7ad627c61303826d19ddd65939c901c90ff0af5ec21c8a4f0849d0636577","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2608.02319, 'Averaging Principle for Ordinary Differential Equations in a Multiscale Random Environment'] For all $n,k\geq1$, $T>0$, $x\in E$ and $y\in\mathbb R^d$ we set
