{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.786915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f6a8d17955bf44c2eb9ad7c968cd85becde91f614fb557cf94d98e94f6f1fbc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 (Riemannian complex) of arXiv:2609.00183, '2609.00183'] A {\bf Riemannian complex} is a cell complex $Y$ equipped with a collection of metrics $G=\{G^S\}$ such that 
