uniformly in $\mu \in [1 - \delta_2, 1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.250641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f84f9b4c58d9a6d3fa51bee7df4e7b33a26f69aa8eb54d7bc975f0e1e843c23","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2605.22760, 'Extremes of Gaussian fields with a product term in the variance'] Assume \ref{ass:variance}--\ref{ass:correlation}.  Fix \(S_1,S_2>0\).  For every \(\varepsilon>0\), there exists \(\delta>0\) such that, uniformly for \(\bfv\in[0,\delta]^2\) and all sufficiently large \(u\),
\begin{align}
