    where the limit is in $L^2(\mathbb P)$,  $(\xi_k)_{k\geq1}$ are the i.i.d. labels of the loops, and $(\phi^\mathds A_k)_{k\geq1}$ are independent GFFs inside each loop.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.158364+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f93ff63badb7bb9b00f8b6f623d31708a1e3f46eb78a367a934089fe2c2f52c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2604.15874, 'On Continuous Data Assimilation for a class of 2D and 3D stochastic non-Newtonian fluids o'] Assume that condition \eqref{third-grade-paremeters-res} and Hypothesis \ref{hyp-noise} are satisfied. Also, let $\f \in \Vbb^*$ and $\Urm_0 \in \Hbb$. 
