{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.647992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6fce430a0bbb7c594c5d6cc52d7e9db029e60a2441beca4a4bd1888fc4885183","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 106 (Natural Brownian window certificate) of arXiv:2608.08756, 'Infinite-Dimensional L\'evy Area and Spectral Ancestry'] There is a numerical $c_*>0$ such that, for every $L\ge1$ and
