{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.995137+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6fef4a2672fe8f3b9773bd216c7aabea12a91f1292cbe31062938fb9893bad4a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-V3 of arXiv:2609.02552, 'Resolvent Estimates for the Stokes Operator \\ in a Three-Dimensional Lipschitz Domain'] Suppose  $q>3$ and $r= |\lambda|^{-1/2}$, where $ \lambda\in \Sigma_\theta$.
Let  $(u, \phi)\in W^{1, q} (B_{Nr}; \mathbb{C}^3) \times L^q(B_{Nr}; \mathbb{C})$ be a weak solution of
\begin{equation}
\left\{
\aligned
-\Delta u +\nabla \phi +\lambda u & = F &\quad & \text{ in } B_{Nr},\\
\text{\rm div} (u) & =0 & \quad & \text{ in } B_{Nr},\\
\endaligned
\right.
\end{equation}
where $N\ge 4$ and $F\in L^\infty(E_{Nr}; \mathbb{C}^3)$.
Then
\begin{equation}
\aligned
|\lambda| \| u \|_{L^\infty(B_r)}
& \le C \left\{
\| F \|_{L^\infty (B_{Nr})}   N^{\frac{3}{q}}
+ |\lambda| \| u \|_{L^\infty(B_{Nr})} N^{\frac{3}{q}-1}\right\}\\
& +C |\lambda|^{\frac12} \left(\fint_{B_{Nr}} |\nabla u|^q \right)^{1/q}  N^{\frac{3}{q}-1} 
+ C |\lambda|^{\frac12} \inf_{\beta\in \mathbb{C}} \left(\fint_{B_{Nr}} |\phi -\beta |^q \right)^{1/q}  N^{\frac{3}{q}-1},
\endaligned
\end{equation}
where $C$ depends only on $\theta$ and  $q$.","status":"unverified"}

