{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.184155+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70164f72abc330a503637f8e304913a28d60d5fd274902014bb458a7d3e9f761","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:tree of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] There is a tree $T = ([d], E)$ such that for every edge $e = (i,j) \in E$, we have
