{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.667641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_701925b0bb846ee4e7add89f141d31b57f388665639b41be995941b95e4d9668","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 12 of arXiv:2608.30859, 'Conservation Laws with Discontinuous Flux:\\ A First Application to Traffic Flow'] Let $y(t)$ be the solution to the Cauchy problem \eqref{eq:Yode}. Then
