{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.275192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_701a70c6273794f0db96c57739d379ce30693cc93e0cbfe3ba99e7ba45ff84ff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:matrix_azuma-gtp of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\mathcal{Y},\hat\mathcal{Z},T)$ be a sequential gamble space, $T\in\mathbb{N}$, satisfying Condition~(cond:usa-minimax of the paper).
