        For every $(s,x;t,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{4}_{\uparrow}(R)$ and every $s<r<t$, we have 
        \begin{align*}
            \mathcal{L}_R(s,x;t,y) = \sup_{z\in(x_0,y_0)}\left(
                \mathcal{L}_R(s,x;r,z) + \mathcal{L}_R(r,z; t,y)
