{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.729988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70957f67c3d4b6b3b6c6db2062fe50d5b916bc448f68cd74b887e718b829d2a6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2605.18136, 'L\'evy processes with partially stochastic resetting'] Let $p \in [0,1]$ and $q >0$.  We fix $[u_1,u_2] \subset \B$ Then, for  $\gamma \in \R$ and $x, \, y \in \B$, we define the resolvent series
		\begin{equation}
			\overline{\V}^{(p)}_\gamma [\f^{(q)}](x,y) :=  \sum^{\infty}_{k=1} \gamma^k \V ^{(p)}_{k}[ \f^{(q)}](x,y) 
		\end{equation}
in terms of the recursion
		\begin{align}
			\V_{1}^{(p)}[\f^{(q)}](x,y) &:=\f^{(q)}(x,y), \notag \\

			\V_{n}^{(p)}[\f^{(q)}](x,y) & : = \int^{u_2}_{u_1} \f^{(q)}(x,z) \, \V_{n-1}^{(p)}[\f^{(q)}](pz,y)\, \dd z, \quad n \geq 2, 
