{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.846313+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70eab6146c18d9a8ff63734c652be9c2c23de8bdb67dd42cf6c0500970a8617c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem:bounded of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] Assume that $\nabla^{k}\Upsilon_\tau$ is bounded for all $\tau\in{\mathcal T}^{\le N}$ and $k+|\tau|\le N+1$. Then, for any solution $Z$ of (equation eq: sol Davie branched of the paper),
