{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.353723+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70f629335eec6f374e69f29bb472464c5c59c350d53955ba3729ccc0d68eec64","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2506.16260, 'Fractional Compound Poisson Random Fields on Plane'] For $\alpha_2=1$, the distribution function of (\ref{tfcprfml}) is given by
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathrm{Pr}\{\mathscr{Y}_{\alpha_1,\alpha_2}^\beta(t_1,t_2)\leq y\}=E_{\alpha_1,1}(-\lambda t_1^{\alpha_1}t_2)\textbf{1}_{[0,\infty)}(y)+\int_{-\infty}^{y}f_{\mathscr{Y}_{\alpha_1,1}^\beta}(x,t_1,t_2)\,\mathrm{d}x,\ y\ge0,\ (t_1,t_2)\in\mathbb{R}^2_+,
	\end{equation*}
	where
	\begin{equation*}
	f_{\mathscr{Y}_{\alpha_1,1}^\beta}(y,t_1,t_2)=\frac{1}{y}\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}(\lambda\sigma t_1^{\alpha_1}t_2y^\beta)^nE_{\alpha_1,\alpha_1 n+1}^{n+1}(-\lambda t_1^{\alpha_1}t_2)E_{\beta,\beta n}^n(-\sigma y^\beta).
	\end{equation*}
	It solves
	\begin{equation*}
		\sigma\frac{\partial^{\alpha_1}}{\partial t_1^{\alpha_1}}f_{\mathscr{Y}_{\alpha_1,1}^\beta}(y,t_1,t_2)=-\bigg(\lambda t_1+\frac{\partial^{\alpha_1}}{\partial t_1^{\alpha_1}}\bigg)\frac{\partial^\beta}{\partial y^\beta}f_{\mathscr{Y}_{\alpha_1,1}^\beta}(y,t_1,t_2),
	\end{equation*}
	with $f_{\mathscr{Y}_{\alpha_1,1}^\beta}(y,0,t_2)=0$. Also,
	\begin{equation*}
		\int_{0}^{\infty}f_{\mathscr{Y}_{\alpha_1,1}^\beta}(y,t_1,t_2)\,\mathrm{d}y=1-E_{\alpha_1,1}(-\lambda t_1^{\alpha_1}t_2).
	\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.075880+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70f67538fc619bb341a504a415cd5cd78be62d17d0b4050ca4f17159fc5e7e83","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Lipchitzness-random-environement of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Let $F^{(t)}$ be an $s$-holomorphic function on the $s$-embedding $\mathcal{S}^{(t)}(\Lambda_{n})$ obtained via Lemma (lem:SDE-embedding of the paper). Then, with $\mathbf{P}$-probability at least $1-O(n^{-4})$, there exist a constant $C(\omega)>0$ such that for any $0\leq t \leq t^{(\alpha)}_n$, the function $F^{(t)}$ is Lipchitz at every scale, meaning that for any  $z_{1,2}\in B(u,d)$ one has 
