{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.825002+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7120487e31bc3b74550578c552f893791607b251441307284d866430e528a4b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem lyapunov-poincare of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] (Stitching Theorem)

    Denote $K = \{q \in \cS: b(q) > 0\}$ and $\nu_K(q) = \frac{\nu(q)}{\nu(K)} \, \forall q \in K$.
    Under Assumptions (assumption: ctmc of the paper), (assumption: foster-lyapunov of the paper) and (assumption: weighted-poincare of the paper), the following inequality holds

    \begin{align}
        \Var_\nu(f) \leq \frac{1 + \br{\sum_{q \in \cS} b(q) \nu_K(q)} C_b}{\gamma} \langle f, -\cL f \rangle_\nu \, \forall f \in \ell_{2,\nu},
    \end{align}
    where $C_b$ is the weighted local Poincar\'e constant in Assumption (assumption: weighted-poincare of the paper), $\nu$ is the stationary distribution of the CTMC and $b: \cS \rightarrow [0,\infty)$ is the positive drift term in Assumption (assumption: foster-lyapunov of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.768266+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71210da40a416015853e5ff185f3562cd0f1e190f8b0289d4650ca0eac970d34","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 23 of arXiv:2608.26803, 'On bubbling of Fueter maps'] Let $K$ be a compact smooth manifold of dimension $k$ and let $\cR \subset W$ be a codimension $n$ Fredholm $C^1$-rectifiable subset of a Banach space $W$. If $k < n$, then the exceptional locus
  \begin{equation*}
    \cE_K (\cR) \coloneq \{ f \in C^1(K, W) \, | \, f(K) \cap \cR \neq \emptyset \}
  \end{equation*}
  is Fredholm $C^1$ rectifiable of codimension $n-k$ in $C^1(K, W)$.","status":"unverified"}

