{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.744406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71394f6f323d47e5422e5e55c4e504c59f5a5a0e5ffd56df55bc5889abbf6489","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor partitionFunctionTemperatureInterpolation of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Assume $0\le\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}/2$ and $\mu\in L^\infty\cap\mathcal{P}({\mathbb{R}}^\mathsf{d})$; if $\mathsf{s}=0$, assume (equation eq:logEnergyAssumption of the paper).  Set
\begin{align}
a_{N,\mathsf{s}}\coloneqq
\begin{cases}
\log(e+N), & \mathsf{s}=0,\\
N^{\mathsf{s}/\mathsf{d}}, & 0<\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}.
\end{cases}
\end{align}
For every $B>0$, there is a constant $C_B(\mu)<\infty$ such that
\begin{align}
\sup_{N\ge1}\ \sup_{0\le\beta\le B}\ {\mathsf{K}}_{N,\beta}(\mu)\le C_B(\mu)
\end{align}
and, for all $\beta\ge0$ and $N\ge1$,
\begin{align}
{\mathsf{K}}_{N,\beta}(\mu)
\le C_B(\mu)\exp\pa[\Big]{C_B(\mu)\,(\beta-B)_+\,a_{N,\mathsf{s}}}.
\end{align}
In particular, for every $B_\ast>0$ and $\gamma\in{\mathbb{R}}$, there is a constant $C_{B_\ast,\mu}<\infty$ such that, along the temperature scaling $\beta_N=\beta_\ast N^\gamma$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{0\le\beta_\ast\le B_\ast}\ \log {\mathsf{K}}_{N,\beta_\ast N^\gamma}(\mu)
\le
\begin{cases}
C_{B_\ast,\mu}, & \gamma\le0,\\
C_{B_\ast,\mu}\,N^\gamma\log(e+N), & \gamma>0,\ \mathsf{s}=0,\\
C_{B_\ast,\mu}\,N^{\gamma+\mathsf{s}/\mathsf{d}}, & \gamma>0,\ 0<\mathsf{s}<\mathsf{d}/2.
\end{cases}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.659129+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71397f59b9837adc672373e25a053f262323026b1de7a34936eea3d16300e59c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 20 (An equivalent condition for matrix scalability; Thm. 4.1 in \cite{menon1969spectrum}) of arXiv:2604.23461, 'Scaling limit of Sinkhorn-rescaled Random Matrices \\ via Stability of Static Schrödinger '] Let $\A\in \R_{\ge 0}^{m\times n}$ be an $m\times n$ nonnegative matrix and let $(\r,\c)$ be an $m\times n$ margin with strictly positive row and column sums. Then the following are equivalent:
