{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.548106+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7180ac0fa70c0fd338fb0526ae3fad54ebc0abaea5886fa3ff362cf83dd4f3f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 34 (The support of ooSBM) of arXiv:2604.01852, 'The on/off Brownian snake'] Let $\mu_{\rm d}$, $\mu_{\rm a} \in \mathcal{M}_F(\mathbb{R}^d)$ be such that $\mu_{\rm d} + \mu_{\rm a}$ is a non-zero measure and let $\gamma$, $c$, $\Tilde{c}>0$. Let $\mathcal{Y}=(\mathcal{Y}^{(\rm d)}, \mathcal{Y}^{(\rm a)})$ be an $\text{ooSBM}(\gamma, c, \Tilde{c})$ with initial measure $(\mu_{\rm d}, \mu_{\rm a})$. Then we have that
    \begin{equation*}
        (\text{supp}(\mathcal{Y}_s^{(\rm d)}) \cup \text{supp}(\mathcal{Y}_s^{(\rm a)}))_{s \geq 0}
    \end{equation*}
    is an increasing process a.s. That is to say that a.s. the support of ooSBM is monotonically increasing at all times.
    \par
    Furthermore, we also have for any $s>0$ that
    \begin{equation*}
        \text{dim}\Big(\text{supp}(\mathcal{Y}_s^{(\rm d)}) \cup \text{supp}(\mathcal{Y}_s^{(\rm a)})\Big) = \text{dim}(\text{supp}(\mu_{\rm d})) \vee \text{dim}(\text{supp}(\mu_{\rm a})) \vee (4 \wedge d) \text{   a.s.}
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:50:44.858117+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71865ea1358685cb47c48506d3d99cb391380e2efa4e93b5ddc138f26a7d0d15","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 25 of arXiv:2607.16479, 'The Site Frequency Spectrum in an Exponentially-Growing Population with Selection'] There exists constants $C_1>0$ such that if $k>\frac{C_1}{\varepsilon}$, then:
