{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:10.025429+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_718962f3c94fcb8d13a94aba9f3771c64932c3814a05e9a1564d0688fbaae3aa","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:tail of arXiv:2607.19844, 'Binomial probabilities at a fixed distance from the mode:\\ size-biasing and the complete '] For $|t|<Np$,
	\begin{equation}
		\sum_{k\ge1}\frac{1}{N^{k}}\cdot\frac{(-1)^{k}t^{k}}{k\,p^{k}}
