{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.527934+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71e8e1720a917d738a17dce74c7463e49248c3b867a26c851630b236a64e7307","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 14 of arXiv:2604.01748, 'Largest-loop-first loop-erased random walk on $\mathbb{Z}^{4}$'] Let $e_{n} = n (\log n)^{-\frac{1}{8}}$ and $K_{n} = (\log n)^{\frac{1}{8}}$. We partition the time interval $[0,n]$ into $K_{n}$ subintervals of equal length $e_{n}$ as follows:
