{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.896871+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71ea69e8470a0ad5f9b313097ff6cc51c724bc9183be2d0dc3862fd21f511ae7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def-RV-sph of arXiv:2510.16431, '\Large Liouville quantum gravity: from random planar maps to conformal field theory'] Let $\alpha_i\in\mathbb{R}$  and $z_i\in \mathbb{C}$ for $i = 1, ..., N$ where $N\ge 1$ and all the $z_i$'s are distinct.
        Sample $(h, \mathbf c)$   from $ C _{\mathbb C}^{(\alpha_i,z_i)_i}  P_{\mathbb C} \times [e^{(\sum_i \alpha_i  - 2Q)c}dc]$ where  $C _{\mathbb C}^{(\alpha_i,z_i)_i}=\prod_{i=1}^N|z_i|_+^{-\alpha_i(2Q -\alpha_i)} e^{\sum_{i < j} \alpha_i \alpha_j G_{\mathbb C}(z_i, z_j)}$.
Then the field
\begin{equation}
    \phi = h -2Q \log |\cdot|_+  + \sum_{i=1}^N \alpha_i G_{\mathbb C}(\cdot, z_i) + \mathbf c
\end{equation}
is called the  \emph{Liouville field on $ \mathbb C$ with insertions $(\alpha_i,z_i)_{1\le i\le N}$}. We denote its law by $\mathrm{LF}_{ \mathbbm{C}}^{(\alpha_i,z_i)_i}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.492279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71ecfcba037c9055b2aa83158056e1d2e5eab131cb47fb047ae581627411b65a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 30 of arXiv:2509.09589, 'Geometry of critical discrete structures: long-range percolation on the hierarchical latti'] [Lower bound]
