{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.079599+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7231ed676997146d03e0d4cb12232a13523191a7e342a14911af190de592c8e5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 (Per-step Descent for Smooth Losses) of arXiv:2608.27763, 'Fast Weight Attention for Continual Learning'] Let $f:\mathbb{R}^{d_x\times d_v}\to\mathbb{R}$ be $L$-smooth with respect to the Frobenius norm. For any step size $\eta\in(0,2/L)$, the gradient step $\Sbb^{+}=\Sbb-\eta\nabla f(\Sbb)$ satisfies
