{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.845263+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7286254a9a792666f2d062a0c0c1fff7142ecfe2a4dbea9ff12a04b4d267f5cf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th: a priori branched of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] Under Assumption (As: regularity assumption of the paper), for any solution $Z$ of (equation eq: sol Davie branched of the paper) we have
		\begin{equation*}
			\|Z^{[N+1]}\|_{(N+\beta)\alpha,\mu} \lesssim_{\mathbb X,\sigma,T} 
