{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.118946+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72b1aa02d470f895d8f36addd4386ee4824bbf7c0fd4fc22855e11a3aebd10fc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary Ergodic:AsymptoticDriftDiffusion of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] Fix $\epsilon>0$. There exists positive constants $C_1,C_2$ depending on $d$, $\|b\|_{0,\alpha}$ and $\|\sigma\|_{0,\alpha}$ such that, for all $t$ sufficiently large (depending on $d$, $\|b\|_{0,\alpha}$, $\|\sigma\|_{0,\alpha}$ and $\epsilon$),
