{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.690526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72e4e3f52ba610c721d919413cea8239c36d1602a00b173e2a5ce633d20efcd3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:concentration3 of arXiv:2411.10235, '\textbf{Smooth transport map via diffusion process}'] There exists  $0<C_\star<C_2$ such that if $t\in [0,1)$  and $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$ satisfy \begin{equation}
