{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:06.117009+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72f2583cc58677107e1080fbf11a17e072b460cffd9f48417fd5555dba06ec2d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 (Bartlett spectrum) of arXiv:2608.22342, 'Completely Positive Entropy and Fourier Central Limit Theorems for Stationary Random Measu'] Let $\eta$ be stationary with local second moments. There is a unique positive
translation-bounded Radon measure $\sigma_\eta$ on $\bR^d$ such that
\begin{equation}

    \int (\mathbb S f)^\circ\,\overline{(\mathbb S g)^\circ}\,d\eta
    =\int_{\bR^d}\hat f(\xi)\overline{\hat g(\xi)}\,
      d\sigma_\eta(\xi),
    \qquad f,g\in\mathcal S(\bR^d).
