{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.873128+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72fde1e92115e62e06e01b089a9812b5fa8d6508072e6e3a615b60a894ffa82c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:EnergyMeas of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] Let $(X,d,\mu,\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ be an MMD space.
		The \emph{energy measure} $\Gamma(f,f)$ of $f\in\mathcal{F}$
		associated with $(X,d,\mu,\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ is defined,
		first for $f\in\mathcal{F}\cap L^{\infty}(X,\mu)$ as the unique ($[0,\infty]$-valued)
		Borel measure on $X$ such that
		\begin{equation}
			\int_{X} g \, d\Gamma(f,f)= \mathcal{E}(f,fg)-\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{E}(f^{2},g) \qquad \textrm{for all $g \in \mathcal{F}\cap C_{\mathrm{c}}(X)$,}
		\end{equation}
		and then by
		$\Gamma(f,f)(A):=\lim_{n\to\infty}\Gamma\bigl((-n)\vee(f\wedge n),(-n)\vee(f\wedge n)\bigr)(A)$
		for each Borel subset $A$ of $X$ for general $f\in\mathcal{F}$. The signed measure $\Gamma(f,g)$ for $f,g \in \mathcal{F}$ is defined by polarization.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.393875+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7306404ab3a87c708804d5db2bad4121040c5259943c10c1a18d47e5c1dcea21","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2609.04139, 'The conformally invariant metric on CLE$_4$ II:\\ existence of geodesics'] Fix constants $0<c_1<c_2<c_2^\prime<c_3<c_4<1$.  Then,  there exists a constant $C>1$ depending only on $c_1,c_2,c_2^\prime,c_3$,  and $c_4$,  such that the following is true for each $0 < r \leq \widetilde{r}$ and each compact set $K \subset V_{\widetilde{r}}$ with $\dist(K , \partial V_{\widetilde{r}}) \geq c_4,  \sup_{z \in K} \Re(z) - \inf_{z \in K} \Re(z) \leq c_4^{-1}$,  and $K \subset V_{c_3 r , \widetilde{r}}$: with probability at least $1 - C / r$,  we have that
