{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.163802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_730773d6ca74a0d870b8f198028ca278a55173671aceef400c1301cc84d961e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma convolutioninequality of arXiv:2411.16103, 'Non-commutative Stein's Method: Applications to Free Probability and Sums of Non-commutati'] If $\gamma_1, \rho_1, \dots, \gamma_n, \rho_n \in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R})$ are probability measures with finite first moments, then 
