{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.356846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_730b6b1276d70617c53015a640930bd6d2fe6f92beea83ea6aa6598dd34fa3e9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:lm:aniso of arXiv:2607.20956, 'Sharp moduli of continuity for Gaussian fields and stochastic PDEs via correlation bounds'] Fix $t_0 \in I$.
    Suppose either
    \begin{enumerate}[(1)]
        \item $\ell(x) = \log\log(x)$ and $h_n = e^{-\rho n^\gamma}$, where $\rho>0$ and $\gamma>0$; or
        \item $\ell(x) = \log(x)$ and $h_n = n^{-\gamma}$, where $\gamma>0$.
    \end{enumerate}
    Then, under Assumptions (a:sigma:aniso of the paper) and (a:psi:lil of the paper), we have
    \begin{align}
        \lim_{h\to0^+} \sup_{t\in I: 0<\phi(t-t_0) \le h} \frac{|X(t)-X(t_0)|}{\phi(t-t_0)\sqrt{\ell(1/ \psi(\phi(t-t_0)))}} = C \quad \text{a.s.}
    \end{align}
    for some non-random number $C=C(t_0)$ such that
    \begin{align}
        C \le \begin{cases}
        (\sqrt{2}+KC_4/2)C_2 & \text{in Case (1),}\\
        (\sqrt{2/\nu}+KC_4/2)C_2
        & \text{in Case (2),}
    \end{cases}
    \end{align}
