{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.452389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73221aa55d6704cb2f30f21b11ddd0cc0206abff7f128799a1235f4374799381","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eqn : Intro/framework/LDP_general case of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] Let $\mathbb{X}$ be a Hausdorff topological space. We call \emph{rate function} a lower semicontinuous map $I:\mathbb{X}\rightarrow \intervalleff0\infty$, i.e. a map whose sublevels $\set{x \in \mathbb{X}}{I(x)\le t}$, for $t\ge 0$, are closed. We further say that $I$ is a \emph{good rate function} if its sublevels are compact.

    We say that a random process $(X_n)_{n\ge 1}$ with values in $\mathbb{X}$ follows the \emph{large deviation principle} (LDP), at speed $a_n$, with the rate function $I$ if for every Borel set $A\subseteq \mathbb{X}$,
\begin{equation}

    \inf_{x\in \overline{A}} I(x)
    \le \liminf_{n\to\infty}-\frac{1}{a_n} \log \Pb{ X_n \in A } 
    \le \limsup_{n\to\infty}-\frac{1}{a_n} \log \Pb{ X_n \in A } 
    \le \inf_{x\in \mathring{A}} I(x).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

