{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.267105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73b21b4c8b9077c7e8cc2589ece7a10ad31e953c3c36fa4adc7aa6dad00fea91","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th marche of arXiv:2411.05541, 'Gaskets of $O(2)$ loop-decorated random planar maps'] Let $\nu$ be a probability distribution on $\mathbb{Z}$ such that $h^\downarrow$ is $\nu$-harmonic on $\mathbb{Z}_{\ge 1}$ and such that $\nu$ is not the Dirac mass at zero $\delta_0$. Assume that
