{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.840442+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73d1fba6a80eef3d71e703713427fbeb4a6805a588193179f90efe27a5a1a57b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 of arXiv:2608.13374, 'Nearly Sharp Comparison Results for sliced and max-sliced Wasserstein distances'] For $1 \leq k < d$ and $U \in \mathfrak{G}_{d,k}$, write $U\cY := \sbrac{Uy : y \in \cY} \subseteq \R^k$ and $d(z, U\cY) := \inf_{y \in \cY}\norm{z - Uy}$. Then
