{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.943546+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7404d24cd0eb4ab2122d91600f95d16ae67fa3c5e5582db616dd4b1ae5f9b2b0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm ldp of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Fix $\Lambda$, $R\subset \mathbb{R}^d$ compact, connected with piecewise smooth boundary, and a boundary asymptotic flow $b$ on $\partial R$ which is extendable outside. Let $R_n\subset \frac{1}{n}\Lambda$ a lattice approximation of $R$, fix thresholds $\theta_{n}$ going to zero sufficiently slowly, and probability measures $\rho_{n,N}$ as above. 

    The measures $(\rho_{n,N})_{n,N\geq 1}$ satisfy a large deviation principle in the iterated limit as $N$ and then $n$ go to infinity in the weak topology on flows with good rate function $I:\text{AF}(\Lambda,R,b)\to \mathbb{R}$. That is, for any Borel set $B$ in the weak topology on flows, 
    \begin{align*}
        -\inf_{\omega\in {B}^{\circ}} I(\omega) \leq \liminf_{n\to \infty} \liminf_{N\to\infty} \frac{1}{Nn^d} \log \rho_{n,N}(B) \leq \limsup_{n\to \infty} \limsup_{N\to \infty} \frac{1}{Nn^d} \log \rho_{n,N}(B) \leq -\inf_{\omega\in \overline{B}} I(\omega)
    \end{align*}
    where $\overline{B}, B^{\circ}$ denote the closure and interior of $B$ respectively. Further, if $\omega$ is an asymptotic flow, the rate function $I$ is given explicitly by 
    \begin{align}
        I(\omega) = C_b +\int_R \sigma(\omega(x)) \, \mathrm{d} x,
    \end{align}
    where $C_b\geq 0$ is an additive constant and $\sigma$ is the surface tension for $\Lambda$ from Theorem~(thm:legendre_duality of the paper), i.e., it is the Legendre dual of the free energy on the torus $F(\alpha) = \log \sum_{j=1}^D \exp(e_j\cdot \alpha)$. In particular $C_b =-\min_{\omega\in \text{AF}(\Lambda,R,b)} \int_R \sigma(\omega(x))\,\mathrm{d} x$. If $\omega$ is not an asymptotic flow, then $I(\omega) = \infty.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.286158+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_740820b3f57a7fb85f08d08b47a187baebb79cfbffcd71ded895a80afa112c54","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem M of arXiv:2411.01847, 'Well-Posedness of Stochastic Chemotaxis System'] Suppose $h=(h_k)_{k=1}^\infty$, is an $\ell^2$-valued

progressively measurable function on $\Omega\times[0,T]\times\mathcal{O}$ such that $$\mathbb{E}\|\|h\|_{\ell^2}\|_{2,2,T}^2< \infty.$$
 Then $M(t)=\int_0^te^{-(t-s)A}h(s) \, dW_s$ is the solution to the following SPDE:
	\begin{equation*}
		\begin{cases}
dM(t) = -A M(t)  \, dt + h(t) \,  \, dW_t, \\
M(0) = 0,
\end{cases}
	\end{equation*}
	in $L^2(\mathcal{O})$, and has the $L^\infty$-regularity:
	\begin{align}
		\mathbb{E} \sup_{t\in[0,T\wedge\tau]}\|M(t)\|_\infty^\eta\leq C(1+T)^{C'}\mathbb{E}\|\|h\|_{\ell^2}\|_{2r,2q,T\wedge\tau}^\eta.
	\end{align}
for any $\eta>0$, $r,q\in(1,\infty]$ with $\frac{1}{r}+\frac{1}{q}<1$ and stopping time $\tau$. The constants $C,C'$ may depend on $\eta, r, q $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

