{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.288354+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_745f76822b40389961c00797f4bf45cb3937a74fa19eee1833945d74d9dddc3f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main Thr  of arXiv:2411.01849, 'A tamed-adaptive Milstein scheme for stochastic differential equations with low regularity'] Assume conditions \textbf{A0-A2} hold. 
	   Then, for any $T>0$,  $ l_0 \geq \max\{2,  \frac{4l}{3(1+\alpha)}\},$ $p_0 \ge 4(l + \alpha + 1)$, there exists a positive constant $C_T$ depending on $x_0, \gamma, \eta, \alpha, l, l_0, \lambda, p_0$, and  $T$ such that
