where $j(\xi)$, $\Omega_{j(\xi)}$ and the functions $f_{j(\xi)}^{(\xi,k)}$ are as in Lemma (lemma_RN_infty of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.576971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_747108e00a5d076e3e021ec5dc7ffbfa4cbd558b4db21be3776db4d309a7a37c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem-trick of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] For any $x \in \bb R$ and any random variable $Z$,
