{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.609178+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_747876dd696024bead589abc1811088611d76f3742867f88e0a16e27118af762","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-5.8 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] For each~$\alpha_0\in(0,\ffrac12)$ there exists~$\tilde\epsilon>0$ such that 
