{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.713545+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75283e9f351b8c2c18280a651345389acdfae43a83cbe1a2445d825a81572ddb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Pro:Barlow of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] For every $y\in\mathbb{Z}^d$, there exist finite positive constants $C$ and $s$ depending on $d,\mathfrak{p}$ and a nonnegative $\omega$-measurable random variable $\mathcal{R}(y)$ satisfying 
		\begin{equation}
			\forall r>0,\quad \mathbb{P}_\mathfrak{p}(\mathcal{R}(y)\geqslant r)\leqslant C\exp\left(-\frac{r^s}{C}\right),
		\end{equation} 
		such that for almost every $\omega\in\Omega$ and every $y \in \mathscr{C}_\infty$, when $R>\mathcal{R}(y)$, we have
		\begin{equation}
			\forall T>0,\quad P^\omega_y\Big(\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\vert S_t-y\vert>R\Big)\leqslant C_1\Psi\left(C_2R,T\right),
		\end{equation}
