{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.086557+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_756909e39e42e4345124c274ddd0c2a269aaaed671ba69d5b57f4b736c51ac67","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 18 of arXiv:2607.13849, 'Rearranged Stochastic Heat Equation with an Entropy Gradient Structure'] For $\delta >0$, 
let $(X_t, \mathscr{J}_t)_{0 \le t \le T}$ be a weak limit in $\mathcal{C}([0,T], \mathcal{H}^{-1}_{\mathrm{Sym}}(\mathbb{S})\times \mathcal{H}^{-(3+\delta)}_{\mathrm{Sym}}(\mathbb{S}))$  of the sequence of pair processes $\{(X_t^{(h)},\mathscr{J}_t(X^{(h)}))_{0 \le t \le T}\}_{{h \in T/{\mathbb N}^*}}$ when $h\searrow 0$. 
