{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.363307+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7569fe8ac22e336a8a76ee17aec97a7fe325afb06ac2fe4f70c1a84e95448ff3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-limit of arXiv:2507.09922, 'A scaling limit for Vlasov equations with electrostatic fluctuations'] Assume that the initial condition $f_0$ belongs to $(L^1\cap L^3)(\mathbb{T}^3\times \mathbb{R}^3)$ with finite kinetic energy
  $$\mathcal K(f_0)= \int_{\mathbb{T}^3\times \mathbb{R}^3} |v|^2 f_0(x,v)\, dx dv<+\infty. $$
Let $W_N$ be a sequence of smooth noises whose covariance functions $Q_N$ verify the condition (equation condition-covariance of the paper). For any $N\ge 1$, let $f^N$ be a weak solution to the stochastic Vlasov equation
  \begin{equation}
  d f^N + v\cdot\nabla_x f^N\, dt + (E_{\rho^N} + B v\times \bm{e}_3) \cdot\nabla_v f^N \, dt + \sum_k \sigma^N_k \cdot\nabla_v f^N \, d W^k_t = \kappa \Delta_v f^N\, dt
  \end{equation}
with initial condition $f^N_0= f_0$. Then any convergent subsequence of $\{f^N\}_N$ converge weakly, in the topology of $C\big([0,T], H^{-\epsilon }_{x,v, loc} \big)$, to weak solutions of (equation limit-Vlasov of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.525131+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_756a849cba09613538444a5ea1c4f530d291e0c255db483a2d2f6857a478b880","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:locality_upper_semi_continuity of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{prop:upper_semi_continuity}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \in \mathbf{N}$, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel satisfying $J(x,y) = \Omega(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ for $\alpha \in (0, 2)$. 

