{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:53.204189+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75700b635ad51faa5478ac96f80067f8e762c19ca315e62adff8101f38fab7bc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 of arXiv:2606.12670, 'The censored stochastic six-vertex model and parabolic Kazhdan--Lusztig $R$-polynomials'] For $\lambda\leq\lambda'$ it holds that $v_\lambda\preceq v_{\lambda'}$, i.e., for any decreasing set $E\subset\mathcal P$ and any $\lambda\leq\lambda'$ it holds that
