for certain positive constants $C_{1}$ and $C_{2}$, which are independent of $m$ and $\eta$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.224113+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75791150c9fa12b807e5eedf60631a2b61f203aaa157aa3e97c4c972e163b315","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm potential-zero of arXiv:2411.16376, 'Higher order approximations in arcsine laws for subordinators'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t\geq0}$ be a killed subordinator which is not identically zero. Assume that the Laplace exponent $\Phi(z)$ satisfies the following condition:
\begin{enumerate}[label={\upshape (\Alph*')}]
\item There exist constants $n\in\ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}\cup\{0\}$, $c_0\in(0,+\infty)$, $c_1,\dots,c_n\in\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}\setminus\{0\}$ and $\beta_0<\beta_1<\dots<\beta_n<+\infty$ with $\beta_0\in(0,1]$, and a locally integrable function $R:(0,+\infty)\to(0,+\infty)$ such that $R(t)$ is non-increasing on $(r,+\infty)$ for some $r>0$, $R(t)=o(t^{-1-\beta_n})$, as $t\to+\infty$, and
\begin{align}
    \frac{d}{dz}
    \bigg(
    \frac{1}{\Phi(z)}
    -
    \sum_{k=0}^n
    \frac{1}{c_k z^{\beta_k}}
    \bigg)
    =
    O(R(|z|)),
    \quad
    \text{as $z\to\infty$ in $\{z\in\ensuremath{\mathbb{C}}\mid {\rm Re}\,z>0\}$}.	
\end{align}
\end{enumerate}
Then the potential measure $U|_{(0,+\infty)}$ restricted over $(0,+\infty)$ admits a continuous density $u(x)$ $(0<x<+\infty)$ which can be estimated as
\begin{align}
   u(x)
   =
   \sum_{k=0}^n
   \frac{x^{-1+\beta_k}}{c_k\Gamma(\beta_k)}+O(\varepsilon_1(x)),
   \quad\text{as $x\to0+$,}
\end{align}
where
\begin{align}
    \varepsilon_1(x)
    =
    x^{-2}R(x^{-1})+x^{-1}\int_{x^{-1}}^{+\infty} R(t)\,dt.	
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.049162+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_757b34b8e846bd7342654632d05f969857875e037217159cf691eb97a58e3019","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 7 (Supercritical cutoff for $X^{(N)}$) of arXiv:2608.15914, 'Absorption cutoff and stationary singularities for rounded Gaussian random dynamical syste'] Under the assumptions of \cref{thm:gaussian-process-cutoff}, $X^{(N)}$ has
