{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:26:02.365030+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_757beaea70f083609fc4957f1126e5b95fa55396171bf5ef6c80823da0a786e5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\mathcal{G}$ denote the standard horizontal foliation on the neighborhood $N(\mathcal{W}) = [-1,2]^2_{x,z}$ of the square window $\mathcal{W} = [0,1]^2$, i.e., $\mathcal{G}$ is tangent to $\partial_x$. Let $\star \in \{ \sharp, \flat\}$. A \textbf{$\star$~modification of $\mathcal{G}$ in $N(\mathcal{W})$} is a smooth foliation $\mathcal{G}^\star$ on $N(\mathcal{W})$ satisfying
     \begin{itemize}
        \item $T\mathcal{G}^\star$ is either tangent or transverse to $T \mathcal{G}$; it is positively transverse if $\star = \sharp$ and negatively transverse if $\star = \flat$,
         \item $\mathcal{G}^\star$ coincides with $\mathcal{G}$ near $\partial N(\mathcal{W})$,
         \item $\mathcal{G}^\star$ is transverse to $\mathcal{G}$ in a neighborhood of $\mathcal{W}$.
     \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.635144+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_757cca8a8bce434b24c4619c26f241a78dc574f188d4f5ad76c442cc4702e1d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theo:existence mixed of arXiv:2512.12124, 'A discontinuous percolation phase transition on the hierarchical lattice'] For all $L\in \mathbb{N}, d \in \mathbb{N}$, and $a>1$ there exists $q\in (0,1)$ and $N_0, N_1 \in \mathbb{N}$  such that site-bond percolation on the hierarchical lattice $\mathbb{H}_L^{d}$ with the kernel $J$ defined by 
	\begin{align*}
	J(e) = \begin{cases}
		 \frac{a L^d \log\log(|e|)}{|e|^{2d}} & \text{ for } |e| \geq N_1\\
		 N_0 & \text{ for } |e| < N_1
		 \end{cases}
	\end{align*}
	satisfies $\mathbb{P}_{q,J} \left( |K_0| = \infty \right)> 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.639832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7581dd3d5735fb0c4834503d0be8ccff0d0268371517dd2112e53da3c4c92438","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 (Non-explosion) of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Assume \ref{ass:growth:p2}. Let $X$ be any $\Cc$-valued weak solution, defined up to its explosion lifetime, satisfying either the singular equation \eqref{eq:thm:existence-sde} or the degenerate interior equation \eqref{eq:degenerate-existence-indicator}. Then
