Here $C$ is a universal constant and $K:=(Cr)^{q_0}\|X_{\rm F}\|$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.199141+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75970bac4a012f45dcdb1fb9ac9ba657a72967a7a2e4a3dd8c42b4d8ecadea8b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Maintheorem 2 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] For the equation given by \eqref{eq NS},\eqref{eq xi} with $\xi=\eta$ given by \eqref{eq eta}, and any $B_0>0$, there exists an integer $N=N(B_0)\in\N^+$ such that the following holds. If $\{b_j\}_{j\in\N^+}$ satisfies
	\begin{equation*}
	\sum_{j\in\N^+}b_j^2\leq B_0\quad\text{and}\quad b_j\neq0\quad\text{for }1\leq j\leq N,
	\end{equation*}
    then the Markov process associated to the coupled system \eqref{eq NS},\eqref{eq eta} admits a unique invariant measure $\mu_*$ on $\mathcal X$.  Moreover, there exist constants $C,\alpha,\gamma>0$ such that
	\begin{equation}
	\left|\E\varphi(U(t,U_0))-\int_{\mathcal X}\varphi d\mu_*\right|\leq Ce^{-\alpha t}\exp\left(C\gamma\|U_0\|_{\mathcal X}^2\right)\|\varphi\|_{\mathcal X,\gamma}
	\end{equation}
    for any $\varphi\in\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal X,\gamma}$, $U_0\in \mathcal X$ and $t\geq0$, where
	\begin{equation*}
	\mathcal{O}_{\mathcal X,\gamma}=\left\{\varphi\in C^1(\mathcal X):\|\varphi\|_{\mathcal X,\gamma}<\infty\right\},\quad\|\varphi\|_{\mathcal X,\gamma}=\sup_{U_0\in \mathcal X}\left(e^{-\gamma\|U_0\|_{\mathcal X}^2}(|\varphi(U_0)|+\|\nabla\varphi(U_0)\|_{\mathcal X})\right).
	\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:53:51.341576+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_759b0000771fe40b2490059d97708c748bfbba513de326d443298dddf485aff8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2605.04860, 'Branching Brownian motion with rank-based selection and reaction-diffusion equations'] Consider the PDE $U_t = \frac12 U_{xx} + G(U)$ with initial condition $U(x,0)=U_0(x)$ such that $U_0(x)\to 1$ as $x\to-\infty$ and $U_0(x)\to 0$ as $x\to\infty$. We say that the solution $U(x,t)$ \textit{spreads up to (the value) $u^\star$ at speed $c^\star$} if:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\lim_{t\to\infty}\inf_{x\leq ct} U(x,t)\geq u^\star$ for all $c<c^\star$,
        \item $\lim_{t\to\infty}\sup_{x\geq ct} U(x,t)=0$ for all $c>c^\star$.
    \end{enumerate}
    More generally, we may say that the solution \textit{spreads up to (the value) $u^\star$ with speed at least $c^\star$} if just condition 1. holds.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.182901+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75a16740e3a814b2c71cd7391116b946469d2dd1bc9d56e35457b4e82fed39eb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2606.30080, 'Ergodicity of reflected stochastic reaction-diffusion equations driven by space-time white'] Let $u^i(t,\cdot)$ denote the solution to equation \eqref{1.1} with initial value $u_0^i$, $i=1,2$. 
\begin{itemize}
  \item [(i)] Suppose that (H2) holds. 

Then for any $ t\geq 0$,
\begin{align}
    \mathbb{E} \Vert u^2(t) - u^1(t)\Vert_{L^1} \leq 2 e^{-\alpha t} \mathbb{E}\Vert u_0^2 - u_0^1 \Vert_{L^1} .
\end{align}
  \item [(ii)] Suppose that (H1) and (H2) hold. Assume that
   \begin{align}
     \sup_{t\in [0,T]}\mathbb{E}\int_{0}^{1}|u^2(t,x) - u^1(t,x)|^2  dx <\infty, \qquad \forall \ T\geq 0.
   \end{align}

  If $\alpha\geq 0$ when $L_{\sigma} = 0$ or $\alpha>\frac{L_{\sigma}^4}{8}$ when $L_{\sigma} > 0$, 
then for any $\kappa$ satisfying 
\begin{align}
  \begin{cases}
     0\leq \kappa \leq \alpha, & \text{ when } L_{\sigma} = 0,\\
    0\leq \kappa<\alpha - \frac{L_{\sigma}^4}{8}, & \text{ when } L_{\sigma} > 0,
  \end{cases}
\end{align}
there exists a constant $C_{\alpha,\kappa}>0$ such that for any $t\geq 0$,
\begin{align}
\left(\mathbb{E} \int_{0}^{1} |u^2(t,x) - u^1(t,x)|^2  dx\right)^{\frac{1}{2}} \leq 2 C_{\alpha,\kappa} e^{-\kappa t}\left(\mathbb{E}\Vert  u^2_0 - u^1_0 \Vert_{L^2}^2\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}.
\end{align}
    \item [(iii)] Suppose that (H1) and (H2) hold. Assume that for some $p>2$, 
    \begin{align}
      \sup_{t\in [0,T]}\sup_{x\in [0,1]}\mathbb{E}\left[|u^2(t,x) - u^1(t,x)|^p\right] <\infty \quad\text{for any }\ T\geq 0.
    \end{align}
  If 
  \begin{align*}
    \alpha > \left\{\frac{\sqrt{4p}}{\pi}\left(\frac{1}{2\sqrt{\pi}}\right)^{\frac{1}{p}+\frac{1}{2}} \left(\Gamma\Big(\frac{p-2}{6p}\Big)\right)^{\frac{3}{2}} \times L_{\sigma}\right\}^{\frac{4p}{p-2}},
  \end{align*}
  then for any $\kappa$ satisfying 
  \begin{align}
    0<\kappa< \alpha - \left\{\frac{\sqrt{4p}}{\pi}\left(\frac{1}{2\sqrt{\pi}}\right)^{\frac{1}{p}+\frac{1}{2}} \left(\Gamma\Big(\frac{p-2}{6p}\Big)\right)^{\frac{3}{2}} \times L_{\sigma}\right\}^{\frac{4p}{p-2}},
  \end{align}
there exists a constant $C_{p,\alpha,\kappa}>0$ such that for any $t\geq 0$,
\begin{align}
\left(\mathbb{E} \Big[\sup_{x\in [0,1]} |u^2(t,x) - u^1(t,x)|^p \Big]  \right)^{\frac{1}{p}} \leq 2 C_{p,\alpha,\kappa} e^{-\kappa t}\left(\mathbb{E}\Big[ \sup_{x\in [0,1]} | u^2_0 - u^1_0 |^p \Big]\right)^{\frac{1}{p}}.
\end{align}
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.607377+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75a39d626c17335cb28f8b8c02415d7da9f4ead5c31b70ef420921de7757d019","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Eq:weakconvergence of arXiv:2606.03079, 'Mean Field Limits for Stochastic, Underdamped Reactive Langevin Dynamics Models'] (Weak Convergence). For any $\Phi \in \mathcal{S}$ and $0 \leq r_{1} \leq r_{2} \cdots \leq r_{W}=s<t<T$ and $\{\psi_{w}\}_{w=1}^{W} \subset$ $B\left(\otimes_{j=1}^{J} M_{F}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times \mathbb{R}^{d})\right)$, we have that
