{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.073741+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75b55379f3af17b7a19309f860de71c70a5fb5b12fe40b2e98fd707c71ed4bec","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition RSB induced by an external field of arXiv:2411.14105, 'Simultaneous replica-symmetry breaking \\ for vector spin glasses'] Let $p,q\in\mathcal Q_\infty$ satisfy $p=\partial_q \psi(q+t\nabla\xi(p))$ for some $t\geqslant 0$ and $\xi$. Assume that $\supp P_1$ spans $\mathbb{R}^{D}$. 
