{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.578340+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76cad7318bbfd9ad5006c647380c2f3b772592f78610e2c9b69da8add3bffa4d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 47 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$, $\beta>0$, $h\geq 0$, and $n\geq 1$. Let $J\in (\mathbb R^+)^{E(\mathbb Z^d)}$ which satisfies $J_e=\beta$, for every $e\in E(\Lambda_n)$. Let $\Lambda$ be a finite subset of $\mathbb Z^d$ containing $\Lambda_{2n}$. Then, for every $S\subset \Lambda_n$, 
