{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:02:34.834272+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76da95014179d098a7c7f6225268280fdf1c2bfebd7a00b9245e621a7f4fbe11","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 (Independent-row comparison) of arXiv:2607.20329, '2607.20329'] Let $A\in\mathbb K^{n\times n}$ have independent rows
		$R_1,\ldots,R_n$.  Suppose that, for some $\sigma_1,\ldots,\sigma_n>0$,
		\begin{equation}
			\E R_i^*R_i=\sigma_i^2I_n,
			\qquad
			\gamma_{1,\beta}
			\le_{\mathrm{Lt}}
			\frac{|R_ic|^2}{\sigma_i^2\|c\|_2^2}
			\quad(c\in\mathbb K^n\setminus\{0\}).
		\end{equation}
		Then
		\begin{equation}
			\Delta_n^{\mathbb K}
			\le_{\mathrm{Lt}}X_n^{\mathbb K}
			\le_{\mathrm{Lt}}
			\frac{|\per_{\mathbb K}A|^2}
			{n!\prod_{i=1}^n\sigma_i^2}.
		\end{equation}
		Consequently, for every $\varepsilon>0$,
		\begin{equation}
			\Pp\left(
			|\per_{\mathbb K}A|
			\le\varepsilon\sqrt{n!}\prod_{i=1}^n\sigma_i
			\right)
			\le
			\min\left\{1,
			\left(\frac{2\pi e}{\beta}\right)^{\beta/2}
			\kappa_{n,\beta}\varepsilon^\beta
			\right\}.
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.512048+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76dc71438de15d6451af442282d308b54835d838a6b90e8ea0fc6bb0efd3b569","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 (Opposite-jump monotonicity) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] Let $X$ and $Z$ be independent variables in the standing class.

\begin{enumerate}
\item If the L\'evy measure of $Z$ has no positive jumps, then
\begin{equation}
 \cplus(X+Z)\leq\cplus(X).

\end{equation}
\item If the L\'evy measure of $Z$ has no negative jumps, then
\begin{equation}
 \cminus(X+Z)\leq\cminus(X).

\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}
Suppose in addition that $0<\tplus(X)<\infty$ and
$\cplus(X)=1/\tplus(X)$. Under the assumption in part 1,
\begin{equation}
 \cplus(X+Z)=\cplus(X).

\end{equation}
The reflected boundary statement holds on the left.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.258310+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76e01b05c6724e3752388347a397324312f06e098a0e9994bd9b0627717789c6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:blocks_somewhere of arXiv:2607.08914, 'Linear spreading speed in non-monotone population models'] There exist $\Cl{c:bsbig},  \Cl{c:bstilde} \in (0,\infty)$
