{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.244020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76e3d3f639ca63161e5882c47d7b59a7efe1adfa1e1910d7055581c8f7f86ecf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm restate of limiting profile of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] Let $c\in\mathbb{R}$ be an absolute constant. Let $(n_N)_{N\ge 1},(m_N)_{N\ge 1}$ and $(l_N)_{N\ge 1}$ be sequences of positive integers, such that 
\begin{enumerate}
\item $m_N,l_N\ge 2$ for all $N\ge 1$, and $\lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}l_N=\infty$.
\item $n_N=m_Nl_N$ for all $N\ge 1$.
\end{enumerate}
For all $N\ge 1$, let $t_N=\frac{n_N}{2}(\log n_N-\frac 12\log l_N+c)$. Let $\sim_{l_N}\backslash P_{n_N}^{*t_N}$ be defined as in (defi: Pnk and its convolution of the paper), and let $\sim_{l_N}\backslash U_{\mathfrak{S}_{n_N}}$ be defined as in (defi: quotient of space of the paper). Then, we have
$$\lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}d_{TV}(\sim_{l_N}\backslash P_{n_N}^{*t_N},\sim_{l_N}\backslash U_{\mathfrak{S}_{n_N}})=2\Phi\left(\frac{\exp(-c)}{2}\right)-1$$
when $\lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}m_N=\infty$, and 
$$\lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}d_{TV}(\sim_{l_N}\backslash P_{n_N}^{*t_N},\sim_{l_N}\backslash U_{\mathfrak{S}_{n_N}})=2\Phi\left(\sqrt{1-\frac 1m}\frac{\exp(-c)}{2}\right)-1$$
when $m_N=m\ge 2$ is fixed. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.583681+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76e751211b0c2fc25045178daee4e4bf6174fab389a4c7ec693897eccf4b5b3c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 32 (Concentration of the Stein witness map) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target}, \ref{ass:ksd-kernel} and \ref{ass:concentration}, there are constants $c_{\mathrm{KSD}}>0$ and $1\le C_{\mathrm{KSD}}<\infty$ such that
