{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.506129+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77749c1ada64dfd5f4d642cd0f306d82f40c5de94c0292318188c61fb879e136","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 106 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] \cite[Thm. 2.5]{Tappe}
Let $f_0 \in \Lip([0,T] \times W,D(A))$ and $$f \in C_b^{2\beta,3}([0,T] \times H, L(U,D(A^2)))$$ be mappings such that
\begin{align*}
&f_0|_{[0,T] \times D(A)} \in \Lip([0,T] \times D(A),D(A^2)),
\\ &f|_{[0,T] \times D(A)} \in C_b^{2\beta,3}([0,T] \times D(A), L(U,D(A^3))).
