{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.875268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_778baabbf47cae38a54d75bc9540648e43b745a2511568ec1ce9ec29a74aeacb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn hext of arXiv:2608.27939, 'Entropy and domination for quasi-Hitchin representations'] Let $\mathcal{P}(g_1,g_2)$ be the (possibly infinite) collection of plaques separating $g_1$ from $g_2$, with the linear order induced by the transverse orientation. A map $$M:\mathcal{P}(g_1,g_2) \to \mathrm{SL}_n(\mathbb{C})$$
is said to be \textit{H\"{o}lder-extendable} if there exist constants $A,\nu>0$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
    \lVert M(T) - \text{I}\rVert \leq A d_\infty(x_{T,1}, x_{T,3})^\nu
\end{equation*}
where $(x_{,1}, x_{T,2},x_{T,3})$ are the ordered set of vertices of $T$ between $g_1$ and $g_2$ and $d_\infty$ is a metric on the ideal boundary of $\tilde{S}$ that is the standard metric on the circle.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.645405+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7792e57d70d70ded96a438886e4381245f9fb6945b28b9913d31158e119b2697","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 7 (Simplex cap) of arXiv:2607.23980, 'Sharp small-deviation inequalities for sums of independent\\nonnegative random variables'] Let $y=(y_1,\ldots,y_n)\in[0,\infty)^n$, and write $s(y)=\sum_i y_i$. If $s(y)>0$ and $0\le t\le s(y)/(n+1)$, then
