{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.829131+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77a9847def96f39526453e80c48642f3b4b0bdf3404081eb0c56f414e30460ed","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2608.13235, 'Mixing Properties of Random Laguerre Tessellations'] Let $a > 0$ and denote $\Hat{\Theta}_{r,K_3,K_1} \coloneqq (E^3_{r,K_3} \cup E^1_{(K_3+1)r,K_1})^c$ for $r \geq \max \{a,1\}$ and $K_1,K_3  > 0$. Then for any $\mathsf{A} \in \tailF{a}^1$ we have
