{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.505312+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77abf9c4adc08d7ca0e29a29ad74e1c32005fda88883aa18a14dc71ff3100227","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 93 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $Y : [0,T] \to D(A)$ be measurable and bounded. We define the path $Z : [0,T] \to W$ as
