{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:29:35.085967+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77e0a85fe574eabc137c6cc62cf0cf5cebf047bb9814763bf6b1fca0c69780b8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2609.03819, 'Stochastic damped wave and Euler-Bernoulli equations with singular locally H\"older contin'] Assume \ref{H0}, \ref{H1} and \ref{H3} hold. Then, there exist positive constants $C_1,C_2$, independent of $t\in(0,\infty)$ and $n\in\N$, such that
\begin{align}

\left\|e^{tA_n}\mathcal V_n\right\|_{\mathscr L(U,H_n)}\leq C_1t^{-\gamma}e^{-C_2\mu_1^{\alpha\wedge (1-\alpha)}t}, \qquad t\in(0,\infty), \qquad n\in\N.
\end{align}
where
\begin{equation}
\gamma:=\begin{cases}
\dfrac{\beta}{\alpha}, & \alpha\in\left(0,\frac12\right],\\[2mm]
\max\left\{\dfrac{\beta}{\alpha};\ \dfrac{\beta+\frac12-\alpha}{1-\alpha}\right\}, 
& \alpha\in\left[\frac12,1\right),
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
We notice that, for $\alpha\in[\frac12,1)$, $\gamma=(\beta+\frac12-\alpha)(1-\alpha)^{-1}$ if and only if $\beta\geq\frac14$ and $\alpha\leq 2\beta$.","status":"unverified"}

