{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:15:54.947528+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77e92bee69129fd92bbeecc100c9efcc8d5656a1f9dcda8f1ac80a2f8c6e7e6b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:igl-via-semantics of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] {das_intuitionistic_2024}}] 
  We say an IK-frame $\mathfrak{F} = (W, \leq, \sqsubset)$ is \emph{composite Noetherian}
  if $({\leq} \cdot {\sqsubset})$ is converse well-founded,
  that is, if there are no sequences $(x_n)_{n < \omega}$ and $(y_n)_{n < \omega}$ in $W$
  such that $x_n \leq y_n \sqsubset x_{n+1}$ for every $n < \omega$.
  Since $\leq$ is reflexive, $\sqsubset$ is also converse well-founded on every composite Noetherian frame.
  An IK-frame is said to be an \emph{IGL-frame} if it is composite Noetherian and $\sqsubset$-transitive.
  We let $\mathcal{B}\textbf{IGL}$ be the set of all formulas in $\mathscr{L}_{\Box\Diamond}$ that are h-valid on every IGL-frame.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.296448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77ec5c309aa8e2906b46dc33175d30b710be3edde7428ebe7955f8bd9c61925d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:recentered_conv of arXiv:2605.22787, 'Invariant measures for half-space geometric LPP: classification and the one force--one sol'] As $n \to \infty$, the law of the process
