{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.354031+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77eca2efdbc2a42940b69e2a39e04a1353615c7c494dfc00148ae4ef7b762f0c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:local_smoothing_homogenized of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Suppose that Assumption (ass:forcing_regularity_iteration of the paper) holds. Fix $\mu>0$, $r\in (1,\infty)$ and $p_0\in (2,p)$. Let $(v^{N,\delta},\pi^{N,\delta},(\widetilde{\pi}^{N,\delta}_{k,\alpha})_{k,\alpha})$ be a local solution to the stochastic Stokes system (equation eq:turbulent_Stokes_scaling_quantitative_iteration of the paper) on $Q$ for some $N\geq 1$ and $\delta\in (0,1]$. Let  $(\overline{v}^{N,\delta},\overline{\pi}^{N,\delta})$ be the solution to the homogenized Stokes system (equation eq:homogenized_PDE_linear of the paper) on $(1/2)Q$ provided by Proposition (prop:local_well_posedness_homogenized_SPDE of the paper).
