{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.722938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77fe10f8513b8c7eace8974fa030382d310d225d6a4098d155fe9b6b02e917a3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 34 of arXiv:2609.00285, 'Multicrossing complex of knot and secant classes'] The \emph{secant $(m,l)$-invariants} of the knot $K$ are defined by the formula
