{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.576487+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_787fe65a453c73ffc4fd4fe35132cb3b6aed8b61ca0fb62af3feebb33b5471ac","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem-Burkholder of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] For any $r \in (0, 2 + \delta]$, there exists a constant $c>0$ such that for any $n \geqslant 1$, 
