{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.869139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78830ed3190f5c66ee5099067f516b291d81a79e52a8d3b525af08490f5b5847","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop regularforitselfreflecting of arXiv:2605.06488, 'Continuous-state branching processes with L\'evy-Khintchine drift-interaction: Laplace dua'] Let $Y^{\mathrm{e}0}$ be the extension of the minimal $\mathrm{CBDI}(\hat\Psi,\Psi)$  at $0$ with the latter regular (Theorem~(thm2zero of the paper)). The boundary $0$ is non-sticky for $Y^{\mathrm{e}0}$ if and only if $\infty$ is regular for itself for $X^{\mathrm{e}\infty}$: 
