\end{center}
Similarly, by exchanging the roles of the processes and the boundaries, $\infty$ is non-sticky for $X^{\mathrm{e}\infty}$ if and only if $0$ is regular-for-itself for $Y^{\mathrm{e}0}$.","status":"unverified"}

