{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.948686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_788b6b8a31505ab1a99878a34ba4d1ae18487cafdeb3bc0b7af0008cd0e2e82d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 2 (Very high probability event) of arXiv:2606.24887, '2606.24887'] Let $\Omega$ and $\Xi$ be events that depends on $N \in \NN$ and $\nu >0$. We say that $\Omega$ holds \emph{with very high probability} if for each $\nu>0$, there is $\mathcal C \equiv \mathcal C_\nu$ such that 
