{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.206204+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_788d4a03980b1bcc72bfbe6aab05286d1e2fe5eb581910b374a8d36e6ee4cf07","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2604.27205, 'An Analysis of the Diaconis-Holmes-Neal Markov Chain Sampler Under Generalized Unimodal Un'] Assume the requirements of Lemma~\ref{step1} hold true, let $f_1$ be the number of flips and stationary moves in any path of length $x = cn$ before shortening, and let $f_2$ be the number of flips and stationary moves included in the path while shortening. Then the path has occurrence probability bounded below by
