{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.992109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78ea83386bafce1afaac582905b4f7b65912aac61423bb849584e8cf8ca1c213","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro1 of arXiv:2412.01070, 'A note on Lévy-driven McKean-Vlasov SDEs under monotonicity'] Under Assumptions of Theorem $(thm of the paper)$ with $g\equiv{\bf0}$, (equation E1 of the paper) has a unique strong solution $(Y_t)_{t\ge0}$ satisfying that,
