                \frac{n_1}{n_1+n_2}\left(1-\frac{1}{p}-\frac{p-1}{p(p-2)!}\right)^t                                                                 & \text{if }|H\sigma H|=p^2.\end{cases}
        \]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.722509+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_790498f4f1ca84b4653b3cfed2b30efd4eb791351c0c0e028c6e2ea4e9809a02","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm5.1' of arXiv:2606.01944, 'Propagation of Chaos for Mean-field Mean Reflected Backward Stochastic Differential Equati'] The reflected BSDE (equation eq7' of the paper) has a unique solution $(\{Y^i,Z^i\}_{1\leq i\leq N},K^{(N)})$ with $K^{(N)}\in \mathcal{A}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)})$, $Y^i\in \mathcal{S}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)})$ and $Z^i\in \mathcal{H}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)};\mathbb{R}^N)$ for $i=1,\cdots,N$. Moreover, there exists a constant $C$ independent of $N$, such that
\begin{align*}
    \mathsf{E}\left[|K^{(N)}_T|^2\right]\leq C.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.318759+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_79049cbc0678c01b4b44db03fd0bc7f62aa3790a4ded8f9b1ee37748d49c17af","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.30973, 'Pseudo-Anosov flow and dynamics on guts'] A oriented embedded surface \(S\subset M\) is \emph{relatively carried by} \(\tau\) if
\begin{enumerate}
\item \(S \setminus \mathrm{int}(T_{\tau})\) is carried by the branched surface \(\tau^{(2)}\) in \(M\setminus \mathrm{int}(T_{\tau})\), and
\item each component of \(S\cap T_{\tau}\) is either a meridional disk or an annulus.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.446631+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7907a6fa2a802d4ea3e04b234a943b4464e768781034cac696a4e7f1ae3ec779","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2606.15843, 'Long-time behaviour of DLRA for SDEs'] Suppose Assumptions~(H1)--(H5) hold, and let $(U_t,Y_t)_{t\ge0}$ be the solution of Eqn.~\eqref{eq:DO} with initial condition $U_0 \in V_r(\bb R^d)$ and $Y_0 \in L^2(\Omega,\bb R^r)$. Assume further that there exists $\sigma_{Y_0} > 0$ such that $\bb E[Y_0 Y_0^\top] \succeq \sigma_{Y_0} I_r$.
For any $Q\in O(r)$, define $\al R_Q(u,y) := (Qu, Qy)$. Then, for any $t>0$ we have
\begin{equation}
    \scr L_{(U_t^{\al R_Q(U_0,Y_0)},Y_t^{\al R_Q(U_0,Y_0)})}=\scr L_{(QU_t^{(U_0,Y_0)},QY_t^{(U_0,Y_0)})},
