{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.963409+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_79083f8a6370549e7a199b73a603bdd9d5be5f8a72eabf9a567feebcc00594e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2604.00742, 'Delayed Logistic equation as a limit\\ of long memory Markov chains'] For each $p \geq 1$ and $N \in \N$, there exists a constant $K_{N} \in (1, 1+1/N)$ such that 
	\begin{equation*}
		\E\left[\bigg(\sup_{t \in [0,T]} Z^{N}(t)\bigg)^p\right] \;\leq\; (2\mu)^p \exp\left\{pK_{N}^{p-1}T\right\}.
	\end{equation*}
	In particular,

