{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.667311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7936794ef7df85ffec17b240d0d027979aaeb1c20282a86d408f092948f602db","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary corollary_contraction_on_observables_with_limits of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] Let $d \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $f:\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{R}^d$ be such that the limits
