{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:39:18.535233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_793ffbb24c0575cdbcc23bfa09ae00527cbb124121494a227707e2d0a72f2fcf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2609.02294, 'Existence and Blow-Up for Non-linear Fokker-Planck with Controlled Drift Divergence'] Every solution $u$ of Proposition $\ref{prop:local}$ can be approximated with a sequence of function $u_\varepsilon$ such that 
