{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.638410+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_795aafefafee811e5ffd2d4414c2b5f902b797d2df93b11a93def7a5625f8da3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 7 ({{\bf {\boldmath$\mathscr{E}_{\alpha}$}-subharmonicity}}) of arXiv:2506.17979, '\large\bf A remark on subharmonicity for symmetric Dirichlet forms'] {\rm Fix $\alpha>0$ and an open set $D$. A function $u:E\to\R$ is called \emph{$\mathscr{E}_{\alpha}$-subharmonic} (resp.~\emph{$\mathscr{E}_{\alpha}$-superharmonic}) \emph{in $D$} if $u\in 
