{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.615208+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7973624e17a93af83129a1058bca44347c1d6f7e61b53f4ee4d6cbf4064cdf71","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There exists a $\delta_0>0$ such that for any fixed $\delta<\delta_0$, the event $\latapx_n$ defined by
