\end{equation}
has a unique solution $u\in C([0,T]; \, H^{k+2}(\Omega)\cap H_0^1(\Omega))$. Moreover, the norm of the solution operator $F\mapsto u$ is uniformly bounded in $\eps\in [0,\eps_0]$, for $\eps_0\ll1$ possibly depending on $m$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.630623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a3240fecfeac34c55ad2c55626a9a0a9cd213deb95ccb578ee533e82796b4db","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:iso of arXiv:2411.07809, 'Pirogov--Sinai Theory Beyond Lattices'] Suppose $G$ is infinite, one-ended, quasi-transitive, and has
