{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.024672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a3c96a61b56e9d0eaf0c8f8e8da65e7496f1ca7f981a87fd02a854a3a476c0c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 (\citeauthor{F10}, \citeyear{F10}, Lemma 5.9) of arXiv:2606.06739, 'The relationship between the transition functions of the labeled and unlabeled versions of'] For $\bm m=(m_1,\ldots,m_k)$ with $m_1\ge\cdots\ge m_k\ge1$, $\bm n=(n_1,\ldots,n_l)$ with $n_1\ge\cdots\ge n_l\ge1$, $k,l\in{\bf N}$, $m=|\bm m|$, and $n=|\bm n|$,
