{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.446241+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a6f26e4ddd7fc399710f57be1491c31c6bd2c4a644eee9c02eca288b1bf035b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def weak of arXiv:2601.10568, 'Hydrodynamic Limit with a Weierstrass-type result'] For $ \rho^{\rm ini}:\mathbb{T}^d\to[0,1] $ a measurable function, we say that $ \rho:[0,T]\times \mathbb{T}\mapsto [0,1] $ is a weak solution of the equation
        \begin{align}
		\begin{cases}
		    \partial_t\rho
            =\partial_u^2\Phi(\rho), & \text{in } (0,T]\times\mathbb{T}^d,\\
            \rho_0=\rho^{\text{ini}},& \text{in }\mathbb{T}^d
		\end{cases} 
	\end{align}
    if
	\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\Phi(\rho)\in L^2([0,T];\mathcal{H}^1(\mathbb{T}^d))$;
	\item for any $ t\in[0,T] $ and $ G\in C^{1,2}([0,T]\times \mathbb{T}) $, $\rho$ satisfies the formulation $\mathfrak{F}_t(\rho^{\rm ini},\rho,G)=0$, where   
		\begin{equation}
			\mathfrak{F}_t(\rho^{\rm ini},\rho,G)
			:=
			\langle \rho_t,G_t\rangle-\inner{\rho^{\rm ini},G_0}
			-\int_0^t
			\bigg\{
			\langle \rho_s,\partial_sG_s\rangle
			+
                \langle \Phi(\rho_s),\partial_u^2 G_s\rangle
			\bigg\}
			\mathrm{d} s
			.
		\end{equation}
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.662555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a71916885f5d54d4c15126517b749e687ff48ac60e47b5f3c1dc7b7e9346488","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2605.09372, 'Sharp weighted norm estimates for martingale square functions'] Let $1<p<\infty$. Given a matrix weight $W\in A_p$, we have
