For $j=0,2$, the Fourier transforms $\widetilde{u}_0(\alpha,y\mathord{;}z)$ and $\widetilde{u}_2(\alpha,y\mathord{;}z)$ follow immediately by the identities in equation (\ref{algebrain}).","status":"unverified"}

