{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.162348+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7af5976a8788068f777c8c9089d254041bb15a45ba08af558cfca61d3f28fc09","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:final of arXiv:2603.00773, 'Long-time $L^p$ Wasserstein contraction for diffusion processes without global dissipativi'] For $\overline{\rho},\overline{\rho}',\overline{S},\overline{M},\overline{\theta},\overline{q}>0$, $\overline{S_2}>\overline{S}$ and $p\geqslant 1$, there exist $\overline{\delta},\overline{C},\overline{\lambda}>0$ (depending only and explicitly on $\overline{\rho},\overline{\rho}',\overline{S},\overline{S_2},\overline{M},\overline{\theta},\overline{q},p$) such that the following holds. Let  $d\in\mathbb N^*$, $b\in\mathcal C^1(\mathbb R^d,\mathbb R^d)$ and $\sigma\in\mathbb R^{d\times d}$ satisfying Assumptions~(assum:decomposeYZ of the paper) and (assum:Contract_at_infty of the paper) with
\begin{equation}

\min(\rho_1,\rho_2) \geqslant \overline{\rho}\,,\quad \max(L_1,L_2,L_3,|Q|,|Q^{-1}|,|\sigma|) \leqslant \overline{M}\,,\quad S^* \leqslant \overline{S},\quad \theta \geqslant \overline{\theta},
