{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:48:43.535409+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b00097771483c180510d054c70672c67a4107e4f754427b17a26c40c96c540d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2608.06646, 'Three-dimensional stochastic wave equation with non-Lipschitz coefficients'] Given a positive integer $N$, let $A,B_i\ge 0$ and $k_i>-1$ for $i=1,2,\dots,N$. Assume that the real valued function $f: [0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ is non-negative which satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        f(t)\le A+\int_0^t\lr{\sum_{i=1}^N B_i(t-s)^{k_i}}f(s)\ud s\,,\quad\text{for all $t>0$.}
    \end{equation}
    Then, it holds that
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{t\in[0,T]}f(t)\le 2A e^{\beta t}\,,
    \end{align*}
    for all $T\ge 0$ and $\beta\ge \max\bigl\{\lr{2NB_i\Gamma(k_i+1)}^{\frac{1}{k_i+1}}\vee 1:i=1,\dots,N\bigr\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.454027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b01611010784598756c398b521b62005acfe89a8d12336a4cd3c3a6cf5e44bb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 43 of arXiv:2604.03213, 'Asymptotic expansion for transport maps \\ between laws of multimatrix models'] Let $V_0, V_1 \in \cC^4(X_1,\dots,X_d)$ be self-adjoint, i.e., such that for all $(\cA,\tau) \in\W$, $x_1,\dots,x_d\in\cA$ self-adjoint, $V_0(x)$ and $V_1(x)$ are self-adjoint. Let $(\bX_t^{s,H})_{t\geq 0}$ be the solution of
    \begin{equation}

        \bX_{t,p}^s(H) = H - \frac{1}{2} \int_0^t \bD_p V_s\left( \bX_u^s(H) \right) du + S^N_p(t),\quad 1\leq p\leq d,
    \end{equation}
    where $V_s\coloneqq s V_0 + (1-s) V_1$, $\bD_p \coloneqq \cD_p + \id\otimes\tr \circ \widetilde{\partial}_p$, and $S^N_p(t) \coloneqq S_{t,p}(X^N)$ where $X^N$ is a family of independent GUE random matrices and $S_{t,p}$ is as in Equation \eqref{skgjnslvms}. We set 
    \begin{equation}

        \Psi_s:H\in\M_N(\C)_{sa}^d \mapsto \left( -\frac{1}{2} \int_0^{\infty}\E\left[ \bD_p\left( \dot{V}_s\circ \bX_t^s\right)(H)  \right]  dt \right)_{1\leq p\leq d},
    \end{equation}
    where $\dot{V}_s = V_1-V_0$.
    Then, if $(T_s^N)_{0\leq s\leq 1}$ is solution to the linear differential equation
    $$ \dot{T}_s^N = \Psi_s \circ T_s^N,\quad T_0^N=\id_{\M_N(\C)_{sa}^d},$$
    then it is a transport map between $V_0$ and $V_1$. Concretely, for all measurable function $f$,
    $$ \int_{\M_N(\C)_{sa}^d} f(H) \frac{e^{-N\Tr_N(V_s(H))}}{Z_{V_s}}\ dH = \int_{\M_N(\C)_{sa}^d} f\circ T_s^N(H) \frac{e^{-N\Tr_N(V_0(H))}}{Z_{V_0}}\ dH. $$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.602406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b018d0dc90727d59ed809700ef5041ef66b6257f7f54ac8d2e79735ed617c6f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 37 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] The augmented semigroup is strongly lumpable with respect to $(x,u)\mapsto x$ if and only if each coordinate kernel $R_{e_i}$ is strongly lumpable with respect to the same projection. In that case the coordinate kernels of $Y$ induce commuting kernels $P_{e_i}^Z$ on $\X$, and

