{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.251221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b33c5d982063eb615c9c8f501b16c1390298cac63d4389d0879b340e26f2b86","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] Let $\sigma\in(\frac{1}{2},1)$. For any $v_0\in L_\sigma^2(\IR^2)\cap H^\sigma(\IR^2)$ and $(p,q)$ a Strichartz pair such that
