{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.665727+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b3a6bd134c344c8a75ac8d5fec405f665e5446b7cbea55dbcb013b6af3ad11f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2604.23656, 'Doubly Reflected Backward SDEs Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Quadratic Generator'] Let $\xi,f$ satisfies (H1) and (H3). Assume that $L,U\in S^{2p}_G(0,T)$ satisfies $L_t\leq N_1\leq U_t$, q.s. for any $t\in[0,T]$, where $p>1$ and $N_1\in\mathbb{R}$. Suppose that $(Y,Z,A)\in \mathcal{S}^{2p}_G(0,T)$ is a solution to the doubly reflected $G$-BSDE with parameters $(\xi,g,L,U)$ such that $(Y,A)$ satisfies $(\textmd{ASC}_{2p})$. Moreover, assume that 
