\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.243829+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b7ca9de58b85afc93c80b2310f8c832040d5868e4ccad98e6a5e619db9c35d8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem1 of arXiv:2607.01463, 'Two Multi--Draw Coupon Collector models with different retention rules'] Consider the  $d$ coupon collector's problem (d--CCP), where in each run we keep \textbf{all} the new observed coupons. Let $T_{N,d}$ be the number of trials until all $N$ different types of coupons, which are uniformly distributed, are collected (at least once). Then,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb {E}\left[T_{N,d}\right]=\binom{N}{d} \sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(-1\right)^{k+1}\binom{N}{k}\Bigg(\binom{N}{d}-\binom{N-k}{d}\Bigg)^{-1}.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.998499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b81ec405d2c3ad5b03e3bf095baab13428540bb8d0baa6614abcff0441106ea","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-expinteraction of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] Suppose that the interaction potential $v$ satisfies Assumption (V). Recall that $W=W_R=[-R,R]^d$ and $W'=W_{R+M}\setminus W_R$. For any $M\in(0,\infty)$, there is a constant $C\in(0,\infty)$ (only depending on $d$, $\beta$, $v$ and $M$) such that, for any $R\in(0,\infty)$, and for any $ y, y_1,y_2\in W',x, x_1,x_2\in (W')^{\rm c}$,
\begin{eqnarray}
\mathbb{E}_{y,x}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({W'}})}}}\Big[\sum_{j_1,j_2=1}^{\ell(B)}\1_{\{j_1\not= j_2\}}V(B_{j_1},B_{j_2})\Big]
&\leq& C |y-x|,\\
\mathbb{E}_{y_1,x_1}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({W'}})}}}\otimes \mathbb{E}_{y_2,x_2}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({W'}})}}}\Big[\sum_{j_1=1}^{\ell(B^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({1}})}}})}\sum_{j_2=1}^{\ell(B^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({2}})}}})}V(B^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({1}})}}}_{j_1},B^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({2}})}}}_{j_2})\Big]
&\leq& C \Big(\big|[\underline y_1,\underline x_1]\cap [\underline x_2,\underline y_2]\big|+1\Big),\\
\mathbb{E}_{y,x}^{{{\scriptscriptstyle{({W'}})}}}\Big[\sum_{j_1=1}^{\ell(B)} V(B_{j_1},f)\Big]
&\leq& C g({\operatorname {dist}}(K_f,[y,x])),\qquad  f\in {\mathcal C }(W),
\end{eqnarray}
where $g$ is a function with $\lim_{r\to\infty}g(r)=0$, and we wrote $K_f$ for the $C_v$-neighbourhood of $ \{f(t)\colon t\in [0,\beta]\}$, where $C_v={\operatorname {supp}}\sup v$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.946552+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b847d064e8ea6521ac1746251fde211bab82fd87f33f2badac52cbcab439c94","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:CLTplus of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] Let $s>0$. A family of probability measures $(\mu_t)_{t>0}$ is said to have the property $C(s)$ if 
    \begin{enumerate}
    \item for each $t>0$, $\mu_t$ is ad-invariant and invariant by inversion,
    \item for all $v,w\in \mathfrak{g}$, $\int_G \langle \log(g),v\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}} \langle \log(g),w\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}}  \mu_t(\mathrm{d} g)=t\left\langle v,w \right\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}}  +o(t) $,
    \item $\int_G \vert \log g\vert^{3}\mu_t(\mathrm{d} g)=O(t^{\frac{3}{2}}) $,
    \item For all $t>0$, $\mu_t$ has the following Fourier decay,
    \begin{equation}
\exists C>0; \forall \lambda\in \widehat{G},\forall t>0, \vert \widehat{\mu_t}(\lambda) \vert \leqslant \dim(V_\rho) C\left(1+\sqrt{tc_2(\rho)} \right)^{-s}
\end{equation}
where $c_2(\lambda)$ is the second Casimir number of the representation $\lambda$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.245569+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7b8a9fced5855d784433fd2d0a70802cec8b7b6e570e9146d604b07dead0569e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 69 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix some $K\in \N$ and $0 < t_1 < t_2 < \dots < t_K$. Then for any $\varepsilon'>0$ and initial data $\hfixp_0 \in \UCp$, we have
