{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.889790+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bc5d3bfe5fb6befeafc0c081adc0606fac087dbd7ebc00e54247860548a437c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm star<->complete of arXiv:2606.29829, ''] For every $n\geq 1$, let $\mathfrak{f}_n:S_n\rightarrow \{0,1\}$ be a Boolean function. Then,
