{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.920785+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bcee491042e4e261daf4d9735b0d81dfa3f15d88db1f074e2973ca628e8a721","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:CQ of arXiv:2601.21762, 'Navier-Stokes with a fractional transport noise as a limit of multi-scale dynamics'] Suppose that for a Gaussian process $Y$, $H\in(0,1)$, $c_H>0$, and all $ 0<h<t-s$, the following holds:
    \begin{equ}
        \mathbb{E} \left[ |Y_{s,t}|^2\right] \leq c_H |t-s|^{2H}, \qquad 
