{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.338440+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c03965f38c451453f7f03e130212fe5d908bf52d0ae82bd0aefc92f2ed4e1a8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem BBM tightness of recentered maximum of arXiv:2606.19207, 'Extrema of cooling branching Brownian motion and related Gaussian fields'] Fix any $\alpha\in(0,1/2]$. There exist constants $C>0$, $c>0$, $T_*>1$, and $\lambda_*>1$ such that for all $T>T_*$ and $\lambda>\lambda_*$,
	\begin{equation}
