{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.590597+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c04f8a21c40f1d886624246e8bc8ea1bf7ff47b2bd4fce5b8fceb2b2db35ece","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Maruyama_stationary_increments_1 of arXiv:2602.19773, 'Regularization of a stationary point process by a stationary increments perturbation'] Let $B$ be a real-valued Gaussian process with stationary increments.
		\begin{itemize}
			\item $B$ is ergodic (and weakly-mixing) if and only if $\mu$ is non-atomic,
			\item $B$ is mixing if and only if
			\begin{equation*}
				V_{a,b}(t) \underset{\|t\|\to +\infty}{\longrightarrow}  0, \quad a,b \in \mathbb{R}^{d},
			\end{equation*}
			where 
			\begin{align*}
				V_{a,b}(t)&=\cov{B_{-a}}{ B_{t+b}-B_{t}}\\
				&=v(t+a)+v(t+b)-v(t+a+b)-v(t).
			\end{align*}
		\end{itemize}
		In particular, if $\mu$ is absolutely continuous, then $B$ is mixing. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.853920+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c0885e78d41f59a78de38fb556917c6ed4a4b6eabd61e34378969ce143c3d11","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 (Averaged diagonal self-averaging) of arXiv:2608.20998, 'Free-Probability Kernels for Zero-Rollout Hyperparameter Selection in Reservoir Computing'] Let $A_n=(1-\alpha)I_n+\alpha W_r^{(n)}$. For every fixed
