{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.399047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c0efca8aff8d8c07b68eb700823309a94b0ebbed20f16b9a4bc9edba6f45bf9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2609.04143, 'The Geometry of Real Anisotropic Bohnenblust--Hille Constants'] Let $\mathbf q$ be a Bohnenblust--Hille exponent with $\sigma(\mathbf q)>0$. Then
\[
 2^{\frac{\sigma(\mathbf q)}{2}\left(1+(m-2)Y_1(\mathbf q)\right)}
 \le C_{\mathbf q}^{(m)}
 \le
 2^{\frac{\sigma(\mathbf q)}{2}\left(1+(m-2)\max\{Y_1(\mathbf q),1/2\}\right)}.
\]
In particular, if $Y_1(\mathbf q)<1/2$, then
\[
 2^{\frac{\sigma(\mathbf q)}{2}\left(1+(m-2)Y_1(\mathbf q)\right)}
 \le C_{\mathbf q}^{(m)}
