{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.947619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c79062f0ef526c1f2bcd6df4085c47ba75c4e5c7e654004c19a5eb71227299a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main1 of arXiv:2412.03511, 'Near-optimal shattering in the Ising pure $p$-spin and \\ rarity of solutions returned by '] Consider the pure $p$-spin case $\xi(x) = x^p$.
For all $\varepsilon>0$, there exists an integer $p_0=p_0(\varepsilon)$ such that for all $p \ge p_0$ and all $(1+\varepsilon)\sqrt{(2 \log p) /p} \le \beta \le (1-\varepsilon)\sqrt{2\log 2}$, there exits a random collection of subsets $\mathcal{C}_1,\cdots,\mathcal{C}_m \subset \{-1,+1\}^N$ (measurable with respect to $\bm{G}$) with the following properties: 
\begin{enumerate}
\item Small diameter: $\max_{\bm{\sigma}_1,\bm{\sigma}_2 \in \mathcal{C}_i} d_H(\bm{\sigma}_1,\bm{\sigma}_2) \le rN$ for all $i \le m$.
\item Pairwise separation: $\min_{1\le i \neq j \le m} d_H(\mathcal{C}_i,\mathcal{C}_j) \ge R N$. 
\item Small Gibbs mass: $ \operatorname{\mathbb{E}} \max_{1\le i\le m} \mu_{\beta,\bm{G}}(\mathcal{C}_i) \le e^{-cN}$.  
\item Collective coverage of the Gibbs measure: $\operatorname{\mathbb{E}}\mu_{\beta,\bm{G}}\big(\bigcup_{i=1}^m \mathcal{C}_i\big) \ge 1 - e^{-cN}$.
\end{enumerate}
In the above, $d_H$ is the Hamming distance, $c = c(\varepsilon)>0$ and there exists $\delta = \delta(\varepsilon)>0$ such that one can take $r = 1/p^{1+\delta}$ and $R = \delta/p$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.301771+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c797841794311bb31e78e0d6b9d807923d77cf8a97fbe34ffd0439e249b85b5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:results:convergence of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Let $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption  (as:results:strongCoercivity of the paper) and Assumption (as:results:fixedPoint of the paper), and $\lambda \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$ satisfy $\mathbb{H}_\kappa(\lambda) < \infty$.       Let $(\mu, \gamma)$ be a linear growth solution to the $\kappa$-MLFE{} on $[0, \infty)$ with potentials $(U, W)$ and initial condition $\lambda$.
