{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.899181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c7fb49d31cf71013c227b2a72542593b8c460a1f5c73eef38da4c7578e3bdb7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop space-averaged-sublinearity of arXiv:2411.06861, 'Quenched invariance principle for random walks in random environments admitting a cycle de'] Let $\rho = \rho(d, q) := d/(d-2+d/q)$. It holds that for $\mathbb{P}$-a.e. $\omega$, and all $i=1, \dots, d$, 
