{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.098049+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7cd919f68a39b44b1e0f518a0068502911ea82a4a2f8d5d6e12b72e257c68208","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2608.28198, 'Performative Privacy: When Differential Privacy Maximizes Utility'] Let a mechanism output $o_t$ be perturbed by additive isotropic Gaussian noise $\eta_t \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \frac{\gamma^2}{N_t} I_{d \times d})$, representing the noise. The log-likelihood ratio $\Lambda(o_t|z)$ conditioned on $Z_t$ is given by:
