{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.188557+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d25c80d0a8141d0aef9e56db48885d7ceb32d7d78ebeeba9df2be308f123248","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2606.30938, 'Poissonian potential measures for refracted-reflected L\'evy processes'] Let $q \geq 0$. Then, for $\lambda, \gamma > 0$, $x,b \in [0,a]$ and $u \in [0,\infty)$,
			\begin{align}
				&\mathbb{E}_x \Bigl(\int_0^{\infty} e^{-q t} 1_{\left\{U_t \in \dd u, t < T_{b,U}^{-,\gamma} \wedge T_{a,U}^{+,\lambda} \right\}} \mathrm{d} t\Bigr) \big/ \dd u \notag \\
