{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.318083+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d3932ee4bf7f5d5c0b1ce7e092ba884ac9e92cb23303362ed6af51b3c2b43c1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2607.27786, 'Gaussian free field in annulus: \\BPZ equations and crossing probabilities for level lines'] Fix an even number $n=2N$ and $\bs{\theta}=(\theta_1, \ldots, \theta_{n})\in\LX_{n}$. We write $x_j=\ee^{\ii\theta_j}$ for $1\le j\le n$.  
Let $\varphi_n$ be the bounded harmonic function in $\U$ with alternating boundary data:
\begin{equation} 
\pi\text{ on }\cup_{j=1}^N (x_{2j-1}x_{2j}), \qquad 0\text{ on }\cup_{j=1}^N (x_{2j}x_{2j+1}). 
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation} 
\| \varphi_n\|_{\nabla(\U),\mathrm{reg}}^2= -2\pi \sum_{1\le i<j\le n} (-1)^{j-i} \log |x_i-x_j|. 
\end{equation}
Moreover, its regularized Dirichlet energy is related to the partition function $\LZ_n$ in~\eqref{eqn::LZunitdisc_def}:
\begin{align*}
\LZ_n(\bs{\theta})=\exp\left(-\frac{1}{4\pi}\| \varphi_n\|_{\nabla(\Omega),\mathrm{reg}}^2\right)=\prod_{1\le i<j\le n}\left|\ee^{\ii\theta_i}-\ee^{\ii\theta_j}\right|^{\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{j-i}}. 
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.297578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d3c51e44c7a70167deaa5778b7ec585c3774c745feb2b108c555ffdcda914d3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma bnevent of arXiv:2605.22787, 'Invariant measures for half-space geometric LPP: classification and the one force--one sol'] Fix $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$.
