{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.761927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d648e09d78ab5dc90ab2d93be134cded8f7b88e4ce5489596c2a6f77d940147","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma technical lemma to change exponent of arXiv:2604.27682, 'Multifractional Stable Motion with Random Hurst Exponent'] Let $\alpha \in (0, 2)$ and $0 < \underline{c} < \overline{c} < 1$. Then there is a constant $C(\alpha, \underline{c}, \overline{c})$ such that for all functions $a: \mathbb{R} \to [\underline{c}, \overline{c}]$ and $b: \mathbb{R} \to [\underline{c}, \overline{c}]$ satisfying $|a(x) - b(x)| \leq \Delta$ for all $x \in \mathbb{R}$, and for all $h \in (0,1/e)$,
