{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.204278+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d7a08f1a251c5d21206fb1912dd41c4dd6204d5e77529fda65d7efbaec5a52e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm solMild of arXiv:2506.08202, 'Stochastic dissipative systems in Banach spaces driven by L\'evy noise'] Assume that either Hypotheses (Hyp1C of the paper) or Hypotheses (Hyp2L of the paper) holds. For every $T>0$ and $x\in E$, (equation eqFO of the paper) has unique $E$-valued càdlàg mild solution $\{X(t,x)\}_{t\in [0,T]}$. Moreover for every $t>0$ and $x,z\in E$ we have
