{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.677078+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7dc9ec7bc5f5a0a021d711b415ee5f96913307d258d4eafb466f0fbbf6ac8e65","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 16 (Recurrence relations) of arXiv:2608.16752, 'Absorption Probabilities for Random Convex Hulls: Distribution-Freeness via the Wall-Cross'] For every $d\geq 1$, we have
\begin{align*}
N^{\mathrm{Wend}}_{n,d}&=N^{\mathrm{Wend}}_{n-1,d}+N^{\mathrm{Wend}}_{n-1,d-1}, \qquad n\geq d+1,\\
    N^{\mathrm{walk}}_{n,d}&=(2n-1)N^{\mathrm{walk}}_{n-1,d}+N^{\mathrm{walk}}_{n-1,d-1}, \qquad n\geq d+1,\\
    N^{\mathrm{br}}_{n,d}&=(n-1)N^{\mathrm{br}}_{n-1,d}+N^{\mathrm{br}}_{n-1,d-1}, \qquad n\geq d+2.
