{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.492846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e09472773cf3458a21308f3badb306057235909c368f8f1254e9c5e5575d230","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2512.02538, 'On the spectral geometry of Liouville quantum gravity'] For a Borel nonnegative function $f:\Sigma \to \R$, if $\mathbf{T}_\Sigma = \inf\{ t\ge 0: Z_t \notin \Sigma\}$,
