{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.732290+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e0fbd957bbb837b17cd130b9c24760dee3e0d03d940e7eaabc6d38fba8c3fc3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:alephunobstructed of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] We say that $\Phi$ is \textbf{$\aleph$-obstructed} if it has a transverse compact planar surface with any of the following degeneracy signatures:
