{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.636198+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e5bcacf2afd640a88970c0b302259c8abb547c7fa311f5c6f0c4ff277b83071","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 (Proposition 5.1 in \cite{lambertpopovic2013}) of arXiv:2506.17470, 'The coalescent of a sample from a linear-fractional branching process'] Let $p\in (0,1), r\in [0,1]$ with $p\neq r$. Consider a BGW process $\{Z_n, n\ge 0\}$, whose offspring distribution is $(p,r)$-linear fractional. Then, the branch lengths of the coalescent point process $\{H_i, i\ge 1\}$ are i.i.d. with distribution given by 
