{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.569002+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fb905a70baca4e8ecace5f2053c2bb78066dd2b5ce7b2990ea2c4f13498efa1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 (Conditional propagation of chaos) of arXiv:2606.14170, 'Uniform-in-time error estimates for McKean-Vlasov SDEs with common noise and stochastic al'] Let $X_0^{i,N}=X_0^i$ for all $i\in\mathbb{S}_N$. Suppose that Assumptions \ref{A1} and \ref{A2} hold and that $\sigma_0\sigma_1\neq 0$. Then there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $t>0$ and $i\in\mathbb{S}_N$, 
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{W}_1\big(\mathcal{L}(\mu_t^i),\mathcal{L}(\nu_t^{i,N})\big)\le C\psi(N),
\end{align*}
in the case of $\mathbb{E}|X_0^i|^q<\infty$ for some $q>1$, where $\mu_t^i=\mathcal{L}(X_t^i\vert \mathcal{F}_t^W)$ stands for the regular conditional distribution of $X_t^i$, determined by \eqref{NIPS}, $\nu_t^{i,N}=\mathcal{L}(X_t^{i,N}\vert \mathcal{F}_t^W)$ stands for the conditional distribution of $X_t^{i,N}$, determined by \eqref{IPS} with $\widetilde{b}(x,\mu)=b(x,\mu), \theta_t=\overline\theta_t=t$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.588569+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fbb958487c8639eafc4ad9db525167df075c34e4d8d5382338f21b48da08547","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Problem Irregular Degree Sequences of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] Extend the $N^{-1/6}$ rate to graphs with irregular degree sequences. For random graphs with degree sequence $(d_1, \ldots, d_N)$ satisfying:
