{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.606909+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80040accc7470a9acf9d9a596c34e94317c4763cd79c23deb35c1759fe64fcbf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2506.08775, 'Markovian multivariate Hawkes population processes: Efficient evaluation of moments'] Let $\bm{N}(\cdot)$ be a Markovian multivariate  Hawkes process as given in Definition~\ref{def: multivariate Markov Hawkes process}.
