{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.665518+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_801abbef10fe34dfffa4d1a1a2e07934f5509da77f4288e5fe97668b542c0d06","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:locprob of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] Under the conditions of Theorem (thm:lattice of the paper) one has for $z=x/\sigma$
\begin{align*}
    \mathbf P(S_n = x) 
=
    e^{-\frac{z^2}{2 n}}
    \sum_{j=0}^{2r+2}
        \frac{P_j^{(0)}(z)}{n^{j+1/2}}     
+
    w_n(x)
    , \quad n\ge1,
\end{align*}
where every $P^{(0)}_j(z)$ is a polynomial of degree 
$\lfloor\frac{3j}{2}\rfloor$ and $P^{(0)}_0(z) = 1/(\sigma \sqrt{2 \pi})$.\\
The remainder term $w_n$ satisfies
\begin{align} 
    |w_n(x)| \le \frac{C}{(1+|x|)^{r+2}}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.493937+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80209c88e64b331116112dfcb482a1daa62d692704229598d563f158fb47b91b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 18 of arXiv:2512.02538, 'On the spectral geometry of Liouville quantum gravity'] Let $0< \gamma <2$.
