c_\gamma = \frac1{\pi(2- \gamma^2/2)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.777008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8024d74e63700fd05123d05b92e964d52bdb46cccb601486f9d9bc58c77c1446","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 6 of arXiv:2603.25459, 'Cram\'{e}r-type moderate deviation for double index permutation statistics'] Let $(X,X^{\prime})$ be an exchangeable pair satisfying the condition (D1), and $(W,W^{\prime})$ is also an exchangeable pair, $\Delta = W-W^{\prime}$. Let $\max\{|\Delta|,|D|\}\leq \delta$ for some constant $\delta>0$. Assume that there exits a constant $\tau>0$ such that 
\begin{itemize}
    \item [$(A_{1}):$] $\mathbb{E}\{e^{tW}\}<\infty$,
    \item [$(A_{2}):$] $\mathbb{E}\{\big|1-\frac{1}{2\lambda}\mathbb{E}\{D\Delta|W\}\big|e^{tW}\}\leq \delta_1(t)\mathbb{E}\{e^{tW}\}$,
    \item [$(A_{3}):$] $\mathbb{E}\{|R|e^{tW}\}\leq \delta_2(t)\mathbb{E}\{e^{tW}\}$,
\end{itemize}
where for each $j =1,2$, the fucntion $\delta_{j}(\cdot)$ is increasing and satisfies that $0\leq \delta_{j}(\tau)<\infty$. For $\theta>0$, let $\tau_{0}(\theta) := \max\{0\leq t\leq \min\{\tau,1/\delta\}:t^2(t\delta+2\delta_{1}(t))/2+3t\delta_{2}(t)\leq \theta\}$. Then for any $\theta>0$, $0\leq z\leq \tau_{0}(\theta)$,
\begin{align}
    \left|\frac{\mathbb{P}(W>z)}{1-\Phi(z)}-1\right|\leq 31e^{\theta}(1+9\delta)\left\{(1+z^2)[\delta_1(z)+\delta+\delta\cdot\delta_{2}(z)]+(1+z)\delta_2(z)\right\}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.337398+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_802e87140665ad81524ce42176c922e4ed5d2d1ac43fc02b65c03e8cccb9e499","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cvar-linear-tilt of arXiv:2411.09075, 'Weak Poincar{\'e} Inequalities, Simulated Annealing, and Sampling from Spherical Spin Glas'] {CE22}}]
    Let $(\mu_t)_{t \in \Z_{\ge 0}}$ be a linear-tilt localization process.
    Suppose that for all $t \le T$ we have
    \begin{align*}
        \opnorm{\Cov(Z_t | \mu_t)^{1/2} \cdot \Cov(\mu_t) \cdot \Cov(Z_t | \mu_t)^{1/2}} \le K_t,
    \end{align*}
    where $K_t \in [0, 1]$.
    Then for any function $\varphi$,
    \[ \frac{\E \Var_{\mu_{T}}[\varphi]}{\Var_{\mu}[\varphi]} \ge \prod_{t = 0}^{T-1} (1 - K_t). \] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.743464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_802ec64a51d377fb991dcaa3aeb23c50b997e6124501c8e34393dd3d4b27df2d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm012504-26 of arXiv:2606.07353, 'The Gaussian structure of a perturbed KPZ'] There exists a unique invariant, Borel probability measure
 $\nu_V \in {\mathcal M}_1\big( {\rm H}\big)$ for
 the solution of (equation 011804-26 of the paper), i.e.
 \begin{equation}

   \int_{\mathrm{H}}{\mathcal U}^V_tF(u) \nu_V(du)=\int_{\mathrm{H}}F(u) \nu_V(du),\quad
   t\ge0,\,F\in B_b(\rm H).
 \end{equation}
  The measure $\nu_V$ has the following properties:

 \begin{itemize}
   \item[i)] for any $F\in C_b({\rm H})$ and $\mu\in {\mathcal M}_1\big( {\rm H}\big)$, we have
 \begin{equation}

   \lim_{t\to+\infty}\int_{\mathrm{H}}{\mathcal U}^V_tF(u) \mu(du)=\int_{\mathrm{H}}F(u) \nu_V(du),
 \end{equation}
 \item[ii)] for any $p\in[0,+\infty)$   we
have
\begin{equation}

   \int_{\mathrm{H}} \|u \|_{H^{-1}(\mathbb{T})}^p  \nu_V(du)<+\infty,
 \end{equation}
