{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.610380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80518666eafd10a9b3baf65c9053f9579b162a14cd7aba1e57abed0d99fea8dd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor inv of arXiv:2606.21049, '\textsc{Locality of rough path lifts}'] Let $H \in (1/4,1/2]$, $\eta\in (0,H)$ as in (thm:localfbm of the paper), and $\boldsymbol{X}$ be a local, square-integrable $\eta$-RPL of $X$. Let $\varphi = (0, \varphi^{(2)}, \varphi^{(3)})$ be as in (thm:localfbm of the paper). In the following, statements regarding third levels should be omitted if $H > \frac 13$.
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\alph*)]
\item  $\boldsymbol{X}$ is stationary jointly with the underlying noise in the sense that $\boldsymbol{X}_{s,t} \sim \boldsymbol{X}_{0,t-s}$ if and only if $\varphi_{s,t}^{(n)} = (t-s)A^{(n)}$ with $A \in \mathcal G^{\lfloor 1/H \rfloor}(\mathbb R^d)$ for $n = 2,3$.

\item  $\boldsymbol{X}$ is scale-invariant in the sense that $\boldsymbol{X}^{(n)}_{s,t} \sim (t-s)^{nH} \boldsymbol{X}^{(n)}_{0,1}$ for $n = 2,3$ if and only if it is stationary as above and either $H = \frac 12$, $H = \frac 13$ with $A^{(2)} = 0$, or $A = 0$.

\item  $\boldsymbol{X}$ is coordinate permutation-invariant in the sense that $\sigma_*\boldsymbol{X} \sim \boldsymbol{X}$ for $\sigma \in \mathfrak S_d$ if and only if $\varphi^{\alpha\beta} = 0$ and
\begin{align}
\varphi^{\alpha\beta\gamma} = (\delta^{\alpha\beta} - 2 \delta^{\alpha\gamma} + \delta^{\beta\gamma})\phi
\end{align}
for some $3\eta$-H\"older function $\phi\colon [0,1]\to\mathbb{R}$.
\end{enumerate}
In particular, all three conditions can only hold if either $\varphi = 0$ or for $H = \frac 13$, and in the latter case there is a one-dimensional continuum of such rough paths, namely for $\varphi^{\alpha\beta} = 0$ and $\varphi^{\alpha\beta\gamma}$ as in (equation eq:phiequi of the paper) with $\phi(t) = \lambda t$, $\lambda \in \mathbb R$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.624756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8051d0b5101485ee50690b7ef2868647be4eac91280c17b21cf74951b12f13c9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: identical sequence of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] A process (sequence) $\{X_t\}_{t\in \mathbb{T}}$ ($\mathbb{T}\subset \mathbb{R}_+$) of d-dimensional random vectors on a sublinear expectation space $(\Omega, \mathcal{H}, \hat{\mathbb{E}})$ is called
        \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
            \item  an identical process (sequence) if $X_t$ and $X_s$ are identically distributed for all $t,s\in \mathbb{T}$;
            \item a stationary process (sequence) if for any $n\geq 1$, $t\in\mathbb T$ and $\{t_i\}_{i=1}^n\subset \mathbb{T}$ with $\{t+t_i\}_{i=1}^n\subset \mathbb{T}$
		\begin{equation*}
			(X_{t_1},\cdots,X_{t_n})\stackrel{d}{=} (X_{t+t_1},\cdots,X_{t+t_n}).
		\end{equation*}
        \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.870917+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_805251491f30a205fa522e688f4f9bf7b2f6aee019d943e22a8212d5e74ad1ed","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-moments-W-x of arXiv:2504.20963, 'Exponential moments of truncated branching random walk martingales'] Under the above assumptions, fix  an arbitrary $\rho\in(1,  \gamma \wedge 2]$. There exist constants $K,\mkern 1mu\overline{\mkern-1mu \theta\mkern-1mu}\mkern 1mu>0$ such that for every   $n\in\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$, 
