{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.935582+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8053042f70141e33fc75fc37c0f22ffabbda01b563186c75ac47ae50e6cc1008","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 29 (Theorem 1.1 in \cite{MSS23}) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $G = (V,E)$ be a graph with $|V|=n$, which is either of the following: 
