{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.328493+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80663ea2d00ac92e131044a697b040863f443d452e1963296414001406dd86af","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor ev_V-corep of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\varphi\colon H\to G$ be a homomorphism of compact Lie groups, let $V$ be an $H$-representation with corresponding homomorphism $\rho\colon H\to{\textup{O}}(V)$, let $W$ be a faithful $H$-representation, and let ${\mathcal{U}}_H$ be any complete $H$-universe. Then $\varphi_!(\textbf{\textup{O}}(V,-)\smashp\textbf{\textup{L}}(W,-)_+)$ corepresents the composite
    \begin{equation}
