{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.051305+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8072c5c0353f040959f0b01d5acb73e9f358ac5d6cff055e0a219a84fdb4cf5d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:rep of arXiv:2607.12564, 'Power-law and log-periodic degree tails for a family of probability generating function eq'] Let $Y$ be a geometric random variable, independent of $(D^*_n)$, with
