{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.828955+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8074eeff095cc9922d511254fa8ed71856756af22667b8d9a2a261450331e827","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn wrap of arXiv:2609.01751, 'Orthogonal polynomials which are eigenfunctions of a partial differential operator'] Let $d_1$ and $d_2$ be positive integers and let $\Omega_1^{d_1} \subset {\mathbb R}^{d_1}$ and 
$\Omega_2^d \subset {\mathbb R}^{d_2}$ be two domains with non-empty interior. Let ${\bm W}_1$ be a weight 
function on ${\mathbb R}^{d_1}$ and ${\bm W}_2$ be the weight functions defined on $\Omega_2^{d_2}$. 
The wrapped product weight function ${\bm W}_1 \rtimes {\bm W}_2$ is defined by 
\begin{equation}
{\bm W}^{\Omega_1\rtimes \Omega_2}({\bm x},{\bm y}) ={\bm W}_1\left( \frac{{\bm x}} {\rho({\bm y})} \right) {\bm W}_2({\bm y}) , 
   \qquad ({\bm x}, {\bm y}) \in \Omega_1^{d_1} \rtimes \Omega_2^{d_2}
\end{equation}
where the warpped domain $\Omega_1^{d_1} \rtimes \Omega_2^{d_2}$ is defined by 
\begin{equation} 
\Omega_1^{d_1}  \rtimes \Omega_2^{d_2}:= \left\{({\bm x},{\bm y}): \frac{{\bm x}}{\rho({\bm y})} \in \Omega_1^{d_1} , 
\quad {\bm y} \in \Omega_2^{d_2} \right\}, 
\end{equation}
where $\rho: \Omega_2^{d_2} \mapsto {\mathbb R}_+$ is nonnegative and specified according to one of the two cases,
\begin{enumerate}[    ]
\item[] {\bf Case 1}. $\rho$ is a polynomial of degree $1$; \smallskip
\item[] {\bf Case 2}. $\rho$ is the square root of a polynomial of degree at most $2$, and $\Omega_1^{d_1} $ 
and ${\bm W}_1$ are both centrally symmetric. 
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.321928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_80783e0c1d6063ddea41138be6368d76cbcc8eb1938e734354c8f57b0e8fd792","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:maximum_principle of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] Fix $T > 0$, $\kappa > 0$, and $m > 2$. Suppose $f_{\rm in} \in L^\infty_{{\rm rapid}}(\mathbb T^3\times \mathbb R^3)$ and $g\in L^\infty(0,T;L^\infty_m)$ satisfy $0 \le f_{\rm in},\,g\le 1$.
    Then, for every $\ell > 0$, the unique solution $f$ to (equation eq:semilinear of the paper) satisfies
    \begin{equation}
         \left\|f(t)\right\|_{L^\infty_{\ell}} \le \exp\bigl\{C(\kappa + \Lambda)t\bigr\}
         \norm{f_{\rm in}}_{L^\infty_\ell}, 
    \end{equation}
    where $C$ depends only on $m$ and $\ell$ and where $\displaystyle \Lambda \coloneqq \left\|g(t)\right\|_{L^\infty(0,T;L^\infty_m)}$. In particular, $f(t) \in L^\infty_{{\rm rapid}}$ for each $t \in [0,T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.199690+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_807a009e257b60ba36723ce526ae75ad08d0103179296df3839523063b3e0231","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 58 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] The length $\alpha_{\tot}\log(N)$ string $x\in [k]_0^M$ is a \textbf{collision-likely prefix} (we write $x\in \Pre$) if for all $(i,l)\in T$,
        \begin{equation}
            x \mbox{ contains } \alpha_l^{(i)}\log(N) \mbox{ of } l\mbox{-digits in positions } \{1\leq t\leq \alpha_{\tot}\log(N): \bn^{(t)}/N\in D_i\}.
        \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:15:16.653497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_807cd11cf2b7386acc9973a529f1866a965a57115ddccc16d8274ea1093c8fe3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 13 of arXiv:2608.30752, '2608.30752'] Under the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:energy-quasi-convexity},
