{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.856531+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_814dc065e14c1039e3202477e29cfdfbebd5198cd6fc6a9d08b913f6c968835a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:LehnerFormula of arXiv:2510.01021, '\Large Random Matrices, Intrinsic Freeness, and Sharp Non-Asymptotic Inequalities\relatedv'] [Lehner's formula~[LehnerFormula1999] (see also~[bandeira2023free])]

Let $A_0,A_1,\dots,A_n$ be self-adjoint matrices and $X_{\mathrm{free}}$ as in Definition~(def:Xfree of the paper):
\begin{equation}
\big\| X_{\mathrm{free}} \big\| = \max_{\varepsilon\in\{\pm1\}} \inf_{Z\succeq 0} \lambda_{\max}\left(Z^{-1} + \varepsilon A_0 + \sum_{k=1}^n A_k Z A_k \right).
