{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.958890+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8155ac9581d119c977c20cabfb9feacf40b002510459898ffc9669aacd600f90","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 (Spectral domination of root events) of arXiv:2607.13210, 'Punctured Wilson--Evolving Sets and Root Identities for Massive Kirchhoff Forests'] For distinct $x_1,\ldots,x_k$ elements of $V$, let $A=\{x_1,\ldots,x_k\}\subset V$. Then, it comes:
