{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.330392+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_819b10f0970ec18e7790ed3f47419e90c74061c9682685b3979bec84c21b3857","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma sigma-bullet-left-adj of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] The global functor $\Sigma^\bullet_+\colon\ul{{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_\textup{gl}\to{\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{gl}$ is a left adjoint.
    \begin{proof}
        By the aforementioned Proposition (prop:Sigma-bullet-homotopical-left-Quillen of the paper), $\Sigma^\bullet_+$ is left Quillen, proving the existence of a pointwise right adjoint. To prove the Beck--Chevalley condition for these right adjoints it then suffices to observe that also the restriction functors $\cat{$\bm{G'}$-OrthSp}\to\cat{$\bm{G}$-OrthSp}$ are right Quillen (Lemma~(lemma:restr-gl-sp-right-Quillen of the paper)) and that the Beck--Chevalley condition holds for the underived functors (in fact, for the standard choice of adjunctions and counits, the Beck--Chevalley map will even be the identity).
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.210870+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_819f4e58048f9ffcb907fc5329867fdb9845031e285445c24992c01ffee1d190","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2604.27485, 'On large deviation principles for general random processes \footnote{Research supported by'] {\rm
We will say that a statement~$\mathcal S$  whose formulation involves a function $\varepsilon=\varepsilon_T >0$ {\em is satisfied for $\ept $ that tends  to zero slowly enough  as\/} $T\to\infty $ (and will denote this property of the function~$\ep$ by writing  ``$\varepsilon =\oo (1)$ as $T\to\infty $'') if
