almost surely as $\mathcal{E}^n_{\ell,r}(\mathbf{X})$-measurable random variables.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.754232+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81abfb1e4bdd3c6d6c37172d7801cb7fbdffcda3da4e710df12ade22686760eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 29 of arXiv:2604.11682, 'Semilocalization for inhomogeneous random graphs'] Let $\nu > 0$. There exists $C_{\nu} > 0$ such that with $\nu$-high probability,
  \begin{equation*}
      \|\hat{A} - A^{\pp}\| \leq C_{\nu} \sqrt{\frac{\log N}{\log \log N}} \quad \text{ and } \quad \|\hat{A} - A\| \leq C_{\nu}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{\log \log N}}\,.
  \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:22:39.767662+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81b44cfd380aa4adffae01dc3ee19b46d1679b52a7879782f8467960299cd512","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d:corfun of arXiv:2508.21658, 'Infinite-dimensional stochastic differential equations for Coulomb random point fields'] A symmetric, locally integrable function $ \rho_\nu^m $ on $ \Rdm $
is called the \emph{$ m $-point correlation function}
of an RPF $ \nu $ (with respect to Lebesgue measure) if
\begin{align}\notag &
\int_{ A_1^{ k_1 } \times \cdots \times A_n^{ k_n } }
\rho_\nu^m ( \x ^1 , \ldots , \x ^m ) \, d\x ^1 \cdots d\x ^m
=
\int_{ \sSS }
\prod_{ i = 1 }^{ n }
\frac{ \sss ( A_i ) ! }{ ( \sss ( A_i ) - k_i ) ! }
\, \nu ( d\sss )
,\end{align}
for any disjoint bounded measurable sets
$ A_1 , \ldots , A_n $
and nonnegative integers
$ k_1 + \cdots + k_n = m $.
Here, $ \sss ( A ) $ denotes the number of particles in $ A $
when $ \sss = \sum_i \delta_{ \si } $,
and the fraction is interpreted as zero
if $ \sss ( A_i ) - k_i < 0 $.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:45.011857+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81b4549c92a3d44be2a3fbc8b49e65d9099e6b9196acafbecb769e62fbc08ae2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2605.11877, 'Fluctuation analysis for a randomly perturbed dynamical system with state-dependent impuls'] Given $\delta>0$ same as the in set $G^\eps_{\cdot}$, the following holds,
	\begin{equation*}
		\|J^\eps_{\cdot} -1\|_\infty \le  \frac{2\delta}{\alpha}\wedge \frac{\delta}{\sfT-\ren(\sfT)\alpha}
	\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.737898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81ba356433ef0db2dd7415847b62abefdc5318821d890ee022e9a7b8a8c571e0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:Woodbury of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] Let $K$ be dressing compatible with $(\Psi, \Phi)$,
and suppose that $\dim E < \infty$ and that
$F(u) \vcentcolon= \det_H(I - zK(u))$
is well-defined for every $u \in \mathcal{V}$.  Then
\begin{equation}
F(u) = F(Tu)\det_E\bigl(\mathcal{M}(Tu)\bigr).
\end{equation}
In particular, for each $i \in \mathbb{N}$,
