{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.762988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_82605b7927a0302e26af09ff9ceb59ead1b514ec2701f3a39f810328755846b2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:lemflow of arXiv:2411.02541, 'The hockey-stick conjecture for\\ activated random walk'] \thlabel{lem:flow}
  Let $u$ be an extended odometer on $\ii{0,n}$.
  Let $f_v=\rt{u}{v}-\lt{u}{v+1}$, the net flow from $v$ to $v+1$.
  Let $s_v=\sum_{i=1}^v\1\{\mathsf{instr}_i(u(i))=\ensuremath{\mathtt{sleep}}\}$.
  Then $u$ is stable on $\ii{1,n-1}$ for initial configuration $\sigma$ if and only if
  \begin{align}
    f_v = f_0 + \sum_{i=1}^v\abs{\sigma(i)} - s_v\quad\text{for all $v\in\ii{0,n-1}$.}
  \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.077248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_826336b607db92ad5594f115479abe01715d0606d664740fd5c2b9314e57164d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro dqgsr of arXiv:2507.00737, 'Dispersion models on a circle: universal properties and asymptotic results'] For all compact interval $\Lambda\subset[0,+\infty)$
	\begin{equation}
