{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:44.405091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_826367345bd8f67aafb6e3c5e4e0112712285a8ba3931ccca908fc93fe131a29","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2609.03187, 'Duality for a Martingale Transport Problem with Moment Constraints'] For every $\lambda \in \mathbb R^N$ the function $\Psi_\lambda(a)$ is finite, convex, and continuously differentiable on $\mathbb R$, with
