{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.872828+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8264114f985b711ee6606f41bbcbc45b7ff8ea1aad20fe84c4a1414ef036d760","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:control-sixth of arXiv:2608.26765, 'Beyond Client Averaging: A Client-Independent Second-Order Stationary-Bias Component in St'] There exist $\gamma_{0,H}^{(C6)}>0$ and $C_{\xi,6,H}<\infty$, independent of $N$ and $\gamma$, such that for $0<\gamma\le\gamma_{0,H}^{(C6)}$,
