{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.144147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8265bcfcca75eeaea604fccac16b9e8a92a2f0d484e60d44b3ea037cad420f2e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 8 of arXiv:2604.06122, 'REM universality for linear random energy'] We have 
 \been{

 g(0)=g'(0)=0,\quad g''(0)=1-m^2.
 }
 For  any $\lambda\in \mathbb{R}$
\been{

