{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.889406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_826634ea0a3dbf3e8ae5712921b0d911381d62b9f8444b61bbc4da129ad6e23b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Teorema 19 of arXiv:2506.11937, 'Random rotational invariance of integration by parts formulas within a Bismut-type approac'] A stochastic transformation $\ T=(\Phi, B, \eta,h) \in S_m(M)$ is a (weak) symmetry of  $ SDE_{\mu,\sigma}$ if and only if

