{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.630514+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_828e68b3354f5c390e293aed397cefebdf972c3431ccbfdbb838daabc98d9c85","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop P:two-point-bd of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Take $n \in \mathbb{N}$, parameter $\alpha \ge 1/2 - n^{-1/6}$, and $x, y, z_0 \in \llbracket0, n/100 \rrbracket$, $a > 0$ satisfying
\begin{equation}

C_0 \max \left(\frac{z_0^2}{n}, \frac{z_0 |y-x|}{n}, z_0(1/2 - \alpha)\vee 0 \right) < a < C_* z_0,
\end{equation}
where $C_0>0$ is a universal constant, and $C_*>0$ is any large enough number.
Then for a constant $c>0$ depending only on $C_*$, we have
$$
\mathbb{P}\left(\max_{z \in\llbracket0,z_0 \rrbracket} \left|\bar X[x, 1; y + z, n]_\textsf{L} - \bar X[x, 1; y, n]_\textsf{L} \right| \ge a \right) \le 2\exp(- c a^2/z_0) + 2 \exp(-c \sqrt{n}).
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.576780+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_828f2a2fcbaa9a1402166c4011e06fabbb9e1512dacf71266a944ea56ca12673","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem-bound for V-001 of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] There exists $c>0$ such that, for any $x \geqslant 1$, 
