{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.445035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8290c882a024c0b2226239bd1dee383de7bf6c26b04193456eed419bebf17331","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary corr: superdiffusive a.s. conv eg 1 of arXiv:2505.05921, 'Limit Theorems for step reinforced random walks\\ with regularly varying memory'] {}
    Let $\{S_n\}_{n\geq 0}$ be the SRRW-RVM with zero mean, unit variance innovation sequence $\{\xi_n\}$. Then for $p=p_c$ and $\{\mu_n\}$ satisfying Assumption~(eg 1 of the paper) with $\alpha+\gamma+1<0$,    
