{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.985001+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_82bf2b2f7a40ec5ab3430ceac6fa3d49af941e1ec11b0b0fbaf073d62e047f3b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemme compl. of arXiv:2412.00865, 'On the spectral problem and fractional diffusion limit for Fokker-Planck with(-out) drift '] Let $\eta, \lambda_0>0$ fixed small enough. Let $\lambda \in \mathbb{C}$ such that $|\lambda|\leqslant \lambda_0$. Then, for all $\psi, F \in \mathcal{H}_\eta$ such that $|a(\psi,\psi)| \leqslant C \| F \|_{\mathcal{H}_\eta} \| \psi \|_{\mathcal{H}_\eta}$, the following inequality holds
