{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.040329+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_82ceceb8749192f697bfc265e6bad283e023a35b08b4c47915b7b4bf807af616","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2608.15805, 'Spectral duality structures and the Fisher--Rao geometry of reset distributions'] $\widetilde P$ is the symmetric tridiagonal matrix with constant
