{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.674787+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_830a8c76991a0ee940f8c4e87f245b79052eb5466b096746b2e083ede7b967e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 37 of arXiv:2608.09700, 'A general paracontrolled ansatz for singular SPDEs'] Suppose we are given a smooth admissible stochastic data $\mcZ=(Z_\tau)$. Let a tree $\tau= X^k \Xi_\ell \prod_{j=1}^n\mcI_{b_j}(\tau_j) \, $ with $|\tau|<0$.
