{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.443256+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_831216a8ef32f45b383f426e0953aa5a53322f8e496f839d56bbef841261341e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:defXYGFF of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] We fix an integer $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, an integer $n \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}^*$ and three inverse temperatures $\beta, \beta_1, \beta_2 > 0$ and define three models of height functions (see Figures~(fig:XYheight of the paper) and~(fig:XYGFFheight of the paper)):
\begin{itemize}
    \item The first one is the XY height function on the multigraph $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^d_{n-\mathrm{mult}}$ with inverse temperature $n \beta$ on each edge, i.e.,
    \begin{equation*}
        \mu_{\Lambda_L, n, \beta}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}(\left\{ \varphi \right\}) := \frac{1}{Z_{\Lambda_L, n, \beta}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}}  \prod_{x \sim y}    \left(I_{\left(\varphi(x) - \varphi(y)\right)} \left(n \beta \right)\right)^n.
    \end{equation*}
    \item The second one is an XY height function multigraph $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2_{n- \mathrm{mult}}$ with $n \geq 2$ and with two inverse temperatures $\beta_1 , n \beta_2  \geq 0$ (see Figure~(fig:XYheight of the paper)):
\begin{equation*}
        \mu_{\Lambda_L, n, \beta_1 , \beta_2}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}(\left\{ \varphi \right\}) := \frac{1}{Z_{\Lambda_L, n, \beta_1,  \beta_2 }^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}}\prod_{x \sim y} \left( I_{\left(\varphi(x) - \varphi(y)\right)} \left( \beta_1 \right) \right)^2   \left( I_{\left(\varphi(x) - \varphi(y)\right)} \left(  n \beta_2 \right) \right)^{n-2}.
\end{equation*}
    \item The third one is a height function on the multigraph $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2_{3-\mathrm{mult}}$ where the interaction between two vertices is a product of the integer-valued Gaussian distribution and the modified Bessel function (see Figure~(fig:XYGFFheight of the paper))
    \begin{equation} 
        \mu_{\Lambda_L, \beta_1 , \beta_2}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}/\mathrm{GFF}}(\left\{ \varphi \right\}) := \frac{1}{Z_{\Lambda_L, \beta_1 , \beta_2 }^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}/\mathrm{GFF}}} \prod_{x \sim y} \left( I_{\left(\varphi(x) - \varphi(y)\right)} \left( \beta_1 \right) \right)^2 \exp \left( - \frac{\left( \varphi(x) - \varphi(y) \right)^2}{2\beta_2} \right).
    \end{equation}
    We refer to this model as the $\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}$-XY/GFF height function.
\end{itemize}
We denote by $\mathrm{Var}_{L, n,  \beta}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}$, $\mathrm{Var}_{L, n, \beta_1 , \beta_2}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}$ and $\mathrm{Var}_{L, \beta_1 , \beta_2}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}/\mathrm{GFF}}$ the variances with respect to these three measures.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.240927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8315338b5ef83b11915bbf4309257766fcdf24135204a5af34fa4c174d8ee2fa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:honest-region of arXiv:2608.20295, 'Physical-Support Confidence Sets for Highly Coherent Dictionaries'] Under Assumption~(ass:frozen-shell of the paper) and the calibration coverage condition
