{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:58:40.872554+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_832dbd8cfe2286a071eea219bb483313db225e2e012cf997375c06756237a40a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:supp-zero-proj of arXiv:2605.10491, 'Zero-couplings of infinite measures with cyclically monotone support and multivariate regu'] Let $\gamma \in \mathrm{M}_{0}(\reals^d\times\reals^d)$ and let $\mu = \varphi_1\gamma\in\mathrm{M}_{0}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ denote its left zero-marginal. Then $\operatorname{spt}\mu \subset\operatorname{spt}\phi_1\gamma= \operatorname{cl} (\operatorname{proj}_1 (\operatorname{spt} \gamma))$. 


