{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.191819+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_832f73bfb3bc8b5437d52ed3bbeedcc15b725bc97ba5738e19fb5c0999fd8ae4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Non-degenerate support) of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] Let $\chi$ be either real or complex random variable. Denote the law of $\chi$ by $\mu$, which is a probability measure on $\R$ or $\C$, respectively. We say that $\chi$ has non-degenerate support if the following holds:
\begin{itemize}
\item[$\bullet$]  [Real case] The support of $\mu$ contains infinitely many points.
\item[$\bullet$]   [Complex case] There is no nonzero polynomial $P(z,\overline{z})\not\equiv 0$, such that the support of $\mu$ is contained in the zero set of $P$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.490796+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8331f67ee1e259d88aa115c9e8ddc8cded186b30d31f4c1abf8f5424c08d11e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2607.04012, 'Hölder regularity for backward stochastic Volterra integral equations and applications to '] Suppose that $\Psi \in L^{p}\big(\Omega; L^2(0,T) \big)$, that
    $G^0 \coloneqq G(\cdot, \cdot, 0, 0) \in \mathcal{H}_\Delta^{p}(0,T)$, and that $G$ is uniformly Lipschitz in $(y,z)$. More precisely, assume that there exists a constant $[G]_L>0$ such that, $d\mathbb P\otimes dt\otimes ds$-a.e. on $\Omega\times\Delta(0,T)$,
    \begin{gather*}
        | G(t, s, y_1, z_1) - G(t, s, y_2, z_2)|
        \leq
        [G]_{L} \big( |y_1-y_2| + |z_1 - z_2|  \big),
    \end{gather*}
    for all $(y_1,z_1),(y_2,z_2)\in\mathbb R^2$. Then \eqref{eq:bsvie-intro} admits a unique solution $(Y,Z) \in \mathcal{H}^p(0,T) \times \mathcal{H}_{\Delta}^p(0,T)$.

    Moreover, define $Y(t,s)$ by
    \begin{flalign*}
        Y(t,s) \coloneqq \mathbb{E}_s \bigg[ \Psi(t) + \int_s^T G(t,r,Y(r),Z(t,r))dr \bigg], \quad  0 \leq t \leq s \leq T.
    \end{flalign*}
    Then there exists a constant $C>0$, depending only on $p$, $T$ and $[G]_L$, such that
    \begin{flalign}
       \mathbb{E}\Bigg[ \sup_{s \in [0,T]}  \bigg( \int_0^s |Y(t,s)|^2 dt \bigg)^{\frac{p}{2}} + \bigg( \int_0^T |Y(t)|^2 dt \bigg)^{\frac{p}{2}} + & \bigg( \int_0^T \int_t^T  |Z(t,s)|^2 ds dt \bigg)^{\frac{p}{2}} \Bigg] \leq C \Big( \norm{\Psi}_{2,p}^p + \norm{G^0}_{\mathcal{H}_\Delta^p}^p\Big).
    \end{flalign} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.992452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83321195d6f170e5c94a04b659ea550f5f95165d85f070a6dbb5e917e8e1082c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2609.03386, 'Twisted Gradient Flow Approach to Vegetation-Rainfall-Bushfire Interactions Model'] There exists a constant $C_{15}>0$, which depends on $\delta$, $T^*$, $\|u_0\|_{H^1(\Omega)}$, $\|v_0\|_{H^1(\Omega)}$ and $\|w_0\|_{H^1(\Omega)}$, such that

