{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.060138+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83383521cbc100e4fbd4779b9d545e0ed65db6cfbe23183160a9e37ffd3a5200","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conj left-asymptotics of arXiv:2606.19507, 'The $t$-Split Two-Periodic Aztec Diamond Model'] The macroscopic boundary of the $t$-split two-periodic Aztec diamond to the left of the interface is governed by the saddle function
    \begin{equation}
        \varphi_{\alpha,\beta}(z;x,y) = (1+y) \log z - \log(z-1) + (t-x) \log r_{\alpha,2}(z) + (1/2 - t) \log r_{\beta,2}(z),
