{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.044161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_836d67a47470791e3561fd713f4e9a50629bc31affa24c155da6e5a8226ec6e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 19 of arXiv:2510.24244, 'Statistical properties of Markov shifts: part II-LLT'] There are positive constants $\del_0,c_1,c_2,C_1,C_2$ such that for every finite sequence of functions    
$(v_j)_{j=n}^{n+m-1}$ with $a:=\max\|v_j\|_{j,\omega}\leq \del_0$ 
