{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.813372+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_842cdc53216212cd93a2f20be5f7d79ba98f0cacfd0851b23872954633f30677","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2512.18435, 'Indistinguishability for recurrent clusters'] We call \textbf{Simple Delayed Random Walk} (or \textbf{SDRW}) on some percolation configuration $\omega$ the Markov chain with the following transition probabilities:
    $$
p(x,y):=\begin{cases}
    \frac{1}{\deg_G(x)},&\text{if $x$ and $y$ are neighbours in $\omega$,}\\
    1-\frac{\deg_\omega(x)}{\deg_G(x)},&\text{if $x=y$,}\\
    0 &\text{else.}
\end{cases}
    $$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:25:35.657511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_842df1ff661a8c7a58cd01d87a77fed95cd9eecd5b78d50aa94dc3d60c85d073","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma add_new_boundary of arXiv:2603.05491, '\textbf{Local limits of uniform triangulations with boundaries in high genus}'] Let $\varepsilon > 0$. 
There exists $C_{\varepsilon} > 0$ such that for all $g \ge 0$ and $n \ge 2g-1$ with $\frac{g}{n} \le \frac{1}{2} - 4\varepsilon$ and all $p_1,\dots,p_{\ell} \ge 1$ with $|\mathbf{p}| \le \varepsilon n$,
\begin{align*}
    \tau_{(p_1,\dots,p_{\ell})}(n,g) \le (6n)^{\ell - 1} \tau(n,g),
