{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.485414+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8435bb5d4fe949ceb65f67b34bc6ee7e298aa256f85ecbb8ff49a7300c30d4d0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:directed-spectral-gap of arXiv:2505.02685, 'On the Spectral Expansion of Monotone Subsets of the Hypercube'] The \emph{dynamical spectral gap} of $G$ is the quantity $\lambda^-(G) \in [0, +\infty]$ given by
