{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.784502+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8438024b40037f91b92747f480952ae28a314435724c3adf7ec7e768471513ba","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem rarity-of-disagreement-regions of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists $M_0(d)$ such that for all $M\ge M_0$ the following holds. Suppose that $\mathbb P(\widetilde{D}_{k-1}(B') =1)\le q_{k-1}$ for all $B' \in \mathscr{B}_{k-1}$. Then for every $B \in \mathscr{B}_k$, one has 
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb P(|\mathsf{Dis}_{k-1}(B)|>s_k ) \le q_k/10\,.
