\]
where $f_i, g_i \in (x, y) \subset \mbC [x, y, s, t, w]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.770216+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8476e3ecd289eac8841d44adbbb0335cb4f61d4e32bc3ded2b7f287636bda171","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (\cite{KirkpatrickMeckes2013,KirkpatrickNawaz2016,FangKoike2022}) of arXiv:2512.05340, 'The rate of convergence of the critical mean-field $O(N)$ magnetization via multivariate n'] Fix $N \geq 2$ and let $W_{n} := \sqrt{N-\beta}\,S_{n}/\sqrt{n}$ and $Z \sim N\left(0, \id\right)$, where $\id\in\RR^{d\times d}$ is the
