{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.728976+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_853a790991f528185dba292ea63947225cc8592ef66bf41a652e995695d55bfa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:hitting-time of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] Suppose that $\alpha>1$ and $\theta>\theta_{0,L}$, and let $C_E$ denote the lower bound obtained from Corollary (coro:m_easy of the paper) for the region $|m(x)| < \mathsf{m}_{3}$. Fix any initialization $X_0$ and let $\tau_{m,\varepsilon} $ denote the first time $|m_t| \geq \varepsilon$, then for any $r>0$ we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb P[ \tau_{m,\varepsilon} > T+r ] \leq  2e^{-r}\,,\quad
        \text{ where } \quad &T=\frac1{C_E}\Big( \log \sqrt{N}+\log(\sqrt{\frac{\beta C_E}2}\arcsin\varepsilon)\Big)\,.
    \end{align*}
    In particular, $|m_t|$ hits the threshold $\mathsf{m}_{3}$ of~(equation eq:def-of-m-1-2-3 of the paper)  with probability at least $1-2e^{-100}$ in time $T_{\text{hit}}$, where $T_{\text{hit} }$ is given by: 
    \begin{align} 
        T_{\text{hit}}=100 \frac{ \tfrac{1}{2} \log N+\log (\sqrt{\frac12\beta (\lambda_1-\lambda_2)(\mathsf{m}_{\textsc{e}}^2-\mathsf{m}_{3}^2)}\arcsin \mathsf{m}_{3})}{(\lambda_1-\lambda_2)(\mathsf{m}_{\textsc{e}}^2-\mathsf{m}_{3}^2)}\,.
    \end{align}
    Note that if $\lambda_1 - \lambda_2 = \Omega(1)$, then $T_{hit} = O(\log N)$.","status":"unverified"}

