{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.903386+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85671cb322fb0760347358684729458ea7190ae1ccd9674b45bd56abc495b376","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 (Explicit Form of the Predictable Compensator) of arXiv:2606.20925, 'Explicit Predictable Compensators for Single Jump Processes with Initial Information'] Let $X$ be the special semimartingale satisfying the integrability conditions introduced above. Its unique predictable compensator is given by $A_t=C(t\wedge\gamma)$, where the $\cH$-measurable function $C(t)$ is explicitly computed as follows.
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
