{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.811898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_856e6acd71c89665bc884cb657a05eb12b36485f6a76900e466798761350f6d3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma claim-1 of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] For any continuous-time reversible Markov chain with the state space $\cS$, the generator $\cL$ and the stationary distribution $\pi$, the following inequality holds for any test function $f \in \ell_{2, \pi}, m \in \R$ and the Lyapunov function $V$ such that $V(q) > 0 \, \forall q \in \cS$:
