{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.219933+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8573018910962f9b0306d5cdfd4a566c5d8fafe29491019374f760f305449131","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:7 of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] Assume that the test function $h (q)$ satisfies the assumptions of Theorem (Thm:M of the paper). Then $G_{n, \tau} [h]$  converges, in the scaling limit $n\to \infty$, $n\tau=t>0$, to
