{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.581881+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8582f35e17b90af519d2caffb5c0cf8a7022d5515ae57647dd9b5c63c2bddc89","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary Prop.BoundR of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $p\geq 1$, there exists a constant $C>0$ independent of $n$ and $t$ such that
