{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.825306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8584e4d4ccb8f11ed0ee3977521b5d93d9ba733a720fc3fb5f22cb4e6305645e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma drift-lemma-super-HW of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $V$ be defined as in (equation eqn: mmn-lyapunov of the paper) and $\cL$ be the generator of the $M/M/n$ queue in the super Halfin-Whitt regime (i.e. $\alpha > 1/2$) with arrival rate $\lambda_n = n-n^{1-\alpha}$. Then, there exists $\gamma_n \geq \br{\sqrt{n}-\sqrt{\lambda_n}}^2$ and a function $b: \Z_{\geq 0} \rightarrow \R_{\geq 0}$ such that:
