{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.732571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85942243a059977b21da8bfb411445bd07567e0e1715e7f8ec97809bf9a8dd8c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] Given regularisation scales $0 < \delta < \eps$, throughout this section, we define the smooth and stationary random noise assignment $\tilde{\pi}^{\eps, \delta}: \tilde{\mfL}_- \to C^\infty(\mbR^2)$
