$\{(x,g,s):x\in B(K),g\in B(\hat{M}+MK),s\in\mathcal{N}\}$, for all $u$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.663188+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85bdb9a653981c73971b36fb895075e4fc6ccd69ea754bcb97ea844627c799ee","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Tsteinm of arXiv:2604.06012, 'Large fringe trees for random trees with given vertex degrees'] Let ${\mathbf{n}}$ and ${\mathbf{m}}$ be two degree statistics.
