    is non-negative and non-decreasing in $t$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.035450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85c14e8cfa485ea228f89f71d0e72f1bcce56756691986efa88fe116b3673fc6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2605.03100, 'Berry-Esseen bounds for multivariate martingale difference sequences in the Kolmogorov dis'] \cite[Lemma 2.3]{Kojevnikov2022}
Let $\bm{X}$ denote a $d$-dimensional Gaussian random variable with mean $\bm{0}$ and variance $\bm{\Sigma}$. Then for every $s \geq 2$, there exists a constant $C_s$ depending only on $s$, such that
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}\|\bm{X}\|_{\infty}^s \leq C_s \log_+^{\frac{s}{2}}d \cdot (d_{\max}(\bm{\Sigma}))^{\frac{s}{2}};
\end{align*}
furthermore, for any $\delta \in (0,1)$, 
\begin{align*}
\|\bm{X}\|_{\infty} \lesssim \sqrt{d_{\max}(\bm{\Sigma}) \log \frac{d}{\delta}}.
\end{align*}
with probability at least $1-\delta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.537789+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85c2907b38082eeaddd69a29c9ecb5b70a29dfd94a5e6d4fa3db4608e9f48a82","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2603.28226, '2603.28226'] Assume that $(\mathcal F_n)_{n\ge1}$ is an $\alpha$-regular atomic filtration. Let $f\in L^1(\Omega,\mathbb P)$ with $f\ge0$, and set $f_n=\mathbb E_n[f]$. Then for every $n\ge2$,
