{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.086895+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85cdec7e25eaeb1b30611c10f37d2ef7470202cfabf5ee74ba20adfd5dfe3867","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemm 20 of arXiv:2607.13849, 'Rearranged Stochastic Heat Equation with an Entropy Gradient Structure'] Let $(\psi_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be any continuous deterministic trajectory valued in the space $\mathcal{H}^6_{\mathrm{Sym}}(\mathbb{S})$, such that $|\langle \psi_t, e_k\rangle| \leq Ck^{-6} .$ Then, the quantity
