{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.501136+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85ddc04180e6f08f9701aa6f1fe1ceda8fc27c63da57366c549548e6b58a5d25","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lm 11 of arXiv:2609.02576, 'Sharp estimates for the Jacobi and trigonometric Dunkl heat kernels'] Let $t\geq 1$ and $0<y\le x<\infty$ be such that $x\le 2t$. The following identity holds:
