{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.728995+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8640380d83062181c79b18c8bcc0c1c187477ac018533366c1c2757774ef4ece","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-H-1 of arXiv:2411.04500, '\LARGE Probabilistic Approaches to The Energy Equality in Forced Surface Quasi-Geostrophic'] For any $ f\in L^2{(\mathbb{T}^2)},$ there exists a constant $ C>0 $ such that
