{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.797175+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8658b2e867d84ad817ec3f7b11afdf778064942ac31be3a54e1f8e11c2bfa157","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:two-edges_delta=1/gamma-1 of arXiv:2509.23496, 'Crossing probabilities in geometric inhomogeneous random graphs'] Suppose $2<\delta=\frac 1 \gamma-1$. The two-edges crossing probabilities are given~by 
    \begin{align*}
        \pi_{(u),R}^{(2)} 
        &\asymp \pi_{(u),R}+ \big(u^{-\gamma} R^{d(1-\delta)}\log R \big)\wedge 1\\
        &\asymp \begin{cases}
                    u^{-\gamma} R^{d(1-\delta)}\log R & \text{ on } \{u \geq (\log R)^{-\frac 1 {1- 2\gamma}}\},\\
                    u^{-\gamma \delta} R^{d(1-\delta)} & \text{ on } \{R^{d(\frac 1 {\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma)} \leq u \leq (\log R)^{-\frac 1 {1- 2\gamma}}\},\\
                    1 & \text{ on } \{u\leq R^{d(\frac 1 {\gamma \delta}-\frac 1 \gamma)} \}.
                \end{cases}
    \end{align*}
    \begin{align*}
        \pi_{r,R}^{(2)} 
        &\asymp \pi_{r,R}+ r^{\frac d \delta} R^{d(1-\delta)} \log R 
        \asymp \begin{cases}
                    r^{\frac d \delta} R^{d(1-\delta)}\log R & \text{ on } 
                    \{ r^d \leq  (\log R)^{\frac \delta {\delta-1}}\} ,\\
                    r^d R^{d(1-\delta)} & \text{ on } \{(\log R)^{\frac \delta {\delta-1}} \leq r^d, R\geq 2r  \}.
                \end{cases}
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.464701+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_865d34b9a1b27f34d4d00ca008c46c1326a26421ed4abe39c1db81d1b8f32928","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2606.29131, '2606.29131'] Suppose that Assumption {\rm\ref{a1-1}(iii)} and Assumption {\rm\ref{a1-2}} hold, and that there exists $\beta>0$ such that
