{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.306398+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_865d5b9ce03b9483dedace17430a038c685c3240a68ebc4cbb442b4e0cb2afb3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:finite of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] Suppose that $\mathbf{q} \in \mathcal{Q}$ satisfies $q_{\ell} > 0$, $q_{h} = 0$, $h \ge \ell + 1$ with some $\ell \ge 2$ and $|\mathbf{q}| \ge 2$. We denote by $k = k(\mathbf{q})$ the second largest element in $\mathbf{q}$, i.e., 
                \begin{align}
                    k := \max\left\{1 \le h \le \ell -1 ; q_{h} > 0 \right\}.
                \end{align}
            Then, for any $i \in {\mathbb{Z}}$, (equation def:step_M of the paper) converges weakly to the Brownian motion with variance $G_{k}\left(\mathbf{q}\right)$ under $\nu_{\mathbf{q}}$, where $G_{k}\left(\mathbf{q}\right)$ is given by 
                \begin{align}
                    G_{k}\left(\mathbf{q}\right) &= \frac{4q_{\ell}}{\left(1 - q_{\ell}\right)^{2(\ell-k)}} \left(1 + \frac{4 q_\ell}{\left(1 - q_{\ell}\right)^{2(\ell-k)}}\right)^{-\frac{3}{2}}.
                \end{align}
            In addition, for any $i \in {\mathbb{Z}}$, the limit $\Lambda^{M{,i}}_{\mathbf{q},k}\left(\lambda\right)$ exists {and does not depend on $i$}. In addition,  $\Lambda^{M}_{\mathbf{q},k}\left(\lambda\right) {:= \Lambda^{M{,0}}_{\mathbf{q},k}\left(\lambda\right)}$ is a smooth monotone convex function, which is explicitly given by 
                \begin{align}
                    \Lambda^{M}_{\mathbf{q},k}\left(\lambda\right) &= \log\left(\frac{\left(1 - q_{\ell}\right)^{\ell-k}e^{\lambda} }{2} + \sqrt{\frac{\left(1 - q_{\ell}\right)^{2( \ell - k)}e^{2\lambda}}{4} + q_{\ell}}\right).
                \end{align}
            In particular, the assumptions of Theorem (thm:main of the paper) ((item:1 of the paper)) and ((item:2 of the paper)) are satisfied with the above $\mathbf{q}$ and $k, \ell$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.650151+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_865ef1c3d8c4fa41602d43447c7b7aa09b9af664584670c19f1db88f62d4434f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm quantitative_discrete_continuous_convergence of arXiv:2411.13964, 'Long-time analysis of a pair of on-lattice and continuous run-and-tumble particles with ja'] \begin{itemize}
