{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.680163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86939da397de6aa37ce9fc8f7490829e9fb85d1016bb534785750c1d60630922","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2607.25986, 'Asymptotics of a two-species particle system associated to the doubly parabolic Keller-Seg'] Let $F: \R_+ \times \R^2 \to \R$ be of class $C^{2}_b(\R_+ \times \R^2)$. For all $u\geq 0$,
\begin{align*}
\E \Big[ \int_0^u F(u-s, R^{1,2}_{u,s}) \dd s \Big ] =& \E \Big[ \int_0^u F(0, R^{1,2}_{s,s})
\dd s \Big ] + \E \Big[\int_0^u \int_0^t (\partial_t F + \Delta F) (t-s,R^{1,2}_{t,s})  \dd s \dd t \Big]\\
&+ \chi \E \Big[\int_0^u \Big(\int_0^t \nabla F (t-s, R_{t,s}^{1,2})  \dd s \Big) \cdot D^{1}_t \dd t \Big].
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:33:06.566440+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8698579efce7502ce1877cb99071a8277dbd201cdb350cd20a0d25392861362c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 41 of arXiv:2608.26068, 'All once-extended 3D TQFTs are Reshetikhin--Turaev theories'] Let $K,\ol{K}$ be ribbon-colourings that extend $\mathbf{K}$, so we have an inclusion $\iota: \mathcal{V}_{K}(\Gamma) \otimes \mathcal{V}_{\ol{K}}(-\Gamma) \rightarrow \mathcal{V}_\mathbf{K}(\Gamma) \otimes \mathcal{V}_\mathbf{K}(-\Gamma)$ of vector spaces.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item If $K=\ol{K}$, the following diagram commutes:
        \begin{equation}
            \begin{tikzcd}
                {\mathcal{V}_{K}(\Gamma) \otimes \mathcal{V}_{K}(-\Gamma)} && {k}\\
                \\
                {\mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{K}_{/T}}(\Gamma/T) \otimes \mathcal{V}_{\mathbf{K}_{/T}}(-\Gamma/T)} && {k}
                \arrow["{\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_\Gamma\circ\iota}", from=1-1, to=1-3]
                \arrow["{(\bigcirc\otimes\bigcirc)\circ\iota}", from=1-1, to=3-1]
                \arrow["{\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{\Gamma/T}}", from=3-1, to=3-3]
                \arrow["{\cdot\dim(K|_T)^{-1}}", from=1-3, to=3-3]
            \end{tikzcd}
        \end{equation}
        \item If $K\ne\ol{K}$, then we instead have $$\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_{\Gamma/T} \circ (\bigcirc\otimes\bigcirc) \circ \iota = \langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle_\Gamma\circ\iota = 0.$$
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.421935+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_869ee5e54ad966f326621d1dc9522c0113ecb210ee02be696ff57131a6a44cdb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma mix line and cycles of arXiv:2607.22156, 'A random matrix approach to lamplighter groups'] Let $C_{1},\cdots,C_{K}$ be test-graphs whose underlying graphs are cycles of length $c_{1},\cdots,c_{K}$ respectively. Let $L_{1},\cdots,L_{M}$ be test-graphs whose underlying graphs are lines of length $l_{1},\cdots,l_{M}$ respectively. We have the following equality,
        \begin{multline}
            \mathbb{E}\left[\prod_{k=1}^{K}\mathrm{Tr}^{0}(C_{k}(V_{N}))\prod_{m=1}^{M}\mathrm{Tr}^{0}(L_{m}(V_{N}))\right]=\\mathbb{N}^{K+M}\mathbb{E}\left[\prod_{k=1}^{K}\frac{c_{k}\eta_{c_{k}}}{N}\prod_{m=1}^{M}\left(1-\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{l_{m}-1}j\eta_{j}}{N}\right)\right]
        \end{multline}
        where $L:=\mathrm{max}\{c_{1},\cdots,c_{K},l_{1},\cdots,l_{M}\}$ and for all $1\leq j\leq L$, let $\eta_{j}$ is the number of cycles of length $j$ of $V_{N}$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:10:43.768221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_869f0b19c93df3f68f9f9634e258f99c317fcebdd696dc010e463a8a057d12fe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma doublestep of arXiv:2412.04284, 'Approximately jumping towards the Origin'] Let $k \equiv -1$ modulo 4. Then if $z_k$ exists and $|z_k|<\sqrt{2}$, we have at least one of the following:
