where \(\mathcal E_l(\lambda,\gamma)\) is given by
\eqref{eqn: derivation_of_boundary}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:37.803073+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86c4d398c55be84b980fad9962214104d8d2225da1e5af1175bb14f134ccbfaa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (\cite{MMO26}) of arXiv:2609.03558, 'Local well-posedness of the higher-order nonlinear Schr\"{o}dinger equation on the half-li'] Suppose $0 \le s < \frac12$, $2 \le \lambda \le \frac{7-2s}{1-2s}$, and
