{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:40:59.364241+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86ca1e5dc13ccf5f278ef2def26a7d841291d3b7a02520985c8802c8fff128c0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 (Weak shifted Jacobi inequality) of arXiv:2609.03958, '2609.03958'] Let $n\geq 2$, $K\geq 0$, $u\in C^4(B_{10})$ and $f\in C^2(B_{10})$ with $D^2u\geq -KI$ and $\inf_{B_{10}}f >0$. If $M=\{(x,u(x)):x\in B_{10}\}\subset\R^{n+1}$ is a smooth 2-convex graph satisfying the scalar curvature equation \eqref{eq:intro-main}, then there exists some constant  $C>0$ depending only on $n$, $K$, $\inf_{B_{10}}f$, $\sup_{B_{10}}f$ and $\|Df\|_{L^{\infty}(B_{10})}$ such that
