{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.076220+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86eb064f472ff286258edb797a85ade560e765a0b2ef69d0bbc616a0478efea1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sineb_corr of arXiv:2509.15446, 'On the pair correlation function of the $\Sineb$ process'] Let $\beta>0$, $\lambda>0$, and consider the unique strong solution $\alpha_{\lambda}(u)$ of the following stochastic differential equation on $(-\infty,0]$:
    \begin{align}

	d\alpha_\lambda = \lambda\tfrac{\beta}{4}e^{\frac{\beta}{4}u} du -\frac{\beta}{2} \sin(\alpha_\lambda(u)) du+ \Re[(e^{-i\alpha_\lambda(u)}-1)dZ], \qquad \lim_{u\to -\infty} \alpha_\lambda(u)=0. 
\end{align}
    The  pair correlation function of the $\operatorname{Sine}_{\beta}$ process is given by
\begin{align}
        \rho_\beta^{(2)}(0,\lambda)=\frac{1}{4\pi^2}+\frac{1}{2\pi^2}\sum_{k=1}^\infty  \frac{(-\beta/2)^{\uparrow k}}{(1+\beta/2)^{\uparrow k}} E[\cos(k \alpha_\lambda(0)].
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:58:24.509952+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86eb304991112b9231cf03a3eba8d9d72eeb9ddd7c30c709e250fe8e761d41b3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn defhaplone of arXiv:2601.09537, 'Gene genealogies in haploid populations evolving according to sweepstakes reproduction'] Suppose a population evolves according to Def.\ (hschwpop of the paper).    Let
