{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.890245+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86fff62f1a6392e6a0124f5811bd235c4858dc77220341365457ad57d8805d0f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:euclidWeyl of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] Let $\alpha\in [0,1]$ and $\beta_\ell=o(\alpha \ell)$ as above. 
If $M=\mathbb{R}^n$, for any $k\in \mathbb{N}$, the error $\delta^{\mathbb{R}^n}_{[\ell-\eta_\ell,\ell]}=\delta^{\mathbb{R}^n}_{[\ell-\eta_\ell,\ell]}(\alpha,\mathcal{C}^k,[0,\rho_\ell])$ in the scaling bound (equation eq:scalimRW of the paper) satisfies
\begin{gather}
\delta_{[\ell-\beta_\ell,\ell]}^{\mathbb{R}^n}

={\mathrm{O}(1)\begin{cases}
    \frac{\beta_\ell}{\ell} & n\ge 3

    \\



    m_\ell \sqrt{\frac{\beta_\ell}{\ell}} 
    & n =2 
    \\

    m_\ell^2& n =1
\end{cases}
}
\\
\delta_{ [\alpha\ell-\beta_\ell,\ell]}^{\mathbb{R}^n}=O\left( \frac{\beta_\ell}{\ell}
\right),\  \text{if $\alpha\in [0,1)$}.
\end{gather}
in bounded range $0\le \rho_\ell \le \mathrm{diam}(M)$, as $\ell\to+\infty$. In particular, if $n\ge 2$, then $\delta_{[\ell-\beta_\ell,\ell]}^{\mathbb{R}^n}=\mathrm{o}(1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.612928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_870205d73ccbf62aee61265f14e93be8491e7d68df1d947ea732c17cc3202f4d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2605.16868, '\ttl'] With definitions \eqref{eq:infliftqueue}--\eqref{eq:infliftlm}, 
the lifted system $\widetilde{Q}_u^N(t)$ can be written as: for $u \in [0,1]$ and $t \ge 0$, 
\begin{equation*}
\widetilde{Q}_u^N(t) = \bar{Q}_u^N(0) + \lambda_u^Nt + \Big(\int_0^1 G^N(v,u)\mu^N_v dv - \mu^N_u \Big) t -  \int_0^1 G^N(v,u)  \mu^N_v \widetilde{I}^N_v  dv  +  \mu^N_u  \widetilde{I}_u^N(t).
\end{equation*}
Equivalently, we write
\begin{equation} \

\widetilde{Q}^N (t) = \widetilde{X}^N (t) + (\mathbf{1}-(\boldsymbol{G}^N)^T) \widetilde{Y}^N (t), 
\end{equation}
where
