{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.283168+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87eec2d62e7dacff47b94b16c00861171af90cd0a7d16b3c4148c07d7760d084","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 (Kernel-perturbation certificate) of arXiv:2608.21496, '2608.21496'] If $f,g\in\cF$ agree under every actual audit kernel, then
\begin{equation}
|\langle\widetilde k,f-g\rangle|
