{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.318510+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87ef61f23b61499cab572be3522452481193953004bec107132b669187ed9b2a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma id-g-fixed-points-vs-ev of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\Phi\colon\ul{{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_\textup{gl}\xrightarrow{\;\smash{\raisebox{-0.25ex}{\ensuremath{\scriptstyle\sim}}}\;}\ul\Spc_\textup{gl}$ be the unique equivalence, and fix any homomorphism $\varphi\colon H\to G$ of compact Lie groups. Then the composite
    \[
        {{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_\textup{$G$-gl}\xrightarrow[\raise2pt\hbox{$\scriptstyle\smash{\sim}$}]{\;\Phi_G\;} \PSh(\textup{Glo}_{/\mathbb B{G}})\xrightarrow{\;\ev_\varphi\;}\Spc
    \]
    is equivalent to
    \begin{equation}
        {{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_\textup{$G$-gl}\xrightarrow{\;\smash{\raisebox{-0.25ex}{\ensuremath{\scriptstyle\sim}}}\;}{{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_\textup{$G$-gl}^\textup{closed}\xrightarrow{\;(-)^\varphi\circ\ev_{{\mathcal{U}}_H}\;}\Spc
    \end{equation}
    for any complete $H$-universe ${\mathcal{U}}_H$.
    \begin{proof}
        Using that $\Phi$ is a global functor, and comparing the functoriality on both sides, it suffices to consider the case where $H=G$ and $\varphi=\textup{id}_H$. In this case, combining Lemmas~(lemma:fixed-point-corep of the paper) and~(lemma:resolve-pt of the paper) shows that $((eq:phixed-points of the paper))$ is corepresented by the terminal object. On the other hand, the terminal object of $\PSh(\textup{Glo}_{/\mathbb B{H}})$ is represented by $\textup{id}_H$, so it corepresents evaluation at $\textup{id}_H$ by the Yoneda lemma. Adjoining over, it will therefore suffice that the left adjoint of $\Phi_H\colon{{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_\text{$H$-gl}\to\PSh(\textup{Glo}_{/\mathbb B{H}})$ preserves the terminal object; but as this left adjoint is again an equivalence, this is clear.
    \end{proof}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.567852+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87f24f14e06665aabb2be888a265f467cdc84ef448d3a5ee536cc4d8cb9a0e2a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:proba of arXiv:2411.12003, 'Central Limit Theorem for non-stationary random products of $\SL(2, \R)$ matrices'] Let the family $\widetilde{\xi}_{a;n}$ satisfy the assumptions~((a:center of the paper))--((a:growth of the paper)). Then there exist constants $C_1,C_{2}$ and a number $n_0$ such that for every $n>n_0$
