{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.828540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_880365d81f0da38f2610b2375bcb774b4040a426ce2134f5b9965971372a2d39","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:ito-sums of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $X:[0,T]\to E$ be a finite-variation pure-jump c\`adl\`ag{} path, constant between jumps, with jumps $z_a=\Delta X_{\tau_a}$ at $0<\tau_1<\cdots<\tau_n\le T$, and let $\mathrm{Sig}^I(X)$ be its forward lift
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Sig}^I_{0,t}=\mathbf 1+\int_{(0,t]}\mathrm{Sig}^I_{0,u^-}\otimes\,\mathrm{d} X_u .
\end{equation}
Then for every word $w=(i_1,\ldots,i_k)$,
\begin{equation}
\inner{\mathrm{Sig}^I(X)_{0,T}}{w}
=\sum_{1\le a_1<\cdots<a_k\le n}z_{a_1}^{i_1}\cdots z_{a_k}^{i_k}
=\inner{\mathrm{Sig}^{\mathrm{sum}}(z)}{w},
\qquad
\mathrm{Sig}^{\mathrm{sum}}(z)=\overrightarrow{\textstyle\prod}_{a=1}^n(\mathbf 1+z_a).

\end{equation}
In particular $\mathrm{Sig}^I(X)$ is a character on the quasi-shuffle Hopf algebra.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.083542+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8804c113bb8c5c71f239d992a334bf9e431866dcb0c878415b9662e3c2edb98f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main1 of arXiv:2504.18739, 'discrete analogues of second-order Riesz transforms'] \begin{itemize}
