{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.434092+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8836ce77339e7f3a14d7df650987775f54a97bcab34b0ed6c8d904da1c441323","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition proposition4.12 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Fix $0<\nu\leq 2^{-15}$, $c_0\leq 2^{-50}B^{-4}$, $d\in\mathbb{N},\alpha\in(0,1)$. Consider $k\leq 2^{-17}B^{-4}\nu\alpha d$ and a sequence of positive real numbers $\mathbf{t}=(t_1,\cdots,t_\ell)$. Consider a tuple of vectors $Y_1,\cdots,Y_{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^d$ satisfying, for some $\alpha\in(0,1)$, $$\operatorname{LCD}_{L,\alpha}^\mathbf{t}(\mathbf{Y})\geq 256B^2\sqrt{\ell},\quad\text{where } L=(\frac{8}{\sqrt{\nu p}}+\frac{256B^2}{\beta})\sqrt{\ell}.$$
   Let $W$ be an $2d\times k$ matrix satisfying $\|W\|_{op}\leq 2$ and $\|W\|_{HS}\geq\sqrt{k}/2$. We also consider two random vectors $\tau\sim\Phi_\nu(2d;\zeta)$ and $\tau'\sim\Xi_{\nu'}(2d;\zeta)$ where $\nu'=2^{-7}\nu$. Let $\beta\in[c_0/2^{10},\sqrt{c_0}]$ and $\beta'\in(0,1/2)$.

    Then we have the following estimate
    \begin{equation}
        \mathcal{L}(W_\mathbf{Y}^T\tau,\beta\sqrt{k+2\ell})\leq (\frac{R}{\alpha})^{2\ell}(\prod_{i=1}^\ell t_i^2)\exp(4\beta^2(k+\ell))\left(\mathbb{P}(\|W^T\tau'\|_2\leq\beta'\sqrt{k})+\exp(-\beta'^2k)\right)^{1/4}
    \end{equation} where we take 
    $R=2^{36}B^2\nu^{-1/2}c_0^{-2}(\frac{8}{\sqrt{\nu p}}+\frac{256B^2}{\beta})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.246632+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88373768fda32bdeb5b3a4c826fc6ef7c17f13b1de50302542f481facf2099db","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:crit of arXiv:2607.01946, 'Second-order fluctuations for a phase transition in random partitions'] If $j_n = \floor{rn^{\alpha/(1+\alpha)}}$ for $r>0$, then
\[
\pp{C_{j_n}(\floor{s_n(t)})}_{t\in{\mathbb R}}\stackrel{a.s.w.}\to ({\mathcal C}_{\alpha,r}(t))_{t\in{\mathbb R}}
\]
in $D({\mathbb R})$ equipped with the local $J_1$ topology, with respect to ${\mathcal P}$, where, conditionally on ${\mathcal P}$, $({\mathcal C}_{\alpha,r}(t))_{t\in{\mathbb R}}$ is a stationary immigration--death process with immigration rate $c_\alpha(r)S_\alpha$ and unit per-particle death rate. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.826307+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88376aa6cc3672976d84c4c77d9ad9c8b3008161bf25412cc4d69d3f61b21a6e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop l2-convergence-from-van-doorn of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $\pi_{n,t}, \nu_n$ be the queue length distribution at time $t$ and the steady state distribution of the continuous-time $M/M/n$ system with arrival rate $\lambda_n$ and unit service rate, respectively. We have
    \begin{align*}
        \chi(\pi_{n,t},\nu_n) \leq e^{-\zeta_n t} \chi(\pi_{n,0},\nu_n) \, \forall t \geq 0
    \end{align*}
    for some positive parameter $\zeta_n$ such that $\zeta_n \geq \min \left\{(\sqrt{n}-\sqrt{\lambda_n})^2, \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{\frac{\lambda_n}{n}}\right\}$. Moreover, when $\lambda_n = n-n^{1-\alpha}$ for $\alpha \in (0, 1/2)$ or when $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{\lambda_n}{n} = c$ for $c \in [0,1)$, we have $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \zeta_n = \frac{1}{2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.331283+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88449d466e023c6e1b0779fb99d65d6879325964f48c10949944bc884b32e385","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:Jintegrals of arXiv:2411.06827, 'The Exponential Lie Series and a Chen--Strichartz Formula for L{\'e}vy Processes'] \begin{equation}

