{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.310408+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8863c39662828864eecab4ba953784e3cfea36dad59a3ba816dfd68a8467441d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:var_lb_stat_rand_meas of arXiv:2411.08848, 'Stationary random measures: Covariance asymptotics, variance bounds and central limit theo'] Let ${\mathcal X}$ be a stationary random measure on $\mathbb{R}^d, d \geq 2$ whose truncated correlation measure ${\bf K}$ has finite total variation and $\widehat{{\bf K}}$ vanishes at $\infty$. Let ${\mathcal X}_L$ be the scaled random measure defined by ${\mathcal X}_L(A) := {\mathcal X}(LA)$,  $L \geq 1$.  Then,  there exists a constant $c >0$ (depending only on $d$) such that for any bounded set $W$ and for all $L \geq 1$,  

\begin{equation}

{\rm Var}\!\left({\mathcal X}_L(W)\right)  \geq c\lambda_D \min \{|W|L^d,  |W|^{\frac{d-1}{d}}L^{d-1}\},
\end{equation}

where $| \cdot |$ denotes the Lebesgue measure. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.788010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88661e0aa74a96bcb9a0e4cd50eb31e9793c2ccc5a74b0e435266c01887bff8e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:converge2 of arXiv:2411.08295, 'Improving the convergence of Markov chains via permutations and projections'] Let $\pi \in \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X}), P \in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$ and $Q \in \mathcal{I}(\pi) \cap \mathcal{L}$ to be an isometric involution transition matrix. Let $\Pi$ be the matrix where each row equals to $\pi$. We have
	\begin{align*}
		D^{\pi}_{KL}(\overline{P} \| \Pi) &\leq  D^{\pi}_{KL}(P  \| \overline{P} ) +  D^{\pi}_{KL}(\overline{P} \| \Pi) = D^{\pi}_{KL}(P \| \Pi),
	\end{align*}
	and the equality holds if and only if $P \in \mathcal{L}(\pi,Q)$ so that $\overline{P}(Q) = P$. 

	Similarly, if $P$ is further assumed to be $\pi$-reversible, then
	\begin{align*}
		c_{KL}(\overline{P}(Q)) &\leq c_{KL}(P).
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.414299+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_886686b640487a01cc64ab0d40aef6578cd7ac45b65e8c1836c7a0cfe2647ceb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: wm around S2:2 of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] For every $\gamma\in (1,2)$, there exists $\bar \varepsilon_\gamma >0$ such that for all $(\lambda,C^2) \in S^0$ with $\tfrac{p-1-\lambda}{p}-  C^2 \leq \bar \varepsilon_\gamma $ we have the estimate
