{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.787559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8870611512e976db4328033847711fc8da9431b8d91de24ba8c081357bff828a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:clustercluster of arXiv:2608.05105, 'Cluster-Cluster model in $\mathbb{Z}^d$'] We define the Cluster-Cluster model
$\rb{\mathfs{A}_t^\alpha}_{t\ge 0}$ with parameter $\alpha \in {\mathbb{R}}$  as follows. 
Suppose at time $0$, we are given a forest $\mathfs{A}_0^\alpha=(\mathfs{V}_0,\mathfs{E}_0)$, containing only finite trees a.s. 

For $t\geq 0$, every cluster $\mathfs{C}$ in the graph $\rb{\mathfs{V}_t,\mathfs{E}_t}$ receives a rate $|\mathfs{C}|^{-\alpha}$ Poisson clock.
When the clock of a cluster $\mathcal{C}$ rings at time $t$, the cluster attempts to perform a random walk move, i.e.~we consider the cluster $\mathcal{C}'=(\mathcal{C}_{V}',\mathcal{C}_{E}')$ with vertex set
\begin{equation*}
    \mathcal{C}_{V}' = \mathcal{C}_{V} + r := \{ v'\in  {\mathbb{Z}}^d \colon  v'=v+r, v\in\mathcal{C}_{V}   \}
\end{equation*}
 and edge set 
\begin{equation*}
    \mathcal{C}_{E}' = \mathcal{C}_{E} + r := \{ e'\in  \mathcal{E}({\mathbb{Z}}^d) \colon  e'=e+r , e\in\mathcal{C}_{E} \} , 
\end{equation*} where $r$ is chosen uniformly at random from the unit vectors $(\pm\textup{e}_i)_{i \in 1,\dots,d}$ in $\mathbb{Z}^d$.
 If the target is vacant, i.e. the cluster $(\mathcal{C}_{V}',\mathcal{C}_{E}')$ satisfies
 \begin{equation}
   \mathcal{C}_{V}' \cap \tilde{\mathcal{C}}_V = \emptyset
 \end{equation} for all clusters $\tilde{\mathcal{C}}=(\tilde{\mathcal{C}}_V,\tilde{\mathcal{C}}_E)\neq \mathcal{C}$ in $\mathfs{A}_{t_-}^\alpha$, then replace $\mathcal{C}$ by $\mathcal{C}'$ in $\mathfs{A}_{t}^\alpha$. Otherwise, let $\mathfs{I}_{V}$ denote the union of all  $\tilde{\mathcal{C}}_V$ so that the intersection in (equation eq:Intersection of the paper) is non-empty, and let
 \begin{equation*}
    \partial C^r := \{ e \in  \mathcal{E}(\mathbb{Z}^d)  \colon e=\{v,w\} , v\in \mathcal{C}_{V} , w \in \mathfs{I}_{V} \}
 \end{equation*}
denote the set of all edges to vertices, blocking the cluster $\mathcal{C}$ from moving in direction $r$. Pick an edge $\tilde{e} \in \partial C^r$ uniformly at random, and add it to $\mathcal{C}$ (this results in merging the cluster $\mathcal{C}$ with another cluster connected to $\mathcal{C}$ via $r$). All remaining clusters are left unchanged.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.255521+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8871fa7ad15c422fc71e434730e85958dd7a91d85952622925ebc383aa7fbbc9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 37 ({\cite[Theorem 10.4) of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] {Kig12}}]
  Suppose that $(F,R)$ is boundedly compact and let $U$ be a non-empty open subset of $F$.
  Then there exists $p_U:(0,\infty)\times F\times F\to[0,\infty)$ which satisfies the following conditions:
  \begin{itemize}
    \item The function $p_U$ is continuous on $(0,\infty)\times F\times F$. Define $p^{t,x}_U(y):=p_U(t,x,y)$. Then $p^{t,x}$ lies in the domain of the Dirichlet form corresponding to $X^U$.
    \item It satisfies $p_U(t,x,y)=p_U(t,y,x)$ for any $(t,x,y)\in (0,\infty)\times F\times F$.
    \item For any Borel measurable function $u$ on $F$ and any $x\in X$, it holds that
    \begin{align*}
      E_x[u(X^U_t)]=\int_{X}p_U(t,x,y)u(y)\mu(dy).
    \end{align*}
    \item For any $t,\;s>0$ and $x,\;y\in X$, it holds that 
    \begin{align}
      p_U(t+s,x,y)=\int_{X}p_U(t,x,z)p_U(s,y,z)\mu(dz).
    \end{align}
  \end{itemize}
  Furthermore, let $A$ be a Borel subset of $X$ which satisfies $0<\mu(A)<\infty$. 
  Then
  \begin{align}
    p_U(t,x,x)\leq \frac{2\sup_{y\in A}R(x,y)}{t}+\frac{\sqrt{2}}{\mu(A)},
  \end{align}
for any $x\in X$ and any $t>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

