{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.345692+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8910c9cc4faba92f38b697679f87ad44ed44565dc5b5a6231aab0aba928b1533","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition covariance of arXiv:2507.08757, 'Strong existence and uniqueness of the tilt-indexed Busemann process in the planar corner '] A measurable function ${\widehat B}:\widehat\Omega\times\mathbb{Z}^2\times\mathbb{Z}^2\to\mathbb{R}$ is 
