{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:01.951635+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89263318b52ebc998e099d9030bbd1174c8dbfa29813811525a4a6b13ceb0651","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition step1 of arXiv:2512.19897, 'On the convoy of the ASEP speed process'] We have 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}_{x}\left[q^{Q_{n+1}}\right] = \sum_{k=0}^{n}c^k\left(q;q\right)_{k+1} \left(q^{-1};q^{-1}\right)_k h_{n-k}\left(1+ca_1,\dots 1+ca_{k+1}\right).
