{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.862340+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_893ad0264984c9716a7dc8fc61d550cc5512cf49ed1a0ffbc1f5bcd5726b90de","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lower-bound-prob-2 of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Assume Assumption~(ass:non-persistence of the paper) is satisfied, with $C' > 0$ satisfying Item~(item:non-persistence-two of the paper) of Assumption~(ass:non-persistence of the paper). Suppose that $(X_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$ and $(X'_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$ are independent sequences of random variables, with $X_{i} \sim X'_{i}$. Suppose, moreover, that $n, \phi_{n} \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$ are given such that
