{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.350405+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8958b892f5a9b80883bf5190fb63f668f6e90512b610b6dca619f29c0bcc8c2c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 6 of arXiv:2506.15736, 'Coming down from infinity for coordinated particle systems'] For a coordinated particle system that has $b$ particles at site $u \in V$, the rates at which $k$ of these particles coalesce, die, migrate to site $v \in V$, or reproduce at site $v \in V$ are

    \begin{align*}
        \lambda_{b,k}^{(v)} &= \int_{0}^1 z^k(1-z)^{b-k} \frac{\Lambda_v(dz)}{z^2},\\
        d_{b,k}^{(v)} &= \int_{0}^1 z^k(1-z)^{b-k} \frac{D_v(dz)}{z},\\
        m_{b,k}^{(u,v)} &= \int_{0}^1 z^k(1-z)^{b-k} \frac{M_{uv}(dz)}{z},\\
        r_{b,k}^{(u,v)} &= \int_{0}^1 z^k(1-z)^{b-k} \frac{R_{uv}(dz)}{z},
    \end{align*}

    \noindent respectively. Similarly we can write the total rate of mergers at site $v \in V$ when there are $b$ particles present as

    \begin{align*}
        \lambda_b^{(v)} = \sum_{k = 2}^b \binom{b}{k} \lambda_{b,k}^{(v)}.
    \end{align*}

    \noindent Similar formulas hold for the total rates of death, migration, and reproduction and we shall denote these quantities $d_b^{(v)}, m_{b}^{(u,v)},$ and $r_{b}^{(u,v)}$ respectively. Note we may drop the superscript denoting the site if $|V| = 1$ or the site is clear from context.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.861936+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_895bed539f83b0fec3f2ab7addf2a2cc69b4bbc343713640c4170499eb249a42","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2605.21424, 'A dice game, a multinomial walk, and the inverted Dirichlet distribution'] Let \(m\ge 2\) be an integer, \(n_1,\ldots,n_m\in \N_{\ge 1}\) and 
