{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.010548+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89792c1a5a71659f622b0e7b4bd68a80c4d652ff71e739513075dd24fb779bcc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2607.13308, 'No infinite clusters at criticality for two-dimensional dependent percolation under abstra'] Given $\varepsilon>0$< there exists $\uc{c:approximation_environment}>0$ such that, for every $\lambda \in \R$, $r \geq 2$, and $x \in \Z^{2}$,
