{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.594888+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_897a73771abb6863f2d176079d03ad32bb5892aed3bebdcffdb49ecb63e7bb57","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma uux u M of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] Let $d\ge1$, $s>\frac{d}{2}+1$. Then there exists a constant $\mathscr{c}=\mathscr{c}_{s,d}>0$ such that
