{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.354466+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89823fe2425a277d647c843f443bdb22c34345b7485f4b190fa83350d4caa4a6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2506.16260, 'Fractional Compound Poisson Random Fields on Plane'] The density $g_\alpha(x,t_1,t_2)=\mathrm{Pr}\{H_\alpha(t_1,t_2)\in\mathrm{d}x\}/\mathrm{d}x$, $x\ge0$, $(t_1,t_2)\in\mathbb{R}^2_+$ solves the following fractional differential equation:
