        \mathbb E \left[\sup_{t \leq T}\,(X_t)^2 \right] \leq C\,\left(1 + \int_0^T\,\left|R_{-C\bar K(T) K}(s) \right|\,ds \right)\,,
    \end{equation}
    where $\bar K := \int_0^{\cdot}\,K(s)\,ds\,$, and $R_{-c\bar K(T) K}$ is the resolvent of the second kind of $t \mapsto -C\bar K(T)\,K(t)$ (see Appendix (app:resolvents of the paper)).

    Moreover, for $s \leq t \leq T\,$, we have 
