	then $R^{(N)}_{G} \to 0$ uniformly in $\mathbb{R}$ as $N \to +\infty$.

	Further, if the stronger assumption (equation E: decay two of the paper) holds,  and if $R^{(N)}_{G}$ is instead defined by
		\begin{align*}
			( \mathscr{L}^{(N)} G_{N^{-\frac{1}{3}}} )( N^{\frac{1}{3}} x ) = N^{- \frac{2}{3} } \sigma | \partial_{x} G ( x ) |^{2} + N^{ -1 } a | \partial_{x} G ( x ) | \partial_{x}^{2} G ( x ) + N^{ -1 } R_{G}^{(N)}(x),
