{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.305556+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89b915ea854da59a001528fc268d80f9777a7e8883dcb5e67ba7468388c9b1cb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:good_scales_merging_multiple of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Suppose that $h$ is a GFF on $D$ with some bounded boundary values. For any $b>0$ and $q \in (0,1)$ there exist $M,p>0$ so that the following is true. 
