{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.787159+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89b9d1bfa2ad28ad1286ff09bdac2e00f5c42d51f6405c37ba9f82c49c6761be","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:projectFrob of arXiv:2411.08295, 'Improving the convergence of Markov chains via permutations and projections'] Let $M \in \mathcal{M}$, $Q \in \mathcal{I}(\pi) \cap \mathcal{L}$ and $N \in \mathcal{M}(\pi,Q)$. We have
