{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.039293+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89e63c6402c575d4c9eb9ccab8379c57a1199a1d48f57459520dcf34ceffe15e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2-l13 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Fix a finite subset $D$ of ${\mathbb Z}^d$. Then, there exists a finite
constant $C_0$, depending only on $D$ and the bounds (equation 2-38b of the paper),
