{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.242551+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89f3c7377ac80f6720665b97f9a751c13de504ef6884991c47e7cc46bd650189","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2604.15152, 'The Multinomial Allocation Model and the Random Box Load'] For $0\le r,t\le n$ and $r\ne t$,  the following three approximation formulas hold
\begin{align}
\rE[\hat q_r]&=\rE[p_{r}(\xi)]+(2n)^{-1}\rE[p_{r}(\xi)(r-(\xi-r)^2)]+n^{-2}R_1(n,r), \\
