{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.900710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89f54f508314b14ad717fe0864f3ad9393984caafe9c48db3d4a71328823552e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2608.02319, 'Averaging Principle for Ordinary Differential Equations in a Multiscale Random Environment'] For all $n,k\geq1$, $0<S<T$, $x\in E$ and $y\in\mathbb R^d$ we set
