{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.514292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89fa522e24f99a617e2eb0242ba5b6b1ce54a08bc48092e8d519dadf13d481ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor of arXiv:2411.11759, 'Milstein-type schemes for McKean--Vlasov SDEs driven by Brownian motion and Poisson random'] Let Assumptions \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:ic of the paper)} to \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:convergence2 of the paper)} be satisfied  with  $\bar p\geq (\eta+1)\max\{4(\varepsilon+2)/\varepsilon,(\eta+2)(\varepsilon+2)/\varepsilon,4(\eta+1)\}$  where $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$. Then, there exists a $K>0$, independent of $n$ and $N$, such that
