{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.258653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a2969b059db1761eddd0f3de67aa79c1e2d585f7c68edd7a5738de055fd4ba9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:7 of arXiv:2410.23250, 'Strict inequalities for arm exponents in planar percolation'] For every $\delta\in(0,1/1000)$ there exists $C(\delta)\in (0,\infty)$  such that
