{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.461151+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a600470b873c4cf0616691c5aaaca7ed593bc094e1199de5538294109d55a9f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:trees of arXiv:2609.02234, 'An $n(\log n)^{o(1)}$ bound for nested cycles without geometric crossings'] For every $i\in[q]$ and $\xi\in\{-,+\}$, there is a complete $b$-ary tree $T_i^\xi$ of depth $h$ rooted at $r_i^\xi$ such that
