Here $\Delta_{0} := \Delta_{g_0}$, $J_0 := J_{g_0}$ and $A_0 := A_{g_0}$. Then there exists a conformal metric $\tilde{g}\in[g]$ with positive scalar curvature $\tilde{R} > 0$ and positive $Q$-curvature $\tilde{Q} > 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.417630+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8aa403a7fb4ba6f8e3da8c75f1e0296e18e3942de980a493c9d2944ed3a2b809","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 of arXiv:2605.16560, 'Seasonal Statistics of Shannon Rate in a Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Cellular Network'] Suppose $k\geq 1$. For any point $(s,h)\in \cup_{i\in \N}C_i$ that lies on $\Lcal^{(k)}_e$:

