{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.638035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ab4b24924da4f7244683a14b8edbca4af338228989f557593e55a3be137ff44","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2605.23461, 'An almost sure invariance principle for the Takagi--van der Waerden class functions'] Suppose that \eqref{Assump2:A_n_to_infinite} and \eqref{Assump2:last_term} hold. Then, there exists a probability space $(\onetorus \times [0,1), \Borelsigma(\onetorus)\otimes \Borelsigma([0,1)), \nu)$ on which a random variable $U$ uniformly distributed over $\onetorus$ and a standard Brownian motion $\{B(t)\colon t\ge 0\}$ are defined such that
