with $\Phi$ associated to $\varphi$ as in (equation eq:Phidef of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.728711+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b1238026b2276b29a58b79d939ee33c64677a4b645851b7c47df756628477e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm moment of arXiv:2503.22334, 'Probabilistic analysis of optimal multi-pivot QuickSort'] Let $K\in {\mathbb N}$. For the number $X_n$ of key comparisons using optimal $K$-pivot QuickSort we have 
  \begin{equation}
    {\mathbb E}\left[X_n\right] = \alpha_K n\ln n + \beta_K n + o(n) \quad (n\to\infty),
  \end{equation}
with a constant $\beta_K \in \mathbb{R}$ and $\alpha_K= \gamma_K/(H_{K+1}-1)$, where $H_n := \sum_{i=1}^n \frac1i$ are the harmonic numbers. In the case of $K≤4$, the error term $o(n)$ can be replaced by $\mathrm{O}(\log n)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.100226+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b174b9e519b9f864fcf5186b66dfeecca9b081c6ede08e6b74644958c5c1c25","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LM21 of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] Let $({\mathscr E},{\mathscr F})$ and $({\mathscr E}',{\mathscr F}')$ be two Dirichlet forms on $L^2(E,m)$,  whose associated semigroups (as described in [MR92]) are denoted by $(T_t)_{t\geq 0}$ and $(T'_t)_{t\geq 0}$,  respectively.  The following assertions are equivalent:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(1)] $T'_t f\leq T_tf$ for all $t\geq 0$ and all non-negative $f\in L^2(E,m)$. 
\item[(2)] ${\mathscr F}'\subset {\mathscr F}$,  $\mathrm{b}{\mathscr F}':={\mathscr F}'\cap L^\infty(E,m)$ is an algebraic ideal in $\mathrm{b}{\mathscr F}$,  and 
\begin{equation}
	{\mathscr E}'(f,g)\geq {\mathscr E}(f,g)
\end{equation}
for all non-negative $f,g\in {\mathscr F}'$.  
\item[(3)] ${\mathscr F}'\subset {\mathscr F}$,  ${\mathscr F}'$ is an order ideal in ${\mathscr F}$,  and (equation eq:21 of the paper) holds for all non-negative $f,g\in {\mathscr F}'$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.387249+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b176e60771a1f401a69877cc7da4d122e1cfacf62dd354ae4e4c0b9cd56a971","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop x(s) of arXiv:2411.02156, 'Martin boundary of a degenerate Reflected Brownian Motion in a wedge'] The parabola~$\mathcal{P}$ (see~(equation paraboleP of the paper)) admits the following parameterisation:
