{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.728132+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b230d7a755201d9c8e58d93d114979d8b4103227c9ce0c7bca737b72b59e3c6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-entropy-estimate of arXiv:2411.04500, '\LARGE Probabilistic Approaches to The Energy Equality in Forced Surface Quasi-Geostrophic'] For every $\theta\in \mathcal{C}_0$ with $ \mathcal{I}(\theta)< \infty $, let $ g\in L^2([0,T];H)$ be the control such that $ \theta $ solves (equation PDE-SQG of the paper) weakly.
