{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.707476+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b2d74bc9f7b91c9e4bef5b88614321e5f3dbad51f6fb83a16d756460f4101c6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:infvol2pt of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Let $d \ge 4$,  $\eta \in [0,1/2)$,  $L$ be sufficiently large and $g>0$ be sufficiently small.
Then there exists $\nu_c  \equiv \nu_c (g) = O(g)$ such that
\begin{align}
	\lim_{N\rightarrow \infty} \langle \varphi_{\sf o}^{(1)} \varphi_{\sf x}^{(1)} \rangle_{g,\nu_c,  N} =: \langle \varphi_{\sf o}^{(1)} \varphi_{\sf x}^{(1)} \rangle_{g,\nu_c,  \Z^d} =: \C_{\sf x}
\end{align}
exists and satisfies 
\begin{align}
	\C_{\sf x} \sim c_1 |{\sf x}|^{-(d-2+\eta)} \quad \text{as} \quad |{\sf x}| \rightarrow \infty 
\end{align}
for some constant $c_1$ such that $c_1 = \gamma(d,\eta) + O(g)$ when $\eta = 0$ and $c_1 = \gamma(d,\eta)$ when $\eta \neq 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:53:39.212146+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b2f544308c0d4175ba2b0388a077c3216b6e541c0f872adb9fe217f2c99c4fe","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 8 of arXiv:2608.27022, 'On LCK Geometry of Gauduchon Connections'] Let $(M, J, \omega)$ be an lck manifold and assume $\omega$ is Gauduchon satisfying the second Bismut--Einstein equation
