{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.471577+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b43459c43f95c1879d01820ad33f2a1ec39187d918b3edf92959ae6473e3094","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 102 (Modified versions of the derivatives of $\mytr_{\gtorus} \upchi$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] The \emph{fully modified quantity} $\fullymodquant{\tander^N}$ is defined to be: 
