{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.450097+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b476686fdf36ccee5897d33927a544199bda0f8aa53df0f145d9753cc6382fb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:coexistence-ratio of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:coexistence}
Fix \(p\ge3\), \(\sigma>1\), and let \(\mu_{p,\sigma}\) be the law from
(thm:counterexample of the paper).  For every fixed \(L,\varepsilon>0\),
