{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.573388+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b536a0fbf12d7900f5b4d0b354bcb2c55c06d3f0312299640d98060dce4d545","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 27 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 4$. There exists $C>0$ such that the following holds. For every $n\geq 1$, there exists $S\subset \Lambda_n$ containing $0$ which satisfies the following properties:
\begin{enumerate}
	\item[$(i)$] $\varphi_{\beta_c}(S)\leq C(\log n)^{\mathds{1}_{d=4}}$;
	\item[$(ii)$] one has
	\begin{equation}
		\beta_c \sum_{\substack{x\in S\cap \Lambda_{n/2}\\y\notin S\\x\sim y}}\langle \sigma_0\sigma_x\rangle_{S,\beta_c}\langle\sigma_0\sigma_y\rangle_{\beta_c}\leq C\frac{(\log n)^{\mathds{1}_{d=4}}}{n^{d-2}}.
	\end{equation} 
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.762928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b565ccd930bcfcc6b8bcda8a0c76d2ebafecdbeb0b18cf141db3f2d2e68492a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:RFGbound of arXiv:2604.28068, 'Mean-square Stability and Bifurcations for Dissipative SDEs'] Suppose Assumptions~(assum:FG_bounds of the paper) and (ass:dissipative of the paper) hold and let $Y$ be the solution of (equation eq:main_YSDE of the paper).
