{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:19.042837+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b57e206bea03fb32851c090650344a16323e2df4cc9e342aaf11cd9d2c8b54c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm-I of arXiv:2609.02552, 'Resolvent Estimates for the Stokes Operator \\ in a Three-Dimensional Lipschitz Domain'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain in $\mathbb{R}^d, d\ge 2$.
Let $T$ be a bounded linear operator from $L^2_\sigma(\Omega)$ to $L^2(\Omega; \mathbb{C}^d)$.
Suppose that 
\begin{equation}
\aligned
\| Tu \|_{L^2(\Omega)} &  \le M_2 \| u \|_{L^2(\Omega)}  & \quad & \text{ for } u \in L^2_\sigma(\Omega),\\
\| Tu \|_{L^\infty(\Omega)} & \le M_\infty  \| u \|_{L^\infty(\Omega)}  & \quad & \text{ for   } u \in C^\infty_{0, \sigma}(\Omega).
\endaligned
\end{equation}
Then $T$ is bounded from $L^p_\sigma(\Omega)$ to $L^p(\Omega; \mathbb{R}^d)$ for  any $2< p\le  \infty$, and 
\begin{equation}
\| Tu \|_{L^p(\Omega)} \le C_p M_2^\theta M_\infty^{1-\theta}  \| u \|_{L^p(\Omega)}
\end{equation}
for any $u\in L^p_\sigma (\Omega)$, 
where $\theta=\frac{2}{p}$ and $C_p$ depends only on $p$ and $\Omega$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:04:39.222809+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b59111038045b96a6befbb31588c2514419de0b2061c0bc7d9e900643fc6cc8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 32 of arXiv:2608.13976, 'Boundary Harnack principle for diffusion with jumps on metric measure spaces'] For each $R>0,$
