{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.228233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ba49061003a4252f5d6f63aa6bd70839ae750aba8319c2e78ca3937f85d9fea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma critical-case-lower-bound of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] There exist constants $r, C_2 >0$ such that for all $t$ large enough and $z\geq -\frac{1}{2} \log t $, 
