{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:53.202592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8bb1c0b8fef86d604884875850b8afff158886ef73c450c31504f63bc4a50cf8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (Blocking Measure) of arXiv:2606.12670, 'The censored stochastic six-vertex model and parabolic Kazhdan--Lusztig $R$-polynomials'] Let 
\begin{equation} 
    A = \{\eta\colon\Z\to\{0,1\}: \sum_{x = -\infty}^0 \eta(x) = \sum_{x = 1}^{\infty}(1- \eta(x))<\infty\}
\end{equation} denote the set of all possible configurations that can be obtained if we start with the initial condition $\eta(x) = 1_{x > 0}$ and perform a finite number of moves. Further let $$\hat{\pi} = \otimes_{x \in \Z} \text{Ber}\left(\frac{q^{-x}}{1 + q^{-x}}\right).$$
We then define the blocking measure $\pi$ to be the projection of the measure $\hat{\pi}$ to the set $A$, i.e., $\pi(\cdot)=\hat{\pi}(\cdot|A)$.\footnote{We have an explicit formula for $  \hat \pi(A)$ (see e.g. \cite{MR3765898}):
$\hat \pi(A) = \frac{1}{ \sum_{l = -\infty}^{\infty} q^{l(l+1)/2}}.
$}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.729008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8bb1cc4050fdbb95945d9bb5bb85fefc0e91c26ccd81dda4750a0b528194698c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop lem:triangular of arXiv:2606.08325, 'Digit Mixing under Polynomial Maps'] Fix an integer \(q\ge1\) and a real number \(0<\rho<1/2\). There exist constants $c=c(q,\rho)>0$ and $C=C(q,\rho)<\infty$ with the following property.
			Let \(A(k_1,\ldots,k_q)\), \(1\le k_1,\ldots,k_q\le L\), be real coefficients satisfying
			\begin{align}
				&\left\|A(k,k,\ldots,k)\right\|\ge\rho \qquad(1\le k\le L) , \\
				\text{and} \quad &A(k_1,\ldots,k_q)=0
				\quad\text{if}\quad (k_1,\ldots,k_{q-1})\succ(k_q,\ldots,k_q).

			\end{align}
				Let \(U_{j,k}\) be as in Lemma~(lem:GCS of the paper). Then
