{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.632438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8bce2e810f1c332ae0d0847fc158b2bb785c800350c945ba3d3e8822dbb4b8ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 16 (Corollary $6.6$ in \cite{HeyLod25}) of arXiv:2505.06187, 'Preferential Attachment Trees with Vertex Death: Persistence of the Maximum Degree'] Suppose that $b$ and $d$ are such that Assumptions~\eqref{ass:A1} and \eqref{ass:C1} are satisfied, and let $\cS\coloneq \{\lim_{t\to\infty}|\bp(t)|=\infty\}$ be the event that the process $\mathrm{BP}$ survives. Then,  
