{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.197576+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c09757b8ac6508f0e71104384dc661697b03fcb159a01c55408195ecd23ba7b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 42 (\hspace{-0.05em}{\cite[Lemma~5.3) of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] {mark2022cutoff}}]
    Let $A$ be a random subset of a finite set $\mathcal A$ and let $\mathcal F$ be a $\sigma$-algebra. Let $A'$ be an independent copy of $A$ and let $A_{\mathcal F}$ and $A_{\mathcal F}'$ be conditionally independent copies of $A$ given $\mathcal F$. Then
