{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.608662+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c0a2d1523b89745ed61b1c261cd2667aedba390298508253dd6e66d58882b5b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2608.25772, 'Propagation of Chaos and Gaussian Fluctuations for Mean-field Coupled Maps'] Fix $T\in\N$. Under the assumptions \textup{\textbf{(A1.2)}} and \textup{\textbf{(A2)}}, there exists $\Delta_0>0$, such that if $\Delta<\Delta_0$, then it holds that
