{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.498734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c1078c691de1db0803fdf7ce2c14282ad5376efe197701f32349d4f7cbb9131","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 (Weighted Volterra decomposition identity) of arXiv:2605.09706, 'A dyadic construction of a three-dimensional attractive point interaction Markov family'] Let \(s,t>0\), \(a,b\ge 0\), and \(\lambda>0\). Then
\begin{align}
\int_0^\infty e^{\lambda v}
\int_0^v
P_s(v+a-u)\,P_t(u+b)\,du\,dv
&=
\int_0^\infty e^{\lambda v}
\int_0^\infty
P_s(a+r)\,P_t(v+r+b)\,dr\,dv \nonumber \\
&+
\int_0^\infty e^{\lambda u}
\int_0^\infty
P_s(u+a+r)\,P_t(r+b)\,dr\,du \nonumber \\
&+
2\lambda
\int_0^\infty\int_0^\infty
e^{\lambda(u+v)}
\int_0^\infty
P_s(u+a+r)\,P_t(v+r+b)\,dr\,du\,dv. \nonumber
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.985175+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c10b08c68bdc127da88fd9cbfe623adb284f0a09ab86e3401c31b20b8e6ca95","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 (Convolution-induced Grassmann map) of arXiv:2609.03361, 'Grassmann--Pl\"ucker Parametrization of Convolutional Filter Subspaces:\ Regularity and Cl'] Define
\begin{equation}
  \Gamma_{\cC}:\Gr(q,\cK)\longrightarrow\Gr(q,H),
