{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.752038+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c1f2aee9186b6d96a617e24657f3951380f7ba91053f46f7ac67030d211b911","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:equiv_MP_weak of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $s\in [0,T)$, $\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, and let $\mathbb{P}$ be a probability measure on $(C_{[s,T)}, \mathcal{B} )$, such that
