{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.705212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c2f5bf047b58b089bf8a46b79275e635e7e26596f1e9fdd88f203624a3ca2cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemZhaoBound of arXiv:2411.18563, 'Lower tails for triangles inside the critical window'] For $0 \le \eta< \eta_\ell $, 
   \begin{equation}
       \lim_{c \to \infty} \frac{\Phi_{n,c/\sqrt{n}}(\eta)}{c n^{3/2}} < -\frac{1}{2} h \left ( \eta^{1/3} \right)  \,, 
   \end{equation}
   where $\eta_\ell \approx .0091$ is given explicitly in~[zhao2017lower] as the maximum of a single variable function on the unit interval. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.846446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c329b18ebb500e7dbfac8bd9f1267410793cf4d013c03d7dd5ff191710c2c2b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Tightness of arXiv:2607.08187, 'Asymptotic behaviours of critical branching random walk in $\mathbb{R}^d$'] For any $A>0$, it holds that 
