{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.959357+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c3536e5cfbfc5e75e82d31a281bd09fa238be30d4d5c63559ef3579ee38d214","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.12070, 'Central limit theorems for a heavy-tailed subcritical Galton-Watson process with state-dep'] Suppose   the process $\mathbf{X}=\{X_n:n\geq0\}$  is defined by \eqref{111} and satisfies {\bf (A)}. Then as $n\to \infty$,  
