{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.297102+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c38747bba020a4df20a85ec32d0795a18b2124ae1a9e54a0802b929efcd2b11","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:trunc of arXiv:2605.20587, 'Persistence and entropic repulsion of stationary Gaussian fields with spectral singularity'] Let $\mu = \mu_1 + \mu_2$, let $f'$ be an SGF with spectral measure $\mu_1 + \phi_s^2 \mu_2$. Then for every $0 < s <T$ and $\ell \in \mathbb{R}$,
\[  \mathbb{P} \Big[ \inf_{x \in B(T)} f(x) \ge \ell \Big]  \le  \mathbb{P} \Big[ \inf_{x \in B(T-s)} f'(x) \ge \ell  \Big] .\]
 Moreover, if $\eta \in \mathcal{M}$, then for every $0 < s <T$, $\ell,\ell' \in \mathbb{R}$, and $\delta > 0$,
\begin{align*}
& \mathbb{P} \Big[\inf_{x \in B(T)} f(x) \ge \ell , \langle 
 f,\eta \rangle \ge \ell' \Big] \\
& \qquad \le  \mathbb{P} \Big[ \inf_{x \in B(T-s)} f'(x) \ge \ell , \langle f',\eta \rangle \ge \ell' -\delta \big]  + \mathbb{P} \big[ \sup_{u \in B(s/2)} | \langle f, \eta - \eta_u \rangle | \ge \delta  \Big],
\end{align*}
where $\eta_u(\cdot) = \eta(\cdot - u)$ is the translation of $\eta$. The same result holds in the discrete case after replacing $\phi_s$ with $\tilde{\phi}_s$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.121641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c39523acc92a9b5a62eeb12689239778eb6b67151f9b7ce8f42c2f919fccb81","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:elementary-expansion of arXiv:2608.18293, 'Critical tensor covariance at the Marchenko--Pastur threshold'] For $a_n=d/n$,
