{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.042346+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c8b70852af638bc08406e570ae56103cabc2976637714c25e104a838361a22f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma talagrand-bousquet of arXiv:2608.12056, 'Deviation inequalities for U-processes of growing order, with applications to half-space d'] [boucheron2013concentration]
Let $\mathcal F$ be a class of measurable real-valued functions and let $X_1,\ldots,X_N$ be i.i.d. Assume that $\mathbb{E}f(X_1)=0$ for all $f\in \mathcal F$ and that $\sup_{f\in \mathcal F} |f(X_1)|\leq U$ with probability $1$. Denote $Z=\sup _{f \in \mathcal{F}} \sum_{k=1}^N f\left(X_k\right)$.
