{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.768227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d29a203bb3ccdd06407e659536d8f69624bae4319f767428de8f94e68d104e2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 51 of arXiv:2512.04807, 'Existence and uniqueness of the canonical Brownian motion in non-simple conformal loop ens'] Almost surely, there exists a countable set $\{z_m\}_{m \in \N} \subseteq \Upsilon_\Gamma$ that is dense with respect to $\dpathY$ and such that the following holds. Suppose that $V \in \metregions$ is separated from $\Upsilon_\Gamma \setminus \ol{V}$ by a finite set of points $Z$ contained in $\{z_m\}_{m \in \N}$. Then the following holds for sufficiently large $m \in \N$. Let $A = \{z_1,\ldots,z_m\}$ and $A_V = A \cap \ol{V}$, let $w$ (resp.\ $w_V$) be the weight function associated with $\rmet{\cdot}{\cdot}{\Gamma}|_{A}$ (resp.\ $\rmetres{V}{\cdot}{\cdot}{\Gamma}|_{A_V}$). Then
 \begin{itemize}
  \item $w(x,y) = w_V(x,y)$ for each $x,y \in A_V$,
  \item $w(x,y) = 0$ for each $x \in A_V \setminus Z$, $y \in A \setminus \ol{V}$,
  \item $w(x,y) = 0$ for $x,y \in Z$.
 \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.013320+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d2af40891e4ceffc86f7794b4892b6a424a420b9cd0c51be855ff6f4f734879","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 24 (Comparison theorems) of arXiv:2605.04359, 'Well-posedness of reflected BSDEs with default time and irregular barrier: An application '] Assume that:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item $\xi^1 \leq \xi^2$.
		\item $
		f^1\left(t, Y_t^2, Z_t^2,U^2_t\right) \leq f^2\left(t, Y_t^2, Z_t^2,U^2_t\right),~t \in [0,T],~d\mathbb{P}\otimes dt\text{-a.e.}
		$
	\end{itemize}
	Then, we have
	\begin{itemize}
		\item[(i)] Comparison theorem: $Y^1_t \leq Y^2_t$, $\forall t \in [0,T]$ a.s.
		\item[(ii)] Strict comparison theorem: Suppose moreover, that $\psi>-1$ a.s., and $Y^1_{t_0}=Y^2_{t_0}$ a.s. for some $t_0 \in [0,T]$. Then $\xi_1=\xi_2$ a.s., and $Y^1=Y^2$ on $[t_0,T]$. 
	\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.258401+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d2b903c2e19fa2947e7bfb16b5f9ebb80fd0d1374fd5f4c872f7a6d018282f7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sion of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] {sion1958general}}]
  Let $\mathcal{X}$ be a convex subset of a linear topological space and $\mathcal{Y}$ a convex subset of a linear topological space, where at least one of $\mathcal{X}$ and $\mathcal{Y}$ is compact.  If $f:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}\to\mathbb{R}$ satisfies
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item $\forall x\in \mathcal{X}$, $f(x,\cdot)$ is upper semicontinuous and quasi-concave on $\mathcal{Y}$, and
  \item $\forall y\in \mathcal{Y}$, $f(\cdot,y)$ is lower semicontinuous and quasi-convex on $\mathcal{X}$,
  \end{enumerate}
  then $\min_{x\in \mathcal{X}}\sup_{y\in \mathcal{Y}} f(x,y)=\sup_{y\in \mathcal{Y}}\min_{x\in \mathcal{X}}f(x,y)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.720730+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d2cc311d07c9a81d8f65d5af20d399454afbb92b8ca4c19489a352c53cc56ed","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 24 of arXiv:2511.13404, 'Asymptotic stability and mean ergodicity of Feller processes on Polish spaces'] Let $\mathfrak{F}\subset B(\X)$ be such that $L_b(\X)\subset \mathfrak{F}$ and satisfy Hypothesis $\mathbf{(H_1)}$. Suppose that $\Phi$ is equicontinuous w.r.t $\mathfrak{F}$ on $\X$, then the following statements are equivalent:
		\begin{itemize}
			\item [(\runum{1})] $\Phi$ is asymptotically stable w.r.t $\mathfrak{F}$ with unique invariant measure $\mu$.
			\item[(\runum{2})]  There exists $z\in\X$ such that $\Phi$ satisfies the lower bound condition \eqref{eq:LBC_P} at $z$.
		\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.667899+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d2ed9891c18eb2142ee6b958016ff35c730ef5d99959b4422a28b8b9869de13","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_restriction_of_measure_good_approx of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] Suppose $\alpha_{0} \neq 0$, and fix $\varepsilon < \frac{\alpha_{0}}{2}$. Let $R>\max\{R_{\overline{\mathbb{Z}}}(\varepsilon),R_{\mu_0}(\varepsilon)\}$, $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $w \in \Omega_n^{(0)}(\mu,2^{-R}\varepsilon)$. Then,
\begin{equation*}
