{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.700890+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d48ac338bd3141a223faf1f528c8318a3ac393f54ce97151c583954e5445c95","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop basis of arXiv:2609.00672, 'Deciding superellipticity and computing the Weierstrass normal form'] The differential $\omega_{a,b}$ is holomorphic on $C$ if and only if $(a,b)\in A$, where

\begin{equation}
