{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.424472+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d7ae922ac313854f12310089812e2972dcc4649f7843543f69858fd4f733319","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary thm.mtg1 of arXiv:2605.17725, 'Limit theorems for random walks with spatio-temporal drift'] Let $(M_n)$ be an $\mathbb{R}^d$-valued martingale converging almost surely and in $L^2$ to $M_\infty$.
    Define $\Delta_n = M_n - M_{n-1}$ and 
