{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.294975+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d7ca4196d39062d4ec16c25d50a2868125e1e493d009087f643f52d90408c02","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Buse_from_geod of arXiv:2605.22787, 'Invariant measures for half-space geometric LPP: classification and the one force--one sol'] Let $\gamma$ be any semi-infinite geodesic rooted at $\gamma(0) = (m,n) \in \mathbb{Z}^2_{\mathrm{HS}}$ and such  that $\gamma(-k)\cdot \mathbf e_1 \to -\infty$ as $k \to \infty$. Then, for every $\mathbf x \le \mathbf \gamma(0)$ in $\mathbb{Z}^2_{\mathrm{HS}}$, the limit
	\begin{equation} 
	b(\mathbf x) := \lim_{k \to \infty} G(\gamma(-k),\mathbf x) - G(\gamma(-k),\gamma(0))
	\end{equation}
	exists. Furthermore, for any $j \in \mathbb{Z}_{\le n}$,
	\begin{equation} 
	\begin{aligned}
		&b(\gamma(0)) = 0  = \max_{i \in \llbracket j,m \rrbracket} [b(i,j-1) + G\bigl((i,j),(m,n)\bigr)],  \quad\text{and}\\
		&i_j^\star := \max\{i \in \mathbb{Z}: \gamma(-k) = (i,j-1) \text{ for some } k \in \mathbb{N} \} \in \argmax_{i \in \llbracket j,m \rrbracket}[b(i,j-1) + G\bigl((i,j),(m,n)\bigr)].
	\end{aligned}
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.590197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d7e238a25e425de5a69c09eff2fec2a9990482d24588b4ff9c82c6eddff0c93","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Satz: Kov.matrix Laengen Potenz Funktional of arXiv:2509.15790, 'Covariance matrices of volume power functionals of random simplicial complexes -- an asymp'] [[AkinwandeReitzner]]

Let $(k_1, \alpha_1), \ldots ,(k_n, \alpha_n)$ be an admissible sequence. The random vector $(\tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{k_1}^{(\alpha_1)}, \ldots, \tilde{\mathcal{V}}_{k_n}^{(\alpha_n)}) $ has the asymptotic covariance matrix 
\begin{align} 
\Sigma_n := \begin{cases}  
A_0^{<1} &\text{ for } \, \lim\limits_{t \rightarrow \infty} t\delta_t^d =0,  \\
\sum_{m=0}^{2k_n}A_m^{<1}c^{m/2}& \text{ for } \,\lim\limits_{t \rightarrow \infty} t\delta_t^d =c \in (0, \, 1],   \\
\sum_{m=0}^{k_n}A_m^{>1}c^{-m} & \text{ for }\,\lim\limits_{t \rightarrow \infty} t\delta_t^d \in [1, \,\infty), \\
A_0^{>1} &\text{ for }  \,\lim\limits_{t \rightarrow \infty} t\delta_t^d =\infty \\
\end{cases}  
\end{align} 
with 
\begin{align} 
A_m^{>1} := \left( \mu_{k_l,k_j:m+1}^{(\alpha_l,\alpha_j)} \frac{\mathds{1}(m\leq \min_{i\in \{l,j\}} k_i)}{(m+1)!(k_l-m)!(k_j-m)!}\right)_{l,j=1, \ldots ,n}    
\end{align}
 and 
\begin{align}

  A_m^{<1}  := \left(\mu_{k_l,k_j: \frac{k_l+k_j-m+2}{2}}^{(\alpha_l,\alpha_j)} \frac{\mathds{1}(m-|k_l-k_j| \in \{0,2,4, \ldots, 2 \min_{i\in \{l,j\}} k_i\})}{(\frac{k_l+k_j-m+2}{2})!(\frac{m-k_l+k_j}{2})!(\frac{m+k_l-k_j}{2})!}\right) _{l,j=1, \ldots, n}.  
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.750142+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d8613791c28cd1bc43d010415b53e8376cfb51f2fc8fb3bf1153072bab290bb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Ylim of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Consider the same notation and conditions as in Proposition~(prop:depthlabelsinglevertex of the paper). Additionally, recall $\mathcal{S}_n^+(a_1)$ from~(equation eq:definition_selection_sets_ungreedy_depth_single_vertex of the paper), fix $y\in \mathbb{R}$ and, conditionally on $\mathcal{S}_n^+(a_1)$, define the random variable
