{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.293782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d8ed6b7f6e0957ce1772c5153988ab66ea915b46b44b22e88462ca040ece585","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition order of arXiv:2605.08624, 'On the sum-of-digits measures and Cusick's conjecture via stopped random walks'] Define two maps $L, R \colon 2\mathbb{N}+1 \to 2\mathbb{N}+1$ by
