{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.367898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d933d4732b5f6daaa756eb617c8fcd54b20eeb27958f941c4740c9185000f19","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:LSI of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] A measure $\theta \in \mathcal{P}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m)$ satisfies a log-Sobolev inequality (LSI) with constant $C <\infty$ if for every continuously differentiable function $f: \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m \rightarrow \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$ such that $\mathbb{E}^\theta[f^2] = 1$, we have
