    \] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:32:58.356275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8de781a2dc6e0e1aa4f93a5098631bb7f2bcfc32910f60682e7fc2ee0741bd2a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ConvBd of arXiv:2506.06559, 'Bi-infinite incipient cluster in high dimensions'] {HaraHofstSlade03}}}]
Suppose $a\ge b>0$ and $f,g\colon \mathbb Z^d\to\mathbb R$ satisfy $f(x)\le c_1|x|^{-a}$ and $g(x)\le c_2|x|^{-b}$ for constants $c_1,c_2>0$. 
