{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.201396+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e181388578ce13de1e3729b10a4dbb392b8ba369546b4b7d988ecfe6530361c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:dropping of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $a,b>0$ such that $a>3b/2$, let $I:=\llbracket -\frac12 N_n^{2/3} (\log L)^a,-\frac12 N_n^{2/3} (\log L)^a\rrbracket$, and 
