{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.726054+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e9a46d23aee3f1d5fa24cb6573c3fd140508dbe5026d296bcef461520be8136","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2411.19163, '\bfseries Random polytopes in convex bodies:\\ Bridging the gap between extremal container'] Fix integers $d\geq 2$ and $m\in\{1,\ldots,d\}$, and an $m$-tuple $\operatorname{bd}=(d_1,\dotsc,d_m)\in \mathbb{N}^m$, such that $d_1+\ldots+d_m = d$. Further, let $\beta_1,\ldots,\beta_m\geq 0$ and set ${\boldsymbol{\beta}}:=(\beta_1,\ldots,\beta_m)$. We consider the random block-beta polytope $\mathcal{P}_{n,\operatorname{bd}}^{\boldsymbol{\beta}}$ and define $k_{\max} := \max\limits_{i=1,\dotsc,m} k_i$ and $\#k_{\max} := \#\left\{i: k_i = k_{\max}\right\}$. 
Then,
\begin{equation*}
    \mathbb{E} f_{d-1}(\mathcal{P}_{n,\operatorname{bd}}^{{\boldsymbol{\beta}}}) \asymp n^{\frac{k_{\max}-1}{k_{\max}+1}} (\ln n)^{\#k_{\max}-1}.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.262506+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e9d0cabb0773942a8c06de22efde000099c3175cb5a1e3d3a67c38e4a2ed310","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma kzetaestimate-short of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Fix any {\small$\delta>0$} (independent of {\small$N$}). There exist constants {\small$\beta,\kappa>0$} (also independent of {\small$N$}) and a high probability event on which the following holds for any {\small$\s,\t\in[0,1]$} with {\small$\s\leq\t$} and {\small$|\t-\s|\leq N^{\beta}N^{-\zeta}$}:

\begin{align}
\sup_{\x\in\Z}\sum_{\y\in\Z}\exp(\tfrac{\kappa|\x-\y|}{N})\cdot|\mathbf{K}^{N,\zeta,\sim}_{\s,\t,\x,\y}|&\lesssim N^{\delta}.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.305545+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e9e10162fcc648de162e6e1a786d6c0085ca7dde36d2fbbded92851d8054874","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 4 of arXiv:2606.24167, '\bf On the stability of rarefaction for stochastic viscous conservation law'] A continuous $L^2(\mathbb{R})$-valued $\mathcal{F}_t$-adapted process $(\phi(t))_{t \in [0, T]}$ is called a \textit{(probability strong) solution} of \eqref{perturbation}, if we have $\bar{\phi} \in X_1(T)$ and for every test function $\varphi \in C_c^\infty(\mathbb{R})$, the following equality holds {\rm{a.s.}} for all $t \in [0, T]$:
\begin{equation*} 
\begin{aligned}
\langle \phi(t), \varphi \rangle &= \langle \phi(0), \varphi \rangle + \int_0^t \left\langle f(\bar{\phi} + \bar{u}) - f(\bar{u}), \partial_x \varphi \right\rangle ds \\
&\quad - \int_0^t \left\langle b(\bar{\phi} + \bar{u})\partial_x(\bar{\phi} + \bar{u}), \partial_x \varphi \right\rangle  ds \\
&\quad - \sum_{i=1}^\infty \int_0^t \left\langle \sigma_i(\bar{\phi} + \bar{u}), \partial_x \varphi \right\rangle \circ dB_i(s),
\end{aligned}
\end{equation*}
where  $\bar{\phi}$ is any $H^1(\mathbb{R})$-valued progressively measurable $dt \otimes P$-version of $\phi$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.164055+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e9e29b23e43479790394fc937b96080b65b4990fdd27242b56bdc2385f8ff9c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Prop_KerDRD of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] For every $(g,[{\mathfrak l}]) \in \mathbf{Met} \times \mathbf{Ram}$ the following hold:
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item

    The kernel of $D_{R_D,g}^{\mathfrak l}$ consists precisely of the $L^2$ harmonic ${\mathfrak l}$--twisted $1$--forms;
    that is:
    \begin{equation*}
      \ker D_{R_D,g}^{\mathfrak l}
      =
      \mathscr{H}^1(g,[{\mathfrak l}])
      \coloneq
      \set[\big]{
        \alpha \in L^2\Omega^1(X{\backslash} Z,{\mathfrak l})
        :
        {\rm d} \alpha = {\rm d}^*\alpha = 0
      }
    \end{equation*}
  \item

    Pulling back along $\pi \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace \tilde X \to X$ induces an isomorphism
    \begin{equation*}
      \mathscr{H}^1(g,[{\mathfrak l}]) \cong {\rm H}_\mathrm{dR}^1(\tilde X)^-.
    \end{equation*}
    Here ${\rm H}_\mathrm{dR}^1(\tilde X)^-$ denotes the subspace of ${\rm H}_\mathrm{dR}^1(\tilde X)$ which is anti-invariant under the sheet-swapping involution $\tau$.
  \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.087939+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ea02269f8e531d2cbe3fb2394d53e243786cdba215fba5cc0db070b72d582d8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2608.19976, 'Random valuations'] Assume that $\Phi$ is a random valuation such that almost all of its
  realisations are continuous translation-invariant valuations. Then
  \begin{equation}

    \Phi(K)=\sum_{i=0}^d \Phi_i(K),
  \end{equation}
  where each $\Phi_i$ is a random valuation such that almost all its
  realisations are continuous, translation-invariant valuations
  which are homogeneous of degree~$i$, that is,
  $\Phi_i(cK)=c^i\Phi_i(K)$ a.s.\ for all $K\in\Kd$ and $c>0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.452530+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ea139b6aa7ab9f223d988a8c8391ca1a56c877442d16f05c5783f270028cce3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 27 of arXiv:2604.03213, 'Asymptotic expansion for transport maps \\ between laws of multimatrix models'] Let $f\in\cC^k(X_1,\dots,X_d)$ then if $f^j$ is the function defined in Corollary \ref{cor:taylorineq}, $g_{a,b}\in\cC^k(X_1,\dots,X_d)$ for $a\in [0,j],\ b\in [1,d] $ , then
    $$ \cg \coloneqq f\circ\big( ( g_{a,b} )_{0\leq a\leq j, 1\leq b\leq d} \big)$$
    belongs to $\cC^k(X_1,\dots,X_d)$. Besides, for some constant $C_k$,
    \begin{equation}

        \norm{\cg}_{\cC^{k-j},R} \leq C_k \norm{f}_{\cC^k,S} \left( \sup_{1\leq a\leq j}\ \sum_{b=1}^d\ \norm{g_{a,b}}_{\cC^k,R} \right)^j,
    \end{equation}
    where
    $$S\coloneqq \sup_{1\leq b\leq d} \sum_{a=1}^d \norm{g_{0,b}}_{0,R}.$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:57:51.763826+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ea33d171723f493783f5b94e76c58072de7909506b6558e6645b9e4206ca0b1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (Potential-bearing Robin--Lieb localization) of arXiv:2608.30211, '2608.30211'] Let $D$ be a uniformly $C^{2,\gamma}$ domain, let $V\in L^\infty(D)$ be real,
and let $\varrho\in[0,1]$.  For every $R>0$,
\begin{equation}
 \lambda(-\Delta+V,D,\varrho)
 \geq \inf_{z\in\R^d}
 \lambda(-\Delta+V,D\mid B_R(z),\varrho)
 -\lambda_1(B_1)R^{-2},
\end{equation}
where empty intersections are assigned eigenvalue $+\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.677145+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ea3e9d54d93e1ce8f8a3aed31124fdda7bf7ee9d630292c1792376d488a1ebc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 (Canonical truncation morphism) of arXiv:2608.30875, 'A Decomposition Theorem for Topological Semi-small Maps'] Let $f : X \longrightarrow Y$ be a continuous map of topological spaces and let
        	$Rf_* : D(X) \to D(Y)$ be the right derived direct image
        	functor between the unbounded derived categories of sheaves of abelian groups.
        	For every integer $k$ there exists a unique natural transformation
        	\begin{align*}
        \gamma_\mathcal{F}:	\tau_{\leq k} \circ Rf_*  \longrightarrow  Rf_* \circ \tau_{\leq k}	
        	\end{align*}
        	of functors $D(X) \longrightarrow D(Y)$, which makes the following diagram commutative
        	 	\begin{align*}
        		\begin{array}{ccccc}
        			\tau_{\leq k}Rf_*\mathcal{F} & \longrightarrow & Rf_*\mathcal{F} & \longrightarrow &
        			\tau_{\geq k+1}Rf_*\mathcal{F} \\
        			\downarrow{\gamma_\mathcal{F}} & & \parallel & & \\
        			Rf_*\tau_{\leq k}\mathcal{F} & \longrightarrow & Rf_*\mathcal{F} & \longrightarrow &
        			Rf_*\tau_{\geq k+1}\mathcal{F}
        		\end{array}	
        	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.228298+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ea497fa5e0c2d4839087b71e37edf579a3f9fa0e01fe27d1aab43717ead5088","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma-on-difference-U_M-for-critical of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Given $b>0$, there exists $K, C_1, C_2>0$\footnote{We stress that we are here and in (equation quant-bound-for-super-critical-for-difference of the paper) writing ``there exists a $K>0$" rather than writing ``for all $K>0$". We expect (equation quant-bound-for-super-critical-for-difference of the paper), (equation quant-bound-for-difference-critical of the paper) to hold for all $K>0$ rather than only for $K$ large enough. We were able to verify (equation quant-bound-for-super-critical-for-difference of the paper), (equation quant-bound-for-difference-critical of the paper) only for large enough $K>0$, which will be sufficient for our purposes.} such that for all $t$ large enough and $z\in [-\frac{1}{4}\log t , b t]$,
    \begin{align}
        C_1 t^{-\frac{3}{2}} (z+\log t)e^{-\sqrt 2 z}e^{-\frac{z^2}{2t}}\le u_M(t,  &\sqrt{2}t + z - K ) - u_M(t, \sqrt{2}t + z + K ) \\ \nonumber & \le C_2 t^{-\frac{3}{2}} (z+\log t)e^{-\sqrt 2 z}e^{-\frac{z^2}{2t}}.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.095379+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ea4bc119dfe97fa65665add3dbf1c18aecb9c4fc1415ead48c744e565244212","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 22 of arXiv:2608.19976, 'Random valuations'] If $\Phi$ is a $\sigma$-continuous non-negative stationary isotropic
  ID valuation with independent increments, then the corresponding
  L\'evy measure on $\sC\times(0,\infty)$ is given by
  \begin{equation}

    \nu(\sC_L\times A)
    =\sum_{k=0}^{d} \int_A \int_{G(d,k)}
    \E(V_{d-k}(Y_{E,r}+\Pi_{E^\perp}L))\gamma_k(dE) a_{k,r}\mu(dr)
  \end{equation}
  for each compact set $L$ in $\R^d$ and Borel $A\subset(0,\infty)$,
  where $\gamma_k$ is the normalised Haar measure on $G(d,k)$,
  $Y_{E,r}$ is a random compact convex set in $E^\perp$ such that
  $Y_{RE,r}$ has the same distribution as $RY_{E,r}$ for each
  deterministic rotation $R$, and $a_{k,r}$ is a measurable non-negative
  function of $r>0$. If $K\in\Kd$, then
  \begin{equation}

    \nu(\sC_K\times A)=\sum_{k=0}^{d} \sum_{j=0}^{d-k}
    c_{0,d}^{d-k-j,k+j} 
    V_{d-k-j}(K) \int_A \E V_j(Y_{E,r})a_{k,r}\mu(dr).
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

