{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:56:00.633232+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8eb943b6c83cc4c4aab62b0363bbe58e1979487eb3585f0faf4616f17c8a3875","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition c3.7 of arXiv:2603.14447, '\Large \bf Backward doubly stochastic differential equations with and without reflection u'] \sl
		For \(i=1,2\), assume that the parameters \((\xi^i,f^i,g^i)\) satisfy
		\textbf{(A1)}, \textbf{(F1)}, \textbf{(G1)}  and \textbf{(G3)}  with common structural constants, and that \(f^i\) is Lipschitz continuous in \(z\).  Let $(Y^i,Z^i)\in S^2_{\mathbb{F}}([0,T];\mathbb{R})\times L^2_{\mathbb{F}}([0,T];\mathbb{R}^d)$  be the unique solution of the following BDSDE:
		\begin{align*}
			Y^i_t=\xi^i+\int_{t}^{T}f^i(s,Y^i_s,Z^i_s)ds+\int_{t}^{T}g^i(s,Y^i_s,Z^i_s)dB_s-\int_t^TZ^i_sdW_s,\quad\ 0\leqslant t\leqslant T.
