{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.322068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ebd3acdc6d023ae1aafc3361d57029a860571765b0e08290018c858e7b0440d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:DeGiorgi of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] Suppose $g$ is a weak solution to (equation eq:linear_kinetic of the paper) in $Q_2$ and satisfies (equation eq:uniform_ellipticity of the paper) in $Q_2$ for some values of $\lambda$ and $\Lambda$. Then, there exists an $\alpha \in (0,1)$ depending only on $\lambda$ and $\Lambda$ so that $g\in C^{0,\alpha}_{\rm kin}(Q_1)$ and
