{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:57:51.738116+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8eddde4bccc7e437a7615dd58d3ed2b4e85ecf3abe669141ab7c0756a84e8a1e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2608.30089, 'On the Coefficients of Hurwitz-Type Matrix Polynomials'] For $n\geq1$, the matrix polynomial  $\f_n$ is an HTM polynomial if and only if $\f_n$ has the following
 representation:
 \begin{equation}
 \f_n(z)=\left\{
 \begin{array}{cl}
   (-1)^m(P_{1,m}^*(-\bar z^2)-z\, Q_{1,m}^*(-\bar z^2)), & n=2m, \\
