{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:19.043081+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ee076874cecf8d2a916051a30f8c26b48d811a7b2da817948564bd8e8de4ef0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem 1.1 of arXiv:2609.02607, 'Spatial inhomogeneity for a three-dimensional doubly degenerate nutrient system with indir'] Let $\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^{3}$ be a smoothly bounded domain and $\ell\geq0$. Then there exists  $C(K)>0$ with the property that whenever $u_0, v_0$ and $w_0$ fulfill (equation 1.2 of the paper) and (equation 1.6 of the paper), the problem (equation 1.1 of the paper) admits a
 continuous global weak  solution $(u,v,w)$  in the sense of Definition (Definition 2.1 of the paper) below, which is such that
    \begin{equation}
