{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.262216+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f1e76cbe9a509cc9b66b2ea55c7c36923bec5b697705eade4071f1b35ac6ff9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lzetasimestimate of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Fix any {\small$\kappa=\mathrm{O}(1)$} and {\small$\delta>0$}. There exists a high probability event on which we have

