{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:59:24.052535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f6c11d2907d9febf42481833791b4ab77ef9a329e9cffe0f1aa53606c1ffc5f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:ritz of arXiv:2608.30888, 'Three-term asymptotics for discrete\\ Hardy--Rellich constants in high dimension'] For every fixed $\ell\geq1$,
\begin{equation}
 \mu_{\ell,N}
 =2^\ell N^\ell+\gamma_\ell N^{\ell-1}
  +O_\ell(N^{\ell-2}),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
 \gamma_\ell
 =3\ell(\ell-1)2^{\ell-2}
  -\frac{\ell^2 2^{2\ell}}{2^\ell-1}.
\end{equation}
In particular,
\[
 \gamma_1=-4,\qquad
 \gamma_2=-\frac{46}{3},\qquad
 \gamma_3=-\frac{324}{7},\qquad
 \gamma_4=-\frac{1936}{15}.
\]
The variational principle therefore gives the upper bound
\begin{equation}
 C_\ell(N)\leq
 2^\ell N^\ell+\gamma_\ell N^{\ell-1}+O_\ell(N^{\ell-2}).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.650594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f727dedec715eaaf107cb0c90e0b90722adbd280b233b139e2ff9f3bb055b82","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:edge_fusion of arXiv:2608.15923, 'Universality of two-dimensional Markovian holonomy fields'] Let ${\mathbb{G}}=(V,E,F)$ be a topological map embedded in a surface $\Sigma_{g,n}$ that contains a subdivision vertex $v\in V$: the two half-edges incident to $v$ belong to two distinct non-loop edge segments $e_1$ and $e_2$, and no other half-edge is incident to $v$. Let ${\mathbb{G}}'=(V',E',F')$ be a new topological map obtained by removing $v$ and replacing $\{e_1,e_2\}$ by a single edge $e_{12}$ whose embedding is given by the same curve as $e_1e_2$. Then
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{R}_*\mu_{{\mathbb{G}},G,Q,\mathrm{vol},\mathfrak{t}}=\mu_{{\mathbb{G}}',G,Q,\mathrm{vol},\mathfrak{t}}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.525706+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f784b161fe3a35ec6f9592a355567283beb8d3f1ec1ea3e6baba497cc53b184","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop e:bwl_bound of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] For any initial data $u[0] = u_{\mathfrak{r}} + u_{\mathfrak{s}}$ with $\|u_{\mathfrak{r}}\|_{\mathcal{C}^{-\kappa}} \leq 2\alpha_0$ and $\|u_{\mathfrak{s}}\| = \lambda$\,, there exists some $C(\lambda)$ such that we have 
