{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.417017+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f85b8d87e727d0ac41c80515e978974299b9cfd04fc7b6048f1395d32d5d983","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:squares_joint_distributions of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] For the hexagon with $L$-dependent sides as in (def:prelimit_barcode_kernel of the paper),
