{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.812403+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f8623ab996fd167fe5a2f8890066e10d998db8aae015a10a36258d5d5dcec69","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma mmn-variance-bound of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $\nu_n$ be the stationary distribution of the $M/M/n$ queue with arrival rate $\lambda = n-n^{1-\alpha}$ and unit service rate, and let $X$ be a random variable that admits $\nu_n$ as the distribution, we have
