{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:32:58.376994+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f8a4c39e32cd6a682979eae3e47b6f309b128ddeddc95cb76d1ef9ff5b16066","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:tPsiBd of arXiv:2506.06559, 'Bi-infinite incipient cluster in high dimensions'] For all $F\in\mathfrak F_{00}$ there exist $C>0$ such that for all $x,x'\in\mathbb{Z}^d$, 
