{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:53.205204+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f9999a54676c5a11657b9fd6c813b6f12535abe117867eaa572c99311c90182","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 37 ({\cite[Chapter 6.1) of arXiv:2606.12670, 'The censored stochastic six-vertex model and parabolic Kazhdan--Lusztig $R$-polynomials'] {MR2133266}}]  Recall the definition of $\widetilde{T}_{\sigma} = q^{\ell(\sigma)}T_{\sigma}$ from Remark \ref{rmk:tildeT}. Then we have 
