\]
as $n\to\infty$. In particular,
\[
p_c(n,K_r)\sim (\gamma n)^{-1/\lambda}.
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:02.035828+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90261a0695a01a173efce7cdaf2620b8113ea497053f37ad763d8646b05f92da","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LEM:T2 of arXiv:2512.23957, 'Concentration and fluctuations of sine-Gordon measure around topological multi-soliton man'] There exist a constant $c>0$ such that for sufficiently large $D$, we have
