{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.570854+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_902ebd864b45686f0a35450356f0a45abbc863180e1219a19c892acbd103afd2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary C:Chung of arXiv:2602.05317, 'Strong local nondeterminism for stochastic time-fractional\\ slow and fast diffusion equat'] Assume condition~(equation E:main of the paper) holds. For part (i) below, further assume $\ell < \alpha(\gamma+1/2)$ if $\beta = 2$ and
  $\gamma \in (0, 2]$.
  \begin{enumerate}[\rm (i)]

    \item If $\rho \in (0, 1)$, then for any compact interval $I$ in $(0,
            \infty)$ and any $x_0 \in \mathbb{R}^d$, there exist constants $C_5, C_5' \in [0,
