{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.062025+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9059fe46c3a15e2dda4233b82087ac162ad7625e8e52d9caa8f67b870ba98cbc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2607.14993, 'Sharp phase transition for percolation with short-range dependencies'] We assume that there exists $\beta_c \in \mathbb R_+^*$ such that $ \theta(\beta) = 0$ for all $\beta \in ]0, \beta_c[$ and $ \theta(\beta) > 0$ for all $\beta \in ]\beta_c, +\infty[$. Then,
