{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.869629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_909bf1841a5838aa10c1bf9a12f2a8523090091ef05ccf821e62f67726047dc6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:interro-real of arXiv:2504.19367, 'Reduced Random Walks in the Hyperbolic Plane\textinterrobang'] The function $\interro$ extends uniquely to a continuous, strictly increasing function $\interro \colon [0, 1] \to \mathbb{R}$. Moreover, the functional equation \[\interro(x) =
