{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.813375+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90a6125e1e9f03b0b0535ecad649748e253b2bdef9fdc9f961e0bdf7c150e88a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p:GZ-uniform-TF of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] {GZ22}}]
    Given $L\geqslant 1$, there exists a random constant $\mathfrak{C}_{(p:GZ-uniform-TF of the paper)}>0$ such that the following is true.
    First, we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}(\mathfrak{C}_{(p:GZ-uniform-TF of the paper)} > m) \leqslant Ce^{-cm^{2}}
        \qquad\text{for all $m\geqslant 0$,}
    \end{align*}
    where $C,c>0$ are constants depending only on $L$.
    Second, for any $(s,x;t,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{4}_{\uparrow}\cap[-L,L]^4$, the geodesic $\Pi_{(s,x),(t,y)}$ satisfies
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{r\in[s,t]}
        \left|
            \Pi_{(s,x),(t,y)}(r) - \frac{x(t-r) + y(r-s)}{t-s}
        \right|
        \leqslant \mathfrak{C}_{(p:GZ-uniform-TF of the paper)} \,
        (t-s)^{2/3} \log^3\left(2 \vee \frac{1}{t-s}\right).
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.668154+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90a6342e4775be00ef3f4e26495f214b196941fb3fccb8c7b77f1c22a89f0f05","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 17 of arXiv:2609.03556, 'An Effective SPDE Model for a Schr\"odinger Equation with a Fluctuating Magnetic Potential'] \label[corollary]{corollary_compactness}
Let $\mathcal{K}\subset \bar{Z}_T$. Then $\mathcal K$ is relatively compact in $\bar{Z}_T$ if
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\sup_{u\in \mathcal{K}}\sup_{t\in [0,T]}\|u(t)\|_{H^{-3}}<+\infty$,
    \item $\lim_{\delta\rightarrow 0}\sup_{u\in \mathcal{K}}\sup_{s,t\in [0,T], |s-t|\leq \delta}\|u(t)-u(s)\|_{U'}=0.$
\end{enumerate}
In particular, for each $R>0$, $s\in(0,1)$, and $p\in(1,\infty)$ such
that $sp>1$, the set
\begin{align*}
    X_{R,s,p}:=\big\{f\in &C_w([0,T];H^{-3}(\R^d))
    \cap W^{s,p}(0,T;H^{-5}(\R^d)): \\
     &\sup_{t\in [0,T]}\|f(t)\|_{H^{-3}}
     +\|f\|_{W^{s,p}(0,T;H^{-5})}\leq R\big\},
\end{align*}
is relatively compact in $\bar{Z}_T.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.650038+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90a646afc79e6b99bb42739cad8e4a83d99632839aced5f4c38a5a2024166a5c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor_Gab_conn of arXiv:2607.04002, 'Collisions of random walks in unimodular random graphs: applications to the random geometr'] Fix~$\mathbf z \in \mathbb{Z}^d$ and~$i \in \{1,\dots,d\}$, and define
\begin{align*}
& \mathcal B(\mathbf z, i) := \{ B_{\mathbf z + \mathbf u}: \mathbf u \in \{0,1\}^d, \mathbf u \cdot \mathbf{e}_i = 0\}, \\[2mm]
& C(\mathbf z,i) := \mathrm{conv}( \{M(\mathbf z + \mathbf u): \mathbf u \in \{0,1\}^d, \mathbf u \cdot \mathbf e_i = 0 \} ), \\[2mm]
& \mathcal Q(\mathbf z,i) := \{ Q \text{ sub-box of side-length } M/\alpha: Q \text{ is contiguous to } Q', \; Q' \cap C(\mathbf z,i) \neq \varnothing  \}.
