Assume the boxes in~$\mathcal B(\mathbf z, i)$ are good. Let~$Q_1,Q_2 \in \mathcal Q(\mathbf z,i)$ be contiguous sub-boxes with~$Q_2 \cap C(\mathbf z,i) \neq \varnothing$, and~$x \in V(\mathcal G_\mathrm{Gab}) \cap Q_1$ and~$y \in V(\mathcal G_\mathrm{Gab}) \cap Q_2$. Then, there exists a path in~$\mathcal G_\mathrm{Gab}$ from~$x$ to~$y$ contained in~$\cup \{B: B \in \mathcal B(\mathbf z, i) \}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

