	and where both $N_\Lambda^\nu(t)$ and $X_n$ depend on the same parameters $\lambda_1, \lambda_2, \dots, \lambda_k$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:58:24.512324+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90bb05e7b3270da8a87b5243b327f8b490588be0daaa48a670227190938537b6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lmuboundtwo of arXiv:2601.09537, 'Gene genealogies in haploid populations evolving according to sweepstakes reproduction'] Suppose a population evolves according to Def.\ (hapltwo of the paper).  Then there is a constant $B > 0$ with 
