{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.631384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90bb8b39b543337e1b19905b6786a0a718335af98181ec3e5a9194e3a2851d82","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (Proposition $1.15$ in~\cite{Iyermonopoly24}) of arXiv:2505.06187, 'Preferential Attachment Trees with Vertex Death: Persistence of the Maximum Degree'] Suppose that $(S_i)_{j\in\N}$ is a sequence of mutually independent, symmetric random variables. If $\sum_{i=1}^\infty S_i$ diverges almost surely, then 
