     \end{equation*}

    where $t_r=A\min\left\{r^2,\frac{1}{K}\right\}$, with the convention that $\frac{1}{K}=+\infty$ when $K=0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.750243+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91042bc1fc73b479ebd0a59e470d5dbba1df5786125abd22d73d1e5b3d587790","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:vector-fourier-lower-bound of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Assume that the dyadic vector-weight law is energy-admissible.  Then
