{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.363065+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9115f2c8be06c87d872f56d48692968b7fa9452d77139d5250522f31c6aa612e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: M covariance interp bdry of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] Let $\alpha_1,\alpha_2\in[0,1)$. Then there exists $C>0$ such that, for every $T>0$,
