{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.180700+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91268266c1356b399cfddf5e87fb699eb8ab0346db03bd2d1c346ca453580e80","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:technique of arXiv:2606.24793, '\LARGE Random sequential nearest-neighbor coloring on trees'] Let $\eta>0$. Then, there exist integers $N,L>0$ such that if $(\varepsilon_i)_{i\le N}$ are i.i.d.\ exponential random variables with parameter 1 and $\sigma_i=\sum_{k=1}^i\varepsilon_k$, we have 
