{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.922029+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91297db064c03fc4b39406116703bff5066b7823b3aabe32a0f2952a216b9055","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 17 (Main Theorem for $n=1$ and $p>0$) of arXiv:2609.00974, 'On Algebraic Integrability\\ of Vector Fields \\ with Rational Function Coefficients\\ tha'] We follow the assumptions and notations from Theorem \ref{Main Formula}. In particular, the prime $p$ is assumed to be big enough. The following are equivalent:
