{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.487815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_915f1e57e6bc6f28791f74ccc68845fb922bfc64a7580707f250169467b63743","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2505.14762, 'Multiple radial SLE($\kappa$) and quantum Calogero-Sutherland system'] Suppose $\Omega$ is a simply connected domain $(\Omega \subsetneq \mathbb{C})$, let $\partial \Omega$ be its Carathéodory boundary (prime ends) and consider the Schottky double $S=\Omega^{\text {double }}$, which equips with the canonical involution $\iota \equiv \iota_\Omega: S \rightarrow S, z \mapsto z^*$. 

