{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.832738+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9171c39e00aee85cf796d36b92df5e85b27b6295381168f3c4e8fdd521392039","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm RSig of arXiv:2609.01751, 'Orthogonal polynomials which are eigenfunctions of a partial differential operator'] For ${\kappa} \in {\mathbb R}^{d_2}$ with $k_i > -1$, $1 \le i \le d_2$, define the fourth-order differential operator 
\begin{align} 
  {\mathfrak D}_{{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}^{{\mathbb R} \rtimes \Sigma} u: = \,& -\frac14 |{\bm y}|^3 \Delta_{{\bm x}}^2 + |{\bm y}| {\langle} {\bm x},\nabla_{\bm x}{\rangle} \Delta_{\bm x} 
   + \left(1+ \frac{1}{2} ({\kappa}_{d_2} + d_1)\right) |{\bm y}|  \Delta_{\bm x}  \\
     &+  2  {\langle} {\bm x},\nabla_{\bm x}{\rangle} \partial_{y_{d_2}}
   - 2  {\langle} {\bm y},\nabla_{\bm y}{\rangle} \partial_{y_{d_2}} + \sum_{i=1}^{d_2} \left[ y_i \partial_{y_i}^2 + ({\kappa}_i+1-y_i) \partial_{y_i} \right]
     \notag \\
    & + 2 |{\bm y}| \partial_{y_d}^2 - {\langle} {\bm x}, \nabla_{\bm x} {\rangle} - (|{\bm k}'|- d_1+d_2-1) \partial_{y_{d_2}}. \notag
\end{align}
Then ${\mathcal V}_n({\mathbb R}^{d_1}  \rtimes {\mathbb R}_\Sigma^{d_2}, \bm W_{{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}^{{\mathbb R} \rtimes \Sigma})$ is an eigenspace 
of $ {\mathfrak D}_{{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}^{{\mathbb R} \rtimes \Sigma}$ for each $n \in {\mathbb N}_0$. More precisely, 
\begin{align} 
  {\mathfrak D}_{{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}^{{\mathbb R} \rtimes \Sigma} u =  - n u, \qquad 
         \forall u \in {\mathcal V}_n\big({\mathbb R}^{d_1}  \rtimes {\mathbb R}_\Sigma^{d_2}, \bm W_{\mu}^{{\mathbb R} \rtimes \Sigma}\big).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.861670+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_917332824166c7c796fcc8da26c92133147ee9ece03dafd92d8b95c5785c1a46","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $h,T$ be such that $\frac Th\in\mathbb{N}$ and $f:\R\to\R$ be three times weakly differentiable with derivatives of polynomial growth. Under Assumptions \ref{Ass:Half_Step} and \ref{Aspt_new}, for $\tiX^{h,\delta}$ and $\hX^{h,\delta}$ respectively defined in \eqref{Eq:Half_step} and \eqref{eq_Xhdelta} it holds for any $p>1$ and $\delta \in (0,1/2)$ that
