{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.777481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9177ff4f70633f0bc2372d791a0cf955e00768400a73cbf44241e3fac4d476ec","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm::onepoint_boundary of arXiv:2411.01467, 'Conformal covariance of connection probabilities \\ in the 2D critical FK-Ising model'] Let $\Omega\subset \mathbb{C}$ be a simply connected domain and $z\in \Omega$. Let $\Omega^{a}\subseteq a\mathbb{Z}^2$ be a sequence of simply connected domains that converges to $\Omega$ under the Hausdorff metric as $a\to 0$. Suppose that $z^a\in \Omega$ satisfies $\lim_{a\to 0} z^a=z$. Then, there exists a constant $C_3\in (0,\infty)$ such that 
	\begin{equation} 
