{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:14.935463+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91c8b86b813be518c1f8e15c6b70ae10604dccf700af2c3e56e395244f229283","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2607.11756, 'Full replica symmetry breaking in the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick model'] The processes above satisfy
\begin{align}
 \dd M_s&=\beta C_s\dd W_s,\\
 \dd C_s&=-\beta^2\alpha(s)C_s^2\dd s+\beta D_s\dd W_s,
 \\
 \dd D_s&=-3\beta^2\alpha(s)C_sD_s\dd s+\beta A_s\dd W_s.

\end{align}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
 \Gamma'(s)=\beta^2\E C_s^2,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \Gamma'(t)-\Gamma'(r)=\beta^4\int_r^t
 \E[D_s^2-2\alpha(s)C_s^3]\dd s.
\end{equation}
If $\alpha(s)=m$ on an open interval $I$, then $\Gamma\in C^3(I)$ and
\begin{align}
 \Gamma''(s)&=\beta^4\E[D_s^2-2mC_s^3],
 \\
 \Gamma'''(s)&=\beta^6\E[A_s^2-12mC_sD_s^2+6m^2C_s^4].

\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.999654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91cb0aa9209878cd2b23bbfc36bfcd5381048f057afda36dda6732a76f08c930","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 20 of arXiv:2512.02661, 'Worst-case mixing estimates for Brownian motion with semipermeable barriers'] There exist absolute constants $c_1,c_2>0$ such that the following holds.
	Denote $R \de c_1\min\{1/\kappa, 1/\lambda_{\max}, \rho \}$ and $C\de (R \lambda_{\min})^{\Delta/R}/\Area(D)$.
	Then, for every $T\geq c_2 \Delta^2$, initial condition $x_0\in D$, and measurable $E\subseteq D$,
