{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.771520+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91f9ebc6ee1b71da34763b0a4c6cbc55470b21bcd54aae45514d8b811d620190","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: discretization application of arXiv:2411.02917, '\hspace*{2mm}\\[-16mm] Stein's Method for Spatial Random Graphs'] Let $(\Xi,\Sigma)$ be an $\mathrm{RGG}(\lambda,\kappa)$ such that $\Xi\sim P^{\lambda}$ fulfills (equation eq: stability cond of the paper). Construct the corresponding discretised graph $(\Xi_{\Lambda},\Sigma_{\Lambda})\sim P^{\lambda_{\Lambda}}\otimes Q^{\kappa_{\Lambda}}$ and intermediate graph $(\Xi_I,\Sigma_I)\sim P^{\lambda_I}\otimes Q^{\kappa_I}$ as described above. Then
