{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.701300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9210534c20bc15f411cbcc9e09450beb5148ad3273a28e5d77e3377ea693682b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Sgn-irred of arXiv:2609.00672, 'Deciding superellipticity and computing the Weierstrass normal form'] Let $g\ge 2$ and $n\ge 2$ with $\mathcal S_{g,n}\ne\emptyset$, and put $m=m(g,n)$. Then

