{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.530898+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9210793343fac938c4dee4593a133560134480f91b1a59ffc98e04241ee28768","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eqn-HR_VR of arXiv:2505.24043, 'Weak solutions of Navier-Stokes Equation with purely discontinuous L\'evy Noise'] Let $B_R$ be the open ball in $\mathbb{R}^d$ centered at $0$ with radius $R>0$. We define the following spaces
