{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.194034+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9237fe1f282e40e845bba7bb47a25bb771e230f333c0d838da31937653a29845","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 4 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] Suppose that $\nu_{\Unif}$ is the uniform distribution on $\mathsf S_N$, $\pi\sim \nu_{\Unif}$, and $G$ is the shuffle graph generated as above. Then we have
