{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.616859+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_927405272840421e0294ef3dd043ebca4c6135450888aefec02a6172c298dfd3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem main_theorem_toric of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $X$ be a smooth, projective, split toric variety over $\mathbb{Q}$ of Picard rank $\rho\ge 2$ with open orbit $U$, and let $\pi\colon Y\to X$ be as in (constr:family-over-toric-base of the paper). Write $\Delta = \sum_{d\in \mathcal{D}} \Delta_d$ and assume (eq:affine-asymp of the paper) for $i\in \mathcal{I}$. If $-\vec \Delta$ is of convergent type, then the number 
	\begin{equation*}
		N(B) = \sharp\{x\in U(\mathbb{Q}) : Y_x(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})\ne \emptyset,\ H(x)\le B\}
	\end{equation*}
	of everywhere locally soluble fibres satisfies
