{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.832634+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_92a139cf4d45678361e722069452d649250c74ba4bb0df5c007730e002f3412c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 26 (Sharp blockwise characterization of strict coarse-depth loss) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] Fix $m<r$ and assume exact depth $r$ at $\theta_0$ together with \cref{ass:regularity}. Let $T\subset T_{\theta_0}\Theta$ be a tangent block and let $T_0\subset T$ be a linear subspace of dimension $p\ge1$. Assume
