{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.845103+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_92d159a71c222c8cdf76546bb9a7d2ed5216b9d330b99921399276855bd1723c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:matrixBernstein of arXiv:2510.01021, '\Large Random Matrices, Intrinsic Freeness, and Sharp Non-Asymptotic Inequalities\relatedv'] Let $\{H_k\}_{k=1}^n$ be a sequence of independent random symmetric $d\times d$ matrices. Assume that each $H_k$ satisfies:
