{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.291823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_92dc2cbf972eb5c62d378e685e95dc57676c48056e323402e02d9c6e4a0370c8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:underline_comp of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Let $X$ satisfy Assumption~(ass:chi of the paper)(i). Fix a (large) $L>0$ and (small) $c_0,\epsilon,\xi>0$. Let $\theta>0$ be a (possibly, $N$-dependent) small parameter. Consider $k_j\in [N]$, $z_j\in\mathbf{C}$, and $w_j=\mathrm{i}\eta_j$ with $\eta_j>0$, for $j=1,2$. Denote $x_j:=k_j/N$, $G_j:=G^{(k_j),z_j}_{x_j}(w_j)$ and assume that $x_1\le x_2$. Recall the definition of $\kappa_4$ from (equation eq:def_kappa_4 of the paper). It holds that
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{E} \langle G_1-\mathbf{E} G_1\rangle \langle G_2-\mathbf{E} G_2\rangle = \frac{1}{2x_1x_2N^2}\left(V_{12}+\bm{1}_{\beta=1}V_{1\overline{2}}+\kappa_4 x_1^2 U_1U_2\right) + \mathcal{O}_\theta\left(\left(\frac{1}{N\eta_*}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{N}}\right)\frac{N^\xi}{N^2\eta_1\eta_2}\right),

