where our contour only encloses the pole at zero. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.918920+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93273c71dc46a5fff4cc6dc8341010816172761596e55195aae2581740038666","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem TeLe1 of arXiv:2411.06974, '{\bf Distribution dependent SDEs with multiplicative fractional noise}'] Let $x,y$ be two positive constants and $0<\alpha<\beta<1$. Then for any $0<r<s$, we have
