{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.164427+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_932a35f48bb910761e775f5d62e455191902e7cdc7c1432c3bc49ee3304df8a3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defn: admissible law of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] An $S'(\mathbb T^2)$-valued random variable $\varphi^0$ is an admissible boundary condition if there exists a coupling $(\Omega^0, \mathcal F^0, \mathbb P^0)$ of $(W^0,Z^0) \in S'(\mathbb T^2)\times S'(\mathbb T^2)$ such that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)]  $\varphi^0$ is equal in law to $W^0+Z^0$.

\item[(ii)] $W^0 = 0$ almost surely or ${\rm Law}_{\mathbb P^0}(W^0) = \mu^0$. 
\item[(iii)] There exists $\kappa > 0$ such that 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E^0\left[\|Z^0\|_{H^{1/2-\kappa}(\mathbb T^2)}^2\right] < \infty,
\end{equation}
where $\mathbb E^0$ denotes expectation with respect to $\mathbb P^0$.
\end{enumerate}
We call the law of $\varphi^0$ an \emph{admissible boundary law}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.856093+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_932c68b7f8a4bb64cf52bb46ef5d03084103139097664990853df39d27bc869e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 11 of arXiv:2605.20115, 'Moment bounds on correctors for the degenerate random conductance model'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{thm.main},  if $\gamma \ge C_2$, the correctors satisfy, for all $x\in \Z^d$,
    \begin{equation}
        \expecb{|(\phi,\sigma)(x)-(\phi,\sigma)(0)|^{\frac\gamma{C_1}}}^\frac{C_1}{\gamma}\lesssim_{ \Lambda }( \gamma\Gamma)^{C_0} \left\{
        \begin{aligned}
            &\sqrt{ |x|},\quad &\text{ if }d=1;\\
            &\log^\frac12(1+|x|),\quad &\text{ if }d=2;\\
            &1,\quad &\text{ if }d\ge3.
        \end{aligned}\right.
    \end{equation}
Hence, if $d\ge3$, there is a unique stationary solution $(\phi,\sigma)$ to the equations \eqref{eq.corrector} and \eqref{eq.flux} such that $\expec{(\phi,\sigma)}=0$. In this case, 
    \begin{equation}
        \expec{|(\phi,\sigma)|^{\frac\gamma{C_1}}}^{\frac{C_1}\gamma}\lesssim_{ \Lambda }( \gamma\Gamma)^{C_0}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.970725+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_932fdb0d7f9f6aa97d6b8df3a12875670624d460a1188795300e3efb5d6be92f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma mianlemma of arXiv:2606.15203, 'The existence of invariant sublinear expectations for $G\text{-}$SDEs'] Let $X_T^{t,x}$ be defined by ((barxTtnew of the paper)), where $b$ is a Lipschitz continuous function with Lipschitz constant $l_b$. Then for each $\varphi \in C_{b,lip}(\mathbb{R}^{d })$, for any fixed $0\leq T <
