{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.005007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9339993b8f97055511f9ffcb30987011df94f5e545be41f3615cc5f71417ac7d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_reset of arXiv:2606.27549, 'On Analytically Tractable Multidimensional Diffusions via Doob $h$-Transforms, with Resett'] Let $\widehat{\bf X}_t^{\rm R}$ and ${\bf X}_t^{\rm R}$ be $n$-dimensional diffusion processes satisfying the SDE's (equation sde_x_r of the paper) and (equation sde_x_r_trasf of the paper), respectively. Both processes reset to an arbitrary state $\boldsymbol{y}^{\rm R}\in {\cal D}$ at any occurrence of the independent nonhomogeneous Poisson processes $N_t$ and $N_t'$, both having intensity $\lambda(t)$, and cumulative intensity 
$\Lambda(t)=\int_{0}^t\lambda(s)\, {\rm d}s$. If the conditions of Theorem (teo_1 of the paper) are satisfied, then the transition p.d.f.\ of ${\bf X}_t^{\rm R}$ is expressed in terms of the transition p.d.f.\ of $\widehat{\bf X}_t^{\rm R}$ via the following product-form relation: 

