for any $\bf{x},\bf{y}\in  {\cal D}$ and $t>\tau\geq  0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.371388+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_933ed88baa527c953e4d5f3cb75c88f04e806b6fc16b732fb2d6ed46a35bbf45","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro thm: UB singlesitemarginals of arXiv:2411.13465, 'Height-offset variables and pinning at infinity for gradient Gibbs measures on trees'] Let $\nu$ be the free measure (or a GGM of height-period $2$ associated with some fuzzy chain $\bar{\mu}$, resp.)
