{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:15:54.946849+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_937225ed02a41f148f130110e23d2ee7abec4e0eaa0cb2b3a9f4c2a4a615adb6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:iglbox-frame-conditions of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] Let $\mathfrak{F} = (W, \leq, \sqsubset)$ be an f-frame, and put ${\sqsubset_\beta} \coloneq (\sqsubset \cdot \leq)$.
  When $\mathfrak{F}$ is $\Box$-p, this is the modal relation of its $\Box$-condensation $\beta \mathfrak{F}$.
  \begin{itemize}
    \item We write
          $\operatorname{Up}_{\leq}(W) \coloneq \set*{ A \subseteq W; \forall x,y\, (x \in A \mathrel{\text{\&}} x \leq y \mathrel{\Rightarrow} y \in A) }$
          for the set of all $\leq$-upsets of $W$.
    \item We say $\mathfrak{F}$ is \emph{$\sqsubset_\beta$-Noetherian}
          if for any $A \in \operatorname{Up}_{\leq}(W)$ such that $A \ne W$,
          there is $w_A \in W \setminus A$ such that $\forall v \in W\, (w_A \sqsubset_\beta v \mathrel{\Rightarrow} v \in A)$.
    \item We say $\mathfrak{F}$ is \emph{$\sqsubset_\beta$-strong} if ${\sqsubset_\beta} \subseteq {\leq}$,
          and is \emph{$\sqsubset$-strong} if ${\sqsubset} \subseteq {\leq}$.
  \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.613365+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9373461241997d3eccf6a4e2fb35b8160fd6f1bc86ff308179678da39a1ded82","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 51 of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] Define 
\begin{align*}
    \mathcal{A}_{n,1}^G &= \{|g_k|\le \log n,\quad 1\le k\le n\},\\
    \mathcal{A}_{n,2}^G &= \{ |Y_k-\sqrt{n-k}|\le  2 \beta^{-1/2}\sqrt{\log(\beta(n-k))},\quad 1\le k\le n-\lfloor\sqrt{n}\rfloor\},\\
    \mathcal{A}_{n,3}^G &= \{\sqrt{\tfrac{{n-k}}{\log n}}\le Y_k\le \sqrt{(n-k)\log n},\quad n-\lfloor\sqrt{n}\rfloor\le k<n\}.
\end{align*}
    Let $\mathcal{A}_n^G=\mathcal{A}_{n,1}^G\cap \mathcal{A}_{n,2}^G\cap \mathcal{A}_{n,3}^G$, then  $\pr(\mathcal{A}_n^G)\ge 1- c_\beta(\log n)^{-\beta/2}$, where $c_\beta>0$ is independent of $n$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.289772+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9376756b29c968c4efa1e0319dd8c1034ac9c31f9e0ade8eec97657846f14fe9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:maindeifnition of arXiv:2411.02030, 'Finite ergodic components for upper probabilities'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},V,T)$ be an UPPS. The upper probability $V$ is said to be of finite ergodic components if there exists a partition $\alpha=\{A_1,\ldots,A_n\}\subset \mathcal{I}$, such that for each $i\in\{1,2,\ldots,n\}$, $V_i$  is an ergodic upper probability with respect to $T$ on $(\Omega,\mathcal{F})$, where 
	\begin{equation}
		V_i(A):=\sup\{P(A):P\in\operatorname{core}(V)\text{ and } P(A_i)=1\}\text{ for any }A\in\mathcal{F}.
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:44.459892+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93774a713de5fbbc399df42ba797ba778d23d0dee5ecb7a7febeb2a525b19da9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2609.03191, 'On lifting representations and actions on curves of the metacyclic groups $C_{p^s}\rtimes '] Suppose that $\chi$ is injective and $m$ is even. Let $\mathcal B$ be a field of characteristic $0$. We consider a short exact sequence of $\mathcal B[G]$-modules
