{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.625340+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9381f176f7cdd071cd60a7fb1c0139ac1d856a65e18701e8ea09ebb9c34651db","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem of arXiv:2411.09988, 'A Study in Markov Chains, Loop-Erased Random Walk and Loop Soups'] Suppose $x \in A$, $V \subset \partial A$ and $H_A(x,V)>0$. Let $\{X_n\}$ be the Markov chain started at $x$ and $T =\min\{k\geq0:X_k \in \partial A\}$. Then for $y \in A_x \cup V$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{P}^x\{X_1=y \mid X_T \in V, x \notin \{X_1, \ldots, X_{T-1}\}\} = \frac{p(x,y)H_{A_x}(y, V)}{H_{\partial A_x}(x, V)}.
    \end{equation*}
    Here $A_x = A \backslash \{x\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.035223+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93824f260b0ecf92365a8e0e279cd44e607f389441aae082e6207db4edd224e3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6t2.2 of arXiv:2609.03926, 'Overcolored Partition $k$-tuples Restricted by Parity of the Parts'] {wom}}}]
