        Hence $m_{\rm fc}=m$, and the rectangular free convolution of $\bnu_0$ with the Mar\v{c}enko--Pastur law at time $t$ and aspect ratio $c_N$ coincides with $\bnu$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.331924+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93869fd9eda65f8cee5f3215f8399a388d30d8140310ab6b3ed8f722f18534c6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition d: fourier smoooth of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Let $p\in[-d, \infty)$ and $f\in L^1(\R^d, \C)$. Suppose that there is a $c>0$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        |\hat{f}(k)| \leq c \frac{1}{(1+\|k\|)^{\frac{d+p}{2}}}, \quad k\in\R^d.
    \end{equation}
    If $p\leq 0$, then also suppose that, as $r\to\infty$,
    \begin{equation}
        \int_{B_2^c} \sup_{s\in B_1} |\hat{f}(r(k+s))|^2\, dk = O(r^{-(d+p)}).
    \end{equation}
    Then $f$ is called \textit{Fourier-smooth with exponent} $p$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.746260+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9388afbed6d99e71ccd1fdb2556d78e5c6d10d76cf698ce14cb8322cd86a0479","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Define 7 of arXiv:2506.10522, 'On the Law of the Iterated Logarithm for $m$-dependent stationary random variables under s'] A  countably sub-additive extension $\Vstar$  of $\hV$   is defined by
