where $\hV$ is defined as in \eqref{eq1.5}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.316411+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9389225e8f97dbf3fa73779fe3536b403e9e75a553618f3bbc9c65450ae735d5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2506.20411, 'Maximal Counts in the Stopped Occupancy Problem'] For every $K\in{\mathbb Z}_{>0}$, as $n\to\infty$,
