{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.762369+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_938c457bc6340d872f6bbc175e52f0731949c878737e7496a60a11cc5a02623a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lmm eq:rooted-L2 of arXiv:2609.02682, 'LDP for tensor forms'] Under the setting of (lem:uniform-core-reduction-ER of the paper), let $K, K'$ be two consecutive  intermediate graphs in the leaf-removal procedure, such that $V(K)=V(K')\cup \{u\}$, where  $u$ is the chosen leaf as in the proof of (lem:uniform-core-reduction-ER of the paper) above. Then, with $\mathcal N(\cdot;d)$ as defined above, we have
