{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.570574+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93c673981b22b8c9315e0ace179b4fc1ef88b98056278bb27e009aae0e6fe25f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:edge-iso of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For $t \leq t_* = N^{-1/3+\varepsilon}$ and $z = E + i\eta$ with $|E-2| \leq N^{-2/3+\varepsilon}$ and $N^{-2/3} \leq \eta \leq 1$, we have for any deterministic $\mathbf{q} \perp \mathbf{e}$ with $\|\mathbf{q}\| = 1$:
