{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.967049+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_941c67aa7dcdc4c9202ce01dee273298e90d626684ce079d0d8fb0f74a5f1bea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 36 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {McDiarmid's via Hellinger Integrals (Theorem 1, \cite{esposito:mondelli2023})}


    Let $\nu$ on $\Omega^n$ be a probability measure with marginals $\nu_i$ on $\Omega$. Let $\nu \ll \otimes_{i=1}^n \nu_i$ and $f : \Omega \to \R$ fulfill the bounded differences property with constants $c := (c_1,...,c_n)\T$. Then, for $t > 0$ and $\alpha > 1$, 
    \begin{align*}
