{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.632974+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_946d59c0d0182e218b47c0f426bdf65c9904010e403ab73b2512096ad0842c13","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2605.17155, '2605.17155'] Let \(B\) be a Banach space and let \(f:\Nzero\to B\) be almost
periodic.  For every \(\eta>0\) there is \(L=L(f,\eta)\) such that, for
every \(h\geq0\), some \(r\in\{0,\dots,L\}\) satisfies
\begin{equation*}
   \sup_{m\geq0}
   \norm{(f(m+h)-f(h))-(f(m+r)-f(r))}<\eta .
