{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.569194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_947f34e942ad7e6aa6ec270a88942e895ecce41bd8787343322db534860d6bd6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2606.14170, 'Uniform-in-time error estimates for McKean-Vlasov SDEs with common noise and stochastic al'] Suppose that $\mathbb{E}|X_0^i|^q<\infty$ for all $i\in\mathbb{S}_N$ and some $q>1$. Let Assumptions \ref{A1} and \ref{A2}  hold with $\lambda_1>2\lambda_2$, then there exists $C>0$ such that for any $L\in[0,L^*]$, $i\in\mathbb{S}_N$ and $\varepsilon>0$,
