{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.841326+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94aae91d42651b4e8024310aecf23d6ae9368da15c9b8443fb9894c14e3e45a8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Satz 3 of arXiv:2506.13661, 'Box-Covariances of Hyperuniform Point Processes'] Let $\eta$ be a hyperuniform point process satisfying the assumptions of Theorem \ref{thm:Cov_integrable} for $d\ge2$, Theorem \ref{thm:Cov_non_int} for $d=1$ and $a>0$, or that of Theorem \ref{thm:Cov_non_int_2} below. 
