{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.299328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94dab30213bcfce63971357ca75e39d549f8bc7651e70ff6194301c3f10832a2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] For every measurable set $A$ of $\mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$, we set 
	\begin{align*}
		\underline s(A)&=\liminf_{n\to \infty}\frac 1n \log \mathbb P(L_n\in A),\\
		\overline s(A)&=\limsup_{n\to \infty}\frac 1n \log \mathbb P(L_n\in A).
	\end{align*}
	Let $\mu\in \mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$.
	We set \begin{align*}
		\underline{s}(\mu)&=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\underline s(\mathcal B_{\mathrm{LP}}(\mu,\delta)),\\
		\overline{s}(\mu)&=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\overline s(\mathcal B_{\mathrm{LP}}(\mu,\delta)).
	\end{align*}
	If $\underline s(\mu)=\overline s(\mu)$, we set $I_{\mathrm{RL}}(\mu)=-\underline{s}(\mu)=-\overline s(\mu)$ and we say that the \emph{Ruelle-Lanford function} of $(L_n)$ exists at $\mu$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.995778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94db34efae0909e661a58d2512cdc59ce36d159c6cb364c2cede9b6de083d61d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm P typ gau of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] There exist a deterministic constant $c_1\in(0,\infty)$
