{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.060044+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94e850a8b71480113a2e51193b260aa7a7b5f65cd76b46ded618f48e92222d71","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:coupl of arXiv:2412.04032, 'Cutoff for the mixing time of the Facilitated Exclusion Process'] [lacoin_simple_2017] Assume that $P=P(K)$ goes to infinity with $K$, and $P\le K/2$ for all $K$. Let $\sigma \sim \pi^{\textsc{ssep}}_{K,P}$, let $x \in \mathbb{Z}$ and $H \ge 0$. Let $\zeta^{(1)}=\zeta^{(1),H} = \Psi(x+H, \sigma)$ and $\zeta^{(2)}=\zeta^{(2),H} = \Psi(x-H, \sigma)$. Notice that $\zeta^{(1)} \ge \zeta^{(2)}$. 
For all $s>0$ and $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, there exists $C(s,\varepsilon)>0$ such that if $H \le s \sqrt{P}$, for all $t \ge C(s, \varepsilon) K^2$,
\eqs{\mathbb{Q}_{(\zeta^{(1)}, \zeta^{(2)})}\left(\zeta^{(1)}(t) \neq \zeta^{(2)}(t)\right) \le \varepsilon,}
using the same coupling as before. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.898653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94ea87ac27aac909b0a638c13ead5f9688936e98a56565866b755586b27cd3a0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 (Solving Nekrasov equations, example with two bands) of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Take eight real parameters satisfying
\[
