{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.960265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94f83d7d44d9c9d1a913461062d23c8846a8529309e8224ec4ea798283a4d97e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 (Exponential Young convolution) of arXiv:2608.08177, 'Uniform-in-Time Smoluchowski--Kramers Approximation\\ in Total Variation for Fractional SD'] Let $w\in C^\gamma([0,\infty))$, $\gamma\in(0,1)$, and
\[
  R_t^\mu(w)=\int_0^t e^{-(t-s)/\mu}\,dw_s.
\]
For every $t\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 |R_t^\mu(w)|
 \le C_\gamma\mu^\gamma
 \sum_{j=0}^{\lfloor t\rfloor}
 e^{-j/(2\mu)}
 [w]_{\gamma;I_{t,j}},
\end{equation}
where
$I_{t,j}=[(t-j-1)\vee0,(t-j)\vee0]$ and empty intervals are omitted.
Consequently, if $w=B^H$ and $p\ge1$, then
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{t\ge0}\norm{R_t^\mu(B^H)}_{L^p(\Omega)}
  \le C_{p,\gamma,H}\mu^\gamma.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.906609+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94f85bf6b0f888b2e358a6ee0bbcc5b54173a842b452f2392135f4922bc44ffc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] For all integers $r,i$,
