{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.758650+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9550a5a64360d57ab6ee9b257da81be6cd8e25d90dbd12f8f89e7d9929297bd0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def fourier of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $d\in \mathds{N}$, $p,q\in (0,\infty]$, $s \in\mathds{R}$.

An \emph{admissible weight} [Triebel2008] is a function $w\in C^{\infty}(\mathds{R}^d,\mathds{R})$ such that for every multiindex $\gamma\in\mathds{N}_0^d$, there exists a constant $c_\gamma>0$ such that the partial derivative $D^\gamma w$ of $w$ satisfies
\begin{equation*}
\left\lvertD^\gamma w(x)\right\rvert\leq c_\gamma w(x)\qquad \text{for all}\qquad x\in\mathds{R}^d,
\end{equation*}
and there exist $c>0$ and $\alpha\geq 0$ such that
\begin{equation*}
0<w(x)\leq cw(y)(1+\left\lVertx-y\right\rVert_2^2)^{\frac{\alpha}{2}} \qquad \text{for all}\qquad x,y\in\mathds{R}^d.
\end{equation*}

If $(\varphi_j)_{j\in\mathds{N}_0}$ is a suitable resolution of unity, cf.~[Triebel2008], then the \emph{(weighted) Besov space} $B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$ is defined as the collection of all $f\in \mathcal{S}^\prime(\mathds{R}^d)$ such that
\begin{equation*}
\left\lVertf\right\rVert_{B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)}\mathrel{\mathop:}=\lr{\sum_{j\in\mathds{N}_0} 2^{jsq}\mnorm{w\cdot(\varphi_j\hat{f})^\vee}_{L_p(\mathds{R}^d)}^q}^{\frac{1}{q}}<\infty,
\end{equation*}
with the usual modifications for $q=\infty$, see [Triebel2008].
(This definition makes sense since $\varphi_j\hat{f}\in\mathcal{S}^\prime(\mathds{R}^d)$ is a compactly supported distribution so that $(\varphi_j\hat{f})^\vee\in C^\infty(\mathds{R}^d)$ is a (smooth) function by the Paley--Wiener theorem.) 

Define $T_0\mathrel{\mathop:}= \left\{F\right\}^d$, $T_j\mathrel{\mathop:}=\left\{F,M\right\}^d\setminus T_0$ for $j\in\mathds{N}$, 
\begin{equation*}
J\mathrel{\mathop:}=\setcond{(j,t,m)}{j\in\mathds{N}_0,t\in T_j,m\in\mathds{Z}^d},
\end{equation*}
 and for a sequence $a=(a_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in J}\in \mathds{R}^J$, following [Triebel2008] with a slight modification, we let
\begin{equation*}
\left\lVerta\right\rVert_{b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)}\mathrel{\mathop:}= \mnorm{\lr{2^{j(s+\frac{d}{2}-\frac{d}{p})}\mnorm{\lr{w(2^{-(j-\delta_{j\neq 0})}m)\abs{a_{j,t,m}}}_{m\in\mathds{Z}^d}}_{\ell_p}}_{j\in\mathds{N}_0,t\in T_j}}_{\ell_q},
\end{equation*}
where $\delta_{j\neq 0}=1$ if $j\neq 0$ and $\delta_{j\neq 0}=0$ if $j=0$.
The \emph{(weighted) Besov sequence space} $b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$ is defined as the collection of all sequences $(a_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in J}\in\mathds{R}^J$ such that $\left\lVerta\right\rVert_{b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)}<\infty$.
We write $B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)\mathrel{\mathop:}= B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$ and  $b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d)\mathrel{\mathop:}= b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$ when $w(x)=1$ for all $x\in\mathds{R}^d$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.572903+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9550f4442f82cd6b785e6d0113aa135a59d51ec39ecbb7cdf1ea77f684b6c801","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 32 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:basic} and~\ref{ass:rand_ent}, for every deterministic vector $\bbx\in\C^L$,
