{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.970313+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95756d8c73d313011edd5b376d7a862b276f7e350fce4909d9501226d1bcbce0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main-fixed of arXiv:2608.19050, 'Online Permutation Embedding: \\ Optimal Stopping and Scaling Laws'] Let $\pi \in \Pi_k$ and let $\mathcal{A}^*\in\mathrm{OA}(\pi)$ denote (alg:canonical-general2 of the paper). Then
    \begin{equation}
        \E{T_{\mathcal{A}^*}}=\beta(\pi),
    \end{equation}
    and, furthermore, for some universal constant $C > 0$,
    \begin{equation}
        \PP[\mathcal{S}]{|T_{\mathcal{A}^*} - \beta(\pi)| > y \,\beta(\pi)^{3/4}} \le C\,y^{-2}\,, \qquad y \ge 1 \,. 
    \end{equation}
    Conversely, for any $\mathcal{A} \in \mathrm{OA}(\pi)$ and any $\delta \in (0,1)$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \PP[\mathcal{S}]{T_\mathcal{A} \le (1-\delta)\beta(\pi) } \le 1-\delta\,.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.246601+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9579c5395c2e001b85728b3726b20cb73c51703c3fb828227a9fc9c4f4ccaa7e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 29 (Augmented liquid region) of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Given  $\delta > 0$ and $N \ge 1$,
