{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.500491+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95b18be1091cad064c8af90ee536222d250f537f3721d6cf3a1699dcdcc60808","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 (Quasi-multiplicativity) of arXiv:2605.30030, 'Critical exponents for planar random-cluster model with cluster-weight~$q=4$'] For every~$1\leq r\leq \rho\leq R$, 
\begin{align}
    \pi_1(r,R)&\asymp \pi_1(r,\rho)\pi_1(\rho,R), \\
     \pi_2(r,R)&\asymp \pi_2(r,\rho)\pi_2(\rho,R), \\
 \Delta(r,R)&\asymp  \Delta(r,\rho)\Delta(\rho,R). 

\end{align}
Moreover,~$\pi_1(R) \asymp \pi_1(1,R)$,~$\pi_2(R) \asymp \pi_2(1,R)$ and~$\Delta(R) \asymp \Delta(1,R)$.

Finally, there exists $c > 0$ such that, for any $1\leq r \leq R$, $\pi_2(r,R)  \leq \pi_1(r,R)^2\leq \pi_1(r,R)\big(\frac{r}R\big)^c$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.613508+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95b1ca843227dd209770934e531d372a93d9bff55c44878b80768563580f0da7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 53 of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] For  $k\ge n_1$ and for $n$ large enough we have 
\begin{align*}
\Big\{\frac{u_k}{u_{k-1}}\ge 1\Big\}\cap\mathcal{A}_n^G \subset \left\{\frac{u_{k+1}}{u_k}>1+\min\Big\{\tfrac12\sqrt{\tfrac{k}{n-k}},n^{1/4}\Big\}\right\}\cap\mathcal{A}_n^G.
