{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.182152+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95bc150442870e91f24ab718643ae727319df346689d6f76d2ef24aa3e41a648","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:MetricComparison of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Fix $\delta > 0$. Then, for all $\eta, \zeta \in \mathrm{Macro}(\delta)$, and $n \in \mathbb{N}$ sufficiently large, we have
