{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.418151+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95c8dbe6c2547b52e509852ee8910e7528de3d67b88335faf78ee133ca35e06e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma UcupU of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] Suppose $s, s'\in \mathbb{R}$ with $s< s'$ and $h, h'\in \mathbb{R}^+$ for which $U^{s}_{h}\cap U^{s'}_{h'}\neq \emptyset$ and $\exists h_1\geq 0$ such that $ \partial^*U^{s}_{h}\cap \partial^*U^{s'}_{h'}= \{(0, h_1)\}$. Then we have 

\begin{align}
\left\vert U^{s}_{h}\cup U^{s'}_{h'}\right\vert&=
\begin{cases}
    \frac{\pi}{2}h^2+{\frac{1}{2}} h_1(s'-s)+{\frac{1}{2}} F_1(h_1, h, h'), &\text{ if } s<s'<0,\\ 
    \frac{\pi}{2}(h^2+h'^2)+{\frac{1}{2}} h_1(s'-s)-{\frac{1}{2}} F_2(h_1, h, h'), &\text{ if } s<0<s',\\ 
    \frac{\pi}{2}h'^2+{\frac{1}{2}} h_1(s'-s)-{\frac{1}{2}} F_1(h_1, h, h'), &\text{ if }0<s<s',
\end{cases}

\end{align}

where 

\[
F_1(h_1, h, h')=h'^2\arcsin(h_1/h')- h^2\arcsin(h_1/h),\;\; F_2(h_1, h, h')=h'^2\arcsin(h_1/h')+h^2\arcsin(h_1/h).
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:14:37.599080+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95d242cf3cbd9409ee34421d0a7c780e974f36de9f9533c65fe89bf99f213cd8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2608.18688, 'Regularity Preservation for Jump-Type Stochastic Transport Equations with Singular Drift'] Take $\lambda, T>0$ and $p,q\in (1,\infty)$. For any $f\in \mL_p^q(T)$, there exists a unique solution $U\in \mH_p^{2,q}(T)$ to the backward parabolic system (\ref{Dackward-PDE1}). For this solution there exists a constant $C$ depending only on $d,p,q,T$ such that  for all $\lambda\geq 0$
\ce 
\|\nabla^2 U\|_{\mL_p^{q}([0,T])}\leq C\|f\|_{\mL_p^q([0,T])}
\de 
Moreover, for any $\vartheta\in[0,2)$ and $p'\in [p,\infty]$, $q'\in [q,\infty]$ satisfying 
\ce 
\frac{d}{p}+\frac{2}{q}<2-\vartheta+\frac{d}{p'}+\frac{2}{q'}
\de 
there exists a constant $C$ depending only on $d,p,q,T, p',q'$ such that  for all $\lambda>0$
\be 
\lambda^{\frac{1}{2}(2-\vartheta+\frac{d}{p'}+\frac{2}{q'}-\frac{d}{p}-\frac{2}{q})}
\|U\|_{\mW^{q'}_{\vartheta,p'}([0,T])}\leq  C\|f\|_{\mL_p^q([0,T])}.
\ee (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.744598+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95d508657db51f2f7beb1530b8521019358e3d68cd12d82ec154c1b9ee2b505a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Uniform Laplace principle of bridges) of arXiv:2511.14757, 'A weak convergence approach to the large deviations of the dynamic Schr\"odinger problem'] Under Assumptions \ref{ass:b-sigma-local-properties}--\ref{ass:log-gradient-convergence}, for any compact set $K \Subset D$,
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{\eta \downarrow 0} \sup_{x,y \in K} \left|-\eta \log \bE\left[\exp - \frac{1}{\eta} F(X^{\eta, xy}) \right] - \inf_{\varphi \in \calC_1} \left[F(\varphi) + I_B^{xy}(\varphi)\right]\right| = 0,
    \end{equation}
    where $X^{\eta, xy}$ is given by the dynamics \ref{eq:R-SDE-main-results}, conditioned on starting in $x$ at $t=0$ and ending in $y$ at $t=1$.
    The good rate function $I_B$ is given by
