{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.730256+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95f16ec74ec70692e194fb8ccdc77684ce96d9bd17a9910f741a94dee94dddcd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm1 9 of arXiv:2608.29797, 'Mean-field branching SDEs: propagation of chaos, scaling limits and phase transitions'] Suppose that Condition \ref{con2} holds.  Then, for every
$0<A<a_*$, there exist strictly positive constants
$C_1,C_2$ and $\lambda$, depending on $A$ and $\mu_0$, such that
for all $t\geq0$, $N\geq2$ and $a\in(0,A]$,
