{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:59:24.049462+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95f4e14d1eb70b01fe95e3746c086e20d58bfebfff2b124521916b2d259186ca","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:groundstate of arXiv:2608.30831, 'Sharp discrete Hardy constants in dimensions three and four\\ and strict upper bounds from'] Let $h>0$ on $\mathbb Z^N\setminus\{0\}$ and set $h(0)=0$.  For every finitely
supported $u$ with $u(0)=0$,
\begin{align}
 \mathcal E_N[u]
 &-\sum_{n\ne0}\frac{(-\Delta_{\!d} h)(n)}{h(n)}|u(n)|^2\notag\\
 &=\sum_{\substack{\{n,m\}\in E_N\\n,m\ne0}}
 h(n)h(m)
 \left|\frac{u(n)}{h(n)}-\frac{u(m)}{h(m)}\right|^2.
\end{align}
In particular, if
\begin{equation}
 |n|^2\frac{(-\Delta_{\!d} h)(n)}{h(n)}\ge\lambda
 \qquad(n\ne0),
