{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.431388+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96575342c5123d92aa1cbe642234f41310149737ed9ae8d35cef7586d6d6f198","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:sdp.certificate of arXiv:2604.22453, 'Adapted Wasserstein Barycenters of Gaussian Processes'] Let $t\in[T]$ and $\mathbf P_t\in\mathscr{P}_+(K,d)$. Suppose there exist symmetric matrices $Z_t^1,\ldots,Z_t^K\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$ such that
