{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.704165+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_966ee0891634d2fe5a700d59b6c4a2575cc460fb95289500e77a39584b2d2f8c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition PROP: gaussian-conc of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] There exists a constant $c>0$ such that for sufficiently small $\delta >0$
\begin{align}
