{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.788662+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_967bcf7c3568dc37a8de62c5a9a2a70694f3d4f3007895b4d1071f351231da2c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:tailrl-binary-recovery of arXiv:2609.02987, 'Tail Likelihood Reinforcement Learning'] When the reward function is binary, the tail-probabilities equal the probability of success and TailRL{} recovers MaxRL at every order of truncation. 

