{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.812703+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96a89283667bcb683080df0ce40d760d821915d1321036653ef1800b0c2c8e1d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma mgf-bound-light-traffic of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $\{\lambda_n\}$ be a sequence of positive numbers such that $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{\lambda_n}{n} = c$. Let $n \geq \max\left\{n_0,\frac{4}{\br{1-c}^2\br{1-\frac{1}{2e}}^2}\right\}$ where $n_0$ is an integer such that $\frac{\lambda_n}{n} \leq \frac{1}{2e} \, \forall n \geq n_0$ and $\nu_n$ be the stationary distribution of the $M/M/n$ system with arrival rate $\lambda_n$ and unit service rate. We have
    \begin{align}
