{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.971595+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96b80ccf480efd0fecf685cd612868d9c40a07b3fa36ecf703fddbf53240809f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:branching_formulas of arXiv:2412.05999, 'Non-Archimedean GUE corners and Hecke modules'] (Branching rule) For $\lambda=(\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_n)\in \Sig_n^+, \mu=(\mu_1,\ldots,\mu_{n-1}) \in \Sig_{n-1}^+$ with $\mu \prec_P \lambda$, let
