{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.204786+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96bba780d7abfe531da75b7e51bdf1c4eb95552e779e5acb9c6210ae18a8bdaa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2512.09077, 'Negative moments of Steinhaus sums'] Let $0 < p < 1$ and $\Phi_p$ be defined in \eqref{eq:def-Phi}. For all $n \geq 2$, $z_2, \dots, z_n \in \C$, we have
