 \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.242959+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96bfcff43e4b20abb39b8bec1ae639cc889d1ca853172c4f6c6616cbbfcba6b0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2604.15152, 'The Multinomial Allocation Model and the Random Box Load'] Denote
\[Q_n(r,t):=(r!t!)^{-1}\rE\Big[\xi^r\eta^t(1-q_X-q_Y)^{n-r-t}\Big],\]
where $\eta=nq_Y$.
Then
\begin{equation}
Q_n(r,t)=\rE[p_r(\xi)]\rE[p_t(\xi)]+n^{-1}(r! t!)^{-1}\rE\Big[\xi^r\eta^t\delta_n(r+t,\xi+\eta)\Big],
\end{equation}
 and 
\begin{align}
 Q_n(r,t)&=\rE[p_r(\xi)]\rE[p_t(\xi)]+n^{-1}\Big((r+t)\big(\rE[p_r(\xi)]\rE[p_t(\xi)\xi]+\rE[p_t(\xi)]\rE[p_r(\xi)\xi]\big)-\rE[p_r(\xi)\xi]\rE[p_t(\xi)\xi]\Big) \nonumber\\
&-(2n)^{-1}\Big(\rE[p_r(\xi)]\rE[p_t(\xi)\xi^2]+\rE[p_t(\xi)]\rE[p_r(\xi)\xi^2]\Big)+n^{-2}(r!t!)^{-1}\rE\Big[\xi^r\eta^r \delta_n^*(r+t,\xi+\eta)\Big]. 
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.304360+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96c175b464be6fe3952a95f4bb497088654435094bc6112966e9f55e523ecd6e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 (Lemma 3.4 in \cite{gotze2021concentration}) of arXiv:2606.24090, 'Sparsity-adaptive concentration inequalities for random polynomials'] Let $A=(a_\mathbf{i})_{\mathbf{i}\in[n]^d}$ be a $d$-tensor, $I\subseteq [d]$ and $\mathbf{i}_I\in [n]^{|I|}$ fixed. Then for any $\mathcal{K}\in \Pi_d$ and $\mathcal{J}\in \Pi(I^c)$,
