    \frac{e^{-bt/n}}{2} \leq\gamma_n^t \leq 2 e^{-bt/n} .
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:25:35.679079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96ccf502cb20cce4f544acfb742892c4022921b4d7a94d349f6ddc8209574484","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition many_events_C of arXiv:2603.05491, '\textbf{Local limits of uniform triangulations with boundaries in high genus}'] Fix $n,g,\ell \ge 0$ and $(p_1,\cdots,p_{\ell}) \in (\mathbb{N}^{*})^{\ell}$. We also fix $t \in \mathcal{T}_{\mathbf{p}}(n,g)$ and $\varepsilon > 0,p\ge 4$. Suppose that there exist distinct edges $e_1,\cdots,e_{1000\varepsilon |\mathbf{p}|}$ on $\partial_1\cup \cdots \cup \partial_{\ell}$ such that for all $1 \le j \le 1000\varepsilon |\mathbf{p}|$:
\begin{center}
$(t,e_j)$ satisfies $(\mathcal{O})$ or $(\mathcal{H}_{2\varepsilon^{-1} p })$.
\end{center}  
Then one of the following two statements holds:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item There exists $I \subset \{1,\cdots,1000\varepsilon |\mathbf{p}|\}$ such that $r:= |I| \ge \varepsilon p^{-1}|\mathbf{p}|$ and denoting by $f_{i}$ for the triangle that lies behind the edge $e_{i}$, we have $t \backslash \bigg(\bigsqcup_{i\in I}f_i\bigg) \in \mathcal{T}_{\mathbf{q}}(n',g')$ for some $\mathbf{q} = (q_1,\cdots,q_{\ell'})$, where $(\ell-\ell')+2(g-g')= r $ and $n' \le n + |\mathbf{p}|$.
        \item There are more than $\varepsilon|\mathbf{p}|$ edges $e \in \partial t$ such that $(t,e)$ satisfies $(\mathcal{C}_{\varepsilon^{-1},p})$.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.524844+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96cfa43ee78d541e40cf7dc99e4b4410796166aabf4aed5bcfd341c9084755a3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{lem:non_integrable_limits}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 2$, and let $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ be the transitive kernel given by $J(x,y) = d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha}$ for $\alpha > 0$.

    Let $(G_n)_{n \in \mathbf{N}}$ be a sequence of transitive graphs and let $(J_n)_{n \in \mathbf{N}}$ be the sequence of transitive kernels given by $J_n(x,y) = d_G(x,y)^{-\dim(G_n) \alpha_n}$ with $\alpha_n > 1$.

    If the sequence $(G_n,J_n)_{n \in \mathbf{N}}$ converges locally to $(G,J)$, then $\alpha = \lim_{n \to \infty} \alpha_n\dim(G_n)/ d$.

    In particular, if $\limsup_{n \to \infty} \dim(G_n)<d$ and $\limsup_{n\to \infty} \alpha_n< d/\limsup_{n \to \infty} \dim(G_n)$ then $\alpha<1$ and the pairs $(G_n,J_n)$ are integrable for all $n$, but not uniformly integrable, and the pair $(G,J)$ is not integrable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.334924+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96cfda9346ab9906c2fa893e9821ccd6390f5617548fbe90d0636b5d4bd24df9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2608.30409, 'Gradient estimates and volume doubling for locally finite weighted graphs with $CD\psi(n,-'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a locally finite weighted graph and let $\psi\in C^1(0,+\infty)$ be a concave function with $H_{\psi}<\infty$. Suppose $0<g\in \mathbb{R}^{V}$. Then for any $x\sim y$, 
    \begin{equation*}
        \log\frac{g\left(y\right)}{g\left(x\right)}\leq\sqrt{H_\psi \frac{\mu_{\max}}{w_{\min}}}\sqrt{\Gamma^{\psi}\left(g\right)\left(x\right)}.
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.368791+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96d1c9d424ddaf5d5455f01a921465be8fcb10988e7b1c1cf5849bfaf2cf6677","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 (Mellin quotient and uniqueness) of arXiv:2606.18458, 'Stable size-biasing and the positive scale-mixture order of generalized Gaussian laws'] Let $p,q>0$. If $V>0$, $V\perp X_q$, and $X_p\stackrel{d}{=}VX_q$, then, for every $t\in\R$,
\begin{equation}
\E V^{it}=\frac{2^{it/p}\Gamma((1+it)/p)\Gamma(1/q)}{2^{it/q}\Gamma((1+it)/q)\Gamma(1/p)}=:\Phi_{p,q}(t).

\end{equation}
Consequently, whenever a strictly positive independent factor exists, its law is unique.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.075990+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96d1d6844b2f88b38c3b16b4b5370532161c97d6c896dbeffc8b0ca7face3d0b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Laplacian-approximation-local of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Consider an s-embedding $\mathcal{S}^{(t)}(\Lambda_{n})$ constructed by Lemma (lem:SDE-embedding of the paper) and a real function $\phi$. Then, with $\mathbf{P}$-probability at least $1-O(n^{-4})$, there exist a constant $O=O(\omega,\alpha)>0$ such that for any $0\leq t \leq t^{(\alpha)}_n$,
