where the supremum are taken in a disc of size $10\delta$ around $v$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.859722+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96d64aacf97961f23515c0719fec976c12fa2cc7562145eef75ec2594ac5ab63","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 10 of arXiv:2608.21090, 'Ornstein--Uhlenbeck process conditioned to have restricted $L_2$-norm'] For each $i=1,\ldots,7$ there exist a $f^{(i)}=f^{(i)}_{\beta,K}(T)\geq 0$ and a $T^{(i)}>T^{(0)}$ such that,
