{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.128688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96ece8f7d344183a6e26d81d157eced2c4a49f4af6d0ba1acd0cfea165444ea1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p.growth of arXiv:2505.07145, 'Nonamenable Poisson zoo'] Consider a Poisson zoo on an infinite transitive graph $G$ with intensity $\lambda>0$ and a lattice animal measure $\nu_o$ that has unbounded support. Assume further that there exist constants $0 < c_1(G,\lambda), c_2(G), C(R) < \infty$ and a function $\vartheta \, : \, \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$ with $\lim_{R \to \infty} \vartheta(R) = \infty$ such that for any $R \in \mathbb{N}$ and for any finite connected subset $A \subset \subset V(G)$ of vertices and any subset $B \subseteq \partial_{\mathrm{ext}} A$ of its exterior boundary for the restricted process of Definition~(def:point_measure_restricted_to_hit_B_but_not_the_closure_of_A of the paper), we have
\begin{equation}

	\mathbb{E} \left[ \left| \mathrm{Tr} \left( \check{ \mathcal{X} }_{A,B}^R \right) \right| \right] \geq 
	c_1(G,\lambda)  \cdot \vartheta(R) \cdot \big[ c_2(G) \cdot |A| - \left( | \partial_{\mathrm{ext}} A | - |B|  \right) \big]
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}

	\mathrm{Var} \left( \left| \mathrm{Tr} \left( \check{ \mathcal{X} }_{A,B}^R \right) \right| \right) \leq
	C(R) \cdot \mathbb{E} \left[ \left| \mathrm{Tr} \left( \check{ \mathcal{X} }_{A,B}^R \right) \right| \right].
