{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.029520+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97704245517ca98366b87c62243cfa424cc3927eb7bdc2fa2199aed00ca5e73f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2609.00736, 'Modalities in non-classical variations of S4'] We say that a $\csf$-model $M = \tuple{W, W^\bot, \preceq, \R, V}$ is:
