{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.135350+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_980831c8e0a0427e4a0b213daa4cee0e64956d63d4903b169884b4a4a8890e95","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 1 of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] For any simple path $\gamma = (x_t,y_t)$, if $\gamma|_{[0,1]}$ has infinite radius of convergence for its log-signature and $x_t\in[-1,1]$ for all $t\in[0,1]$, then looking at any fixed horizontal level $y=a$ of the image $\gamma([0,1])$, we only have the following two cases: 
\begin{itemize}
       \item The right street copies the left street. In the sense that for any $x\in(0,1)$, $(x,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$, we have $(x-1,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$. For any $x\in(-1,0)$, $(x,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$ we have $(x+1,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$.

       \item Both capture the missing points of the other. In the sense that for any $x\in(0,1)$, $(x,a)\notin\gamma([0,1])$, we have $(x-1,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$. For any $x\in(-1,0)$, $(x,a)\notin\gamma([0,1])$, we have $(x+1,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.659522+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9809148171d19c9f9ee8cde7d730a882d60f214a913b6c3415c163a6b9394c71","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem uniform-lln-horizon of arXiv:2604.07183, 'Stopping on the last success with unknown odds: asymptotic minimax optimality of the plug-'] Let~$(p_n)$ be a sequence in~$(0,1)$ such that~$p_n\to 0$ and~$np_n\to\infty$.
Consider
\begin{equation}
I_n:=\Bigl\{t\in\{1,\dots,n\}:\ t\ge t_n \Bigr\},
\end{equation}
where~$t_n\in\{1,\ldots,n\}$ for any~$n$ and~$n/t_n=O(1)$. 
Then, there exist positive constants~$C,c$ such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb P
\bigg[
\sup_{t\in I_n}\Bigl|\frac{\hat p_t}{p_n}-1\Bigr| > \varepsilon
\bigg]
\le

C
e^{-c\varepsilon^2 np_n}
\end{equation}
for all~$\varepsilon\in(0,1)$ and all~$n$ large enough. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.702226+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98129af18778f56c4cc3e8ac824b62680ff3ae50afa5763d2a0868c1f6de52e5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 (Localized mixed-energy identities) of arXiv:2609.02193, 'State-law dynamics of McKean-Vlasov stochastic reaction-diffusion equations on $\mathbb R^'] Let $I=[a,b]$ and let $\zeta\in W^{1,\infty}(\mathbb R^n)$ be real valued. Suppose that
	\begin{align*}
		w\in C(I;H)\cap L^2(I;V)\cap L^p(I;L^p(\mathbb R^n))
	\end{align*}
	and, in $\mathcal D'(a,b;\mathbb V^*)$,
	\begin{align*}
		\frac{dw}{dt}=F_2+F_p,
		\qquad
		F_2\in L^2(I;V^*),
		\quad
		F_p\in L^{p'}(I;L^{p'}(\mathbb R^n)).
	\end{align*}
	Then, for $a\leq r\leq s\leq b$,
	\begin{align}
		\|\zeta w(s)\|^2-\|\zeta w(r)\|^2
		=2\int_r^s\Big[
		\langle F_2(\tau),\zeta^2w(\tau)\rangle_{V^*,V}
		+\langle F_p(\tau),\zeta^2w(\tau)\rangle_{L^{p'},L^p}
		\Big]d\tau.
	\end{align}
	If $U$ is progressively measurable,
	\begin{align*}
		U\in L^2(\Omega;C(I;H))
		\cap L^2(\Omega\times I;V)
		\cap L^p(\Omega\times I;L^p(\mathbb R^n)),
	\end{align*}
	and, in $\mathbb V^*$, $\mathbb P$-a.s.,
	\begin{align*}
		U(t)=U(a)+\int_a^t(F_2(s)+F_p(s))ds
		+\sum_{j=1}^{m}\int_a^t\sigma_j(s)dW_j(s),
	\end{align*}
	where $F_2\in L^2(\Omega\times I;V^*)$, $F_p\in L^{p'}(\Omega\times I;L^{p'}(\mathbb R^n))$ and $\sigma_j\in L^2(\Omega\times I;H)$ are progressively measurable, then, up to indistinguishability,
	\begin{align}
		\|\zeta U(t)\|^2
		&=\|\zeta U(a)\|^2
		+2\int_a^t\Big[
		\langle F_2(s),\zeta^2U(s)\rangle_{V^*,V}
		+\langle F_p(s),\zeta^2U(s)\rangle_{L^{p'},L^p}
		\Big]ds\notag\\
		&\quad
		+\sum_{j=1}^{m}\int_a^t\|\zeta\sigma_j(s)\|^2ds
		+2\sum_{j=1}^{m}\int_a^t
		(\zeta U(s),\zeta\sigma_j(s))dW_j(s).
	\end{align}
	The same formula is valid under the corresponding local integrability assumptions after stopping-time localization.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.298853+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9812cd3ed1c3a0d87fa7a9f5fdaa8fa53b741ededdaaf3e5c62f300015d72e5c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $\mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$ denote the set of probability measures equipped with its weak topology and the corresponding Borel $\sigma$-algebra.
	We say that $(L_n)$ satisfies the full LDP (resp. weak LDP) in the weak topology if there exists a lower semicontinuous function $I$, called the rate function, such that all open subsets $O$ and all closed subsets $F$ (resp. compact subsets $F$) of $\mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$ satisfy
	\begin{align}
		\liminf_{n\to \infty}\frac 1n\log \mathbb P(L_n\in O)&\geqslant -\inf_{\mu\in O}I(\mu),
		\\\limsup_{n\to \infty}\frac 1n\log \mathbb P(L_n\in F)&\leqslant -\inf_{\mu\in F}I(\mu).
	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.702922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9815036a71f9496d6aa2d9cd69947ea385ba3e788ec0e8d58614b3edfb7197da","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2608.06038, 'Efron type identities\\ for stopping sets and Poisson hulls'] Let $B\in\cX_0$ and let $f\colon \bN\times\R_+\to\R_+$ be measurable
  and $k\in\N_0$.  Then
  \begin{displaymath}

    \BE \big[\I\{\eta_Z(\BX)<\infty\}
    f\big(\eta_Z,\lambda_{Z^c}(B)\big)\eta_{Z^c}(B)^{(k)}\big]
    =\int f(\mu,t)t^k\,\lambda^*_B(d(\mu,t)).
  \end{displaymath}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.330120+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9815a92671f524f8d8363992a7b57a516d41831e8f3b4be687e00b2d121b6af7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Splev-cc of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] The global $\infty$-category ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}$ is globally presentable.
    \begin{proof}
        We begin by proving that ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}$ is fiberwise presentable. For this we note once more that if $G$ is any compact Lie group, then ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G})$ is presentable by Proposition~(prop:mySplev-unpar-presh of the paper). Let now $V$ be any $H$-representation; by the previous lemma $\ev_V\colon{\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G})\to{{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_{\textup{$(G\times H)$-gl},*}$ is cocontinuous. Thus, in the naturality square
        \[
            \begin{tikzcd}
                {\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G'})\arrow[d,"\ev_V"']\arrow[r,"f^*"] & {\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G})\arrow[d,"\ev_V"]\\
                {{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_{\text{$(G'\times H)$-gl},*}\arrow[r,"f^*"'] & {{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_{\text{$(G\times H)$-gl},*} 
            \end{tikzcd}
        \]
        all maps except possibly the top one preserve colimits. As for varying $V$ the right-hand vertical maps are jointly conservative, also $f^*\colon{\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G'})\to{\mathpalette\ulhelper{{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{lvl}(\mathbb B{G})$ is cocontinuous, hence a left adjoint by the Adjoint Functor Theorem.

