{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.214406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_981a5fdb2886062fd443948705ddde17193053e7befc0842603ec013907054c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:covreperror of arXiv:2411.16366, 'Connections between sequential Bayesian inference and evolutionary dynamics'] Assume the system properties described by (equation eq:realhidden of the paper) for the true hidden state, (equation eq:asshidden of the paper) for the assumed hidden state and (equation eq:obs of the paper) for the observation model.  Given $r,s$ such that $r <s, r >0$, we have the following evolution equations for the  error covariance $P_t$ and expected squared error $\tilde{P}_t$,
\begin{align}

