where $K_t$ is the continuous time Kalman gain matrix as defined in (equation eq:kalmangain of the paper).  For the special case $s=0,r=1$, it holds that $P_t = C_t, \enskip \forall \enskip t > 0$ if $P_0 = C_0$ where $C_t$ is the solution of the covariance equation of the replicator-mutator.\\
