{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:29:28.003329+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_989adabc4bcbf0d22c78ef691aac290f728547e599961f77ed11fbee075bb5ac","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 30 (Conditional entropy inequality with an additive defect) of arXiv:2608.24863, 'Uniform Logarithmic Sobolev Inequalities for the 2D Coulomb Gas at the Diffusive Temperatu'] Assume $\mathsf H(\mathsf Q\mid\mathbb P_{N,\beta})<\infty$ and
$A_{N,\beta}+N^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^NU_\beta(x_i)\in L^1(\mathsf Q)$.  Then, for every $\lambda>1$,
\begin{align}
 \cS_N(\mathsf Q)
 &\ge\left(1-\frac1\lambda\right)\mathsf H(\mathsf Q\mid\mathbb P_{N,\beta})
 -\log \mathsf K_{N,\beta}(\mu_\beta)\notag\\
 &\quad-\frac1\lambda\log\E_{\mathbb P_{N,\beta}}\left[
