{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.598461+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98f04400458b7ff1f841e79d7e8db72f58f06087e846548053d8d39873489174","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem W1 lower-bound of arXiv:2411.15724, 'Wasserstein Convergence Rates for Empirical Measures of Random Subsequence of $\{nα\}$'] Let $\big\{ I_i \, ; \, i = 1, \ldots, K \big\}$ be a family of disjoint closed intervals (more precisely, closed arcs) contained in $\mathbb{T}$. The length of each $I_i$ is denoted by $L_i$. Then for any $\nu \in \mathscr{P}(\mathbb{T})$, which is supported in the complement of $\cup_{i = 1}^{K} I_i$ (namely, $\nu ( \cup_{i = 1}^{K} I_i  ) = 0$), we have
