{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.163498+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_99077af9155cb8ad5943adc7dfaaad3a9a58cb13584824edfa04f62803134003","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Prop_BundleOfAdmissibleZModTwoZSpinors of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] Consider the tame Fréchet space bundle
  \begin{equation*}
    {\mathbf{F}}_{00} \coloneq w_{\log}^{-1}{\mathbf{E}}_{0}.
  \end{equation*}
  The \defined{universal bundle of admissible $\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}$ spinors} is the tame Fréchet subbundle
  \begin{equation*}
    {\mathbf{E}}_{00}
    \coloneq
    {\mathbf{E}}_{0} \cap {\mathbf{D}}^{-1}{\mathbf{F}}_{00}
    \subseteq
    {\mathbf{E}}_{0};
  \end{equation*}
  indeed, the preceding discussion and direct inspection show that the atlas constructed in (Def_UniversalBundles_Atlases of the paper) induces an atlas for ${\mathbf{E}}_{00}$;
  cf.~(Rmk_BundleOfSingularSpinors of the paper)~(Rmk_BundleOfSingularSpinors_Robust of the paper).
  Of course, the tame Fréchet space structures on the fibres of ${\mathbf{E}}_{00}$ is the one defined in (Prop_K_Tame of the paper).
  Denote by
  \begin{equation*}
    {\mathbf{E}}_{00}^* \subseteq {\mathbf{E}}_{00}
  \end{equation*}
  the open subset of \defined{non-degenerate} admissible $\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}$ spinors;
  that is: the subset consisting of those admissible $\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}$ spinors $({\mathbf{p}},[{\mathfrak l}];\Phi) \in {\mathbf{E}}_{00}$ for which ${\mathbf{L}}_\Phi$ is injective.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:33:06.539174+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_990d5d8ddef0cf758dde59800e81715ebe5069e4e6e22235884819a799d0516b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 10 of arXiv:2608.25829, 'Topology of low-dimensional generalized Ricci solitons and string backgrounds'] Let $(M^7, \varphi)$ be a nontrivial compact strong torsion $G_2$ manifold.  Then
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $b_3 \geq 1$,
