{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.879849+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a241bf9a6592635f263c0d86752ffd7b5cdf7fdaf27cbf4c51623e1bef20898","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:spectral improvement of overline P of arXiv:2509.02996, 'Group-averaged Markov chains: mixing improvement'] Assume that $P\in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$ (and hence $(1/2)(P+P^*)$) is a compact operator. Let $G$ be a locally compact topological group with Haar measure $\mu$ that acts on $\mathcal{X}$, and assume $\pi$ is $G$-invariant. Let $\lambda_2=\lambda_2(P)$ be the third smallest eigenvalue of $\frac{L+L^*}{2}$, which satisfies $\lambda_2>\lambda$. Let $\mathbf{P}_\Omega$ be the projection operator of $L^2(\pi)$ onto any subspace $\Omega$, then
        \begin{align*}
            \lambda(\overline P)\geq \min \bigg\{&\|\mathbf{P}_V\mathbf{P}_W\mathbf{P}_V\|_{2\to 2}\cdot \lambda(P)+\left(1-\|\mathbf{P}_V\mathbf{P}_W\mathbf{P}_V\|_{2\to 2}\right)\cdot \lambda_2(P), \\
            & \|\mathbf{P}_{V^\perp}\mathbf{P}_W\mathbf{P}_{V^\perp}\|_{2\to 2}\cdot \lambda(P)+\left(1-\|\mathbf{P}_{V^\perp}\mathbf{P}_W\mathbf{P}_{V^\perp}\|_{2\to 2}\right)\cdot \lambda_2(P)\bigg\}\geq \lambda(P),
        \end{align*}
    and $\lambda(\overline P)>\lambda(P)$ if $W\cap V=W\cap V^\perp=\{0\}$.

    Specifically, for the cases where $|\mathcal{J}|=1$ such that $W$ has only one basis function $u$ with $\|u\|_\pi=1$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \lambda(\overline{P})\geq \min \bigg\{&\|u_V\|_\pi^2\cdot \lambda(P)+\left(1-\|u_V\|_\pi^2\right)\cdot \lambda_2(P),\\
        & \left(1-\|u_V\|_\pi^2\right)\cdot \lambda(P)+\|u_V\|_\pi^2\cdot \lambda_2(P)\bigg\}\geq \lambda(P),
    \end{align*}
    where $u_V=\mathbb E_{g\sim \mu}\left[U_g[u]\right]$. In this case, $\lambda(\overline P)>\lambda(P)$ holds as long as $u$ is not $G$-invariant and $u_V\neq 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:33:17.672144+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a2a4b7d84b34ba14054ca25b679526260e651f94de3f2fc758427c6d0a326c0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2607.10725, 'From the Airy line ensemble to the Gaussian free field'] Fix $m \geq 1$, $A \geq 1$, and let $h_T$ be as in (\ref{Eq.HeightFunction}). There exists a constant $C_2(m,A) > 0$ such that for all $T \geq e$ and $t \in \mathbb{R}$
