{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.468850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a5555786facb66e4100dd65ee493fb67ad406fe4ed92060dcb1779bb4449810","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 70 (Relationship between $\{\geop{t},\geop{u},\geop{x^2},\geop{x^3}\}$ and $\{\nullgeop{\ubar},\nullgeop{u},\nullgeop{x^2},\nullgeop{x^3}\}$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] The following identities hold:
	\begin{subequations}
