    &\leq \log(r \varepsilon^{-1})\max\{ \sigma \exp(-hR^2r+ hr^{19}(1+R^2+\log \sigma^{-1})^{5/6}\}, \exp\{-hm^{1/12}\}\}.
  \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.775559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a697c83e64b821a4ed561bbadc803b3019a9c432d7cd2ab170aa3a1693ff261","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Gaussian random variable) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] Let $\R$ be the real line, equipped with the $\sigma$-algebra $\cB$ 
of Borel sets and Lebesgue measure $\6x$. A random variable $X:\R\to\R$ is a 
(one-dimensional) Gaussian random variable with mean $m$ and variance $\sigma^2$ if 
its law is  
\begin{equation}
 \mu(\6x) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\sigma^2}} \e^{-(x-m)^2/(2\sigma^2)} \6x\;.
\end{equation}
In that case, we write $X\sim\cN(m,\sigma^2)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.759799+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a6a045a2cf434529f5835b3ce364aaa9f260560de9e456358b296bff88a59b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2608.17493, 'Integrals of some compound processes'] Let $g:\mathbb{N}^2\longrightarrow \mathbb{R}$ and $k:\mathbb{R}\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ such that for $\varepsilon >0\ \exists\ N_\varepsilon$ s.t. $|g(h,n) - k(h/n)|<\varepsilon,\ n\ge N_\varepsilon,\ h=1,\dots, n$. Let $f:\mathbb{R}\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ s.t. $\int_0^1 |f(x)|\dif x<\infty$ and $\exists\ \int_0^1 f(x)k(x)\dif x$. Then, 
	\begin{equation*}
		\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty} \sum_{h=1}^n \frac{1}{n}f\Big(\frac{h}{n}\Big) g(h,n) = \int_0^1f(x)k(x)\dif x.
	\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.851516+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a74ad2eda7b6972fdc264b761447344cbbf1a5a4299dc42ba36bd8fde541c78","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 13 of arXiv:2605.18751, '\mytitle'] Let \((Q_\nu)_{\nu\in\mathcal I}\) be a family of probability measures on \(\N_0\) with common support \(S\subseteq\N_0\), so that \(q_\nu(n)\coloneqq Q_\nu(\{n\})>0\) for \(n\in S\). Denote the density of the compound law \(C_\nu\) by
	\[
	f_\nu(k)\coloneqq \sum_{n\in S} q_\nu(n)F^{*n}(\{k\}).
	\]
If \(\nu\mapsto q_\nu(n)\) is differentiable on \(\mathcal I\) for every \(n\in S\), then for \(k\) in the common support of \(C_\nu\), the compound score is
	\begin{equation}

		s_\nu(k)\coloneqq \partial_\nu\log f_\nu(k)=\E[\gamma_\nu(N)\mid X=k],
	\end{equation}
	where \(\gamma_\nu(n)\coloneqq \partial_\nu\log q_\nu(n)\) and the expectation is taken under the joint compound law at the current parameter value.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.131679+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a76760714c0e6ae260e9d4429dd1c8fa0162e3ce338c8960b40978a3b3d08e8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 ({\cite[Theorem 4.2.4) of arXiv:2608.27450, 'Koszul duality and Morita categories'] {blansblom2025chainrulegoodwilliecalculus}}] 
