\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.592065+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ac6fbbb5278de808b99ff9fcfe741a9c3e625497ee862785841d6df1ce17ec8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 3 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] Let $\phi\in\mathcal{S}([G])$. Then $\phi_P$ is a smooth function on $U(\A)M(F)\bs G(\A)$ with
