		\end{equation*}
		for any $\lambda\in\a^\ast_{P_0}/\a^\ast_G$. Moreover, the same bounds hold for $\mathcal{D}\phi$, for any differential operator $\mathcal{D}$ of $G(F_\infty)$ (with implied constant allowed to depend on $\mathcal{D}$). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.365965+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ac89a5b375d7a94e7e456c743b4de395d5808fed29e0752d25de8734a1452ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 28 of arXiv:2506.20146, 'Parabolic Anderson Model in the Hyperbolic Space. Part I: Annealed Asymptotics'] There exists a universal constant $C>0,$ such that
