{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.766196+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b042d541720d1c1f6fd0bf4a6954a8d2117d64e97747e869199db549afbbdb6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2607.09575, 'Probabilistic estimates for a system of\\noisy integrate-and-fire neurons'] For any given $T > 0$, consider $0 \le t \le t+h \le T$ with $h \in (0,\,1)$. Then, we may find a $C_p > 0$, independent of $h$, and an integer $N_0 = N_0(h)$ such that for all $N \ge N_0$, we have
	\begin{equation}
		\prob\left[F_{t+h}^N - F_{t-}^N > 1 + C_p h^{1/16}\right] \le C_p h^p,
	\end{equation}
	for any $p \ge 1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.007768+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b051d46d09c6ca5e701ad32300295eaa8d358533ad16499dea3b96236c6ce1d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma c and r of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Suppose $c^{\{1\}}_{N}$ is the constant defined in (equation w2 of the paper) with respect to $z_1$. Then
