{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:27:14.855427+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b0f75936b582dc381b6a384351b13ed9d57e51d0e313832e88988950bd91d6b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 of arXiv:2608.23462, '2608.23462'] Let $p \geq 2$ and $\beta > 0$. We say that the frozen variable $(\hat Y_t^x)_{t \ge 0}$ is (uniformly) $p$-dissipative (with constant $\beta$), if for all $x\in \R^{d_1}$ and $y_1,y_2 \in \R^{d_2}$
