{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.660318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b1678e941d20780ec00a54c0e0cfcf800119ae3361300d980501120d4ec8161","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 25 of arXiv:2605.08844, 'Signature Kernel and Schwinger-Dyson Kernel Equations as Two-Parameter Rough Differential '] The set $NC(n)$ constructed over the alphabet $1, \dots, d$, contains 
