     of $M_N(p)+\delta Q_N$ converges weakly in probability to the push-forward $p_*\mathrm{L}$ of the normalized Lebesgue measure on $[0,1]^d_x\times \T_\xi^{d}$ by $p$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.345485+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b25eb5e3ca402050800c731264563ec53cc04f5335b1c06e3443408e017b8c1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition cocycle of arXiv:2507.08757, 'Strong existence and uniqueness of the tilt-indexed Busemann process in the planar corner '] A function $A:\mathbb{Z}^2\times\mathbb{Z}^2\to\mathbb{R}$ is a \emph{cocycle} if 
