{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.917895+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b2a1187540fea6197ec0449e21cd6e776b57c23126e6fb09bd6c459c511fc53","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conj 6 (Algebraic Integrability Conjecture) of arXiv:2609.00974, 'On Algebraic Integrability\\ of Vector Fields \\ with Rational Function Coefficients\\ tha'] Let $K/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(x_1,\ldots,x_n)$ be an algebraic extension of fields. Let $\F$ be a foliation on $K$, which admits a model over the ring of integers $\cO_L$, where $L$ is a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$.

    The following are equivalent:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item The foliation $\F$ is algebraically integrable, i.e., it is of the form $\F=\op{Der}_{W}(K)$ for a subfield $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\subset W\subset K$.
        \item For almost all primes $p$ and all maximal ideals $q$ over $p$ in $\cO_L$ the reduction modulo $q$ of $\F$ is $p$-closed, i.e., it defines a $1$-foliation.
    \end{enumerate} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.572669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b2cd233f1cc6a62f6f8a688efbf74cd85ebd0b915c75466c93018c6d0610fb2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Wishart.Satterthwaite of arXiv:2606.04859, 'Stein's method for the Wishart distribution'] In the setting described above, assume that we have $\sum_{j=1}^N \alpha_j \geq d + 1$. Also, fix $\nu > 3d-3$ and set $\smash{\mathfrak{W}_{\nu} \sim \mathcal{W}_d(\nu, \widetilde{\Sigma}_{\nu})}$ with $\smash{\widetilde{\Sigma}_{\nu} \vcentcolon= \nu^{-1}\overline{\Sigma}}$, so that, in particular, $\smash{\mathsf{E}[\mathfrak{W}_{\nu}] = \overline{\Sigma} = \mathsf{E}[\mathfrak{T}]}$. Let $h\in C_b^{2d}(\mathcal{S}_{++}^d)$ and assume that $\smash{\mathcal{M}_1^{\mathcal{D}, \widetilde{\Sigma}_{\nu}}(h) + \mathcal{M}_2^{\mathcal{D}, \widetilde{\Sigma}_{\nu}}(h) < \infty}$ in Theorem~(thm:smoothness.estimates.wishart of the paper). Then,
\begin{equation}
\big|\mathsf{E}[h(\mathfrak{T})]-\mathsf{E}[h(\mathfrak{W}_{\nu})]\big| \leq \frac{d + 1}{2}\mathcal{M}_2^{\mathcal{D}, \widetilde{\Sigma}_{\nu}}(h)\sum_{j=1}^N \alpha_j\mathrm{tr}(\Sigma_j)\|\Sigma_j-\widetilde{\Sigma}_{\nu}\|_F.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.139597+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b2ce619074a7375e56dba8d9752d6766156672405530d93dee478b7bb363a02","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition P:I to L_interval of arXiv:2507.01236, 'Disintegration theorem for multifunctions, \\ with applications to empirical Wasserstein d'] Let~$\mu$ be arbitrarily specified.  If 
