\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.698016+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b48076c4b3fab2487453d93e25a71c876d218c41b51f5c802e0dab074c15b51","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 19 of arXiv:2608.30990, 'Convergence of symmetries: nilpotency, dimension, and perfectness'] \cite{nsz, carolino}. Let $G_i,$ $G$, $\phi_i$, $B$, $B_i$ be as in Theorem \ref{thm:gleason}. Assume the sequence $G_i$ has the NSS property and  consists of Lie groups, and let $\mathfrak{g}_i$ be the Lie algebra of $G_i$. Then for $i$ large enough there is a genuine norm $\Vert \cdot \Vert _{i} : \mathfrak{g}_i \to \mathbb{R}$ with
    \begin{equation}
     \vert \vv \vert _{B_i} \leq \Vert \vv \Vert _i \leq 2C_0 \vert \vv \vert _{B_i}       
    \end{equation}
    for all $\vv \in \mathfrak{g}_i$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:06.982496+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b4896e9283cee1cd9fa5cd1925c74740a228893c6eb8867cf2ec71827f5596d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Gordonpos1 of arXiv:2607.26551, 'An RDT based confirmation of Lehner's formula for Kronecker-Gaussian matrices'] ([Gordon85,Slep62])
 Let $X_{i}$ and $Y_{i}$, $1\leq i\leq n$, be two centered Gaussian processes which satisfy the following inequalities for all choices of indices
\begin{enumerate}
\item ${\mathbb E}(X_{i}^2)={\mathbb E}(Y_{i}^2)$
\item ${\mathbb E}(X_{i}X_{l})\leq {\mathbb E}(Y_{i}Y_{l}), i\neq l$.
\end{enumerate}
 Then
\begin{equation*}
{\mathbb E}(\min_{i} X_{i})\leq {\mathbb E}(\min_i Y_{i}) \quad  \Longleftrightarrow \quad {\mathbb E}(\max_{i} X_{i})\geq {\mathbb E}(\max_i Y_{i}).
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.409867+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b4a7852b08bd816538e0a0151b9892eb662ef3fe1602e3ad5c45282a1e47c1c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 of arXiv:2608.31070, 'Sub-Laplacians on Compact Lie Groups: Heat Kernels, Distance, and Zeta Determinants'] For every $\Omega\in\Lambda^2\pLie$,
		\begin{equation}
