{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.421309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b4bba4717fd43b24be2bd150fbacf296a12857957a2d254df9af0cfe7b757f7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 11 of arXiv:2607.28215, 'Almost stochastic dominance via optimal transport'] If $c,g$ and $d$ are chosen according to \eqref{eq:Rd}, then Theorems \ref{thm:main1}-\ref{thm:main3} hold and
