{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.501093+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b562d74c57a01487e7c48965fb7b259241db8f4fe6a14ceb79b7fe0d5261ea1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 35 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For all $(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2 \alpha}([0,T],L(V,W))$ we have
\begin{align*}
(Z,Z') := \bigg( \int_0^{\cdot} Y_s \, d \bfx_s, Y \bigg) \in \scrd_X^{2 \alpha}([0,T],W),
\end{align*}
and the estimate
\begin{align*}
\| Z,Z' \|_{X,2 \alpha} &\leq \| Y \|_{\alpha} + \| Y' \|_{\infty} \| \bbx \|_{2 \alpha}
\\ &\quad + C T^{\alpha} \big( \| X \|_{\alpha} \| R^Y \|_{2 \alpha} + \| \bbx \|_{2 \alpha} \| Y' \|_{\alpha} \big)
\end{align*}
with a constant $C > 0$ depending on $\alpha$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.451864+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b589af41faae8e85c1081b9af9c95898a54d7a55b7287886cdc5b1199eb90ce","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-MM1M of arXiv:2505.00198, '\ttl'] Assume that $\mu, \nu, \kappa >0$. The stationary distribution $\pi$ for the M/M/1+M queue with random resetting under the FCFS discipline is given by the following: for $k =0,1,2, \dots$,
\begin{equation}
\pi_{k} = \frac{ \theta^{k} }{\prod_{i=0}^{k-1} (i + \eta) } \times  \frac{ \gamma A_{k} }{ (\gamma + \theta) A_0 - \theta A_1 },  
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation*}
A_{k} = \int_{0}^{1} \gamma (1-t)^{\gamma -1} t^{\eta -1 +k} e^{-\theta t} dt, \qquad \text{for $k =0, 1,2, \dots$}.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.577270+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b5937d7b0981fcc702bff3b8fba570319c962791346c403af3c0dff0c8ef9ea","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma new bound for Ptau_x>n-001 of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] There exists a constant $c >0$ such that 
