{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.225005+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b6e38ab282cc6d01ca6a10bd06d29e5ca4412f4636a8ad683ab791a08ca03d7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] A graph $G=(V,E)$ satisfies the \textbf{volume doubling} condition if there exists $C > 0$ such that for all $x\in V$ and $n\geq1:$
