		\end{equation*}
		In particular, $a_\theta\uparrow 1/2$ as $\theta\downarrow0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.534413+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b73aec6ead0cb1ab0d9d7fe01641114388f6929fd3ac4f4c82450bb63073e23","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.center_cube of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Given $\mathsf{r} \in (\frac{50}{27}, 2)$, then every ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}}_m \in \mathcal{G}^{(N)}_k$ is $N$-$\mathsf{stable}$ for the following property: 



