{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:27:32.354883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b8dedf555ccfdc6fae83ebbb5d843fc83b29ab4b5a1e556a5ddb8e8ca3ad6b6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2509.23069, 'Every cutoff profile is possible'] Let $((X^{(n)}_t)_{t\geq 0})_{n\geq 1}$ be a sequence of ergodic Markov chains, in discrete or continuous time. We say that that $((X^{(n)}_t)_{t\geq 0})_{n\geq 1}$ exhibits a total variation \textbf{cutoff} at a (sequence of) times $\left( t_n \right)_{n \geq 1}$ if for every $\varepsilon>0$, we have 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathrm{d}^{(n)}\left( \left\lfloor (1-\varepsilon) t_n \right\rfloor \right) \xrightarrow[n\to \infty]{} 1 \quad \text{ and } \quad \mathrm{d}^{(n)}\left( \left\lceil (1+\varepsilon) t_n \right\rceil \right) \xrightarrow[n\to \infty]{} 0,
    \end{equation}
where for $n\geq 1$, $\mathrm{d}^{(n)}(\cdot)$ is the distance to stationarity for the chain $(X^{(n)}_t)_{t\geq 0}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.269581+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b8df30ac3e5e5687d80e813c27e2a462f03f5b92d1930e5d69c2c44f1eef729","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2604.15753, 'The truncation property and continuity for \\ the long-range contact process on $\mathbb{Z'] Let $\lambda \in \Lambda$ and $\delta>0$. Then, for any $L,T>0$ and $A \subset B_L$, a.s.\ on $H_{L,T}^{A}(k)$, $k \in \bN$, it holds that
