{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.990066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b8e8f2bf78444fc6d3bf5cbd60555562ba166c45754422c53c98eb1f7f9fee2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 89 (Transfer-impedance matrix) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Recall that we fixed an (arbitrary) orientation of the edges with $e^-$ and $e^+$ denoting the starting and ending points of an edge $e$. Let $v_e(\cdot)$ be the voltage on the vertices when a unit current flow $\theta_e$ is sent from $e^-$ to $e^+$, i.e.\ $v_e(\cdot)$ is the (unique) harmonic function on $V \setminus \{e^-, e^+\}$ with $v_e(e^-) = \effR{}{e^-}{e^+}$ and $v_e(e^+) = 0$. The transfer-impedance matrix $Y$ is a $|E| \times |E|$ matrix with entries given by
    \begin{equation*}
        Y(e,f) := w(f) \big[ v_e(f^-) - v_e(f^+) \big] = \theta_e(f^-, f^+).
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.500659+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b909b627dde06f6fc902ff24edad9df702093f371b9015414ebce9b83277e98","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop : FdTmon/StrMon of arXiv:2412.03320, 'Large deviation principle at speed $n$ for the random metric in first-passage percolation'] Let $D_1, D_2 \in \RegPD$ be distinct pseudometrics satsifying $D_1 \le D_2$. If $\FdTmon(D_2)<\infty$, then
