	\end{equation*}
	uniformly in $t>0$ and $x,y>0$, where $\rho=k_1/2+k_2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.998378+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b9cc4224bad39a805b369901946923ceff5b1aa12b3392638116121997fc489","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-explengthbrige of arXiv:2604.14318, '\large The free energy of the interacting Bose gas:\\\medskip a variational description \\'] For any $M\in(0,\infty)$, there is a constant $C\in(0,\infty)$ (depending on $d$, $\beta$ and $M$) such that, for any $R\in\mathbb{N}$,
