{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:50:44.873044+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9bd65c1c198ff574ea895526a5776e3f35919b18433c4f0979d336e6604e97c8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 34 (Random Schatten interpolation) of arXiv:2607.16724, 'Algebraic Transfer for Operator-Valued Gaussian Chaoses: Oriented Schatten Profiles and Si'] Let $1\le r<2<q<\infty$ and choose $0<\theta<1$ so that
\begin{equation}

 \frac12=\frac\theta r+\frac{1-\theta}{q}.
\end{equation}
If $B\in L^2(\Omega;\Sch_r)\cap L^2(\Omega;\Sch_q)$, then
\begin{equation}

 \norm B_{L^2(\Omega;\Sch_2)}
 \le
 \norm B_{L^2(\Omega;\Sch_r)}^\theta
