{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.287545+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9bdb62b9b1ad74bdb7f9a27b3e3d35e446e3ea8ff847d5eec5eb8317bd32d5a3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 25 of arXiv:2606.22964, 'Signature McKean--Vlasov stochastic differential equations'] Let $p\in(2,3)$. For every $t\in[0,T]$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \begin{aligned}
            &\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_D\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} \Big\lVert \augpr{X}^{\mu,1}_{t_i,t_{i+1}}-\augpr{Y}^{\nu,1}_{t_i,t_{i+1}} \Big\rVert^p_{\mathbb{R}^{d+1}}\right]\\
