{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:57:28.719102+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c5180c489c8600b0605bb3b0d98baf394bef9597b1f36156dc6848a4ea93793","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2609.01166, 'Nonparametric inference for density-dependent McKean--Vlasov diffusions'] Under the same assumptions as in Lemma~\ref{lem:primitive-kl}, there exists a constant \(C_\mathrm{risk}\) depending on \(I,J,\beta,H,\kappa,K,\xi_\star,d\) and \(V\), but not on \(n\), such that
\begin{equation}
  \inf_{\wh\Xi_n}
  \sup_{\xi\in\mathfrak X_\beta(J)}
  \E_\xi\norm{\wh\Xi_n-\xi}_{L^2(I)}^2
  \geq C_\mathrm{risk} n^{-2\beta/(2\beta+3)}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, for constants 
\(C_\mathrm{sep}>0\) and \(p\in(0,1)\)
depending on the same variables as \(C_\mathrm{risk}\),
\begin{equation}
  \inf_{\wh\Xi_n}
  \sup_{\xi\in\mathfrak X_\beta(J)}
  \Pi_\xi^{\otimes n}\!\biggl(
    \norm{\wh\Xi_n-\xi}_{L^2(I)}
    \geq C_\mathrm{sep} n^{-\beta/(2\beta+3)}
  \biggr)
  \geq p.
\end{equation}
The infimum is over all measurable estimators based on \(X_1,\ldots,X_n\sim \Pi_\xi\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:37.802499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c5718eb33b06934972040994c6080597537ee4664f5cbf54303a0154ffc16c6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 (Sobolev estimates) of arXiv:2609.03558, 'Local well-posedness of the higher-order nonlinear Schr\"{o}dinger equation on the half-li'] Let $b\in \{0,1\}$. Then, the unique solution of \eqref{cauchy2} satisfies the space estimate
