{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:25:49.870359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c59d41c3ed9f0fb63555c54b4ca89a0e75a827a1e33c6b408528328d4c48398","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 of arXiv:2609.02050, '2609.02050'] Let $D$ be a diagram that avoids the configurations in Figure~\ref{fig-upper} and let $C^{(1)},\ldots,C^{(m)}$ be all the diagrams $C=(C_1,C_2,\ldots,C_n)$ with $|C_j|=|D_j|$ for $j\in[n]$ and ${\bf x}^{C}={\bf x}^a$, where ${\bf x}^a$ is a monomial in $\chi_{D}({\bf x})$. For simplicity, write ${\bf y}^{(a)}={y}^{F_{led}^{C^{(a)}}}$  Then we have the following results:
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item[(a)] For $1\leq a \leq m$, the leading monomial ${\bf y}^{(a)}$ appears in the polynomial $\det\left(Y_D^{C^{(a)}}\right)$.

			\item[(b)] The leading monomials $\{{\bf y}^{(a)}\}$ are distinct.
		\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.172233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c5b34385a4b6f33e13636d5a2a9133a9bd8703c3324bb9f2780916eb3dabd1b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm_NashMoserSubmersionTheorem of arXiv:2609.02848, 'The universal moduli space of non-degenerate $\Z/2\Z$~harmonic spinors'] Let ${\mathbf{X}}$ and ${\mathbf{B}}$ be tame Fréchet manifolds,
  ${\mathbf{V}}$ a tame Fréchet space bundle over ${\mathbf{X}}$,
  $\mathrm{pr}_{\mathbf{B}} \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace {\mathbf{X}} \to {\mathbf{B}}$ a uniform submersion,
  $s \in \Gamma({\mathbf{X}},{\mathbf{V}})$ a tame smooth section, and
  $\nabla$ a partial connection on ${\mathbf{V}}$ with respect to the vertical tangent bundle $\VerticalTangentBundle{{\mathbf{X}}}{{\mathbf{B}}} \coloneq \ker T\mathrm{pr}_{\mathbf{B}} \subseteq T{\mathbf{X}}$.
  If
  there is a finite rank vector bundle $\mathrm{Def}$ over ${\mathbf{X}}$ and
  a map of tame Fréchet space bundles $\pi \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace T{\mathbf{X}}/{\mathbf{B}} \twoheadrightarrow \mathrm{Def}$ such that the thickening
  \begin{equation}

    \begin{pmatrix}
      \nabla s \\
      \pi
    \end{pmatrix}
    \mskip0.5mu\colon\thinspace
