{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.489655+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9cb46d6b263569cd3c0293298054d9b6e5a64fa2b4e0333ad7562caa2e1bbb85","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 18 of arXiv:2607.03924, 'Tree Coordinates and Range Martingales for Positive Operator-Valued Measures'] Convex decompositions 
\[
E=\frac{1}{2}\left(F+G\right),
\]
where $F$ and $G$ are POVMs on $\Omega_{m}$ with values in $B\left(H\right)$,
are in one-to-one correspondence with positive range martingales $\left\{ X_{w}\right\} $
satisfying 
\begin{equation}
0\leq X_{w}\leq2I_{H_{w}}
\end{equation}
for every finite word $w$, and 
\begin{equation}
X_{\varnothing}=I.
\end{equation}
The correspondence is given on cylinders by 
\begin{equation}
F\left(\left[w\right]\right)=E^{1/2}_{w}X_{w}E^{1/2}_{w}
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
