{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.632922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9cc5b855c02eee1c8b249a4b14ad2d8423cf50783919b1dbf2747d63769996ff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:NL-MC-construction of arXiv:2607.00800, 'Brownian motion in Minkowski normed spaces'] For each $z \in \mathbb{R}^d$, let $u^z$ be a probability solution to the nonlinear Fokker--Planck equation (equation gen-nl-fpe of the paper) with initial datum $z$, such that
    \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
        \item $(t,z) \mapsto u^z(t,x) \,\mathrm d x$ is injective from $[0,\infty)\times \mathbb{R}^d$ to  $\mathcal P$ (here we write $u^z(0,x) \,\mathrm d x := \delta_z$);

        \item for each $z \in \mathbb{R}^d$ and $s \in [0,\infty)\setminus \{0\}$, $u^z_{s+}$ is an extreme point in the convex set of probability solutions to (equation gen:lin-fpe of the paper) with $u^z(s+t)$ replacing $v(t)$ and with initial datum $u^z(s,x) \,\mathrm d x$.
    \end{enumerate}
    Then, for each $z \in \mathbb{R}^d$, there exists a unique weak solution $X^z$ to the McKean--Vlasov SDE (equation gen-DDSDE of the paper) with the prescribed one-dimensional time marginals $\mathcal{L}(X^z_t) = u^z(t,x) \,\mathrm d x$, $t > 0$, and $X^z_0 = z$. 
    The family of solution path laws $\{P^z\}_{z\in \mathbb{R}^d}$, $P^z = \mathcal{L}(X^z)$, is a nonlinear Markov core for $\{u^z(t)\}_{t>0, z\in \mathbb{R}^d}$ and is uniquely determined by $\{u^z\}_{z \in \mathbb{R}^d}$ and (equation gen-DDSDE of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.674957+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9cce48a84e49186ccef7135ad1d02038f75266452faf993acc9cfd309c381b19","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2608.04937, '2608.04937'] Assume that $f^1$ satisfies \textnormal{(B1),(B2)} and that
