{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.221187+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9cd04187b3c4965a3bdc40bf64e7e50716eae73b94f34e787d4fad21ec89d4b5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:5.3 of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] For every $q\in (0,1)$ it holds in the limit $k\to\infty$ that
