    \end{displaymath}
    the minimal eigenvalue $\lambda_{\min}\left(g^{-1}(\lm)\right)$ of the cometric at the landmark configuration $\lm$ satisfies
    \begin{displaymath}
        \lambda_{\min}\left(g^{-1}(\lm)\right)
        \geq \frac{\widehat{k}_M}{2\Gamma\left(1+\frac{d}{2}\right)}\left(\frac{M}{2^{3/2}}\right)^d.
    \end{displaymath} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.760832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9cf57944a7419e610d9adee2ac6081d97fd076e42e4050f1b41768895d636d1a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:IS6V-seed-linear of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The seed functions $\Psi$ and $\Phi$ satisfy the linear
