{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.415660+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d47f8a5b7d6a8ab0c93ed77b95f15613ff2253d3ee0f1863f28369a3e048168","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 97 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Take two variational data satisfying Assumptions~\ref{Assumption_A} and \ref{Assumption_B}. Assume that for any $h \in [H]$ the complex domain $\amsmathbb{M}_h$ in Assumption~\ref{Assumption_B} is common to the two variational data. Then, there exists $\eps > 0$ depending only on the constants in the assumptions such that, if the variational datum $\textnormal{I}$ satisfies the off-criticality Assumption~\ref{Assumption_C} and for any $g,h \in [H]$ the inequalities
