{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:32:58.302063+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d491dc8d137b1d240f835bf49e5b5ef2cc8c947e42ede48b323f556fbd41203","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2505.10256, 'Stochastic Oscillators out of equilibrium:\\ scaling limits and correlation estimates'] A sequence $\{P_{N}, N\geq{1}\}$ of probability measures defined on $D([0,T],H^{-m}(\mathbb T))$ is tight if the following two conditions hold:
