{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.897665+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d51979624a401cdd058f2e452ec9885e6e29a3204484e8a95aba3210d36a543","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 1 of arXiv:2606.19925, 'Asymptotic properties for fully coupled delayed forward-backward stochastic differential e'] \begin{itemize}
\item [(a)] A triple of stochastic processes $(X^{t,x,\varepsilon},Y^{t,x,\varepsilon},Z^{t,x,\varepsilon})$ is said to be an adapted solution of the delayed FBSDE \eqref{Eq1} if, $(X^{t,x,\varepsilon},Y^{t,x,\varepsilon},Z^{t,x,\varepsilon})\in \mathcal{S}^2(\R)\times\mathcal{S}^{2}(\R)\times \mathcal{H}^2(\R)$and if equation \eqref{Eq1} is satisfied $\P$-almost surely.
