{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.289708+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d5f18722bf45556597bbf34d4eea6f201103aaaf9847b38cea8e6b21468e71f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 22 of arXiv:2604.25725, 'What is The Probability That A Random Graph With A Given Degree Sequence is Connected?'] For any $m$ large enough, $0<\gamma<1$, $0<\epsilon<10^{-6}$, $n_1,n_2<\eps m$, $C \le m^{\gamma /20}$, $1\leq i$, $ r\le C(\log m)^2$ the following holds, if $2|E(H_{i-1})|+X_{i-1} \le \epsilon m$ then
\begin{align*}
