{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.404405+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d7d95bf0b9f0a837f4bd583571702036f99a9d57cd2766d10f0725ad56b6c5e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem-le-tv of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] Let $\{\mathcal G_n\}_{n\geq 1}$ be an increasing family of connected subgraphs of $\mathcal G$ whose union is all of $\mathcal G$.
Also let $A\subset \mathcal V\mathcal G$ be a finite set of vertices and let $z \in \mathcal V\mathcal G$.
\begin{itemize}
\item Let $X$ be the random walk on $\mathcal G$ reflected off of $\infty$ started at $z$ and let $\tau$ be the smallest $t$ for which $X_t \in A$. Let $\operatorname{LE}$ be the loop erasure of $X|_{[0,\tau]}$ (Definition~(def-le-infty of the paper)). 
\item For $n\in\mathbbm N$ such that $A \cup \{z\} \subset\mathcal G_n$, let $Z^n$ be the random walk on $\mathcal G_n$ started at $z$ and let $J_n$ be the smallest $j$ such that $Z^n_j \in A$. Let $\operatorname{LE}^n$ be the loop-erasure of $Z^n|_{[0,J^n]}$ (Definition~(def-le of the paper)).
\end{itemize}
Fix $k\in \mathbbm N$ such that $A \cup \{z\} \subset\mathcal G_k$.
As $n\to\infty$, the total variation distance between the following two random variables goes to zero. The random variable which equals $\operatorname{LE}^n$ on the event $\operatorname{LE}^n \subset \mathcal G_k$ and equals $\emptyset$ otherwise; and the random variable which equals $\operatorname{LE}$ on the event that $\operatorname{LE} \subset \mathcal G_k$ and equals $\emptyset$ otherwise.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.864130+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d7e5bd9cd5b1422f59c13be89e3f00ae3b74323b2eb63f1b95c33a749ff3224","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Lower bound on relaxation time) of arXiv:2511.23453, 'Convergence rates of self-repellent random walks, their local time and Event Chain Monte C'] Let $(P_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the transition semigroup of a reversible Markov process and $(\hat P_t)_{t\geq 0}$ an arbitrary second-order lift. Then
