{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.625197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d833c01b4de00501718df46134eec902da4a7019d60839a7d403e4bb00c2857","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm: 0127 of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Let $\{X_k\}_{k=1}^n$ ($n>1$ is finite) be a d-dimensional identical sequence on a sublinear expectation space $(\Omega,\mathcal{H},\hat{\mathbb{E}})$ such that $\hat{\mathbb{E}}[|X_1|^{1+\beta}]<\infty$ for some $\beta\in (0,1]$. Let $v\in C_b^{1,1+\beta}(\mathbb{R}_+\times \mathbb{R}^d)$ with some $\beta\in (0,1]$ be the solution to equation (equation PDE of the paper) with $p(a)=\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\langle a, X_1\rangle]$ and $S_n=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^nX_i$. Then
		\begin{align}
				v(1,0)-\hat{\mathbb{E}}[\phi(S_n)]&\geq -\sum_{i=2}^n\bigg|\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Bigl[v\Bigl(1-\frac{i}{n}, \frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^iX_j\Bigr)\Bigr]-\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Big[\hat{\mathbb{E}}\Bigl[v\bigl(1-\frac{i}{n}, x+\frac{X_i}{n}\bigr)\Bigr]\Big|_{x=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{i-1}X_j}\Big]\bigg|\notag\\
				&\ \ \ \ -4n^{-\beta}\int_0^1|\nabla_xv(s,\cdot)|_{\beta}ds\times \hat{\mathbb{E}}[|X_1|^{1+\beta}]+\underline{f},
		\end{align}
		where 
		$
			\underline{f}:=\inf_{\{0\leq t\leq 1,x\in \mathbb{R}^d\}}f(t,x)
	$, in which $f$ is from (equation PDE of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.622399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d882f7199b95cfb3587bb3d64c91b3ffd8d11888ab0f1b0a88a3767c4adf638","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 188 (The flat elliptic-hyperbolic current) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\SigmatTan$ be a $\Sigma_t$-tangent vectorfield.
