{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.821089+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d8caa936b6600a90bceca45ed4d9389cd35a156d07edd4ea94077fe15e7caf4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:slot_dynamics of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] Assign independently to each slot $(x,i)$ and each nearest neighbor $y$ with $|y-x|=1$ a Poisson clock $\mathcal{P}_{x,y}^i$ on $\mathbb{R}_+$ with rate
  \begin{equation}
    \lambda_i = \frac{1}{2d}\bigl(g(i) - g(i - 1)\bigr).
  \end{equation}
  The \emph{slot dynamics} is defined as follows. 
  Starting from a packed slot configuration $\sigma_0$, whenever the Poisson clock $\mathcal{P}_{x,y}^i$ rings at time $t$:
  \begin{itemize}
    \item If $i \le n(\sigma_{t-}, x)$, the particle at $(x,i)$ jumps to the target site $y$. The system transitions to the new state $\sigma_t = (\sigma_{t-})^{(x, i) \to y}$.
    \item If $i > n(\sigma_{t-}, x)$, the slot $(x,i)$ is empty. 
    The clock ring is suppressed and nothing happens ($\sigma_t = \sigma_{t-}$).
  \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.772229+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d8d2ec28e4527bfd1aadfbe3541ca54d0fa039d65395b32f57497e4cf2c1586","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 53 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Assume the notation in Lemma \ref{Lem.PowerSeriesSG}, and fix $\theta \in (\pi/4, \pi/2)$. There exist constants $\delta_1 \in (0,\delta_0]$ and $\epsilon_1 > 0$, depending on $q, \kappa, c, \theta$, such that for $r \in [0, \delta_1]$
