{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.788379+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9dc24853df400f8f0e471af47a769e6f3f02761b51c22fbe994f5848576bcd85","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 52 (H\"older--Besov spaces) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For $\alpha < 0$, the space $\cC^\alpha(\Lambda)$ consists in all Schwartz 
distributions $\zeta\in\cS'(\Lambda)$ such that 
