{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.421790+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9dd87a7fcf323780e602a4f13b30ec8d80238aeff2193ad45c6beaabd62eabf9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2607.28215, 'Almost stochastic dominance via optimal transport'] If the Borel measurable cost function $c:E\times E \to [0,\infty)$ satisfies the triangle inequality 
