{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.251373+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9df7a6ad099a64f12e68ef4c85739a417922cb0430f73a0b3607ed984004bf9b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:simple-sequential-one-shot of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\mathcal{Y},\hat\mathcal{Z},T)$ be a real-valued simple repeated gamble space for $T\in\mathbb{N}$.
