{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.777535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e165c7dd89cddc24ece016fcd792a58032463b25d348bfceffcc60e86a0d22c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.17493, 'Integrals of some compound processes'] Let $N$ be a renewal process with waiting times $X\sim F$ and $\{A_n\}_{n\ge1}$ be a sequence of real random variables independent of $N$ (and its waiting times),
	\begin{itemize}
		\item[($i$)] with $\gamma\in\mathbb{R}$,
		\begin{equation}
			\mathbb{E} \exp\Biggl( i\gamma \sum_{k=1}^{N(t)} X_k A_k \Biggr) = \sum_{n\ge0}\mathbb{E} \Biggl[\conv_{k=1}^n \Big( e^{i\gamma A_k\sbullet} F(\sbullet) \Big)\ast 1 (t)- \conv_{k=1}^{n} \Big( e^{i\gamma A_k\sbullet}F(\sbullet) \Big)\ast F \ast 1 (t) \Biggr],
		\end{equation}
		where $hF\ast g (t)= \int_0^t g(t-x)h(x)F(\dif x)$ for suitable functions $h,g$ and distribution $F$.
		\item[($ii$)] If $X$ is absolutely continuous with density $f$ and $\mu>0$,
		\begin{equation}
			\mathcal{L} \left\{ \mathbb{E} \exp\Biggl( i\gamma \sum_{k=1}^{N(t)} X_k A_k \Biggr) \right\} (\mu) = \frac{1-\mathcal{L}f(\mu)}{\mu}\sum_{n\ge0}\mathbb{E} \prod_{k=1}^n \mathcal{L}f(\mu+i\gamma A_k).
		\end{equation}
	\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.609694+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e1c8181081f2437cdfd09406e403e536fb0930831761a610be908ba04e888f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thmx 3 (Hard edge limit, \cite{RR}, \cite{RR_err}) of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] Let $\Lambda_{n}\sim \Lag$ with $a>-1$ fixed. Then as $n\to \infty$, we have
