{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.414697+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e40767cfeef5dd5166f32cc53e8831707e8f3620cc247b31337bc8507e9663b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.27904, 'Instantons, indefinite 4-manifolds, and Dehn surgery'] A \textit{pointed instanton $SO(3)$-flow category} $(\mathcal{M}, p)$ is an instanton $SO(3)$-flow category for which each orbit is equipped with a choice of basepoint $p_\alpha\in\mathscr O(\alpha)$ satisfying the following conditions:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item $Up_\alpha = p_{U\alpha}$.
		\item If $\mathscr O(\alpha)\cong S^2$, the basepoint $p_\alpha$ is $SO(2)$-invariant.
	\end{itemize}
The pointing $p$ of $\mathcal{M}$ gives rise to an equivariant identification $\mathscr O(\alpha)\cong SO(3)/\Gamma, \Gamma\in\{1, SO(2), SO(3)\}$ for each orbit, and hence a privileged cell structure on $\mathscr O(\alpha)$ for which $p_\alpha$ is its unique $0$-cell.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:49:21.134151+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e438bd46bfa90067ca5aca9a3a6e8830bb4531899dc38b7ef4e0f8c0e30ea68","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 8 of arXiv:2608.26698, 'Mapping class groups of simply connected closed spin 5-manifolds with no 2- and 3-torsion '] Denote an element $a[S_1 \circ \eta] + b[T_1] \in \pi_3(S^2 \times S^3)$ by $(a, b)$.
