        		\item[(2)] For $b = 2$ or $b \geq 3$ odd, there exists $a \in \{0, 1, \cdots, b-1\}$ such that the homotopy classes $(a + kb, b)$, $(a + kb, -b)$ can be represented by an embedding of $S^3$ for each integer $k$. Such an embedding is not homotopic to $f \circ T_1$ for any diffeomorphism $f$ of $S^2 \times S^3$.
