{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.533261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e5be83e1f00b76a430a7a37e5cb6676874533c5124c3a419337f97b4883d35a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2608.30668, 'Recurrence and capacity of stable branching random walks'] Assume that \(d> \frac{2\alpha}{\alpha-1}\) and \(\theta\) has a finite
moment of order \(d-1\), then we have

