with \(u\) any unitary vector (for \(\lVert \cdot \rVert\)). In particular, \(G\) is \((2\alpha-d(\alpha-1))\)-varying. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.314313+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e5c9c3a5191c0947839d06ff5ae2d798100208465a08a3b6399f0ab6c7f8ac6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:uniform-killed-bridge of arXiv:2607.18070, 'The Brownian loop-catcher'] Let \(K_1,K_2\Subset D\) be disjoint, let
\(x^\delta=x+O(\delta),y^\delta=y+O(\delta)\), and denote by
\(\nu_\delta^{x,y}\) the unnormalized measure of the duration and
interpolated trace of a killed walk from \(x^\delta\) to \(y^\delta\).  Put
\[
 \nu^{x,y}(\,\mathrm d t,\,\mathrm d\gamma)
 =p_D(t,x,y)\,\,\mathrm d t\,\mathbf P_{x,y}^{D,t}(\,\mathrm d\gamma).
\]
On every \([\varepsilon,T]\), uniformly for
\((x,y)\in K_1\times K_2\),
\begin{equation}
 \nu_\delta^{x,y}\Longrightarrow2\nu^{x,y}
\end{equation}
against bounded uniformly continuous functions of duration and Hausdorff
trace.  Both sides have uniform short- and long-duration tails:
\begin{align}
 \lim_{\varepsilon\downarrow0}\limsup_{\delta\downarrow0}
 \sup_{K_1\times K_2}\nu_\delta^{x,y}\{t<\varepsilon\}=0, \qquad \lim_{T\uparrow\infty}\limsup_{\delta\downarrow0}
 \sup_{K_1\times K_2}\nu_\delta^{x,y}\{t>T\}=0,
\end{align}
and likewise for \(2\nu^{x,y}\).  Consequently
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal G_{D^\delta}(x^\delta,y^\delta)\longrightarrow2G_D(x,y)
 \quad\hbox{uniformly on }K_1\times K_2.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.744422+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e5e2f32b48304b1b4a1996f63804871195f063278f6a19ce218e95e7a58fda8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2604.03548, 'Degree-preserving conservative processes and a unified approach for their hydrodynamics'] We have 
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
\frac{d}{dt}\phi(t,i)
&=  2D\Delta\phi(t,i)
\mathbf{1}_{i\neq 0,1,\lfloor N/2\rfloor}
+ p_N D\nabla^- \phi(t,i)\mathbf{1}_{i=\lfloor N/2\rfloor} \\
&\quad+\big\{ 2D\nabla^+\phi(t,1)
+2\mathsf{a} (v_2+1)\nabla^-\phi(t,1)
+ (\mathsf{a} (v_2+1)-D)\|\nabla^+\rho_\cdot(t)\|^2_{\ell^2(\mathbb T_N)} \big\} \mathbf{1}_{i=1} \\
&\quad+ \big\{ 4\mathsf{a} \nabla^+\phi(t,0) + (2D-2\mathsf{a} )\|\nabla^+\rho_\cdot(t)\|^2_{\ell^2(\mathbb T_N)} \big\}\mathbf{1}_{i=0} 
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where $p_N=4$ if $N$ is even, whereas $p_N=2$ if $N$ is odd, and we introduced the discrete derivatives $\nabla^\pm g(i)=g(i\pm 1) -g(i)$, and $\Delta g(i)=g(i+1)+g(i-1)-2g(i)$ for any real sequence $(g(i))_{i\in\mathbb Z}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.460302+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e609f62045fa4544cde3c274290c70f39eae2f6d1f61f952a54673e09db1b68","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:expansion of arXiv:2609.02234, 'An $n(\log n)^{o(1)}$ bound for nested cycles without geometric crossings'] Let $G$ be a $K$-minimal graph of order $n$. If $\varnothing\ne U\subseteq V(G)$ and $u=|U|\le n/2$, then
