{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:15:55.056053+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f0ce492288d7129b703f3633d4a92d859a729415ab4408f20d343b0ec37c6ba","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition recap of arXiv:2608.29708, 'Intuitionistic and Constructive Modal Logics for Classical Modal Logicians'] The satisfaction relations $\Vdash^i$, $\Vdash^{\text{c}}$, $\Vdash^{\text{h}}$, $\Vdash^e$ are defined as follows:
  \begin{itemize}
    \item For the $\bot$ case:
          \begin{itemize}
            \item $x \not \Vdash^\bullet \bot$, for $\bullet \in \set{ i, h, e }$.
            \item $x \Vdash^{\text{c}} \bot \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} x \in W_\bot$, where $W_\bot$ is the set of fallible worlds.
          \end{itemize}
    \item For the $\Box$ case:
          \begin{itemize}
            \item $x \Vdash^\iota \Box \varphi \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} \forall x' \geq x \, \forall y' \sqsupset x' \, (y' \Vdash^\iota \varphi)$, for $\iota \in \set{ c, i, h }$.
            \item $x \Vdash^e \Box \varphi \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} \forall y \sqsupset x \, (y \Vdash^e \varphi)$.
          \end{itemize}
    \item For the $\Diamond$ case:
          \begin{itemize}
            \item $x \Vdash^\iota \Diamond \varphi \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} \forall x' \geq x \, \exists y' \sqsupset x' \, (y' \Vdash^\iota \varphi)$, for $\iota \in \set{ c, i }$.
            \item $x \Vdash^\varepsilon \Diamond \varphi \mathrel{\;\ratio\Longleftrightarrow\;} \exists y \sqsupset x \, (y \Vdash^\varepsilon \varphi)$, for $\varepsilon \in \set{ h, e }$.
          \end{itemize}
  \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

