{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.845481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f214f06598bf025f59f986f6ef0a218aa7eb8174ac819a0d823f94a5e66a04a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:GaussianDiscrepancy of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] Let $A_1,\ldots,A_n \sim \mathrm{GOE}(m)$ independently for some $m = m(n)$.
        \begin{enumerate}[label=(\alph*)]
            \item Assume that $\omega(1) = m^2 \ll n/\log{n}$. Then, for any constants $\beta < 1 < \gamma$,
            \begin{equation*}
                \lim_{n \to \infty} \P{\beta\frac{2}{e^{3/4}}\sqrt{nm}4^{-\xi n/m^2} < \disc(A_1,\ldots,A_n) \leq \gamma\frac{2}{e^{3/4}}\sqrt{nm}4^{-\xi n/m^2}} = 1,
