    is an equivalence in \(\mcalD_{\qcoh}(V)\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.950305+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f780890c0ee0962149ca2923b3e6751fd65a111874211a10a8b4bbf5c329596","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 33 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] Let $X$ have density $f$ with respect to $\pi_{T}.$ If $H(X|\pi_{T}) < \infty$ and $T=\E X,$ then
    \begin{displaymath}
        H \big( T_{a} ( S(X)) | T_{a}(X) \big) = \E_{\pi_{aT}} \Psi \big( P_{T(1-a)}f , DP_{T(1-a)}f \big) < \infty
    \end{displaymath}
    for all $a < 1.$ Moreover, for any $a < 1 $
    \begin{displaymath}
        \Big(  \Psi \big( P_{T(1-b)} f , DP_{T(1-b)} f \big) \Big)_{0 \le b \le a} 
