{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.083409+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9fa8bd27872d72645881d0324b6da59c2a2c65f56c06deaad20002258168abae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:MartTrans of arXiv:2504.18739, 'discrete analogues of second-order Riesz transforms'] Let $A$ be a matrix-valued function with $\|A\|<\infty$. Then 
\begin{align} 
    \mathbb{E}_{(0, T)}| A\star M_T^f|^p& \leq (p^\ast -1)^p\|A\|^p\mathbb{E}_{(0, T)} |M_T^f|^p\\
    &=(p^\ast -1)^p\|A\|^p\mathbb{E}_{(0, T)}|f(X_T)|^p\nonumber\\
    &=(p^\ast -1)^p\|A\|^p\sum_{n\in \mathbb{Z}^d}|f(n)|^p\frac{P_T(n)}{H_T(0)}.\nonumber
\end{align}
Suppose that $b, B$ are constants such that $-\infty<b<B<\infty$ and $A$ has the property that for all $\xi\in \mathbb{R}^d$,
\begin{equation} 
    b|\xi|^2\leq A(\xi, t)\xi\cdot \xi \leq B|\xi|^2,\quad \text{for all} \,\, (x, t)\in\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{R}_+.
\end{equation}
Then, 
\begin{align}
    \mathbb{E}_{(0, T)}| A\star M_T^f|^p\leq C_{p,b,B}^p\|A\|^p \mathbb{E}_{(0, T)}|M_T^f|^p=C_{p,b,B}^p\|A\|^p\sum_{n\in \mathbb{Z}^d}|f(n)|^p\frac{P_T(n)}{H_T(0)}, 
\end{align}
where $C_{p,b,B}$ is the Choi ~[Cho] constant. In particular, when $b=0$ and $B=1$, $C_{p,0,1}=\gamma(p)$ is the constant in (equation RieszSharp2 of the paper) satisfying the basic asymptotics in (equation ChoiAsym of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.420636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9faa533a64d091709bb48c4b1d9c436c6cd94cc969638fe0f6ffb83a85d4a7b5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture conj:barcode_limit_via_F of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] The following limit exists for all
