{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.449362+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0327bcc7b6c976cd308e487fe036a78cd0d63dd3ba736bd26f0ff12b293918f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Integer-valued Gaussian free field on a general graph of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] To each finite connected rooted graph $G := (W , E , \rho)$ (with vertex set $W$, edge set $E$, root $\rho \in W$) equipped with conductances $J := (J_{yz})_{\{y,z\} \in E} \in (0 , \infty)^E$, we associate the space of functions $\Omega_W := \left\{ \varphi : W \to \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}} \, : \, \varphi(\rho) = 0 \right\}$ and equip it with the probability distribution
	\begin{equation*}
	\mathbb{P}_{G , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}\mathrm{-GFF}}( \{ \varphi \}) := \frac{1}{Z_{G , J}} \exp \left( - \sum_{yz \in E}  \frac{\left( \varphi(y) - \varphi(z) \right)^2}{J_{yz}} \right).
	\end{equation*}
	We denote by $\mathrm{Var}_{G , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}\mathrm{-GFF}}$ the variance with respect to the measure $\mathbb{P}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}\mathrm{-GFF}}_{G , J}$.","status":"unverified"}

