{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.437201+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a05822b2c5237c6264ae30314cb0ea2863f59d14dbb41cf0e08d53201c26c0d2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2606.15178, 'The distribution of the de Moivre experiment'] Let $X\sim\mathcal{B}^{(s)}(n,p)$ and let $x_i=\sum_{l=1}^{s}l^ip^lq^{s-l}=E(X_1^i)$. Then, for every $r\geq1$,
	\begin{equation}
		\kappa_r(X)=n\sum_{k=1}^{r}(-1)^{k-1}(k-1)!\,B_{r,k}\big(x_1,x_2,\ldots,x_{r-k+1}\big), \quad \text{ for } p\neq q, 
	\end{equation}
	and
	\begin{equation}
		\kappa_r(X)=n\sum_{k=1}^{r}(-1)^{k-1}(k-1)!\,p^{ks}\,B_{r,k}\Big(\sum_{l=1}^{s}l,\sum_{l=1}^{s}l^2,\ldots,\sum_{l=1}^{s}l^{r-k+1}\Big), \quad \text{ for } p=q.
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.388799+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a05c3be46c9ca7c57140bdf4c37551061817125e292b2bedb0b4b93dcf478e1c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2609.04139, 'The conformally invariant metric on CLE$_4$ II:\\ existence of geodesics'] Let $\alpha \subset \partial \BD$ be a deterministic connected arc. Let $\tau$ be a stopping time for the filtration generated by 
	\begin{equation*}
		\left(\SCB_t(\alpha; D_{\Gamma_\BD}^\BD), \Gamma_\BD|_{\SCB_t(\alpha; D_{\Gamma_\BD}^\BD)}\right)_{t \ge 0}. 
	\end{equation*}
	Let $\{V_j\}_j$ denote the connected components of $\BD \setminus \SCB_\tau(\alpha; D^\BD_{\Gamma_\BD})$.
	Then, there is a coupling $\{(\Gamma_\BD\vert_{V_j}, D^{V_j}_{\Gamma_\BD \vert_{V_j}})\}_j$ such that, conditionally on $\SCB_\tau(\alpha; D^\BD_{\Gamma_\BD})$, the $(\Gamma_\BD\vert_{V_j}, D^{V_j}_{\Gamma_\BD \vert_{V_j}})$'s are independent and have the law of $(\Gamma_{V_j}, D^{V_j}_{\Gamma_{V_j}})$ respectively. Moreover,
		\begin{itemize}
	\item For all $j$, for all $\SCL_1, \SCL_2 \in \Gamma_\BD|_{V_j}$, we have $D_{\Gamma_\BD}^\BD(\SCL_1, \SCL_2)\le D_{\Gamma_\BD|_{V_j}}^{V_j}(\SCL_1, \SCL_2)$.
	\item For all $j$, for all $\SCL \in \Gamma_\BD|_{V_j}, \ t \in [0, D_{\Gamma_\BD}^\BD(\SCL, \partial V_j)]$, we have $\SCB_t(\SCL; D_{\Gamma_\BD}^\BD) = \SCB_t(\SCL; D_{\Gamma_\BD|_{V_j}}^{V_j})$.
	\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.068254+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a05cae5cb584e3accd361f75ae913fa048c7ea1636e01ff5e16d27a2f7b8951b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem elemlemma of arXiv:2506.15500, 'On extinction and survival of the Bak-Sneppen model on arbitrary graphs'] Let $X_n$ be an ergodic Markov chain on a finite state space $\mathcal{S}$ with the stationary distribution $\pi$; assume that $0$ is one of the states. Suppose there is a non-negative function $f:\mathcal{S}\to{\mathbb R}$ such that 
\begin{align}
\begin{split}
f(0)&=0;\\    
\max_{x\in\mathcal{S}: \ p_{0x}>0} f(x)&=c_0;\\
|f(X_{n+1})-f(X_n)|&\le C;\\
{\mathbb E}(f(X_{n+1})-f(X_n)\mid X_n=x)&<-\varepsilon,\quad x\ne 0,
\end{split}
\end{align}
for some $\varepsilon>0$, $c_0>0$, and $C>0$.
Then for some $c_1,c_2>0$ depending on $c_0,C,\varepsilon$ only,
\begin{align}
\pi(A_k)\le c_1 e^{-c_2 k},
\quad\text{where }A_k=\{x\in\mathcal{S}:\ f(x)>k\},\ k>0.  
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.935116+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a05db50077c8b4ac7fca1cdefb6e03f173144b35eaaf67412a7fbfec0cfb9851","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $(G, \weight)$, $|V(G)| = n$, be a finite weighted graph with $\weight(e) = \exp(-\beta \omega_e)$ and (weighted) UST law $\bP^\omega_{G,\beta}$ with partition function $Z^\omega_{G, \beta}$. Recall that the Hamiltonian of $T$ was defined as $H(T,\omega) = \sum_{e \in T} \omega_e$. We have the following (partial) derivatives:
    \begin{align}
        \frac{\partial }{\partial \beta} \bP^\omega_{G,\beta}(\cT = T) &= \bP^\omega_{G, \beta}(\cT = T) \big(\bE^\omega_{G, \beta}[H(\cT, \omega)] - H(T, \omega) \big), \\



        \frac{\partial }{\partial \beta } \bP^\omega_{G,\beta}(e \in \cT ) &= \bE^\omega_{G, \beta}[ 1_{e \in \cT}] \bE^\omega_{G, \beta}[H(\cT, \omega)] - \bE^\omega_{G, \beta}[ 1_{e \in \cT} H(\cT, \omega)], \\

        \frac{\partial }{\partial \omega_f }  \bP^\omega_{G,\beta}(e \in \cT) &= \beta \big(  \bP^\omega_{G,\beta}(e \in \cT)  \bP^\omega_{G,\beta}(f \in \cT) - \bP^\omega_{G,\beta}(e,f \in \cT) \big). 
    \end{align}
    Furthermore, if $(\omega_e)_{e \in E}$ are distributed as independent standard Gaussian random variables, then the partition function $Z^\omega_{G, \beta}$ satisfies
    \begin{equation}
         \frac{\partial }{\partial \beta } \E \Big[ \log Z^\omega_{G, \beta} \Big] =  \beta (n-1) -  \beta \sum_{e \in E} \E \big[ \bP^\omega_{G,\beta}(e \in \cT)^2 \big] . 
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.100822+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a05dd584d7d0110d14036154c627bef98164bfde3e3748ce195c5bb4ac9ab96f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition DEF33 of arXiv:2412.08886, 'On domination for (non-symmetric) Dirichlet forms'] A real-valued process $M=(M_t)_{t\geq 0}$ is called a \emph{multiplicative functional} (MF, for short) of $X$ if it satisfies the following conditions:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(1)] The map $t\mapsto M_t(\omega)$ is decreasing,  right continuous and takes values in $[0,1]$ for all $\omega\in \Omega$;
\item[(2)] $M$ is adapted, i.e., $M_t\in \mathcal{F}_t$ for every $t\geq 0$;
\item[(3)] $M_{t+s}(\omega)=M_t(\omega)M_s(\theta_t\omega)$ holds for all $s,t\geq 0$ and $\omega\in \Omega$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.706265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a05e817c1233c6a13a4b540016e9053597e31d60a9d14132435c02bae7d43081","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:8.2 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] For all $n$ large enough, $x \in {\rm D}_n^\circ$ and $y \in \partial {\rm B}(x; r_n)$, 
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{P}_y \big(\tau_{\partial} < \widecheck{{\mathbf T}}_{{\rm B}(x;r_n)} \big) \leq n^{-\eta_0/3}\,,
	\end{equation}
	where $\eta_0$ is as in~(equation e:2.3 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.551584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a060400e8813d794dbcfd0e6ced5cd1ba1ac97b07acef88bf229492a76a855f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2604.01978, 'Homogenized Transformers'] Let $X^n = §(x^{n}_1,\ldots, x^{n}_1)$ solve 
\begin{equation*}
\de x^{n}_i(t)=\int_{\Uptheta}G_{\mu^{n}(t)}(x_{i}^n(t);\bm{\theta})\mathsf{W}(\de \bm{\theta}, \de t),
\end{equation*}
with $\mu^n = \mu_{X^n}$. 
Let $(\bar x_1,\ldots,\bar x_n)$ be conditionally i.i.d., given $(\mathscr{F}^{\mathsf W}_t)_{t\geq0}$, copies of the unique solution $x$ of \eqref{eq:non_linear_SDE_common}, driven by the same common noise $\mathsf{W}$, and let $\bar\mu$ be their empirical measure. Then for every $T>0$ there exists $C_T>0$ such that 
\begin{align*}
    \max_{i\in[n]} \E \sup_{t\in[0, T]} \left\|x^{n}_i(t)-\bar x_i(t)\right\|^2 &+ \E \sup_{t\in[0, T]} W_2^2(\mu^n(t), \bar\mu^n(t)) \\
    &\leq  \frac{C_T}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n \E \left\|x^{n,i}(0)-\bar x^i(0)\right\|^2.
\end{align*}
In particular, after choosing an optimal coupling of the initial data, the right hand side may be written as $C_T \E W_2^2(\mu^n(0), \bar \mu^n(0))$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.068098+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0615db0afeab78852b930329d08d846cfd209115e7ce80f901b59883fe138de","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2606.00945, 'Ising model and percolation: from hexagonal lattice to 3-12 lattice'] Fix $N\ge 1$ and $2N$-polygon $(\Omega;y_1,\ldots,y_{2N})$. 
Suppose $(\Omega_{\312}^\delta;y_1^\delta,\ldots, y_{2N}^\delta)$ is a family of discrete polygons such that $(\Omega_{\312}^\delta;y_1^\delta,\ldots,y_{2N}^\delta)$ converges to $(\Omega;y_1,\ldots,y_{2N})$ in the close-Carathéodory sense as $\delta\to 0$. 
Let $\LA^\delta_{\312}$ be the link pattern for percolation with $p=1/2$ in $(\Omega_{\312}^{\delta, *}; y_1^\delta,\ldots, y_{2N}^\delta)$ with alternating boundary conditions. Then the scaling limits for probabilities for the link pattern are conformally invariant:
\begin{align}
\lim_{\delta\to 0}\PP_{\Perco}\left[\LA_{\312}^{\delta}=\alpha\right]=\LZ_{\alpha}^{(6)}(\Omega; y_1, \ldots, y_{2N}), \qquad\text{for all }\alpha\in\LP_N, 
\end{align}
where $\{\LZ_{\alpha}^{(6)}: \alpha\in\LP_N\}$ are the pure partition functions for multiple $\SLE_6$ given in Definition~\ref{def::pure_partition}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.630610+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a064dee2d5e08c69ad85e381b4ef09d002d125e39de71a535f52d8735fe80cf2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\psi \in \mathbf{\Psi}$, $A \in \mathcal{A}$, $C_{\psi,A} \in \mathcal{C}_{am}$ and let $L$, $R$ be defined according to eq. \eqref{eq:definition_L_R}. Then 
