{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:10.034169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0b3ce6bd3aca451462591bc74730e782e8d990751b3de24850b61678e632798","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2506.09609, 'Schramm-Loewner evolution contains a topological Sierpi\'nski carpet when $\kappa$ is clos'] There exists a constant $C_1 = C_1(\varrho) \geq 100$ such that the following holds for all $N \geq C_1$ and any vertex sets $\{\mathcal{A}_m\}$ satisfying Conditions~\ref{condition:fractal-1} and~\ref{condition:fractal-2}, and $k \geq 0$.

