{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.765760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0c87c347f12051b60542ca1ec7819d0c445e8d866b8d04de2074eed504ba16d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 (\cites{Hei88, NX21}) of arXiv:2608.26723, 'Extrinsic upper bounds for the harmonic mean of eigenvalues in curved manifolds'] Let $M$ be an $m(\ge 2)$-dimensional closed orientable submanifold in an $n$-dimensional Riemannian manifold $N$ of the sectional curvature $K_N \le \delta$.
