{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:53.164383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0e1a9f8bb9ce446b5f910150f88630e28fe0bfcccde313a82c379819bb124b5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2607.02777, 'Hypocoercivity for Hamiltonian Diffusions \\ with Singular Drift'] Let $(T,D(T))$ be a linear operator on $H$ satisfying $\core \subset D(T)$ and $AP(\core )\subset D(T^*)$. If there is a constant $N<\infty$ such that 
