{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.678424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0e3f63449e019cae603edc7cbd0b59665e4982469788af22ddbe942842566b8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2609.03750, '\bf Pullback Measure Attractors, Zero-Noise Limits, and Moderate Deviations for 2D Stochas'] Suppose Hypotheses \ref{PEeqAssum-2.2}, \ref{PEeqAssum-2.3}, \ref{PEeqAssum-2.4} and \eqref{PETNs-3.01} hold. Let $\tau\in\mathbb{R}$, $T>0$, and let $\mathfrak{B}(\tau)>0$ be a given constant. Then, for every $\zeta\in L^4(\Omega,\mathscr F_\tau;\mathcal H)$ satisfying $\mathbb E[|\zeta|^4+|\partial_z\zeta|^4]\leq\mathfrak B^4(\tau)$,
