{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.374199+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a122abddbcdaacd857ded99c629751adfce81c8839c163fa4d84a84fd318354b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 12 of arXiv:2606.04245, 'Properties of a Special Type of Filtration and its Martingale Criteria'] Assume $P(\gamma=+\infty)>0$, $\EE[\sup\limits_{t\in[0,+\infty)} |F(t)|]<+\infty$ and $\EE[|L|]<+\infty$. 
    Let $M$ be a local martingale on $\RRl_+$ defined by $M_t=F(t)\ind_{\{t<\gamma\}}+L\ind_{\{t\geq\gamma\}}$. 
    A necessary condition for the process $(M_t)_{t\in\RRl_+}$ to be a martingale is that the following equality holds on the set $\{\gamma=+\infty\}$: 
    $$
    \EE[L\mid\cH]\ind_{\{\gamma=+\infty\}}=F(0)\ind_{\{\gamma=+\infty\}}
    $$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.576077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1256caee8cfd05673b625db9996ac5c8b15a12ff3ef39610d971a95babd861b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-inequality for L of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] There exists a constant $c>0$ such that for any $x, x' \in \bb R$, 
