{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:44.969844+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1329ea52708181df364fdfa673646c214c229368e81f817e077cefc0c930553","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 (Small-time expansion of the coordinate profile) of arXiv:2605.11451, '2605.11451'] Let $1\le p<2$ and $n\ge2$, and let $Z\sim N(0,1)$. As $t\downarrow0$,
\begin{equation}
 h_{p,n,t,e_1}(0)
 =
 C_{p,n}\left(1-\frac{n-1}{p}\,\E|Z|^p\,t^{p/2}+O_{p,n}(t)\right),
\end{equation}
and therefore
\begin{equation}
 \Phi_{p,n}(t)
 =
 C_{p,n}\sqrt{v_{p,n}}\left(1-\frac{n-1}{p}\,\E|Z|^p\,t^{p/2}+O_{p,n}(t)\right).
