{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.851010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a15060d207907f66179b63c45f05f4f6b1e881c5e0404ffe3411cba6adfdd26b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2511.11189, 'Sharp asymptotics for the maximal distance from the boundary to the nucleus of a typical P'] For every $t>0$, we have
		\begin{equation}
			\E[\Card(\VOMR)] = (d\kappa_d)^d C_d \sum_{i=0}^{d-1} t^{di} \kappa_d^{i-d+1} \frac{(d-1)!}{i!} e^{-\kappa_d t^d} 
