{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:50:36.765178+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1ac73c0b9f05f6ceb296c34d17870665b397bdf5c09f794b0250f227274a9da","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 (Evaluation of the quadratic Gau\ss\, sum) of arXiv:2609.04155, 'The subconvexity problem for symmetric square\\ $L$-functions in Level aspect'] If $q$ is odd,
			\begin{equation}
				G(a, b; q)= \eps_c \left(\frac{a}{q}\right)e\left(-\frac{\overline{4a}b^2}{q}\right) 
			\end{equation}
			where 
			\begin{equation*}
				\eps_c = \begin{cases}
