for any $0\leq s < t < T$, any $x,y\in\mathbb{R}^d$ and $m=0,1,2$. Here, $p_{\mathscr{K},\cdot}$ is the Gaussian density in (equation eq:kol_dens of the paper).

\item[(iii)] Furthermore, for any $s\in[0,T)$ and $\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, the flow of time-marginal densities of the solution to SDE$(\beta,\sigma;s,\nu)$ is the unique (weak) solution to FP$(\beta,\sigma;s, \nu)$ (see Definition (def:sol_lin_fp of the paper)). In particular, for any $x\in\mathbb{R}^d$, $(p(s,x; t, \cdot))_{t\in(s,T)}$ is a density solution to FP$(\beta,\sigma;s, \delta_x)$.
