{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.338956+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a20a4aebf04f59c3c74f4a963ba66cd8403386c0fabfa1e124eb68789fb2d2bf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition MBBM exceeding particles num for a subset of arXiv:2606.19207, 'Extrema of cooling branching Brownian motion and related Gaussian fields'] Let $\{\xi_\varepsilon^{\alpha,z}(t)\colon t\geq0,\ z\in V_\varepsilon\}$ be the MBBM defined in (equation eqM: MBBM of the paper), and recall $A_\alpha(\cdot)$ from (equation eqIntroduction: A(t) of the paper). Fix $T_r\geq s_0$, with $s_0$ as in Lemma~(lemma: covariance estimate for MBBM of the paper), and assume that $T_r=N_r\log 2$ for some $N_r\in\mathbb{Z}_+$. Then there exist constants $C,c>0$ and $T_*,\lambda_*>0$ such that, for every $N\in\mathbb{Z}_+$ with $T:=N\log 2\geq T_*$ and $\varepsilon:=2^{-N}$, every subset $\Lambda\subset V_\varepsilon$, and every $\lambda\geq\lambda_*$,
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{P}\Bigl(
		\max_{z\in\Lambda}\xi_\varepsilon^{\alpha,z}(T+T_r)
		\geq A_\alpha(T+T_r)+\lambda-n
		\Bigr)
		\leq Ce^{-c(\lambda-n)},
		\qquad n\in\mathbb{Z}_+,\quad n\leq\lambda,
