{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.696222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a21d9e009fb8a00fc2f3023586a0c231f1e3d06fd2158ab8af7d3c072e94d87e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor SDdegbound of arXiv:2411.18563, 'Lower tails for triangles inside the critical window'] Let $\lambda > 0$, $\zeta \in [0,1]$, and $p = \frac{\lambda}{1 + \lambda}$. For any $\kappa > 0 $ we have
