{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.296075+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a290f428b6855e4641e5cf10fc3a75b5e896ad9ae14ca55442ea49d34dc55f7f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mu_continuous of arXiv:2605.22787, 'Invariant measures for half-space geometric LPP: classification and the one force--one sol'] The function $s \mapsto \mu_{c,s}$ over $s \in [r_c,q^{-1})$ is weakly continuous in the space of probability measures on $\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{N}}$. Furthermore, the measure escapes to $\infty$ as $s \to q^{-1}$. That is, for any $A \in (0,\infty)$ and any integers $k > m \ge 0$, 
