{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:50:36.763409+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2936e046d6b236861797c909c010dbb9c98d90839e2df21c2ce8cd7ecaa0880","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 (Poisson summation formula) of arXiv:2609.04155, 'The subconvexity problem for symmetric square\\ $L$-functions in Level aspect'] Let $K:\Z\to\C$ be a $q$-periodic function on $\Z$, and $V\in C_c^\infty(\R)$ be a smooth function. For $X\gg1$,
		\begin{equation*}
			\sum_{n\in\Z}K(n)V\left(\frac{n}{X}\right)=\frac{X}{\sqrt{q}}\sum_{n\in\Z}\widehat{K}(n)\widehat{V}\left(\frac{n}{q/X}\right),
