{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.013450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2a30a325726866f305cbd670e196aa033e13110d22a764d4cd55bccdb685790","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 26 of arXiv:2605.04359, 'Well-posedness of reflected BSDEs with default time and irregular barrier: An application '] Let $Y=\left(Y^1,Y^2,\cdots,Y^n\right)$ be an adapted $n$-dimensional process with regulated trajectories of the form
	\begin{equation}
		Y_t=Y^{\ast}_t+\sum_{0 \leq s <t} \Delta_{+} Y_s,\quad \forall t \in [0,T],

	\end{equation}
	where $Y^{\ast}=\left(Y^{\ast,1},Y^{\ast,2},\cdots,Y^{\ast,n}\right)$ is an RCLL adapted $n$-dimensional semimartingale and $\sum_{s <t} \left|\Delta_{+}  Y_s\right|  <\infty$  a.s. Let $F$ be
	a twice continuously differentiable function on $\mathbb{R}^n$. Then the process
	$\left(F\left(Y_t\right)\right)_{t \leq T}$ also has the form \eqref{form of the process for Ito}. Moreover, almost surely, for each $n \geq 1$ and all $t \leq T$,
	\begin{equation*}
		\begin{split}
			F\left(Y_t\right)
			&=F\left(Y_0\right)+\sum_{k=1}^n \int_{0}^{t} D^k F\left(Y_{s-}\right)dY^{\ast,k}_s+\dfrac{1}{2}\sum_{k,l=1}^n  \int_{0}^{t} D^k D^l F\left(Y_{s-}\right) d\left[Y^{\ast,k},Y^{\ast,l}\right]^c_s\\
			& \quad+\sum_{0 < s \leq t}\left\{ F\left(Y_s\right)-F\left(Y_{s-}\right)-\sum_{k=1}^n  D^k F\left(Y_{s-}\right)\Delta_{-}Y^{\ast,k}_s\right\}\\
			&\quad+\sum_{0 \leq s < t} \left\{F\left(Y_{s+}\right)-F\left(Y_{s}\right)\right\},
		\end{split}
	\end{equation*}
	where $D^k$ denotes the differentiation operator with respect to the $k$-th coordinate,and $\left[\cdot,\cdot\right]^c$ denotes the continuous part of the quadratic variation $\left[\cdot,\cdot\right]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.331443+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2a4057b7f11d280d410823ca6c8639015a2011d506a9c8a4684fea040a8df0f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let ${\mathcal{C}}^\otimes$ be a small symmetric monoidal $T$-$\infty$-category. Then there exists a unique way to equip $\ul\PSh_T({\mathcal{C}})$ with a $T$-presentably symmetric monoidal structure and to make the Yoneda embedding $y\colon{\mathcal{C}}\to\ul\PSh_T({\mathcal{C}})$ into a $T$-symmetric monoidal functor $y^\otimes$. Moreover, if ${\mathcal{D}}^\otimes$ is any $T$-presentably symmetric monoidal $T$-$\infty$-category, then restriction along $y^\otimes$ defines an equivalence
    \[
        {\textup{Fun}}^{\textup{L},\otimes}(\ul\PSh_T({\mathcal{C}}^\otimes),{\mathcal{D}}^\otimes)\xrightarrow{\;\smash{\raisebox{-0.25ex}{\ensuremath{\scriptstyle\sim}}}\;}
        {\textup{Fun}}^\otimes({\mathcal{C}}^\otimes,{\mathcal{D}}^\otimes).\pushQED{\qed}\qedhere\popQED
    \] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.921620+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2a8a146847f4f9db07cc40396e5fc30f70ead6eda4a777e4e6853cc260c3810","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] Let $(X_{t})_{0 \le t \le T}$ be the Poisson F\"ollmer process. Then, we have
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $X_{t} \sim P_{T-t}f \dd \pi_{t}$ for all $0 \le t \le T.$
        \item Denote the compensated process $(\tilde{X_{t}})_{0 \le t \le T}$ as 
        \begin{displaymath}
            \tilde{X_{t}} := X_{t} - \int_{0}^{t} \lambda_{s} \dd s.
        \end{displaymath}
        Then, $(\tilde{X_{t}})_{0 \le t \le T}$ is a martingale.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.468294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2aa8e32914a81acf51ce856dfc157cb7ba50bd01d424e7e5a97b225055fa74a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 40 of arXiv:2604.04267, 'On Sharpest Tail Bounds for Functions \\ of Tail Bounded Random Variables'] The left shift operator $\mathscr{S}_L$ is defined as
\begin{equation*}
\mathscr{S}_L: (f,G) \mapsto (X_1,...,X_n)
\end{equation*}
where $f=(f_1,...,f_n) \in \mathcal{B}_L, \ \emptyset \neq G = G^1 \times \cdots \times G^n$ is closed, and \footnote{This is an analog of \eqref{SRXkeq}, obtained by reflecting about $0$. $f_k^{-1}[s,1], \forall s \in (0,1)$ 
is used instead of $f_k^{-1}[1-s,1]$ because we want $\mathscr{S}_L(f_k,G^k) \in \mathcal{N}$, namely to be monotonically increasing.}
\begin{equation*}
   X_k(s) := \inf \big(G^k\cup [\sup G^k, \infty) \big)_{\geq \inf f_k^{-1}[s,1]}, \ \forall s \in(0,1). 
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.330749+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2aeffd8aa0c37eab8c3bd08fed27148398e5cf0a54a7d74b9a766c806b65969","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop mySp-vs-mySp-gl of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] The inclusion of equivariantly cofibrant orthogonal $G$-spectra induces a fully faithful global functor ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}\to{\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{gl}$. Moreover, its underlying ${\vphantom{\textup{t}}\smash{\textup{Orb}}}$-functor admits a right adjoint which is levelwise a localization at the equivariant weak equivalences.
    \begin{proof}
        Lemma~(lemma:equiv-spectra-vs-gl-spectra of the paper) already shows that ${\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}\to{\mathpalette\ulhelper{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}}\hbox{\rule[-2pt]{0pt}{0pt}}_\textup{gl}$ is fully faithful and admits a pointwise right adjoint which is a localization at the equivariant weak equivalences.
        To complete the proof, it remains to verify the Beck--Chevalley condition for the pointwise right adjoints with respect to \emph{injective} homomorphisms. As the right adjoints are localizations, this amounts to saying that $\alpha^*\colon{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\text{$G'$-gl}\to{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\text{$G$-gl}$ sends $G'$-equivariant weak equivalences to $G$-equivariant ones for any injective $\alpha\colon G\to G'$. This is however immediate from Proposition~(prop:i!-left-Quillen-equiv-sp of the paper).
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.094211+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2b4a9c66a978fd5140631891f5e40d5b943bf607c20df7eca195e11d6e91142","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:biOPE of arXiv:2411.15830, 'Deformations of biorthogonal ensembles and universality'] Let  $(\mathcal X_n)_{n\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence of biorthogonal ensembles of the { form (equation def:BiOEscaled of the paper)} with corresponding sequence of correlation kernels $({\mathsf K}_n)_{n\in \mathbb{N}}$. Let $(\sigma_n)_{n\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence of Borel measurable functions $\sigma_n:\mathbb{K} \to[0,1]$. If Assumption (assumption:sigma of the paper) holds,
then the limit
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\mathcal G_n^{\sigma_n}[h]=\mathcal G^\sigma[h],
\end{equation}

holds true for any continuous function $h:\mathbb{K} \to [0,+\infty)$ with bounded support.

In particular, the deformed biorthogonal ensemble $\mathcal X_n^{\sigma_n}$ converges weakly as $n\to\infty$ to the deformed limit point process $\mathcal X^{\sigma}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:15:09.091500+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2b5ee4943f2ab49dd52710e5e7d42b641961252b6f45227443043ef084bae65","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Berry-Esseen bound Wigner of arXiv:2411.11341, 'Ultra high order cumulants and quantitative CLT for polynomials in Random Matrices'] Let $\mathcal{X}\sim Wigner$. Consider the polynomial $P(\mathcal{X},\mathcal{D})$ in ((def of P of the paper)) and the random variable $\mathfrak{X}$ defined in ((object_normalized of the paper)). Suppose that $\mathbf{C}_1-\mathbf{C}_3$ are satisfied. Then we have the following three conclusions.

(i)({\it CLT with Cram\'{e}r correction}) For any $x\in [0,\tilde{\theta}_2 N^{1/(6M-1)})$ for sufficiently small constant $\tilde{\theta}_2\equiv \tilde{\theta}_2(K, M, \mathsf{C}, \mathfrak{c},t)>0$,
we have 
\begin{align}
\mathbb{P}(\mathfrak{X}\geq x) = e^{{L(x)}}\mathbb{P}(Z\geq x)\left( 1+ O\left( \frac{x+1}{(\sqrt{N})^{1/(6M-1)}}\right) \right).

\end{align}
Here ${L(x)}$  satisfies $$|{L(x)}|= O(x^3/(\sqrt{N})^{1/(6M-1)}). $$ 
If $\mathbf{C}_1'$ is additionally assumed, the parameter $6M$ can be improved to $2M$ in all above formulas. 

(ii) ({\it Berry-Esseen bound}) There exist a constant $C_1 \equiv C_1(K,M,\mathsf{C}, \mathfrak{c},t)$ such that,
$$\Delta(\mathfrak{X},Z)\leq \frac{C_{1}}{(\sqrt{N})^{1/(6M-1)}}.$$
If $\mathbf{C}_1'$ is additionally assumed, the parameter $6M$ can be improved to $2M$ in the above formula. 

(iii) ({\it Concentration}) There exist constants $C_2\equiv C_2(K, M, \mathsf{C}, \mathfrak{c}, t)>0$, $\hat{\theta}_2\equiv \hat{\theta}_2(K,M,\mathsf{C}, \mathfrak{c},t)>0$ and a constant $A>0$ that does not depend on $K, M, \mathsf{C}, \mathfrak{c}, t$ such that,
\begin{align}
\mathbb{P}(\mathfrak{X}\geq x) \leq A \exp\left( -\frac{1}{2}\frac{x^2}{C_2+x^{2-\frac{1}{3M}}(\hat{\theta}_2\sqrt{N})^{-\frac{1}{3M}}}\right)

\end{align}
for all $x\geq 0$. If $\mathbf{C}_1'$ is additionally assumed, the parameter $3M$ can be improved to $M$ in the above formula. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:25:40.141607+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2b635c354577fc4827c591b81d991bf4ed78512823f58d8ed02b87e14f83f79","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma kernel-growth of arXiv:2609.00425, 'Individual and Uniform Eventual Positivity of Self-Adjoint Semigroups'] For each $n\in\mathbb{N}$, let $h_n\colon[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}$ be given by $h_n(t)\coloneqq\mathrm{e}^{-(n-\delta_n)t}-\mathrm{e}^{-nt}$. Then one has
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{\sup_{t \geq 0} h_n(t)}{u_n} \longrightarrow 0
    \end{align*}
    as $n \to \infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.922693+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2b9489d6e5ba9fe75a08759a0d70a716178cdd554f9409eacc0773eaa366375","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2608.29914, 'Fixed points in abstract provability structures'] For each one-variable meet APS term $\triangle v$, we define $\mu(\triangle)\in\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$ recursively as follows:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mu(v)=\infty$, 
    \item $\mu(\Box\triangle)=\mu(\triangle)+1$, 
    \item $\mu(\boxtimes\triangle)=0$, 
    \item $\mu(\triangle_0\land\triangle_1) = \min\{\mu(\triangle_0), \mu(\triangle_1)\}$.
\end{enumerate}
Here, $\infty+1=\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.657881+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2bb4ab5b21341729e321a8587de3870c00365f8697a0519d1440587eb03bfe3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:vertical of arXiv:2608.24830, 'Motion helps the contact process: survival below\\ the percolation threshold on Poisson Br'] There is $c=c(d)>0$ such that the following holds. Let $\eta>0$, $\epsilon\in(0,1)$,
$0<\Delta\le\Lambda$ and $W>0$, and let $\ell$ satisfy
\begin{equation}

  \Delta\ge c_0\ell^2(\epsilon/3)^{-4/\kappa}\qquad\text{and}\qquad\eta\ell^d\ge1 .
\end{equation}
Let $\mathsf G\ge\max\{c_1\Delta^{1/2}(\epsilon/3)^{-1/d},\,12r\}$, and put $K'=W+2\mathsf G$ and
$K=K'+2\mathsf G$. Let
$B\subseteq Q_W\times[0,t_0]$ and $B'\subseteq Q_W\times[t_0+\Delta,\Lambda]$, and let $A,A'$ be
increasing events determined by $B$ and $B'$ in the sense of (lem:Hprops of the paper). Then
\begin{equation}

  \mathbb{P}_\eta(A\cap A')\le\mathbb{P}_\eta(A)\Big[\mathbb{P}_{\eta(1+\epsilon)}(A')
  +\Gamma\,e^{-c\eta\epsilon^2\Delta^{d/2}}\Big]
  +\Big(\tfrac K\ell\Big)^de^{-c\eta\epsilon^2\ell^d}
  +C_d\,\eta\,(K+\Lambda^{1/2})^de^{-\mathsf G^2/(8d\Lambda)} ,
\end{equation}
where $\Gamma=C_d\,\epsilon^{-d}\big(K\Delta^{-1/2}\big)^{d(d+1)}$ is the factor
(equation eq:Gamma of the paper) of (thm:mixingupper of the paper) at mixing parameter $\epsilon/3$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-09T06:55:03+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2c6768429f320cfc463b28045f2fe74d360457c3ceea1c32b07fec273391018","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 19 of arXiv:2507.06186, '2507.06186'] For any $\ka,\eps,t>0$, we let $\mc K_{\ka,\eps}(t)$ denote the integral operator on $L^2(D)$ with kernel
\begin{align}

\mc K_{\ka,\eps}(t;x,y)=p_t(x-y)\mbf E_B\left[\mbf 1_{\{\tau_D(B^{x,y}_t)>t\}}\exp\left(-\ka\int_0^t\xi_\eps\big(B^{x,y}_t(r)\big)\d r\right)\right],\qquad x,y\in D,
\end{align}
where we assume that $B^{x,y}_t$ and $\xi_\eps$ are independent, and we use $\mbf E_B$ to
denote the (conditional) expectation with respect to the randomness in $B$ only.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.693347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2c9d2c767284a04e78c8ae93c4f55c00f6d284f68e691a161771edc49fe4188","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary coro_crdata of arXiv:2609.00645, 'Global persistence of nearly radial concentrated vortices in a bounded domain'] Under the assumptions of (thm:main of the paper), suppose in addition that
\[
  \mathbf a_\varepsilon=\mathbf a_*,
  \qquad
  \omega_{\varepsilon,0}(\mathbf x)
  =\omega_{\varepsilon,0}^*(\mathbf x-\mathbf a_*).
\]
Then, for all sufficiently small $\varepsilon>0$,
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{t\in\mathbb R}\left\{
  \mathcal D(\omega_{\varepsilon,t})
  +\kappa^2\sup_{\mathbf b\in\mathsf C(\omega_{\varepsilon,t})}
  [H(\mathbf b)-H(\mathbf a_*)]\right\}
  \leq C\varepsilon,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{t\in\mathbb R}\mathcal A(\omega_{\varepsilon,t})
  \leq C\varepsilon^{1/2}.
\end{equation}
If $D^2H(\mathbf a_*)$ is positive definite, then, after possibly decreasing
$\rho$,
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{t\in\mathbb R}\ \sup_{\mathbf b\in\mathsf C(\omega_{\varepsilon,t})}
  |\mathbf b-\mathbf a_*|
  \leq C\varepsilon^{1/2}.
\end{equation}
Here $C>0$ depends only on
$D,\mathbf a_*,\rho,\kappa,M$, and $R$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:38:04.518131+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2cd976a7aa6fd1bb6dbdce47f9a0cf78d3b8949edc025b921f7ef8873eb02e0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:biskup_level_0_bad of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{lem:biskup_induction_base}
