{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.323437+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2e8bb2f85cc8e84df35ee217f0f7faf46bc62419a5e0074e7efdd646b7a24eb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:measure-decomp-weak-poincare-glauber of arXiv:2411.09075, 'Weak Poincar{\'e} Inequalities, Simulated Annealing, and Sampling from Spherical Spin Glas'] Let $\pi$ be a distribution over $\{\pm 1\}^n$, and $\pi = \E_{\bz \sim \rho} \pi_{\bz}$ a measure decomposition of $\pi$ such that
