{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.328825+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2ec308f2995f3e9524f1eda2edee8026ea1b0c6f534ca07c127ffbe269a5977","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2607.06428, 'Impact of spinning on the early-warning signs in non-Markovian stochastic systems'] {\em (Wiener-Khintchine)}
    Let $(\mathbf{x}_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a (weakly) stationary process. Then,
    $AC(\tau)$ is a autocorrelation function of some (weakly) stationary process $\mathbf{x}_t$ if and only if there exists a function $F(\omega)$ having the properties of a distribution function on $(-\infty,\infty)$ such that for all $\tau\in\R$
\begin{align*}
    AC(\tau)=\int_\R e^{i\omega\tau}~\txtd F(\omega),
\end{align*}
where $F(\omega)$ is called the spectral distribution of $(\mathbf{x}_t)_{t\geq 0}$. Moreover, if 
$$\int_\R AC(\tau)~\txtd \tau<\infty,$$
we have
\begin{align*}
    F(\omega)=\int_{-\infty}^\omega \frac{S_\mathbf{x}(\theta)}{V(0)}~\txtd\theta.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.206139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2ef247798abdcd3465bf40f31a66079597c1b7e4917f5865e6a15e3c10e6285","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Propn 18 of arXiv:2604.27205, 'An Analysis of the Diaconis-Holmes-Neal Markov Chain Sampler Under Generalized Unimodal Un'] The probability that the path, as constructed in Lemma~\ref{step1}, has exactly $cn$ steps is bounded below by
        \begin{equation}
            P' \geq \frac{\tilde{\tilde{c}}m_{j^*}(n)}{z'}, 
        \end{equation}
        \noindent where $\tilde{\tilde{c}}$ is a constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.806373+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2f0051b4db287daafaaa307290f204959cc253c3e10c46f85afe59d2dfab609","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor l:meas3 of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] Fix $(s,x;t,y)\in\mathbb{R}^{4}_{\uparrow}$ and $s'<t'$ with $[s',t']\subset[s,t]$.
    For any Borel set $S\in \mathcal{B}(C([s,t]))$ and any $z<w$, define
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal{Z}^S_{B(z,w)^c} &= \mathcal{Z}^S_{B(z,w)^c}(s,x;t,y)\\
        &\coloneqq  \mathcal{Z}_\beta^\xi(s,x;t,y)\cdot \mathbb{P}_{\beta,(s,x),(t,y)}^\xi\left(
            S\cap \{X(r)\in [z,w]^c\text{ for all }r\in[s',t']\}
        \right).
    \end{align*}
    Then $\mathcal{Z}^S_{B(z,w)^c}$ is $\mathcal{F}_{B(z,w)^c}$-measurable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.383265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2f4db55d033bdd5d40c43394e11340d5e45408d7b9893e53432ec2b06ae6c42","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local_step_concentration of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] For $\alpha \in (0,\frac{1}{2})$ there is some $c > 0$ such that, for all $e \in \binom{[n]}{2}$ with $v \in e$,
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P} \mleft[ | \mathsf{N}^{\rho \to v}_G(X,e) - \mathsf{d}_\rho p^{\mathsf{e}-1} n^{\mathsf{v}-2} | > n^{\mathsf{v} - 2.5 + \alpha} \mright]
    \leq \Exp{- c n^{2\alpha}}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.954522+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2f63eea62cb52d3ac4ac7d51a3a20f60e1095fc0fa1fc40d1d3649fdda0645e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:two_sided_density of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] Under the assumptions of
Theorem~(thm:conc_density of the paper),
for all $t>0$ and $a>0$, the left tail is bounded via
\begin{align}
  \mathbb{P}^\nu\left(\overline{\rho}_t - \E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t] \leq -a\right)
  \leq
  \left\|\frac{\mathrm{d}\nu}{\mathrm{d}\mu}\right\|_{L^2(\mu)}
  \exp\bigl[-tI^\rho(\E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t] - a)\bigr].

\end{align}
Consequently, the two-sided
deviation probability satisfies
\begin{align}
  \mathbb{P}^\nu\left(\bigl|\overline{\rho}_t - \E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t]\bigr|\geq a\right)
  \leq
  2\left\|\frac{\mathrm{d}\nu}{\mathrm{d}\mu}\right\|_{L^2(\mu)}
  \exp\bigl[-t\min\bigl(I^\rho(\E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t] + a),I^\rho(\E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t] - a)\bigr)\bigr].

\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.055883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2f9aade335944d2558568f2c3493049c72a8bafc2128a76e7cce895b7bd3ca5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2607.01629, 'Quadratic fluctuations of speed-change Kawasaki dynamics'] For every test function  $f$, the sequence of corrected process
        \[
