where $\mathscr{Q} > 0$ is the normalizing constant turning \eqref{eq_Discrete_Gaussian_main} into a probability measure.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.298017+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a319b3bc2614181f5b62380923d24b25611775797a880bf9117c08d8b4885263","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2606.23242, 'Correction to ``The stepping stone model in a random environment'' - limit theorems for th'] As $ n \to \infty $, for $ \mu $-almost every $ \omega \in \Omega $, $ (L_n(t), t \in [0,T]) $ converges in probability to $ ( \gamma L^0_t(X^1-X^2), t \in [0,T]) $ in the Skorokhod topology, where $ L^0_t(X^1-X^2) $ is the local time at zero of $ X^1-X^2 $ and $ \gamma $ is given by
		\begin{equation} 
			\gamma = \int_\Omega \frac{\pi(\omega)^2}{N(\omega)} \mu(d\omega).
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.324950+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a319f7a3c08bbb62bbb4f06efe917e0b455000392b37f13a2f9accf10333bff9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop equiv-sp-compact-gen of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] The stable $\infty$-category ${\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G$ is compactly generated by the collection of suspension spectra $\Sigma^\infty G/H_+$ for all closed subgroups $H\subset G$. In particular, it is presentable.
    \begin{proof}
        By [HA]*{Proposition 1.4.4.1 and Corollary 1.4.4.2} it only remains to show that the spectra $\Sigma^\infty G/H_+$ form a set of compact generators in the triangulated sense, which is an instance of [DHLPS2019Proper]*{Corollary~1.59}.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.628033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a31c09bda3a52e9b0b385578a516831b74268ac13188ba4d84ef61e24baccf27","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:conv_BM_limit of arXiv:2411.03609, 'Asymptotically optimal Wasserstein couplings for the small-time stable domain of attractio'] Let $\bm{\Sigma}$ be a symmetric non-negative definite matrix on $\mathbb{R}^{d \times d}$ and define $\bm{X}^t=((\bm{\Sigma}\bm{B}_{st}+\bm{S}_{st})/\sqrt{t})_{s\in[0,1]}$ for $t\in(0,1]$ where $(\bm{B}_t)_{t \in [0,1]}$ is a standard Brownian motion on $\mathbb{R}^d$ independent of the pure-jump L\'evy process $\bm{S}$ with Blumenthal--Getoor index~$\beta$ (defined in~(equation eq:BG of the paper)).\\
{\nf(a)} Suppose $\beta\in[0,2)$ and fix any $\beta_* \in (\beta,2]$ when $\bm{S}$ is of infinite variation and $\beta_*=1$ otherwise. Then for any $q>0$ with $\mathds{E}[|\bm{X}_1|^q]<\infty$, we have
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{W}_q\big(\bm{X}^t,\bm{\Sigma}\bm{B}\big)
=\mathcal{O}\big(t^{(q\wedge 1)
    (\min\{1/q,1/\beta_*\}-1/2)}\big), 
    \qquad \text{ as }t \downarrow 0.
\end{align*}
{\normalfont(b)} Pick any $\bm{u}_*\in\mathbb{R}^d_{\bm{0}}$ and define $C_*\coloneqq |\bm{u}_*|^{-1}|\psi_{\bm{S}}(\bm{u}_*)|>0$. Then for all $q \geqslant 1$, we have 
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{W}_q(\bm{X}^t_1,\bm{\Sigma}\bm{B}_1)
    \geqslant\frac{C_*}{\sqrt{2}} \sqrt{t}+ \mathcal{O}(t^{3/2}),
\quad\text{as }t \downarrow 0.
\end{align*}
{\normalfont(c)}  Let $\lambda$ be the largest eigenvalue of $\bm{\Sigma}^2$. Suppose there exist $\delta\in[1,2)$ and vectors $(\bm{u}_r)_{r\in(0,\infty)}$ with $|\bm{u}_r|=r$ satisfying $c\coloneqq\inf_{r>1}r^{-\delta}|\psi_{\bm{S}}(\bm{u}_r)|>0$. Then for any $C_*\in(0,ce^{-\lambda/2})$ we have
$\mathcal{W}_q(\bm{X}^t_1,\bm{\Sigma}\bm{B}_1) \geqslant(C_*/\sqrt{2})t^{1-\delta/2}$ for all sufficiently small $t>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.568433+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a31d6ea569029887e7a1e07472a327a7c34d991a2d101748e458a8feca4c2f6b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:Start of arXiv:2411.12003, 'Central Limit Theorem for non-stationary random products of $\SL(2, \R)$ matrices'] Under the assumptions~((a:center of the paper))--((a:growth of the paper)) above, for the normalised variables~$\eta_{a;n}$, defined by~(equation eq:eta-family of the paper), the following estimate holds. There exists $\rho_0 > 0$, such that for any $n\ge n_0$, \emr{where $n_0$ is given by Lemma~(l:var-lower of the paper)}, and any~$a$ the value $N_{\rho_0} (\eta_{a;n})$ is well-defined and satisfies
    \begin{equation*}
        N_{\rho_0} (\eta_{a;n}) < 3 \overline{C}^{\textcolor{black}{2+{\varepsilon}}} \quad \text{and} \quad \rho_0^{\textcolor{black}{2+{\varepsilon}}} N_{\rho_0} (\eta_{a;n}) < \frac{1}{100},
    \end{equation*}
    where $\overline{C}$ is the constant defined in Corollary~(c.3 of the paper).

    Moreover, the choice of $\rho_0$ depends only on the constants under the assumptions~((a:center of the paper))--((a:growth of the paper)).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.305566+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a31e6c603e2ac5918e50c805aae5e3068bc7c32a88e6136cbd58c4d24b76c14e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 65 (Bounds for dominated convergence) of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Assume that we are in the setting of Assumption \ref{ass:QVBounds}. Then there exists some $C,\epsilon > 0$ such that for each $m \geq 0$, each $N \geq 0$ and every $|  {\boldsymbol v}| < \epsilon$, we have  
