{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:16:46.112223+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a32e07d217bd143c74d3322c8e9620fb9ca2c58020708d574648b04227ff77f9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem h-eternal of arXiv:2604.12963, 'Shocks, instability, and the twenty networks\\ of infinite geodesics in the Directed Lands'] For any $\omega\in\Omega_0$, $\theta\in\Theta^\omega$, and $x_0,s_0\in\mathbb{R}$, $h^\theta_{(x_0,s_0)}$ is an eternal solution: for any $x$ and $t>s$ in $\mathbb{R}$,
