{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.741078+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3353588917ecb6a5a17e8986c5607c32bf217729c81a242302a15018305321f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture conj1 of arXiv:2411.19163, '\bfseries Random polytopes in convex bodies:\\ Bridging the gap between extremal container'] Let $m\in\mathbb{N}$. For $i\in\{1,\dotsc,m\}$ let $K_i\subset \mathbb{R}^{d_i}$ be a convex body whose boundary is twice differentiable with positive Gaussian curvature everywhere and such that $\operatorname{Vol}_{d_i}(K_i) = \operatorname{Vol}_{d_i}(B_2^{d_i})$. Consider the product $K=K_1\times\ldots\times K_m\subset \mathbb{R}^d$ with $d=d_1+\ldots+d_m$, and let $\mathcal{P}_{n,d}(K)$ with $n\geq d+1$ be the convex hull of $n$ independent and uniformly distributed random points in $K$. We conjecture that
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{E} f_{j}(\mathcal{P}_{n,\operatorname{bd}}(K)) {\asymp}   \mathbb{E} f_{j}(\mathcal{P}_{n,\operatorname{bd}}(Z_{\operatorname{bd}})) \qquad \text{for $j\in\{0,\dotsc,d-1\}$,}
    \end{equation*}
    and
    \begin{equation*}
        \operatorname{Vol}_d(K) - \mathbb{E} \operatorname{Vol}_{d}(\mathcal{P}_{n,\operatorname{bd}}(K)) {\asymp} \operatorname{Vol}_d(Z_{\operatorname{bd}}) - \mathbb{E} \operatorname{Vol}_{d}(\mathcal{P}_{n,\operatorname{bd}}(Z_{\operatorname{bd}})).
    \end{equation*} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.190213+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a342f128b890433e89842691f4b572975d58976c95379e160487a0b2158ebfb7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 17 of arXiv:2604.19200, 'Stochastic $\Sigma$-convergence in Orlicz setting and Applications'] A function $u\in L^{\Phi}(Q\times \Omega ;\mathfrak{X}_{A}^{\Phi})$ 
			 is said to be admissible if the trace function $(x,\omega
		)\mapsto u(x,T(x/\varepsilon _{1})\omega ,x/\varepsilon _{2})$
