{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.204707+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a34c1d8f0168d18b33dcc5667b4cc416c6c0e051a550398414f22504e62e7e91","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop dissiBanach of arXiv:2506.08202, 'Stochastic dissipative systems in Banach spaces driven by L\'evy noise'] Let $f:{\rm Dom}(f)\subseteq \mathcal{K}{\rightarrow}\mathcal{K}$. $f$ is dissipative if and only if, for every $x,y\in {\rm Dom}(f)$ there exists $z^*\in\partial{\left\|x-y\right\|}$ such that
\begin{equation}
\dscal{f(x)-f(y)}{z^*}{\mathcal{K}}\leq 0.
\end{equation}
If $\mathcal{K}$ is a Hilbert space (equation disban of the paper) reads as
\begin{equation*}
\scal{f(x)-f(y)}{x-y}_{\mathcal{K}}\leq 0.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.988770+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3519cf78ecb273a860f326c2b11d443b9d8c390094700921210f87e87768a93","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 71 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Assume $\omega$ is such that $\cC_1(p_0) \subseteq \cC_1(p_1)$. Denote by $\nu_1$ and $\nu_2$ the laws of $\ClCp{1}{p_0}$ and $\cT_{p_1 \mid p_0}$, respectively. Then
    \begin{equation} 
        \Vert \nu_1 - \nu_2\Vert_{\mathrm{TV}} \leq n^4 e^{-\beta(p_1 - p_0)},
    \end{equation}
    where $\Vert \cdot \Vert_{\mathrm{TV}}$ is the total variation norm. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.829831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a35765bb8bc70f0272afcebb2846ee8c81555b9ac0cc0b2ff252888c3de4d76a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm exponentialconvergence of arXiv:2606.24385, 'Gradient Mean-Field Dynamics with Measure-Valued States: Well-Posedness, Chaos, and Long-T'] Let us suppose that (A4 of the paper),(A7 of the paper)--(A12 of the paper) hold true. Furthermore, suppose that the constants given in the hypotheses satisfy
\begin{align}
\kappa \coloneqq m_x + m_\lambda - 2L_\mu - \sigma_{\lambda}C_{Q}> 0,
\end{align}
and consider $\mu_{\cdot}$ as in (equation misurasol of the paper). Then there exists a unique invariant probability measure $\mu_\infty \in {\mathscr{P}}_{2}({\mathscr Y})$ such that for every initial condition $(Y(0),\Lambda(0))\in L^{2}(\Omega,{\mathscr Y})$ of (equation eq:limitMV_detailed of the paper),
\begin{align}
{\mathcal W}_{2}(\mu(t), \mu_\infty)
\le
e^{-\kappa t} {\mathcal W}_{2}(\mu_0,\mu_\infty),
\end{align}
where $\mu_{0}={\mathcal L}((Y(0),\Lambda(0)))$ is the law of $(Y(0),\Lambda(0))$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:20:30.573892+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a358f3b574a05dcb06fe9242fc3131a1a62a64630adb7167e4cd4d00e4b69f78","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 43 of arXiv:2609.01826, 'An extension theory for fully fractional Schr\"odinger equations with memory'] Let $0<s<1, t>0$, and $z>0$. Then the following oscillatory identity holds:
\begin{equation}
\int_0^t
\frac{e^{i \frac{z^2}{4\sigma}}}{(t-\sigma)^{1-s}\sigma^{1+s}}\,d\sigma =
4^s\,\G(s)\,e^{i\frac{\pi s}{2}}\,t^{s-1}\,z^{-2s}
