{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.055713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3a4ca0a74f5393c76854ab968e33dc8554c586920c0c092f8090a01721a24f9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (\cite{komorowski2012fluctuations}, Kipnis--Varadhan) of arXiv:2607.01629, 'Quadratic fluctuations of speed-change Kawasaki dynamics'] For fixed $t>0$, there exists a uniform constant $C$ such that for centered $ G\in L^2\cap H^{-1}$, we have
