{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.340907+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3a94b02cae3a85cbfcb2b0f50734e111b072353bf4cf80da25c667dbfdf424b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:zeros:betheRegularity of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Let $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption (as:results:invMeasure of the paper). Suppose $\nu \in {\mathcal{M}_{\kappa, d}}$ is a Cayley fixed point{}. Then $\nu$ along with its marginal distributions $\bar{\nu}$, $\nu_0$, and its conditional distribution $\bar{\nu}(\cdot|\cdot)$ are differentiable Lebesgue almost everywhere. Moreover, for almost every $x \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d$ we have
