{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.878318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3ba9186eb7b80a5d84b87d0cd83200935df427a72289ecf68c8b7e99721816a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro cor:cdfbounding of arXiv:2605.07920, 'Primitive Sequences for Probability Measures on Compact Intervals'] Suppose that $c_1, \ldots, c_m$ are the first $m \geq 1$ terms of an admissible sequence for $[a,b]$. Then for every $x_0 \in [a,b]$,
    \begin{equation*}
    \bar{F}_m(x_0; c_{1:m}) := \sup_{\mu \in \pazocal{F}_m(c_{1:m})} \mu([a,x_0]) 
    \quad \text{and} \quad 
    \underline{F}_m(x_0; c_{1:m}) := \inf_{\mu \in \pazocal{F}_m(c_{1:m})} \mu([a,x_0))
\end{equation*}
are attained by $(m+1)$-atomic measures. Equivalently, if $X$ is any random variable on $[a,b]$ with given moments $\mathbb{E}[X^k]$ for $k=1,\ldots,m$, then sharp bounds on $F_X(x_0) = \mathbb{P}(X \leq x_0)$ and on $F_X(x_0-) = \mathbb{P}(X < x_0)$ are attained by discrete random variables supported on at most $m+1$ points.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.785702+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3bc50aab54e73c07b18bf5bdc88091913fc8261a52ea8c9d4d2a9bd4b63798c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem uniform-in-beta-bounds-on-surface-tension-and-stiffness of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists $\beta_0$ such that for all $\beta>\beta_0$, 
