{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.187620+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3d029a19f8879be40b9e6c52d7ac6a9297811aadbb464bda7aadb3ddd563ffe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:momentmatchingPUrel of arXiv:2411.16103, 'Non-commutative Stein's Method: Applications to Free Probability and Sums of Non-commutati'] If a given measure $\rho$ has moment matching rank $q$, then for all $j\in[q]$ and $\theta\geq 0$, 
