{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.625008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a430b2d63f9d563e657adce67946cc63053ae8e8cb6ec78e1f62fc787d617b3b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary coro:Charact of Gamma of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Suppose that $(\Omega, \mathcal{H}, \hat{\mathbb{E}})$ is a regular sublinear expectation space. Then for any $X\in \mathcal{H}^d$ with $X\sim \Gamma$, we have
