{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.273859+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a45b9848460975b92bf72c027062903678cee8cad61f3d332e2c4192f95727ea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_RN_infty of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] For $(\delta_m)_m$ as in Lemma (lemma_thinness_gamma of the paper), almost surely, for $\xi \in \{+,-\}$ with $j(\xi)=L$ if $\xi=+$ and $j(\xi)=R$ if $\xi=-1$,
