{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.232182+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4da060a0c79e98e8a01678e6fab80d953f62988157a031bc20ab86e0d503fd4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 35 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix some $c_0>0$. 
There exists a coupling $\mathbf{P}_{N,n}$ between the patched and periodic LPP landscapes, and constants $c,C>0$, such that for all $n\in \N$, we find some $N_0=N_0(n)$ such that for all $N \geq N_0$, 
