{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.146359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4f844bbb3fb14929c3b14b551625001e561fadafcd4202b484fb77c534a7b17","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:tauoveralphasfreeness of arXiv:2411.16103, 'Non-commutative Stein's Method: Applications to Free Probability and Sums of Non-commutati'] Let $\{A_n\}_{n\geq 1}$ be a sequence of subalgebras of $\mathcal{A}$. For $a\in \mathcal{A}$, denote the centering of $a$ by $\bar{a}:=a-\tau(a)$. We say that $\{A_n\}_{n\geq 1}$ are freely independent, or free, if
\begin{equation}
