{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.932318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a59ab70faeed2478d2dfd7d3e23343be41f5c38b86662411d56039852a0f6170","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 29 (Good scales) of arXiv:2506.19123, 'The longest increasing subsequence of Brownian separable permutons'] Fix $C>0$ as in \cref{lem:existence good scales}. We say that an infinite set $\mathrm{GoodScales}\subset \N$ is a collection of \textbf{good scales} if the following two conditions hold: 
