{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.780861+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5b85795e06d3406494a617c6406585577d2869bff22cd09cd24a713f3879905","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Entry Approximation Thm of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] For some constants $C_{k,T}$ and $n_0(k,T)$, we almost surely have 
