        \lim_{n \to \infty} \sup_{t \in [0,T]} \|E_n(t)-\Tilde{E}_n(t)\|=0.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:04.864485+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5bb8198470dc3c7e1a25491a73aba5258fc07b23134c1292bd998a63d9d97b1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2511.23453, 'Convergence rates of self-repellent random walks, their local time and Event Chain Monte C'] We have
    \begin{equation*}
        \frac{1}{n^2}\int\norm{\nabla^2 g}_F^2\diff\mu + \frac{1}{n^2}\sum_{i=1}^n\int ((\partial_{\ell_i}-\partial_{\ell_{i-1}})g)^2 \diff\mu = \int (2\L g)^2 \diff\mu
