Then $\mu(C)>0$ implies that (equation egtoutf of the paper) does not hold. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.615112+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a6b9c4c19b126c03935d1afc6e103b19145debe60a9d4bca422120300dad6a3e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2604.22644, '2604.22644'] Let the scale function defined for $k \ge 1$ be
\begin{align}
    S(k;p) = \sum_{i=0}^{k-1} \prod_{j=1}^{i} \frac{1 - r^j p}{r^j p}
\end{align}
where the empty product for $i=0$ is defined as $1$. Then, the probability that the first excursion $e_1$ does not reach $N$ is given by:
\begin{align}
    P(e_1 \text{ does not reach } N) = 1 - \int_0^1 \frac{p}{S(N;p)} dp.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.283293+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a6bb662c764aafced0a8b475ec37133046cfa2aa91bc23b3d6187258b018fb6b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:multCLT of arXiv:2604.20327, 'Persistent Homology of the Wiener Sausage II: A Central Limit Theorem for Drifted Planar B'] Let $\psi_1, \ldots, \psi_m$ be bounded Borel functions supported in a common compact
