{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.679697+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a717ecc0bd9af4b5359f58c9f20cebd236ce357b64f69a8dede2e1d2d58c59ac","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2608.30077, 'Lie groupoid integration of singular isometries of the Poincaré disk'] For every $(u(t), z) \in X_n$, there exists a unique smooth path $z(t) \in \Dbarstar$ such that:
