{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.415842+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a72a75e6a52224b3f67a3186faac9fe3aa14c52e0b15c2e6aaae5edc669f12e5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma6.234 of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] For $B>0$ consider $\zeta\in\Gamma_B$ and $X\sim\operatorname{Col}_n(\zeta)$. Let $M_1,M_2$ be two $n\times n$ symmetric matrices, $u\in\mathbb{R}^n$, $t_1,t_2\in\mathbb{R}$ and $s,\delta_1,\delta_2\geq 0$. Then 
