{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.696497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a79f3b950bc2b7684bbfddf0f357bdc03fbb4e4fafb877aa5ff765e8145ecda7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2609.02711, 'Differentiability of the Leading Lyapunov Exponent \\ of a linear differential equation wi'] Under Hypothesis  \ref{hyp:un},
  for all $z$, there exists a measurable
set $\tilde{\Omega}_z$ such that $\prob{\tilde{\Omega}_z} = 1$, a real
number $\Lambda(z)$

