{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.339576+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a7acce55664090d3dda8783afb0e4edd3e2977c3feb6a6484df0b91c8c4a3fe5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:worst-case-md of arXiv:2411.09075, 'Weak Poincar{\'e} Inequalities, Simulated Annealing, and Sampling from Spherical Spin Glas'] Let $\pi$ be a distribution over $\Omega \subseteq \R^N$, and $\pi = \E_{\bz \sim \rho} \pi_{\bz}$ a measure decomposition of $\pi$ such that
