{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.024578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a7b36ad9df2f9a92f9fbad448e245cda230b1dcfbe1f4d309cec37fa60bf3ee5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 (\citeauthor{F10}, \citeyear{F10}, Eq.~(5.101)) of arXiv:2606.06739, 'The relationship between the transition functions of the labeled and unlabeled versions of'] For $\bm m=(m_1,\ldots,m_k)$ with $m_1\ge\cdots\ge m_k\ge1$, $\bm n=(n_1,\ldots,n_l)$ with $n_1\ge\cdots\ge n_l\ge1$, $k,l\in{\bf N}$, $m=|\bm m|$, and $n=|\bm n|$,
