{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.234405+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a7f78c4888c5b13c90284eadb4c8a2144ea28f58a240b4b751be1e91d80116f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 72 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] Assume that $\tr_{d_n}\circ \pi \to\tau$, and let $\phi \in \B(\A,\rmM_k)_+$ and $\psi \in \B(\A,\rmM_\ell)_+$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[a.] If $\rm{diag}(\phi,\psi)$ is asymptotically associated to $\bspi$, then
\[\rmh_{\bspi}(\rm{diag}(\phi,\psi)) = \rmh_{\bspi}(\phi) + \rmh_{\bspi}(\psi).\]
\item[b.] If $k = \ell$, $t \in [0,1]$, and $t\phi + (1-t)\psi$ is asymptotically associated to $\bspi$, then
\[\rmh_{\bspi}(t\phi + (1-t)\psi) \ge t\rmh_{\bspi}(\phi) + (1-t)\rmh_{\bspi}(\psi).\]
\end{enumerate}
\qed (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.008731+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a7f88421a54b16142ef9984dc2c3822f1e4a60df90ae2f71a38190855e3637a1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Consider a matrix $X\in M^{n\times m}(\mathbb{C})$ with all i.i.d.\ complex Gaussian entries such that
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{E} X_{j,k}=\mathbb{E}X_{j,k}^2=0,~\mathbb{E}|X_{j,k}|^2=1
    \end{equation*}
    for any $j,~k$. Then the Hermitian matrix $W_{n,m}:=X^*X\in M^{m}(\mathbb{C})$ is called a \textbf{complex Wishart matrix}, or a \textbf{Laguerre Ensemble}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.537068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a7f8b6b169bb74b292d7a4676948359cb451d7b69788232f135d3c0a0bb9b1cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor.expansion_trunc of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For any $\delta \in [0, 1-\mathfrak{p}]$, the conductivity perturbation $\widetilde\Delta^{\delta}_m$ defined in (equation eq.defDeltaTrunc of the paper) satisfies 
			\begin{equation}
