{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.204438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a837a09c60237eb5441e02e48ef50d3442a3044265bcb6392e7b4e042642107b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm limmild of arXiv:2506.08202, 'Stochastic dissipative systems in Banach spaces driven by L\'evy noise'] Assume that either Hypotheses (Hyp1C of the paper) or Hypotheses (Hyp2L of the paper) holds. For every $x\in H$ and $T>0$ there exists a unique $H$-valued càdlàg process $\{X(t,x)\}_{t\in [0,T]}$ such that for every $\{x_n\}_{n\in{\mathbb N}}\subseteq E$ converging to $x$ we have
