{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.701710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a86f2d9f774deeb3c106dfcb8fb3afae463e3488881b3f8bfcb2982e20072e28","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition PROP:Min of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] For every $D>0$, there exists $Q=Q_D>0$ in $H^1(\mathbb{R})$ such that $\|Q_D \|_{L^2(\mathbb{R}^2)}^2=D$ and 
