{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.007679+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a88e854704dcbca2fd84a05227a318bba59b6a1783c66ce6b392994e8976bc4f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition LUE left soft fac of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Let $\xi_{a,N}$, $\eta_{a,N}$ be the kernel functions defined in (equation explicit xi and zeta of the paper) and $(\tilde{\mu}_{n,N},\tilde{\sigma}_{n,N})$ be a pair with respect to the left-soft-edged scaling $\tau$ satisfying the restriction (equation restriction of recaling of the paper). Define:
    \begin{equation}
