{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.042509+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a89d59625efcdf22611ab6a7245c6209cd5fad24d1a32e144c07e1861f508165","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Talagrand complexity measure) of arXiv:2606.31936, 'Coupling and Maximal Inequalities for Graph-Dependent Empirical Processes'] Let $r>0$, $p>0$ and let $d$ be a (pseudo) metric over $\mathcal B$. The Talagrand complexity measure for $\mathcal B \subseteq \mathcal F$ is defined as
