{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.963855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8b9be35552ca0a70deb6a5b26355b2d6812ae2aa784a692f39cb5c74447fc2c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Bounded Differences Property}

    A function $f : \mathcal X^n \to \R$ fulfills the bounded differences property if for $c_1,...,c_n \geq 0$ and all $i \in [n]$: 
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{y, x_1,...,x_n \in \mathcal X} |f(x_1,...,x_n) - f(x_1,...x_{i-1} y, x_{i+1},...,x_n)| \leq c_i.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.609806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8c0ddaa9b5906e36b463c4fec77e06da7c9f0f239c0e7fef7eacd30ca43aeab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 (Jabin and Wang {\cite[Theorem 4) of arXiv:2608.25772, 'Propagation of Chaos and Gaussian Fluctuations for Mean-field Coupled Maps'] {JW18}}]
    Let $E$ be a Polish space and $\rho\in\mathcal{P}(E)$ be a probability measure on $E$. Suppose that $\phi:E\times E\to\R$ is a measurable function satisfying the following two cancellation rules:
    \begin{equation}
        \int_E\phi(x,y)\dd\rho(x)=0,\quad\forall y\in E;\qquad
        \int_E\phi(x,y)\dd\rho(y)=0,\quad\forall x\in E.
    \end{equation}
    Then there exists a constant $C_1>0$, such that when $\|\phi\|_{L^{\infty}}\leq C_1$, one has
    \begin{equation}
        \sup_{N\geq 2}\int_{E^N}   \rho^{\otimes N}(X_N)\exp{\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i,j=1}^{N}\phi(x_i,x_j)\right)}\dd X_N\leq C<+\infty,
    \end{equation}
    where $X_N=(x_1,x_2,\dots,x_N)$ for $N\geq 2$ and $C$ is a generic constant independent of $N$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

