{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.897866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8dc6abd8e873be772e4a54a7ba7bbda36a0c227868e7e9fc2e62e412cf6459e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Lemma2.1 of arXiv:2411.11408, 'Multidimensional specific relative entropy between continuous martingales'] Let $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $\mathbb{P},\mathbb{Q}\in \mathcal{M}_1(C) $ such that $\mathbb{Q}|_{\mathcal{F}^n}\ll \mathbb{P}|_{\mathcal{F}^n}$. Then $\mathbb{P}$-a.s., 
    \begin{equation*}
        \frac{d\mathbb{Q}}{d\mathbb{P}}|_{\mathcal{F}^n}(\omega)=\frac{d\mathcal{L}_{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0, \Delta_1^n X,\dots,\Delta_n^nX)}{d\mathcal{L}_{\mathbb{P}}(X_0, \Delta_1^n X,\dots,\Delta_n^nX)}(\omega(0),\Delta_1^n\omega, \dots, \Delta_n^n\omega).
    \end{equation*}
    In particular, 
    \begin{equation*}
H(\mathbb{Q}|\mathbb{P})|_{\mathcal{F}^n}=H(\mathcal{L}_{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0, \Delta_1^n X,\dots,\Delta _n ^n X)| \mathcal{L}_{\mathbb{P}}(X_0, \Delta_1^n X,\dots,\Delta_n^nX)).
    \end{equation*}
    Moreover, if $\mathbb{P}$ and $\mathbb{Q}$ are such that $X$ has independent increments. Then
    \[H(\mathbb{Q}|\mathbb{P})|_{\mathcal{F}^n}=H(\mathcal{L}_{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0)|\mathcal{L}_{\mathbb{P}}(X_0))+\sum _{k=1}^n H(\mathcal{L}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\Delta _k^n X)|\mathcal{L}_{\mathbb{P}}(\Delta _k^n X)).\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.718920+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8dd1591277a3a5746b001a1b2c7bf7025755c9e7727481d5ff42ccbf66e3d91","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma fNtNlmt of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Following hold for ${\sf f}_N = L^{\frac{d}{2} N} f_N$.
