{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.079639+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a95aeb60011c309bdafc0e83272ceff9763b54396894241841c3ce95b3d7e3bb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma PAS of arXiv:2601.15223, 'Large time behaviour for a class of 2D and 3D stochastic non-Newtonian fluids of different'] Suppose that condition (equation third-grade-paremeters-res of the paper) and Hypothesis (Hyp-f-B of the paper) are satisfied. Then the non-autonomous random dynamical system $\Phi$ associated with the system (equation STGF of the paper) possesses a $\mathfrak{D}$-pullback random absorbing set $\mathcal{M}=\{\mathcal{M}(\mathfrak{r},\omega):\mathfrak{r}\in\mathbb{R},\omega\in\Omega\}\in\mathfrak{D}$, where  $\mathcal{M}(\mathfrak{r},\omega)$ is defined by 
