{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.699161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a987d211cd5c7274335747cc0ac5285a9aad8d74ab00360bbfbe4e227459187a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:nonresonance of arXiv:2609.00668, 'Rigidity of Euclidean Minimal Hypersurfaces under Nonuniform Diagonal Dilations'] The weights $g_1,\ldots,g_n$ are \emph{pair-sum nonresonant} if
\begin{equation}
g_i+g_j=g_k+g_\ell\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\{i,j\}=\{k,\ell\}
\end{equation}
for unordered pairs $i<j$ and $k<\ell$. Equivalently, the $\binom n2$ pair sums are all distinct.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.553586+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a98dd1fef65ff833289909d69af13f8f0884a3ebd0f6c87e08001b70ccf854ea","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 11 of arXiv:2609.01413, 'Sharp Threshold for Universality of Rational Canonical Forms over a Finite Field'] We have
\begin{equation}
\Aut\left(\bigoplus_{i=1}^k\bigoplus_{j\ge 1}(\F_p[t]/(f_i^{\l^{(f_i)}_j}))\right)=\prod_{i=1}^k\Aut_{f_i}(\lambda^{(f_i)}),
