where the norm on the l.h.s. is defined in terms of the \emph{Fourier coefficients}
of $T\chi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.658234+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa09730944f10bd581a8327a759b896e9549f3df2c55d432efab7516d4cb1cd8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2607.29327, 'Fractal Random Variables\\ Defined by Probability Distributions of Digits\\ of Their $G_2$'] For any number $x\in [0;g_0]$,
