{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.577045+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa5667e1c948045ad5b2236d0802ae50425532e03ce0a30189aa0185b566b093","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] Let $f: M \to \mathbb{R}$ be a bounded and measurable function. Then there exists some $T_0 > 0$ and $C > 0$ such that for all $t \geq T_0$,
