{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.902373+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa56910157f5f2046181f43ce5bd1b4f1e147ae1f92b6fd843d35d1d2272e87e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defin 15 of arXiv:2608.00811, 'Comparison of Dirichlet forms for stable-like random walks on groups of polynomial volume '] Let $\widetilde{S_N}$ be the formal concatenation of $\Sigma_0$ and $S_N$. 
