{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.048673+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa6f52858590efd87c60eeddf81881e7bd1a27df236186bb6e73e8c48e827c06","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 40 (Corollary 1.12 of \cite{St83}) of arXiv:2609.00758, 'Deformations of Compact Calabi--Yau and Fano Varieties with Isolated Singularities'] Let $X$ be a complex $n$-fold, $x\in X$ an isolated singularity and $f:(Y,E)\to(X,x)$ a good resolution. Then for integers $p<n$ and $q>n$ there are exact sequences
