{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.292191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aabbd768b2e10ef76af6b07fb6209944ee064496841a11c9f073128f3e457189","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem incrementalstrong of arXiv:2603.22652, 'A cohesive account on the ergodic behaviours and scaling limits of Random Walks in Cooling'] {AvedCos24game}}]

Assume that ${\mathbb {X}}$ satisfies (equation C of the paper) and 
\begin{description}
\item[\namedlabel{S1}{S1}]\emph{(Polynomial decay)} There is a
