and we have that $\operatorname{Lip}(F)=\operatorname{Lip}(f)$. If $\zeta=1$, then $C(\zeta)=1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.819484+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aaf0ee315aa13daf483ea95d5d46a5c03defeaedd80a4dea813401fbe7e61848","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop MILT convergence of arXiv:2607.17393, 'Optimal Covariance Estimates for Schr\"odinger Semigroups with White Noise in $d=1,2$'] Let $d=2$, $s,t>0$, and $x,y\in\mathbb{R}^d$ be fixed. Then for any Borel measurable $A_1\times A_2\subset[0,t]\times[0,s]$ there exists a random variable, $\alpha_{A_1\times A_2}$, such that 
