{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.832915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab9e1a491b77a286f039f401e06eca2119d87b345545a7584de658ba7bca93af","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem volt-05 of arXiv:2606.25336, '\bfseries Invariant Measures of L\'evy-driven Stochastic Differential Equations'] Assume \textup{(A1)}, \textup{(A2)} and  \textup{(A3)}.  The equation $L^*\rho = 0$ in $\mathcal{S}'({\mathds{R}^d})$ is equivalent to
