{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:06.981999+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aba11f8414580143db411a088b562c9b7bf41909c7315e3e50f0281a3a64889a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:lapl of arXiv:2607.26169, 'Scaling and partial universality of the height zero probability in the 2D Abelian sandpile'] Let $g : \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}$ have continuous and bounded partial derivatives of order up to $3$.
