{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.548365+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abe145724501b57c336c833f96abfae74991ef6a9342312a2cc91f6dbc1176ce","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2603.29473, '$\chi^2$--cut-off phenomenon for Galerkin projections of Fokker--Planck equations with mon'] Let $f(x) = V'(x) = |x|^\gamma$ and $v$ be as in \cref{lem:WKBprime} for some $\gamma > 0$. Then
	for $k\geq 2$ there exists a positive constant  $C_k$ such that
	\begin{align}
		|S_k'(x)|\leq C_k
		\begin{cases}
			|x|^{-(2k-1)\gamma},  & 0<\gamma\leq 1, \\
			|x|^{-(k\gamma+k-1)}, & \gamma>1,
		\end{cases}
		\quad \textrm{ for all }\quad x\geq x^*,
	\end{align}
	where $x^*$ is the corresponding turning point from \cref{lem:WKBprime}.

	When $0<\gamma\leq 1$ and $1/\gamma$ is an odd integer, that is $1-(2k-1)\gamma = 0$, it follows that
	\begin{equation}
		|S_k(x)| \leq  C_k\log(x) \quad \textrm{ for all }\quad x\geq x^*.
	\end{equation}

	In particular, whenever $n > \frac{1-\gamma}{2\gamma}$ the quantity
	\begin{align}
		\frac{S_n''+\sum_{n_1+n_2 \geq n+1}^{n_1 \leq n; n_2 \leq n} S_{n_1}'S_{n_2}'}{\sum_{j=0}^{n} S_j'} \in L^1(x^*,\infty).
	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

