{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.309200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abe9052c177ae2e5a1bf60d7ebbecce7549454549119db5d5a1d461cd7f5d199","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2604.07697, 'Stochastic fractional heat equation with general rough noise'] (\cite[Proposition 2.1, Equation (2.8)]{HHLNT2017}, \cite[Theorem 3.1]{PT2000})
 The  space $\mathfrak{H}$ is a Hilbert space equipped with the scalar  product
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
     \langle\phi,\psi\rangle_{\mathfrak{H}}
     :=&\,c_{H}\int_{\mathbb{R}_{+}}\left(\int_ {\mathbb{R}} \mathscr {F} \phi(t,\xi) \overline{ \mathscr {F}\psi(t,\xi)}  |\xi|^{1-2H}d\xi \right)dt
     \\
     =&\, H\left(\frac12-H\right) \int_{\mathbb{R}_+}\left(\int_{\mathbb{R}^2}[\phi(t, x+y)-\phi(t, x)] [\psi(t, x+y)-\psi(t, x)] |y|^{2H-2} dxdy\right)dt.
