{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.500008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac042f725c49bcb78ba4f99807b0c036d96b0438bd00533191ca247dfb67e11b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 18 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] We introduce the following two paths:
\begin{enumerate}
\item We define the \emph{(one-parameter) bracket} $[ \mathbf{X} ] : [0,T] \to {\rm Sym}(V \otimes V)$ as
\begin{align}
[ \mathbf{X} ]_t := X_{0,t} \otimes X_{0,t} - 2 \, {\rm Sym}(\bbx_{0,t}), \quad t \in [0,T].
\end{align}
\item We define the \emph{(two-parameter) bracket} $[ \mathbf{X} ] : [0,T]^2 \to {\rm Sym}(V \otimes V)$ as
\begin{align}
[ \mathbf{X} ]_{s,t} := X_{s,t} \otimes X_{s,t} - 2 \, {\rm Sym}(\bbx_{s,t}), \quad s,t \in [0,T].
\end{align}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

