{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.979973+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac38796a990c242c79299c997e7dea8a1c946d0fe39b4cdab412b0f043b46f9e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem prefix_sampling of arXiv:2606.15339, 'Uniform integrability of the distance to the nearest leaf in random trees'] Conditional on $\mathcal G_n$, the prefix $(\tilde d^{(U)}_1,\dots,\tilde d^{(U)}_k)$ is a uniform ordered sample without replacement of size $k$ from the multiset $M(\mathcal{T}_n)$. In particular,
