{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.680358+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac46fb4f78e2148f8f766de35b2dcf4bf1eefdaa33257890605d655348be1f17","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 of arXiv:2608.30077, 'Lie groupoid integration of singular isometries of the Poincaré disk'] The map $\Phi:\mathcal{G}_n'\longrightarrow\mathcal{G}(\mathcal{A}_n),$ defined as
