\asymp \sup_{\mu\in \eP(T)}\int_0^\Delta \Big(\sqrt{R_{\mu}(\epsilon^2)}\wedge \beta \epsilon\Big) 
\dif \epsilon.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.812788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac58bb1893608264e7c01996ee8938667aea59d23e748d07d83c34f001dda20e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:2.2.3 of arXiv:2607.18505, 'A Vector Space Approach to Heavy Tailed Analysis'] For $X,Y \in \mathbb{W}_b$, let $a,b$ be arbitrary and define the extremal covariance
