{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.258787+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac6bb3a89d1a42540a73d82431c08880f361def4a31bedb1e20a36f0f580735f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 85 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Suppose that $\alpha$ and $\kappa\in (1/2,1]$ satisfy $\alpha>\frac{\kappa}{3\kappa+4}+5\kappa+\frac{7}{2}$.
  Then it holds for any $K\in (0,\infty)$ and $E<\frac{\kappa}{2(3\kappa+4)(\kappa+2)}$ that
  \begin{align*}
    \bbE\left[\sup_{|x|\le K}\Big|p(t,0,x)-p_n(t,0,\floor{nx}/n)\Big|\right]\lesssim n^{-E}.
  \end{align*}
  In particular, if $\alpha>\frac{121}{14}$, we have 
  \begin{align*}
     \bbE\left[\sup_{|x|\le K}\Big|p(t,0,x)-p_n(t,0,\floor{nx}/n)\Big|\right]\lesssim n^{-E},
  \end{align*}
  for any $K\in (0,\infty)$ and $E<\frac{1}{42}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:59:24.054553+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac6d1a2a19487c647be1ad6f0b63acbffbcc3f60ccea8e411e0a194b0c597c7a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Psi-structure of arXiv:2608.30904, 'Entire monotone solutions of the anisotropic Allen--Cahn equation in dimension 5'] In the frame $\{e_0,e_x,e_y\}$,
\begin{equation}
 \Psi_F(\nu)
 =\begin{pmatrix}
