{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.615646+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_acb6dc783cac35605d8d6e096a9154e28dc87cc0531c216dda3b7aaedd0a22ec","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 37 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There exists $\delta_0>0$ and constants $C,c$ such that for any fixed $\delta<\delta_0$ and all $n$ large enough, we have
