{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.474996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_acf49b3ec33e0f2407d13f3f6741137e8e4059a53fcae2c2c02b633d3d5ba492","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:mesoscopic-cap-condition of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[theorem]{thm:mesoscopic-block-lower}
Suppose the ordered entries are i.i.d., centered, and
\(K\)-sub-Gaussian with common law \(\mu\).  Let \(b,w,c>0\), put
\[
 \pi=\mu([b,b+w]),\qquad
