        R_{2}(\tau^{*}, \sigma^{*})&=\sup_{\sigma\in\mathcal{T}^{\mathbb{SQ}}}R_{2}(\tau^{*},\sigma),
    \end{align*}
    where $\tau^{*}:=\inf\{t\geq 0: X_{t}\geq b^*\sqrt{1-t}\}$, $\sigma^{*}:=\inf\{t\geq 0: X_{t}\leq -d^*\sqrt{1-t}\}$, and the stopping boundaries satisfy $b^*=d^*\in [0,\infty)$.","status":"unverified"}

