{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.539647+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad7c21b6e7e27ba139e76f5c9829515dc2438e1125037de75bf6c3720b480aa3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 20 of arXiv:2603.28702, 'Distribution of the magnetization of the critical Ising model on sparse random graphs'] For the class $\mathcal{L}_0$ we have $|\mathcal{L}_0|=(r_1-1)!!$ and for any $L_0\in\mathcal{L}_0$,
