{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.966420+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae1edd8b67a4cf4e3e90d4c07d97389461102a594cdcadc3c70a2158f83a9275","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Concentration of the Maximum Cut}

    For a fraction $\epsilon \in (0,1)$ the maximum cut of the dependent ERG $G_{\mu^p, \Sigma}(X)$ fulfills 
    \begin{align*}
        \P\Parent{\Abs{\operatorname{MaxCut}(G_{\mu^p, \Sigma}(X))- \E[\operatorname{MaxCut}(G_{\mu^p, \Sigma}(X))]} \geq \epsilon \binom{n}{2}}
        \leq 2\exp\Parent{-\frac{2 \epsilon^2 \binom{n}{2}}{\kappa^\star(\Sigma)}}, 
    \end{align*}

    where $\kappa^\star(\Sigma) := \eigmax{D^{1/2} \Sigma D^{1/2}}$ with $D := \diagonal{\Sigma\inv}$ is the ATE constant for $\Sigma$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:38:57.142084+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae2033aed5c2d16141772c3724ff61811f1e11de4351dfdf796fb38f98840a0c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2604.05910, '\textbf{Well-posedness and Hurst parameter estimation for fluid equations driven by fracti'] The map $\Lambda$ is a contraction on $V^T$ choosing $T$ small enough.
