{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.146562+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae2c6fc727c66795dd328fe5e470872e6ba1376a0dfc988532b1cf86502bba13","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For every $\varepsilon > 0$, there exist constants $c, C > 0$ such that for any $n \ge 1$, any $v \in [n]$ and any $S\in \left[ 1,c (n/v)^{1-\varepsilon} \right]$, the upper tail satisfies
