{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.333470+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae523248b2e9a668b02fc888216158341a343fbf3f57a810cd0a91df5b08005c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 of arXiv:2511.06196, 'Central limit theorem for high temperature spin models via martingale embedding'] In the model \cref{eq:Isingmodel}, assume that all the off-diagonal entries of the interaction matrix are nonnegative and the supremum of the Dobrushin constants satisfies $\sup_{n\geq 1}\alpha_n\leq \alpha<1$.
