{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.050173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae8f27478f6302ff1188278975047fd820267ae82940b73b5ad830ea7aa9fe22","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 50 of arXiv:2609.00758, 'Deformations of Compact Calabi--Yau and Fano Varieties with Isolated Singularities'] Let $X$ be a compact complex $n$-fold with isolated complete intersection singularities and whose resolutions satisfy the $\partial\db$ lemma. Denote by $L=\coprod_{x\in X^\sing}L_x$ the union of the links and suppose that 
