{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.617973+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae994f85ad9681536dc821dda7dfbc4f2df5933ee93f5806e9c4eaf6dea86765","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 70 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There exist constants $g,C,c>0$ such that for all $\delta>0$ and all $0\leq m\leq n$, we have
