{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.541981+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af1662cee2c87a37b8a69f61e115cb5d7ac2cbce0a51baa1dccd5e4967a5c276","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2608.30668, 'Recurrence and capacity of stable branching random walks'] Consider \(f,g: \Z^d \to \R_+\) and \(\lVert \cdot \rVert\) an Euclidian
