{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.291997+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af40498d6d5f49215bfc56e58cb37561bb00673901f900b6af4e4c11cf20130d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:determ_truncation of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Assume the set-up and conditions of Theorem~(theo:main of the paper). For $k_j\in[N]$ denote $x_j:=k_j/N$, $j=1,2$, and assume that $x_1\le x_2$. For any $f_1,f_2\in H^{2+\delta}_0(\Omega)$ it holds that
