{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.631370+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af4bea6a87c600909a570af4bc5f9c93142f2d31807079132eb7186e1a51d3e0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 17 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_\mathcal{W}$, $\psi$ be its corresponding generator, $\vartheta \in \mathcal{P}_\mathcal{A}$, $A \in \mathcal{A}$ be its Pickands dependence function and let $C_{\psi,A} \in \mathcal{C}_{am}$. Then the mass of the $t$-level set $L_{\psi,A}^t$ is given by
