{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.289322+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af57a7e25a2b7105f229ba5058bf4e22de0336247679bf4a61686fa111415ac8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:upper_tail of arXiv:2411.04988, '{\bf A relation between isoperimetry and total variation decay with applications to graphs'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a graph with degrees bounded by $M$. There exists a posiitve constant $c=c(M)$ such that
