{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.752363+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b03e42ecf49cce97e561e46cc295a6a885c5813f6209b420bad660b509631531","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 35 (Anisotropic local law outside the spectrum) of arXiv:2608.29872, 'Local Laws and Outlier Eigenvalues for Spiked Separable Covariance Matrices'] Under the assumptions of Theorem \ref{local_law}, fix any constant $\epsilon>0$. Then, for any 
\begin{equation}
z\in S_{\mathrm{out}}(C_0,\epsilon):=\left\{z= E+ \ii\eta: \lambda_+ + n^{-2/3+\e} + n^{-1/3+\e}  q^2  \le E \le C_0 \lambda_+,  \eta\in [0,1]\right\},
\end{equation}
and any deterministic unit vectors $\uu, \vv \in \mathbb{C}^{p+n}$, the following anisotropic local law holds:
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
\left| \langle \mathbf u, G(X,z) \mathbf v\rangle - \langle \mathbf u, \Pi (z)\mathbf v\rangle \right| & \prec q + \sqrt{\frac{\Im m_{2c}(z)}{n \eta}}  \asymp q + n^{-1/2}(\kappa+\eta)^{-1/4} .
\end{split}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.329266+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b03e7c537d32e5f19d616df386d92a4b59b2343870fe0b35065b2d1200b37977","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:orthovariationalnorm of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] Let $f_1,\hdots ,f_m$ be a sequence of local functions from $\Omega$ to $\mathbb{R}$ that have disjoint supports, and assume that the support of the function $f_i$ has cardinality $\ell_i$ for any~$1\le i\le m$. Assume that $\psi_{f_i}(\rho ,\mathcal{E})=0$ for any $\rho\in [0,1]$, any $\mathcal{E}\in [\rho ,\kappa\rho]$ and any $1\le i\le m$. Then, there exists a generic constant $C_6=C_6(\kappa )>0$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \| f_1+\hdots +f_m\|_{-1}^2 \le C_6 \sum_{i=1}^m \ell_i^2\mathrm{Var}_{\rho ,\mathcal{E}}(f_i).
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:10.015040+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b03ffc6dc9c191ad94367fd8221d6c48c6d86407875941a5573c7d14cd366d6d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 31 of arXiv:2602.14618, 'Finitary coding and Gaussian concentration\\ for random fields'] Let $Y=(Y_n)_{n\in\Z}$ be a renewal process with $\gcd\{k\ge1:f_k>0\}=1$. Then the following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\arabic*)}]
\item $Y$ satisfies Gaussian concentration;
\item $\sum_{k\ge1}s^k f_k<\infty$ for some $s>1$;
\item $Y$ is a finitary process with exponentially decaying coding radius;
\item $Y$ is a finitary coding of an i.i.d.\ process.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.774518+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b04179fee4a533b274a7d18e25e6f9f81022eecb1ef37e6e1f8994dc44f9b255","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2603.25400, 'One-arm probabilities for the two-dimensional metric-graph and discrete Gaussian free fiel'] For all $h\in\R$ and  $0<\alpha<\beta<1$, there exists $c=c(h,\alpha,\beta)>0$ such that for all large $N$,
    \begin{equation}
            \mathbb P[ \text{there exists a circuit in $A_{\alpha N,\beta N}$ that surrounds $B_{\alpha N}$, on which $\varphi_N\ge h$} ]>c,
    \end{equation} 
and hence \begin{equation}
        \mathbb P[ B_{\alpha N}\stackrel{\varphi_N\le h}{\longleftrightarrow} \partial B_{\beta N}]<1-c.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.732354+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b048d16f0711fe00df0eae2701a4948fc34205a4bf4a98e4bde2c8fc4110deb3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:free-energy-band of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] Fix $\alpha>\theta$, then the free energy of a band of overlap $q$ exists $\mathbb{P}_M$ almost surely, and is given by: 
    \begin{align} 
F(q;\alpha,\theta) = 
\begin{cases}
    \frac{\alpha}{2\theta}  (\theta + \frac{1}{\theta}) q^2 + \frac{\alpha^2}{4\theta^2}(1-q^2) + \frac{1}{2} \log(1-q^2) &\text{if} \ q^2> 1- \frac{\theta^2}{\alpha^2} \, ,
    \\
    \frac{\alpha}{2\theta} (\theta + \frac{1}{\theta})   q^2 + \frac{\alpha}{\theta} \sqrt{1-q^2} - \frac{3}{4} - \frac{1}{2} \log(\alpha/\theta) + \frac{1}{4} \log(1-q^2)  &\text{if} \ q^2 \leq 1-\frac{\theta^2}{\alpha^2} \, .
\end{cases}
    \end{align}
    For $1 < \alpha \leq \theta $ the free energy of the band of overlap $q$ is given by: 
    \[
F(q;\alpha,\theta) = \frac{\alpha}{2\theta} (\theta + \frac{1}{\theta}) q^2 + \frac{\alpha^2}{4\theta^2}(1-q^2) + \frac{1}{2} \log(1-q^2) \, .
    \] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.109772+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b049fd48b8f8e244e6ce54a75229deb779129c9c6c3d7dc72800bd2074078fef","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 31 of arXiv:2608.27374, '\Large \bf Distribution-constrained optimal multiple stopping: the Root-type solution'] Let \(\sigma^\xi\) be a stopping time in the induction procedure of Section \ref{sec:proba}. We further assume that
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \(0<\sigma^\xi<\infty\) almost surely and its law is atomless;
    \item \(b_n,b:\mathbb R_+\to[-\infty,\infty]\) are upper
    semicontinuous;
    \item \(b_n\xrightarrow{\Gamma^+}b\).
\end{enumerate}
Let
   $ \tau_n
    :=
    \inf\{t\ge\sigma^\xi:X_t\le b_n(t)\}$ and 
    $\tau
    :=
    \inf\{t\ge\sigma^\xi:X_t\le b(t)\}$.
Then
\[
    \tau_n\longrightarrow\tau
    \qquad\text{a.s.}
\]
in \([0,\infty]\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.424407+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b04a2c11422e83aca8b2f87e775e275bd0c378ad36c00c5c9143b52bc600a32d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:Gaussian-weighted-complexity of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[theorem]{thm:Gaussian-local-complexity}
For every continuous \(V:\mathbb R\to\mathbb R\) bounded below, the Gaussian pure spherical \(p\)-spin field satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \lim_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log
 \mathbb E\sum_{x:\nabla_SH_N^G(\sqrt N x)=0}
 e^{-NV(h_N^G(x))}
 =\sup_{u\in\mathbb R}\{\theta_p(u)-V(u)\}.
\end{equation}
In particular, for every compact interval \(B\subset\mathbb R\) with nonempty interior,
\begin{equation}
 \lim_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log\mathbb E\operatorname{Crt}_N^G(B)
 =\sup_{u\in B}\theta_p(u).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.719181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b04ce567235d8e520fed5a95f3503739a944137701e428a39e85c8644fffd1c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 20 (Exact conditional-control matching) of arXiv:2609.02196, 'Schr\"odinger Bridges on Lie Group Manifolds for Probabilistic Intrinsic Generation'] Under the conditional-kernel regularity in Assumption~\ref{ass:rccbm-conditional-kernel}, we have
\begin{equation}
P^\beta=\int Q^z\,\Lambda^\beta(\dd z).
\end{equation}
Its backward factor and Markov Doob control are
\begin{equation}
h_t^\beta(x)
=\int r_{t,T}^{\mathcal O_T}(y\mid x)e^{\beta_T(y)}\,\nu_T(\dd y),
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\bm u_t^\beta=\alpha\nabla_{\bm\xi}\log h_t^\beta.
\end{equation}
For \(z=(x_0,y)\), the exact conditional bridge has preterminal control
\begin{equation}
\bm v_t^z(x)=\alpha\nabla_{\bm\xi}\log r_{t,T}^{\mathcal O_T}(y\mid x),
\qquad t<T,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation*}
\E[\bm v_t^{Z_c}(X_t)\mid X_t=x]=\bm u_t^\beta(x),
\qquad P_t^\beta\text{-a.e.}
\end{equation*}
Equivalently, on every preterminal strip the conditional squared-error risk has excess risk
\begin{equation}
\mathcal L_{\beta,\tau}(\bm u)-\mathcal L_{\beta,\tau}(\bm u^\beta)
=\int_0^{T-\tau}\lambda_\tau(t)
\int\norm{\bm u-\bm u_t^\beta}^2P_t^\beta(\dd x)\,\dd t.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.153077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b051fa6ab7b7d8ae16254914a51bbb8dcb714808188a7d463ea0d93f13c5dfb6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2604.13819, 'Convolution, cumulants and infinitesimal generators in the formal power series ring'] Let $A(z) = \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} a_{k} z^{k}$ and $B(z) = \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} b_{k} z^{k}$ be formal power series in $\mathbb{R}\llbracket z \rrbracket$, and let $t \in \mathbb{R} \setminus \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$. 
We define the \emph{$t$-deformed convolution} by
\begin{align*}
(A \boxplus^{t} B)(z) \coloneqq \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} \sum_{i+j=k} \frac{(t)_{\underline{k}}}{(t)_{\underline{i}} (t)_{\underline{j}}} a_{i} b_{j} z^{k}.
\end{align*}
For $t = d \in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 1}$, the $d$-deformed convolution is defined by \eqref{d-convolution}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.686663+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b05876cb3e77bd8652e6b6884ca9a61b2a690fcf3b3c7fbd39040fc9c978afef","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 (Foster--Lyapunov condition for the ULA kernel) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] \label[lemma]{lem:lyapunov}
  Consider a continuously differentiable function $G\colon [0,\infty)\to\real$ such that  $|G'(x)|\le C(1+x)$ and
  \begin{equation}
    x\,G'(x)\ge -c_0 x^2 - c_1, \qquad x\ge 0,
  \end{equation}
  for constants $C,c_1\ge 0$ and $c_0\in[0,\lambda)$.  Set $V(x)=x^2$ and
  $\kappa = c_0+C^2$.   For every $h\le h_0 \coloneqq \lambda/(2\kappa\alpha)$,
  the ULA kernel $K_h$ satisfies
  \[
    K_h V(x)  \le  (1-\gamma)\,V(x) + b, \qquad x\ge 0,
  \]
  with $\gamma = \lambda/(\alpha+2\lambda)>0$ and
  $b = \bigl[\alpha h(2c_1+2C^2)+2\delta/\beta\bigr]/(\alpha+2\lambda)<\infty$,
  both independent of $h\le h_0$ and of the initial condition $u_0$.
  Iterating, for every $n\ge0$,
  \begin{equation}
    K_h^n V(x)\ \le\ (1-\gamma)^n V(x)+\frac b\gamma ;
  \end{equation}
  in particular, \cref{ass:moment} holds with $M = b/\gamma$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.502047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0595a7516a4d25a124a41f5ab5a505038130f20f375be32684a78cfe14eb717","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 44 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $(Y,Y') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],W)$, $(Z,Z') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],E)$ and $B \in L^{(2)}(W \times E,\bar{W})$ be arbitrary. Then we have
\begin{align}
(B(Y,Z),B(Y,Z)') \in \scrd_X^{2\alpha}([0,T],\bar{W}),
\end{align}
and the estimate
\begin{align}
\interleave B(Y,Z),B(Y,Z)' \interleave_{X,2\alpha} \leq C \interleave Y,Y' \interleave_{X,2\alpha} \interleave Z,Z' \interleave_{X,2\alpha},
\end{align}
where the constant $C > 0$ depends on $\alpha$, $T$, $X$ and $| B |$. Moreover, for $T \leq 1$ the constant $C$ does not depend on $T$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.797303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b05e33941bea18acba068d39e08cb0905e10846b85c28d1331bef3ca4b2bac52","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2609.00215, 'Hom--Lie Algebras and Explicit MSS Partition Bounds for $(6,3)$ Biangular Frames'] A {\em Hom--Lie algebra}~\cite{Hom,Back2022} is a triple $(\g, [\cdot,\cdot], \alpha)$ consisting of a vector space $\g$, a bilinear skew-symmetric bracket $[\cdot,\cdot]\colon \g\times\g \to \g$, and a linear map $\alpha\colon\g\to\g$ satisfying the Hom--Jacobi identity
		\begin{equation}
			[\alpha(x), [y,z]] + [\alpha(y), [z,x]] + [\alpha(z), [x,y]] = 0 \qquad \forall x,y,z\in\g. 
		\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.795791+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b05f52e729b5f95a9c3a13a63cabe2aee20cd077dafc6ef64b86161933b239b0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemme 46 of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] Let $\mu \in \mathcal{M}_1(\mathbb{R})$ be such that $\Int{\mathbb{R}}{} V(x) \, \mathrm{d}\mu(x) < +\infty$.

Then there are constants $C^{\prime}, C^{\prime\prime} \in \mathbb{R}$ such that
the following lower bounds are satisfied

\begin{align}
&\frac{1}{2}\Int{\mathbb{R}}{}V(x) \, \mathrm{d}\mu(x) - C^{\prime}

 \leq \Int{\mathbb{R}}{} V(x) \, \mathrm{d}\mu(x) - \Int{\mathbb{R}}{} \ln \max\Big\{ 0 ,  1+ \frac{2}{\ell} \Int{\mathbb{R}}{} \ln|x-y| \, \mathrm{d}\mu(y) \Big\} \, \mathrm{d}\mu(x) \\

&\text{and } -\frac{1}{4} \Int{\mathbb{R}}{} V(x) \, \mathrm{d}\mu(x) - C^{\prime\prime}     \leq   - \mathrm{Ent}[\mu] \, .

\end{align}

Thus in particular, $\Int{\mathbb{R}}{} V(x) \, \mathrm{d}\mu(x) < +\infty$ implies that $I[\mu] = +\infty$ if and only if $- \mathrm{Ent}[\mu] = +\infty$.
Combining these two we see that there is a constant $C > 0$ such that

\begin{align}

I[\mu] \geq \frac{1}{4}\Int{\mathbb{R}}{}V(x) \, \mathrm{d}\mu(x) - C \, .

\end{align}

Hence we naturally define $I[\mu] = +\infty$ whenever $\Int{\mathbb{R}}{}V(x) \, \mathrm{d}\mu(x) \, = \,  +\infty$ so that (\ref{ratefunctionlowerbound}) holds for all probability measures.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.732566+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0633b9c4b79ed303553b987c5c72d9fc971258e321ba2a78a7e5ebebebee5f6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:stablemanifold-dcu of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] Let $(d,\eta) = (4,0)$,  $\delta >0$ be sufficiently small,  $g \in (0,\delta)$ and $\textbf{a} \in [0, \delta )$.  Then there exists $\vec{\nu}_{c,\textbf{a}} = ( \nu_{c,\textbf{a}}^{(\emptyset)},  \nu_{c,\textbf{a}}^{({\nabla\nabla})} ,  \nu_{c,\textbf{a}}^{(\Delta)} )$ such that there exists an infinite bulk RG flow with 
