{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.442565+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0ad4bf8a04ee04061cd8cad49b105f70c5fbb1e0a4ff6a18fc504d9cb0ec179","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm theorem:Lp of arXiv:2504.19942, 'The edge-averaging process on graphs \\ with random initial opinions'] For every $p\in[1,\infty)$, there exists $C_p>0$ (depending only on $p$), such that if the i.i.d.\ initial opinions $\{f_0(v)\}_{v \in V}$ are in $L^p$, then for every $t>0$ and every $o\in V$,
