{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.820613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0bb150ca0bafaa0a38e0e6d88f7d8971b8ed9c588e9cab24c6e4239113c6f85","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:horizontal_decoupling of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] There are constants
  $C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:horiz_decoupling of the paper)}}, c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:horiz_decoupling of the paper)}}>0$ which depend only on $\Gamma_+$ and the dimension, such that the following holds.

  Let $B^1, B^2 \subset \mathbb{Z}^d \times [0, T]$ be space-time boxes with spatial projections $S_1, S_2$
  satisfying $\dist_H = \dist_H(B^1,B^2) \ge 8$ and $\diam(S_j) \leq w$ for $j = 1, 2$ and some positive constant $w$.
  Let $f_1, f_2: \mathbb{N}_0^{\mathbb{Z}^d \times \mathbb{R}_+} \to [0, 1]$ be measurable functions with supports in $B^1$ and $B^2$, respectively. Then, for all $\rho > 0$, $T \ge 1$,
  \begin{equation}
    \abs{\cov_\rho(f_1(\eta), f_2(\eta))} \le C_{\textnormal{\tiny (C:horiz_decoupling of the paper)}} w^{d - 1} \rho T^{d/2}
    e^{-c_{\textnormal{\tiny (c:horiz_decoupling of the paper)}} \dist_H \log(1+\dist_H/T)}.
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.904576+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0bd0c13d2d7441153ae75ca9fb63910951715ae67cd771d908fafda4ff774cf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def signed-realizable of arXiv:2607.19511, 'A Conditional Probability Hierarchy for Stochastic Choice\footnote{We thank Samson Abramsk'] A stochastic choice rule $G \mapsto c_G(\cdot)$ is \textbf{realizable as a $\Pi$-based signed probability mixture} if there is a finitely additive signed probability measure $Q$ on $(\Pi, {\cal D}_\Pi)$ such that for all $E \in \cal F$ and $G \in \cal G$:
