{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.302656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b101316f4d0285788bd7a27805cc02941fa514f113edb25ebd65e99ef7f35f33","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop cocycle_cber of arXiv:2608.06644, 'Applications of the cluster graphing'] The following holds:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item The $\mathcal{G}^{\mathrm{cl}}$-component of $\pi({x}) = [(x,u)]_{\Gamma} \in Y$ is isomorphic to the cluster of $u$ in $\pi(x)$.
        \item 
        If $G$ is unimodular, then $\mathcal{G}^{\text{cl}}$ is pmp by [Gaboriau05], [CTT22]. 
        \begin{enumerate}
            \item More generally, if $G$ is a quasi-transitive graph, the equivalence relation $\mathcal{R}_{\mathcal{G}^{\mathrm{cl}}}$ is measure-class-preserving with respect to $\nu$, and the corresponding Radon-Nikodym cocycle is given by
