\end{align}
and $y_0 = z_0 = 0$. 
Let $\mathbb{A}_0 \subset \mathbb{A}$ be the subspace with $x_0 = y_0 = z_0 =0$.
Due to Lemma~(lemma:RcKisBanach of the paper),  $\mathbb{A}$ and $\mathbb{A}_0$ are Banach spaces.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.202776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b116283e3e0062a4c2fc0054ad4f9f77708ae12667b1872bbc464dd4c97ba9c8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 of arXiv:2512.08745, 'Variance strikes back: sub-game--perfect Nash equilibria in time‑inconsistent $N$‑player g'] Let $M$ be an $(\F^i,\P)$-martingale $($respectively, an $(\F_N,\P)$-martingale$)$. There exists a unique process $Z \in \H^2_{\mathrm{loc}}(\F^i,\P,\R^d)$ $($respectively, $(Z^\ell)_{\ell \in \{1,\ldots,N\}}$ with each $Z^\ell \in \H^2_{\mathrm{loc}}(\F_N,\P,\R^d))$ such that
\begin{equation*}
M_{t} = M_0 + \int_0^t Z_s \cdot \d W^i_s \; \bigg(\text{\rm respectively,} \; M_{t} = M_0 + \int_0^t \sum_{\ell =1}^N Z^\ell_s \cdot \d W^\ell_s\bigg),\; t \in [0,T],\; \P \text{\rm --a.s.}
