{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.428553+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b126b4736eb9bbc034822574cf4644c3a907cfdc0858aaf1ee82c46cec524309","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def_SOP of arXiv:2411.16464, 'Generating social networks with static and dynamic utility-maximization approaches'] For a given individuals graph $\mathcal{G}_N(\mathscr{I} , \alpha, C)$, we define the Social Optimization Problem (SOP) as:
\begin{equation*}
\begin{cases}
\argmax_{\alpha} \mathcal{O} (\alpha, C) =  \sum^N_{i=1} U_i(\alpha^i, C^i)\\
\text{s.t} \quad \begin{cases} 
\alpha \in [0,1)^{n_N} \\
