{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.595335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b12ad2f84803a2ae8be0b52f4fb35373a0e3fb3e39be6c2175395e0e1f0c8e35","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 (Approximation accuracy of sparse variational GP) of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] Under the same assumption of \cref{thm:gp-statistical}, the sparse variational GP computed by \cref{alg:gp} with $J \gtrsim T^{d/(d+2\fs)}$  satisfies
