{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.647234+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b12b703f3e26af90849a94fb4e180baa3410206cbccb33054bf56d251c405e81","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem SRWestimates of arXiv:2411.13926, 'Random walks on random walks:\\ non-perturbative results in high dimensions'] Let $(Y_t)_{t \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}}$ be a simple random walk on $\mathbb{Z}^d$ with $d\geq 3$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item There exists $\delta>0$ such that 
\begin{equation} 
\inf_{\gamma\in \Gamma_{-\infty}} P_{o,0}^{RW} \big( Y_i \neq \gamma_i \text{ for all } i \in [-|\gamma|,-1] \big)>\delta.
\end{equation}
\item There exists $C<\infty$ 
such that, for any $\gamma \in \Gamma_{-\infty}$, $t \leq |\gamma|$ and $s>t$, 
\begin{equation} 
\sup_{z \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^d} P_{o,0}^{RW} (Y_{-s} = z \mid Y_i \neq \gamma_i \text{ for all } i \in [-t,-1] ) \leq Cs^{-d/2}. \end{equation}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

