{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.661939+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b141c2d03e3fb8a1fa9fd8c48a7cb4e58edd239ed5d3285ecf1c6cce7ed45886","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:conv-fields-fractal of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $D$ be a Jordan domain such that $\dim_M(\partial D)<2-1/4$. Let $\mathbb E_\delta$ denote the expectation under the (critical) coupling of Theorem (thm:master of the paper) in the discrete approximation $D_\delta$. For any continuous, bounded function $f:\mathbb C\to\mathbb R$ and any $n,k\geq1$, 
