{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.582323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b143cbeddd085731380f6e82ca3898788b09144d8b452864641e96f2b833462b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop precompact of arXiv:2606.30517, '\textsc{Convergence towards Ideal Poisson--Voronoi tessellations with a focus on Diestel--'] Assume that  there exists a real number $ r_0>0$‌ such that $p_1\coloneqq \liminf_r F(r+r_0)/F(r)>1$ and $p_2\coloneqq \limsup_r F(r+r_0)/F(r)<\infty$. Then: 



		\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
			\item  If $t(\lambda)$ is defined by~(equation eq:t of the paper), then the set of measures $\mu_{\lambda}\coloneqq \lambda\iota_{t(\lambda)}^*\mu \in\mathcal M$ is relatively compact.
			\item  Every subsequential limit $\nu$ of $\mu_{\lambda}$, as $\lambda\to 0$, satisfies





			\begin{eqnarray*}
				p_1^{j}\leq \nu\left(\mathrm{Lip}_1^{\leq jr_0}\right), &&\nu\left(\mathrm{Lip}_1^{<jr_0}\right) \leq p_2^j,\\
				p_2^{-j}\leq \nu\left(\mathrm{Lip}_1^{\leq -jr_0}\right), && \nu\left(\mathrm{Lip}_1^{<-jr_0}\right) \leq p_1^{-j}.
			\end{eqnarray*}
			for all non negative $j\in \mathbb Z^{\geq 0}$. In particular, if $p\coloneqq \lim_r F(r+r_0)/F(r)$ exists, then 
			\begin{equation*}
				\forall j\in\mathbb Z: p^j\leq \nu\left(\mathrm{Lip}_1^{\leq jr_0}\right)\leq p^{j+1}.
			\end{equation*}
			\item  The joint distributions of $(\iota_{t(\lambda)}X^{(\lambda)}, \mathrm{Vor}(X^{(\lambda)}))$, $\lambda>0$, are precompact,

			and hence, there exists an IPVT.
		\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.423826+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b146aae809e8f53ebdb5a2ece4c2f580679cd2767feade27733131fe66927bce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p: ind random field convolution formula of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Let $Z$ be a $\C$-valued random field on $\R^d$. Suppose that it has a finite second moment, and define $C:\R^d\to [0,\infty), y\mapsto \BC[Z(y), Z(0)]$. Further, assume that $Z$ and $\Phi$ are independent. Then, as $Z$ and $\Phi$ are independent,
    \begin{align}
        \beta_{Z\cdot\Phi} &= C \cdot \alpha_\Phi + \big|\BE[Z(0)]\big|^2\beta_\Phi,\\
        \hat\beta_{Z\cdot\Phi} &= (2\pi)^{-d}\hat{C} \ast \hat\alpha_\Phi + \big|\BE[Z(0)]\big|^2\hat\beta_\Phi.
    \end{align}
    \begin{proof}
        The formulas are a direct consequence of the more general formula~(equation e: beta transport formula of the paper). We choose $K_x:= Z(x) \delta_x, x\in\R^d$ and use that $\Phi$ and $K$ are independent in this case.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.728017+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b14b4f99b4c6141f2e3dee79ad174e3b0e67e3be5bbd60064b9d2da47db126b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary crl:nl_markov of arXiv:2604.25851, '{Non-uniqueness of nonlinear Markov processes in the sense of McKean associated with parab'] Let $\{u^z\}_{z\in\mathbb{R}^d}$ be such that each $u^z\coloneqq (u^z(t,\cdot))_{t>0}$ is a solution to the FPE (equation eq:Main_FPE_our_paper of the paper) in the sense of (def:FPE-sol of the paper) with initial condition $\delta_z$, satisfying the integrability condition (equation eq:integrability_our_paper of the paper) with $u^z$ replacing $u$. Assume further injectivity of $(t,z)\mapsto u^z(t,x)dx$ and that, for every $(s,z)\in (0,\infty) \times \mathbb{R}^d$, $u^z_{s+} \coloneqq (u^z({s+t},\cdot))_{t\geq 0} $ is the unique solution to the linearized FPE
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{dcases}
        \partial_t v(t,x) = \Delta\Big( a\big(x, u^z(s+t,\cdot)\big)\, v(t,x)\Big) - \nabla \cdot \Big( b\big(x, u^z(s+t,\cdot)\big) \, v(t,x)\Big), \\
        v(0,\cdot) = u^z(s,\cdot),
        \end{dcases}
    \end{equation}
    in 
     \begin{equation}
     \big\{v \geq 0: [t\mapsto v(t,x)dx] \in C(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathcal P),  v(t,x) \leq Cu^z(s+t,x)\,\text{ a.s. for some }C\geq 1 \big\}.
     \end{equation}
     Then there exists a nonlinear Markov core $\{P^z\}_{z\in \mathbb{R}^d}$ for $\{u^z\}_{z\in \mathbb{R}^d}$ in the sense of (def:NMC of the paper), consisting of the unique solution path laws to (equation eq:main_MV-SDE of the paper) with $P^z_t = u^z(t,x)dx$ and $P^z_0 = \delta_z$. In particular, the induced nonlinear Markov process $\{P^\zeta\}_{\zeta \in \mathcal P_0}$, $\mathcal P_0 := \{u^z(t,x)dx| z \in \mathbb{R}^d, t \geq 0\}$, is uniquely determined by $\{u^z\}_{z \in \mathbb{R}^d}$ and (equation eq:main_MV-SDE of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.350200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1514803d4509880fbe9079c4831f54f5b4b698442447b514403270be06d2ee5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 1 (Proposition 6.3 of \cite{niyogi_smale_weinberger}) of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $M \subset \RR^D$ be a compact $C^2$ manifold. Suppose that $x, y\in M$ are connected by a geodesic $\gamma_{xy}$ of length $s$, and write $r = \|x-y\| $. Define $v$ as the initial velocity of $\gamma_{xy}$ at $x$. If $r \le (\sqrt 2 - 1) \reach_M$, the following are true:
