{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.855897+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1563a9288dc9af61ea26febc64b875091e571fb9e0ceb6782d9c3bbfdca7f49","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 19 (Itô's formula on $L^4$) of arXiv:2608.21014, 'The stochastic Cahn--Hilliard equation in critical spaces'] Let $d\in \{3,4\}$, $u_0\in L^0_{\F_0}(\Omega;H^1(\sO))$, and suppose that Assumption~\ref{assumption_weakened_setting} holds. Let $(u,\sigma)$ be the unique maximal solution to \eqref{eq:SCHtorus} and $(\sigma_m)_{m\ge 1}$ a localising sequence for $(u,\sigma)$. Then a.s.\ for all $t\in [0,T]$
