{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.749983+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b168a9299bfbedcc0492b98f6e7e400d2d2e0f9b50a21d4e686ddd3d2128143c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:non_lin_MP of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. A probability measure $\mathbb{P}_{\nu}$, on $(C_T,\mathcal{B})$, is a solution to D-NL-MP$(b,\sigma;\nu)$ if it is a solution to NL-MP$({\bf b}^*,{\boldsymbol\sigma}^*;\nu)$ such that
\begin{equation}

