{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.713820+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b19364b71b4e8f3a46981e89d932ac364a34ffd73dad8425bf98f712c16ce217","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def.CIH of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] We define $\mathsf{CIH}$$(y)$ as the coupling $(S_{t},\bar{B}_{t})_{t\geqslant 0}$ in infinite horizon constructed in the following way. Set 
		\begin{equation}
			T_k :=\frac{1}{2}\left(3^k-1\right),\quad k\in \mathbb{N}.
		\end{equation}
		\begin{enumerate}[label=(\Alph*)]
			\item The processes start from $S_0 = \bar{B}_0 = y$.
			\item Conditioned on $(S_t,\bar{B}_t)_{t\in [0,T_k]}$, we sample $(\Delta_k S_t, \Delta_k \bar{B}_t)_{t\in [0,3^k]}$ satisfying
			\begin{align*} 
				\big(S_{T_k} + \Delta_k S_t, S_{T_k} + \Delta_k \bar{B}_t\big)_{t\in [0,3^k]} \stackrel{d}{=} \mathsf{CFH}(3^k,\lfloor 3^{\frac{k}{3}}\rfloor, S_{T_k}).
			\end{align*}
			Then we extend the coupled process by 
			\begin{align*} 
				\big(S_{T_k + t},\bar{B}_{T_k + t}\big) := \big(S_{T_{k}},\bar{B}_{T_{k}}\big) + \big(\Delta_k S_{t}, \Delta_k \bar{B}_{t}\big),\quad t\in[0,3^k].
			\end{align*}
		\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

