{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.245754+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1ffa184617d6ea86f050dfcae0207f12db0c8421a2d657717c5357504dcd09b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 17 ({\cite[Theorem 1.1) of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] {PW}}]

  Let $\mu\in\mathcal P^+[H_-,H_+],n\in \mathbb N$ and $t_0=0<t_1<\dots<t_n=T$. For any integer $i \in [1,n]$, let $\Lambda_i \subseteq \mathfrak{X}$ be a subset and $H^\pm_i: \mX\mapsto \mathbb R$ satisfy  $H^-_i\le H^+_i$. Let $(\tilde\eta_t)_{t\ge0}$ be the censored Glauber dynamics restricted to $\Lambda_i$ in the time interval $[t_{i-1},t_i)$ (as in Definition \ref{def:restricted}); with ceiling constraint  $\min(H_i^+,H_+)$ and floor constraint $\max(H_i^-,H_-)$ (as in \Cref{def:constrained}); and with initial condition distributed according to $\mu$.  Let $\tilde \mu_t$ be the law of $\tilde \eta_t$, and $\mu_t$ be the law of the unrestricted and uncensored Glauber dynamics at time $t$, with the same initial condition $\mu$. Then, for any $t\le T$:
  \begin{eqnarray}
     \tilde \mu_t\in\mathcal P^+[H_-,H_+]; \qquad \mu_t\preceq \tilde \mu_t; \qquad  \|\mu_t-\pi_{H_\pm}\|\le \|\tilde\mu_t-\pi_{H_\pm}\|.
  \end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

