{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.887789+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2035dec5a7635399625a9b8c2a40787bbdd18e97d005970283d65aa19923231","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 34 (\cite{Hirano-1997}, Theorem 1) of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] Let functions $f$, $h$, and $W$ satisfy the following conditions:

\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] $f$ and $h$ are continuous on $[0,\infty)$.

\item[(ii)] $W$ is continuous on $\mathbb{R}$ and non-negative.

\item[(iii)] There exist positive numbers $a$, $\beta$, $\varepsilon$, $\eta$ such that
\begin{equation*}
  \sup_{x>0} x^{-a}|f(x)| < \infty,
\qquad
\sup_{x>0} x^{\beta}|h(x)| < \infty,
\end{equation*}

and
\begin{equation*}

    \limsup_{x\to\infty} W(x)e^{-\varepsilon x} < \infty,
\qquad
\liminf_{x\to\infty} W(x)e^{-\eta x} > 0,
\end{equation*}
with
\begin{equation}
    \beta\eta > a > 0.
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}

If conditions (a), (b), and (c) are satisfied, then
\begin{equation}

    \EE\!\left[
f\!\left(e^{S_n}\right)
\,h\!\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n} W(S_i)\right)
\right]
\sim c\,n^{-3/2},
\qquad n\to\infty,
\end{equation}
for some constant $c$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.856383+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b20481e73b9bf68883cf72ec87067654e1329e4fbf209d5485d320563dd21a17","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2605.20115, 'Moment bounds on correctors for the degenerate random conductance model'] There exist $C_0,C_1,C_2\ge 1$ depending on $\Lambda$ such that, for any compactly supported $g:\ZZ^d\to\RR^{d}$ and any $1\le i,j,k\le d$, if we define $F_1(A)\coloneqq\int \nabla \phi_i \cdot g$ and $F_2(A)\coloneqq\int \nabla \sigma_{ijk} \cdot g$, then for any $\theta\in(0,\frac12)$,
