{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.597597+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b215a32c9459969885baa706a9512a06e58c80b77ccedae87c855b72a0dcd294","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop lwb of arXiv:2412.03415, 'Critical first passage percolation on random graphs'] Fix $\ell_n =\lfloor n^{\rho/2-\eta/4}\rfloor$ for $0 < \eta < \rho/2$. Under the assumptions of Theorem (thm:main of the paper), there exists a probability space where the distribution of $T_n(u,v)$ can be coupled with two random variables $\theta_{\ell_n}^{(v)}, \theta_{\ell_n}^{(u)}$ such that:
