{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.631527+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b23afdb1379e11359bf466d00c8aec727fe2cc8856e5e72e00a9de9536a153d7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_\mathcal{W}$, $\psi$ be the corresponding generator, $\varphi$ be its pseudo-inverse, $A \in \mathcal{A}$ and $x \in (0,1)$. Furthermore, let $H_x$ be defined according to eq. \eqref{eq:function_H_x} and $\nu_{H_x}$ be its corresponding probability measure. Then the following assertions hold:
