{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:36:49.894714+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b27896d4d9869a3258fe8f8c02e87da9366c65b8610731ef66aee79d2f06a82f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:homogeneous of arXiv:2609.00336, 'Critical points of point charge potentials along lines'] Let $k\geq1$ and $p\geq0$. The space of homogeneous polynomials $P(a,b)$ of degree $k$, even in $b$, and satisfying (equation eq:weighted of the paper), i.e. $P_{aa}+P_{bb}+\frac{p}{b}P_b=0$, is one-dimensional. If $P_{k,p}$ is normalized so that the coefficient of $a^k$ is $1$, then $\nabla P_{k,p}$ does not vanish on $\mathbb{R}^2\backslash\{0\}$ and, on the positively oriented unit circle,
