 There exists a filtrated probability space endowed with two processes $X_{\zeta_1}^{b_1},X_{\zeta_2}^{b_2} \in C(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R}_+)$ and three driving noises $(N_0,B_c,\widetilde{N}_\nu)$ defined as in Theorem~(Main.Thm01 of the paper) such that the following two claims hold.  
