{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.966234+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b30ebb7a13c53e09514af7ecc2245f3536cf8472a4cd7cb62a04043204670630","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm7a_copy of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] (Theorem (thm7a of the paper)) Let $k \ge 3$ be an odd integer, $k_n=k$ for all $n$ and $r$ be a positive integer. Then for all sufficiently large $n$, 
