    \end{equation}
    And there is
$$\diver Q[w]=\diver K[w]=\diver J[w]=0\quad\text{in}~\mathcal{D}'(E).$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:28.016957+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b33af46d935c3037ddc2a23086b5399588a0415ec20d90a70e72572bbc070d2a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sampling of arXiv:2608.09465, 'Balancing fractional Brownian motion'] Given $J\in\mathbb{Z}$ and $\mathcal I\subseteq\{(j, k)\in\mathbb{Z}\times\mathbb{Z}: j\leq J\}$ finite, there is an equispaced grid $\mathcal T_J\subset[0,1]$ with $|\mathcal T_J|\lesssim_H 2^J+1$ such that every function of the form $g(t) = \sum_{(j,k)\in\mathcal I} c_{j,k}G^H_{j,k}(t), t\in [0, 1]$ with arbitrary real coefficients $(c_{j,k})_{(j,k)\in\mathcal I}$, satisfies
\begin{align}
\|g\|_\infty\leq 2\max_{t\in\mathcal T_J}|g(t)|. 
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.012596+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b33d8111169db82c6541ec8e9399a84bc3fb32827ee5b3e7f437ff96f071a0bf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 50 of arXiv:2609.02850, 'Canonical-row Chern flow on Bott--Samelson towers:\\ realizable-volume models for Schubert'] One has
\begin{align}
 \Nrm_{x,z}(\widetilde\Omega_\alpha)
 &=\partial_z^{\length(w)-r_\alpha}
   \Nrm_{x,z}(H_{w,\lambda})\in\RV,
 \\
 \Nrm_x(\Omega_{\alpha,k})
 &=\left.\partial_z^{\length(w)-k}
