{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.060808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3556a74e3615135822604074103c72a0c18fd3da3ec8791adc7e3989660a0cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm diagfluc of arXiv:2508.04954, 'Conditional exponential directed last passage percolation under a one-point upper large de'] Fix $a,b > 0$ and $\ell> \bar{\mathcal{L}}(a,b)$. Let $D=\ell^2-2(a+b)\ell+(a-b)^2$. 
Define the positive real numbers   
\begin{equation} 
    \mathsf{\sigma}= \frac{\sqrt{(a+b)\ell- (a-b)^2} D^{1/4}}{2\sqrt{ab}}
    \quad \text{and} \quad 
    \mathsf{c}_\pm= \bigg(1 \pm \frac{(a-b)\sqrt{D}}{(a+b)\ell -(a-b)^2} \bigg)^{1/2}. 
\end{equation}
Then, 
\begin{equation} \begin{split} 
    &{\rm Law} \left( \left\{ \frac{ \mathcal{L}( t aN +  s \frac{a(\ell-a+b)\mathsf{\sigma}}{\ell\sqrt{D}}   N^{1/2}, t bN -  s \frac{b(\ell+a-b)\mathsf{\sigma}}{\ell\sqrt{D}}  N^{1/2})- t \ell N}{\mathsf{\sigma} N^{1/2}} \right\}_{(s,t)\in {\mathbb R}\times (0,1)}
    \, \bigg| \,  \mathcal{L}(aN, bN)= \ell N \right) \\
    &\xrightarrow{\textit{f.d.d.}}  {\rm Law} \left( \{ \mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_1(t) - |\mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_2(t) - s| \}_{(s,t)\in {\mathbb R}\times (0,1)} \right)
\end{split} \end{equation}
as $N\to \infty$, where 
\begin{equation} 
    \mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_1(t)= \frac{\mathsf{c}_+ \mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_+(t)+ \mathsf{c}_- \mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_-(t)}{\sqrt{2}}  \quad\text{and}\quad 
    \mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_2(t)= \frac{\mathsf{c}_+ \mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_+(t)- \mathsf{c}_- \mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_-(t)}{\sqrt{2}} 
\end{equation}
for two independent standard Brownian bridges $\mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_+$ and $\mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_-$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.258533+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b35a1279620567feacd625ddfeb6946363c2487e479cd0fbeacbaec570b252d5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prp 81 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Set $r_n=n^{\theta},\;\theta\geq 0$ and suppose that $\kappa\in (1/2,1]$ and $\alpha>1$.
Then, for any $\zeta>\alpha^{-1}$, it holds that
\begin{align*}
  d_{\BL^{\kappa}}(\mu^{(r_n)},\mu_n^{(r_n)})
  \lesssim
  \begin{dcases}
    n^{-\frac{\alpha-1}{\alpha}}(\log n)^{1+\zeta}, & \theta=0,\;\alpha\in (1,2),\\
    n^{-\frac{\alpha-1}{\alpha}+\frac{2+\alpha}{2\alpha}\theta}(\log n)^{\zeta(1-\alpha/2)}, & \theta>0,\;\alpha\in (1,2),\\
    n^{-\frac{1}{2}}(\log n)^{1+\zeta},& \theta=0,\;\alpha=2,\\
    n^{-\frac{1}{2}+\theta}(\log n)^{\frac{1}{2}}, & \theta>0,\;\alpha=2,\\
    n^{-\frac{1}{2}}(\log n)^{\frac{1}{2}}, & \theta=0,\;\alpha\in (2,\infty),\\
    n^{-\frac{1}{2}+\theta}, & \theta>0,\;\alpha\in (2,\infty),
  \end{dcases}
  \qquad\qquad
  \bbP\mathrm{-a.s.}
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.950011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b35c6b8dd25aa7d1b08204599fb848e5b81f1457c35cdd554fb7a3d130c99ae5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2606.24887, '2606.24887'] Let $L \geq 1$ be a constant. Then, on the event $\{\Lambda \leq 1\}$ we have with very high probability 
		\begin{align}  
			\absb{s^2 G_{xx} + 2\ii \eta s G_{xx} + s -(\eta^2 + \abs{w}^2) G_{xx} + \ii \eta} &\le  \mathcal{C} \varphi\\ 

			\absb{s^3  + 2 \ii \eta s^2 +(1 - \eta^2 - \abs{w}^2)s+ \ii \eta} & \leq \mathcal C   \varphi .
		\end{align}
		uniformly for all $x \in \mathcal T_{\varphi}\cup \ubarr{\mathcal T_{\varphi}}$ and all $N^{-1+ \delta} \le \eta \le L$ and $ \abs{w} \le 2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.693558+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b35e35fd521e38005e8ef8012a293137faf2c90057597db871fb05b64eb3ddfc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop rest of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $\gamma$ is chosen small enough, then, given any $0 < \eta' < \eta < \frac{1}{2}$ small enough \mbox{(depending only on $\gamma$),} for any fixed $u \geq 0$ we have  
