{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.849212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b377443f9a8b7431b51ee8bbc4da99880d2ac3ba0785471d45fb29e35512ffe9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2511.10814, '\Large \bf \boldmath\ \\ Convergence of the extended Kalman filter with small and state-de'] Let $\widetilde{W}(t)$ be a $\mathbb{F}$-Brownian motion with values in $\mathbb{R}^{r}$, $n \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $A$ be a family of $\mathbb{F}$-adapted $(\K, k)$-stable processes where $\K$ is $\mathbb{F}$-adapted  and $k$ is  some family of deterministic positive and  locally bounded  functions. We suppose that $\x(t)$ is a family of $\mathbb{R}^{n}$-valued semi-martingales satisfying
