{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.610800+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3dad009d3803b1c5fa3540a1a96c47f804e0e32f9229c4bbb0bd18ab712eb5f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 (\cite{DvZ2001}) of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] Suppose that $\xi_k, k\ge 0$ are martingale differences with respect to a filtration $\FF_k,k\ge 0$, and let $M_k=\sum_{j=1}^k \xi_j$. 
Assume that we have the bounds $\ev[\xi_k^2|\FF_{k-1}]\le \sigma_k^2$ on the conditional second moments. For a fixed $\eta>0$ define
\begin{align}
    H_k^{(\eta)}=\sum_{j=1}^k \xi_j^2 \ind(|\xi_j|>\eta)+\sum_{j=1}^k \sigma_j^2. 
\end{align}
Then
\begin{align}
    \pr(\max_{1\le k\le n} |M_k|>t, H_n^{(\eta)}\le L)\le 2 \exp\big(-\tfrac{t^2}{2(L+\eta t)}\big).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.648377+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3e08a53eb18bc76ed265ce3e53cfb245b3b4286deeb8d4dced8554c04c1fe77","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm_voter_model_stat_meas of arXiv:2607.04002, 'Collisions of random walks in unimodular random graphs: applications to the random geometr'] Let~$G$ be a locally finite and connected graph.
