{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.414068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3e69a56d4e69dbecfc303ed42fb17076b3ca9da623c55d1a80fe4f9dfd7f412","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary corollary1streduction of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] To prove  Theorem (mainquasiramdonmess2 of the paper), we only need the following: let $\mathcal{K}$ denote the event $\mathcal{K}:=\{\|A_n\|_{op}\leq4\sqrt{n}\},$ then we can find $\alpha,\gamma,c_\Sigma\in(0,1)$ such that for any $w_0\in\mathbb{S}^{n-1}$,
