{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.188647+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b40d76a432ddbe014586270120d8f302e73ce3fa46128812cd134355c1d02544","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: enhancement converge of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] Almost surely for every $(\varphi_1,\varphi_2) \sim \nu^0\otimes \nu^0$, there exist a random variable
