{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.788057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b45834f2d9a0a877e2ea149c3a590eb73f15f2db79d835bcccbd69dec66a9cbb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lipschitz Bound of arXiv:2411.09260, 'The Hydrodynamic Limit of Hawkes Processes on Adaptive Stochastic Networks'] For any $c \in \Gamma_E$ any $\theta \in \mathcal{E}$, any $z , y \in \mathcal{D}([0,T] , \Gamma)$, there exists a unique $ \lbrace j_{\theta,\eta} \rbrace_{\theta,\eta \in \mathcal{E}}  \in   \mathcal{D}([0,T] , \mathcal{P}( \Gamma_E) ) $, written $ j_{\theta\eta} := (j_{\theta\eta,t})_{t\leq T}$ such that for all $t\leq T$, and all $a \in \Gamma_E$,
