{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.758927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b4634614844f0b3bbfb693e0c015c0344531a3bc07bcf3f0a5d3bfdd0c402197","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Satz thm:wavelet-characterization of arXiv:2411.18155, 'Besov regularity of random wavelet series'] Let $d\in \mathds{N}$, $p,q\in (0,\infty]$, $s \in\mathds{R}$.
Denote by $(\Psi_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in J}$ the orthonormal basis of $L_2(\mathds{R}^d)$ given in 
  \hyperref[{eq:wavelet-tensorization}]{\textup{\tagform@{\ref*{eq:wavelet-tensorization}}}}
.
Assume that $k>\max\setn{s,d\lr{\frac{1}{p}-1}-s}$ if $p\in (0,1)$ and $k>\left\lverts\right\rvert$ else.
Let $f\in\mathcal{S}^\prime(\mathds{R}^d)$.
Then $f\in B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$ if and only if it can be represented as
\begin{equation}
f=\sum_{(j,t,m)\in J} a_{j,t,m}  \Psi_{j,t,m}
\end{equation}
with $a=(a_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in J}\in b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$.
The convergence is unconditional in $\mathcal{S}^\prime(\mathds{R}^d)$.
Furthermore, the representation is unique, i.e., for given  $f\in B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$, the unique element $(a_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in J}\in b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$ such that 
  \hyperref[{eq:wavelet-characterization}]{\textup{\tagform@{\ref*{eq:wavelet-characterization}}}}
 holds is given by $a_{j,t,m}=\skpr{f}{\Psi_{j,t,m}}$, where the duality pairing is suitably defined.
The map
\begin{equation*}
I: f\mapsto (\skpr{f}{\Psi_{j,t,m}})_{(j,t,m)\in J}
\end{equation*}
defines an isomorphism of quasi-Banach spaces $B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)\to b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$, and the map
\begin{equation*}
S:  (a_{j,t,m})_{(j,t,m)\in J}\mapsto \sum_{(j,t,m)\in J}a_{j,t,m}\Psi_{j,t,m}
\end{equation*}
defines an isomorphism of quasi-Banach spaces $b^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)\to B^s_{p,q}(\mathds{R}^d,w)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

