{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.186257+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b496b630031bdbe5f17dd8b85c35444f5459585fb23658e51ac98ab3a052a600","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $3\le d\le 5$, there exists $C>C'>0$ such that for any $M\ge 1$, $N\ge CM$, $v\in  \widetilde{B}(\frac{N}{C'})\setminus   \widetilde{B}(M)$ and $D\subset [\widetilde{B}(M)]^c$, 
