{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.290704+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b50d0d457ac7bab8bdb2b4d580737ecda3e6cbabfb425a8bad3d7e4bded7becb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop error-estimate-no-scale-sep of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] Let $\mu \in C^1([0,\infty);\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X}))$ be a solution to the full forward Kolmogorov equation (equation eq:full-forw-K of the paper) with corresponding coarse-grained dynamics $\hat{\mu}$ and let $\eta \in C^1([0,\infty); \mathcal{P}(\mathcal{Y}))$ be the solution to the effective dynamics (equation eq:eff-dyn-non-cg of the paper) with initial condition $\hat{\mu}_0,\eta_0 \in \mathcal{P}_+(\mathcal{Y})$ satisfying $\hat{\mu}_0(y), \eta_0(y) \geq c_0$ for some $c_0 > 0$ and all $y \in \mathcal{Y}$. Then, for any fixed $T > 0$ there exists a constant $C = C(L,|\mathcal{X}|,T,c_0)$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{split}
            \mathscr{H}_{\eta_t}\left(\dfrac{\hat{\mu}_t}{\eta_t}\right) &\leq 2\mathscr{H}_{\eta_0}\left(\dfrac{\hat{\mu}_0}{\eta_0}\right) + \dfrac{C}{\min_y(\alpha_{\gLSI}(\rho(\cdot |y), M^y))} \left[\mathscr{H}_\rho\left(\dfrac{\mu_0}{\rho}\right) - \mathscr{H}_\rho\left(\dfrac{\mu_t}{\rho}\right)\right]
        \end{split}
    \end{equation}
    for all $t \in [0,T]$. In particular, the implicit prefactor $\min_y(\alpha_{\gLSI}(\rho(\cdot |y), M^y))$ can be replaced by the explicit constant $\alpha > 0$ given in (equation eq:alpha of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:04:39.221180+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b50d3f9d2cd0d7c73723f41fe0fcdd99921cad2ef0a7203bde5cc11c6cbc0e91","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 16 of arXiv:2608.13976, 'Boundary Harnack principle for diffusion with jumps on metric measure spaces'] Suppose ${\bf (\wh{EP})} _{\leq , r_0, \gamma}$ holds with  $r_0>0$ and $\gamma>0.$ There is a constant $C=C(r_0, \gamma)\geq 1$ such that
    for every ball $B$ with radius $r_0$ and $\overline B\subsetneq \sX$,
    each open $U\subset  2^{-1}B$, $\xi\in U$ and $r\in (0, r_0)$,
\begin{equation}
\frac{\E_x[\wh \tau^B_{B_U(\xi,r)}]}{r^\gamma\P_x\big(\wh \tau^B_U>\wh \tau^B_{B_U(\xi,r)}\big)}
\geq C\left(\P_x\big(\wh \tau^B_U>\wh \tau^B_{B_U(\xi,r)}\big)+\frac{\E_x[\wh \tau^B_{B_U(\xi,r)}]}{r^\gamma}\wedge1\right) \quad\hbox{ for }x\in B_U(\xi, 3r/4).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.882830+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b50eae87e312772bf71b946bea55ce4d4a9cd6d4c11616c4a4f210fb2f06299b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2506.11799, 'Quenched limit for diffusive biased random walks in random environment'] For all $\varepsilon>0$ there exist a positive constant $C>0$, such that, for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$ 
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathbb{E}_{0, 0}\left[ \sum_{i \in \mathrm{JRLC}(n)} \left(\frac{\tilde{\mu}^{(1)}_{i}}{n^{1/2}} \wedge 1\right) \left(\frac{\tilde{\mu}^{(2)}_{i}}{n^{1/2}} \wedge 1\right) \right]\le C n^{-1/2 + \varepsilon}.
	\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.242172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5126f214ecefe1a94d14c1ee2a65979d7cce1f32128b3a8a0cc5bbab9cb353e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop max_action of arXiv:2604.23751, 'Large deviation principles for pattern-avoiding permutations, and limit shapes for constra'] For any $\beta\in \mathbb R$, the action $A_{\beta}$ has a unique minimizer $(\pi_1^{(\beta)}, \pi_2^{(\beta)})$ in $\mathcal{D}$. For $\beta \leq 0$, we have $\pi_1^{(\beta)}=\pi_2^{(\beta)}=\frac{1}{2}\Leb_{[0,1]}$. 
    For $\beta>0$, the densities of $\pi_1^{(\beta)}$ and $\pi_2^{(\beta)}$ on $[0,1]$ are given by
	\begin{equation}
	    \rho_1^{(\beta)}(x) := \frac{1}{1+\exp\left(\beta(\frac12-x) \right)}, 
        \quad \rho_2^{(\beta)}(x) := \frac{1}{1+\exp\left(\beta(x-\frac12) \right)}.
	\end{equation}
	In particular, both $\pi_1^{(\beta)}$ and $\pi_2^{(\beta)}$ have total mass $\frac{1}{2}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.338677+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b517445eee78e7fc21626ba56a654f695968853dd327047e4bd49f12b876ffad","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 of arXiv:2512.05687, '$L^p$-Boltzmann-Gibbs principle \\ via Littlewood-Paley-Stein inequality'] Let $p, q>1$ satisfy $1/p+1/q=1$.  Then, 
for $f$ satisfying $E^\mu[f]=0$, we have
$$
\sup_{\fa\not\equiv \rm{const}} \frac{\int f\fa d\mu}{\|(-L_0)^{1/2}\fa\|_{L^q(\mu)}}
\le \|(-L_0)^{-1/2}f\|_{L^p(\mu)} 
\le 2 \sup_{\fa\not\equiv \rm{const}} \frac{\int f\fa d\mu}{\|(-L_0)^{1/2}\fa\|_{L^q(\mu)}}.
$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.090782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5195af761284d237979ca936f6eb5d4fa4570a9b2d92ebaeb75db7e7c0d3dc2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 29 of arXiv:2608.28148, 'Flows and homotopies of Banach Lie algebroids'] Let $\mathcal{X}$ be  a vector field on $E_{U}$.  The following properties are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[{\rm (i)}] There exists a vector field $X$ on $U$ such that  $(\mathcal{X},X)$ is a linear  local vector field on $E$.
\item[{\rm (ii)}]  When we consider $\mathcal{X}$ as a map from $\mathcal{F}(E_{U})$ to $\mathcal{F}(E_{U})$ then $\mathcal{X}(\mathcal{F}_L(E_{U}))\subset \mathcal{F}_L(E_{U})$ and $\mathcal{X}(\mathcal{F}_\pi(E_{U}))\subset \mathcal{F}_\pi(E_{U})$.
\item[{\rm (iii)}] The local flow $\mathfrak{F}_{\mathcal{X}}^t$ of $\mathcal{X}$ is a local bundle isomorphism for $E$ over the flow $\Fl_X^t$ of  $X$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.649159+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b51d044868765f89a23b463b5a1520d16c1b81ae3f19d82a16d4a256b78c8f85","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:logscale of arXiv:2606.05830, '{ Biased Random Walk on $\mathbb Z_+$ with Traps of Linearly Increasing Depth}\footnote{Su'] For $0<\lambda\ne 1,$ we have
