{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.973097+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b51d08d06c2b0dcdfd4515e15c1bd6ef8820b15457666cef34880cdd8654febe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sto of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] For every smooth, compactly supported $\omega:\R\rightarrow\R$, $P{\geqslant1}$, $\eta>0$ and $c>0$ sufficiently small, we have
