{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.902659+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b56a8ab9eeef23405b476698fa5429d07d4239131e7008cc5aba3703998c1a47","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:optimalweightoperator of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] Let $\varepsilon > 0$ and $\mathbf{X} \in \R^{d_1 \times d_2}$ be a matrix with the full singular value decomposition 
$\mathbf{X}= \mathbf{U}_{\mathbf{X}} \diag (\boldsymbol{\sigma}) \mathbf{V}_{\mathbf{X}}^\top$, 
