{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.034406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5c2f0342ff42266686019153cea6b995e321db8aff3044550c592c4562974ea","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 19 (Uniform-in-time first Malliavin derivative bounds) of arXiv:2605.03057, 'Uniform-in-time quantitative fluctuations of large scale interacting particle systems'] Let $p\in\left\{4,8\right\}$. Assume
Assumptions~\ref{ass:smooth}, \ref{ass:second-malliavin-uniform}(i),
\ref{ass:coeff-level-new}(i)(ii), and
\ref{ass:first-malliavin-uniform}. Then, there exists a constant
$C_p>0$ such that, for all $N\ge 1$, all $0\le s\le u$, and all
$i,j\in\left\{1,\dots,N\right\}$,
\begin{equation}

\E\left(
\norm{D_s^j X_u^{i,N}}^p
