{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.643760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b60d4b0c73a66a8e6fc2c3c8b539e2cff301a462fd2a6e73a5a528d53b0f54f8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop FKG phi4 of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] {GunaratnamPanagiotisPanisSeveroPhi42022} and [LammersOtt2021]}] 

Let $\Lambda \subset \mathbb Z^d$ be finite, $\beta\geq0$, $J\in (\mathbb R^+)^{E(\Lambda)}$, and $\mathsf{h}\in \mathbb R^\Lambda$. For any increasing and bounded functions $F,G:\mathbb{R}^\Lambda\to \mathbb{R}$,
