{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:23:25.634284+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6910a757c9ad027ebd1a791019bd99cb1a10dbf07c4313df11ae52cc2308604","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Inverse1 of arXiv:2609.01350, 'New classes of trace-form permutation polynomials and their compositional inverses'] Let $q=2^m$ with $m$ even, and let
$f_1(x)=x+\gamma{\rm Tr}_q^{q^2}(c_1x+c_2x^2+c_3x^3+x^{q+2})$,
$c_1,c_2,c_3,\gamma\in\mathbb F_{q^2}$, be a permutation polynomial of
$\mathbb F_{q^2}$. By Theorem~(Result1 of the paper), one of the following holds,
and in each case the compositional inverse is:
\begin{equation}
  f_1^{-1}(x)=
  \begin{cases}
    x
      & \text{if } \gamma=0,\\[0.6em]
    x+\dfrac{\gamma\,h_1(x)}{1+\gamma{\rm Tr}_q^{q^2}(c_1)}
      & \text{if } \gamma\in\mathbb F_q^*,\ c_3=1,\ {\rm Tr}_q^{q^2}(c_2)=0,\\[1em]
    x+\left(\dfrac{h_1(x)}{{\rm Tr}_q^{q^2}(c_2)}\right)^{q/2}
      & \text{if } \gamma\in\mathbb F_q^*,\ c_3=1,\ {\rm Tr}_q^{q^2}(c_2)\neq0.
  \end{cases}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.900154+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b69182dbc5559f2951196b60e3efb3f7b47ae56a477180547b86f12ba4cc8400","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 30 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Let $n \geq 1$ and $h_1,\ldots,h_n \in [H]$. The \emph{$n$-point correlator} is defined as \emph{joint cumulant} of the $n$ random variables $\Delta
