{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.670959+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7b8ec1c1adf43c96774d71a2002936821375fd3814659df2d11f7b84aaae284","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (transition density) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] On $(0,\infty)$, the Lebesgue density $f$ of the CIR process defined by \cref{eq-CIR4} solves
  \[
  \partial_t f = -\partial_u\!\left(\left(\tfrac{\delta-1}{\beta u}
    -\lambda u\right)f\right) + \tfrac{1}{\beta}\partial_{uu}f.
  \]
  If $p$ denotes the density with respect to the speed measure $m$,
  then at $u=0$ the sticky (Wentzell) boundary condition holds
  \begin{equation}

    \partial_s p(t,0^+) = \tfrac{1}{\mu}\,\partial_t p(t,0),
  \end{equation}
  where $\partial_s = (1/s')\partial_u$ is the scale derivative.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.473979+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7ba5adad4daf82cc1ff4f36dd1294ddd2973ad82d07ca0f38b957674bb077c1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:sharp-nonlinear-constant of arXiv:2606.21006, 'Law of the Iterated Logarithm for Weighted Sums of Functionals of Long-Memory Gaussian Seq'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~(thm:functional-nonlinear-lil of the paper),
\[
    \limsup_{n\to\infty}
