\end{equation}
Also, for any fixed $x \in \mathbb{R}$ (see equation (9.50) of [Bovier_book]), 
\begin{equation}
    C(f(x + \cdot), \alpha(\lambda)) = e^{\mu x}C(f, \alpha(\lambda)).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

