{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.270245+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8472d6d0996c821e1ad28a705991fffa8d02acbef29e0b6e9cd6754e28204f4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sa-slln of arXiv:2509.10225, 'Phase Transitions for Elephant Random Walks \\ with Two memory Channels'] For $p \neq 7/8$, $\boldsymbol{\Gamma}_n\stackrel{a.s.}{\to} \boldsymbol{\Gamma}^{(p)}$. For $p < 7/8$, $\boldsymbol{\Gamma}^{(p)}$ is degenerate at $\boldsymbol{\gamma}_0 := \begin{pmatrix} {1}/{3} & {1}/{3}\end{pmatrix}^{\top}$. For $p > 7/8$, $\boldsymbol{\Gamma}^{(p)}$ takes the values $\boldsymbol{\gamma}_p$ and $\widebar{\boldsymbol{\gamma}}_p$, where
