\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.167012+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b86ade954218c2190cabff1e55e70436845016383df48b1a80b6cd59fd4a0639","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Global Schauder estimate) of arXiv:2604.17973, 'Schauder estimates and classical solutions of the Dirichlet problem for stochastic parabol'] Let $G$ be a domain of class $C^{2+\alpha}$ in the standard sense, and let Assumptions~\ref{ass:compatibility}--\ref{ass:data} be satisfied. If $u$ is a quasi-classical solution of \eqref{eq:main}--\eqref{eq:boundary-initial}, then
