{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.720917+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b86e47e3c47a1ed3c8046fae52acdd98900e5d027714e79d1181222fbc4a54dc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 25 of arXiv:2511.13404, 'Asymptotic stability and mean ergodicity of Feller processes on Polish spaces'] Let $\mathfrak{F}\subset B(\X)$ be such that $L_b(\X)\subset \mathfrak{F}$ and satisfy Hypothesis $\mathbf{(H_1)}$. Suppose that $\Phi$ is Ces\`{a}ro equicontinuous w.r.t $\mathfrak{F}$ on $\X$, then the following statements are equivalent: 
