{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.638836+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b877efba7f0debe519155feab102685fe0480621b28c24b3bd1c836f3d753cf8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem from bR to bP of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] Let $\mathbf{R}, \rho_0,\rho_T, \mathfrak{f},\mathfrak{g},\mathfrak{h},$ be the same as above. Set $\displaystyle S_0:=\set{x\in \mathbb{R}^n:\frac{d\rho_0}{d\mathbf{R}_0}(x)=0}$ and define
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{P}:=\mathbbm{1}_{S_0^c}(X_0)\frac{d\rho_0}{d\mathbf{R}_0}(X_0)\mathbf{R}. 
    \end{equation}
 Then, $\mathbf{P}$ is a path measure with initial endpoint (i.e., $t=0$) distribution $\rho_0$, and the  solution to the dynamic SBP (equation Definition:DynamicSBP of the paper) has the representation: 
