{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.581973+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b87af07183faacf0264278e25dbdf9a3c6d43a5e58dcf5875be56873894768e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm MT_torus of arXiv:2411.09640, 'Random Lipschitz functions on graphs with weak expansion'] There is a constant $C$ for which the following holds. For any $\gamma >C$, if $k> \gamma M^2\log (Mn)$, then for $f$ chosen uniformly at random from $\mbox{\rm{Lip}}_{v_0}(C_{n,k};M)$,
