{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.706133+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b88aff9799d780d9ac0854c2ae55f7bea7684a44467a0c1618fb2db5d52a0694","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem law of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Let $\widetilde{X}^{[0,T]}$ be a CTSRW on the linear graph $\{0,\dots,T\}$ with edge transition rates equal to~$1$ starting from $T$ and denote by $\widetilde{L}_t$ its local time field at $T$-time $t$. Then, for any $t>0$, we have  
	\begin{equation}
		\left( \widetilde{L}_t(T-i) : i=0,\dots,T\right) \overset{d}{=} \left( Y_i : i=0,\dots,T\right), 
	\end{equation} where $Y=(Y_s)_{s \in [0,T]}$ is $\tfrac{1}{2}$ times a $0$-dimensional Bessel process starting from $2t$ (so that $Y_0=t$). In particular, the process $Y$ satisfies, for any Borel measurable function $\varphi : \mathbb R^{T+1} \to \mathbb R$, 
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb E\left( \varphi(Y_0,\dots,Y_T) ; Y_T \neq 0\right) = \mathbb E\left( \varphi(B_0^2,\dots,B_T^2) \sqrt{\frac{\sqrt{t}}{B_T} }\exp\left(-\frac{3}{16}\int_0^T B_s^{-2} {\rm d} s\right) ; \min_{s \in [0,T]} B_s > 0 \right)\,,
	\end{equation} where $(B_s)_{s \in [0,T]}$ is a Brownian motion starting from $\sqrt{t}$ with variance $\frac{1}{2}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:53.186540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b891dbfe164a70c3c9686ff12ee06e04bcfb80182d0321a4dc614c459a670199","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 33 of arXiv:2606.11758, '2606.11758'] Let \(d\in\mathfrak D_{\xi,n}^{\mathrm{osc}}\), and recall that
