{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.251047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8b9c3c600601cf9013c392660a0f89989daaf76e65f56c5c427ea4ccf40c9f0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2605.23222, 'On global solutions to the semidiscrete stochastic heat equation'] Let $\Omega' \in \Fc$ such that $Q(\Omega') = 1$ and $\theta_t(\Omega') = \Omega'$ for all $t \in \R$. A measurable map $Z: \Z^d \times \R \times \Omega' \to (0, \infty)$ is called a \emph{global stationary solution} to~\eqref{eq:sSHE} if: 
\begin{enumerate}
\item For every $y \in \Z^d$, $s, t \in \R$ with $s < t$, and $\omega \in \Omega'$, 
$$
Z(y,t,\omega) = \sum_{x \in \Z^d} Z(x,s,\omega) Z_{x,s}^{y,t}(\omega); 
$$
\item For every $y \in \Z^d$, $t \in \R$, and $\omega \in \Omega'$, one has $Z(y,t,\omega) = Z(y,0,\theta_t \omega)$; 
\item For every $y \in \Z^d$, the map $\omega \mapsto Z(y,0,\omega)$ is $(\Fc_{-\infty,0}^{'}, \Bc_0^{\infty})$-measurable, where $\Fc_{-\infty,0}^{'}$ is the restriction of $\sigma(W^x_u: u \leq 0, x \in \Z^d)$ to $\Omega'$ and where $\Bc_0^{\infty}$ is the Borel $\sigma$-field on $(0, \infty)$.  
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

