{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.972297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8bff718df5b37457580d688ee0c6c5f893a15025cb419b9df5827d1d1c7f390","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Let $\mu \in[0,1]$, $\tau_i \in \mathfrak{T}$, and $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_i} \in {\mcb{C}}[\tau_i]\,$ for $i = 1,2$. 
We can then write 
\[
