{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.327932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8d72f25d8398fdac6e01d0c574df1c3d5998bc8e4dc722cda60df767772cdcd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:heat_content_large of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Assume that $\phi$ satisfies (equation eq:Bernstein_cond of the paper) and $\Omega\subset\mathbb{G}$ is a bounded, open, connected subset. Then the first eigenvalue $\lambda_{1,\phi}$ of $\Delta^{\phi,\Omega}_{\mathcal H}$ is simple and admits an eigenfunction $f_\phi$ such that $f_\phi(x)>0$ for all $x\in\Omega$, and $\|f_\phi\|_{L^2(\mathbb G, dx)}=1$. Moreover, 
