{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.146758+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8e641b01893f8505e8df4997604a6bb4d4d76fe6f94cb95e44dab65cc491280","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 12 of arXiv:2604.13149, 'The Distributional Tail of Worst--Case Quickselect'] For every \(t>0\),
\begin{equation}
\PP{\Svar>t}
\le
\inf_{\theta>0}\exp\!\bigl(-\theta t+2e^\theta\bigr).
\end{equation}
In particular, for every \(t>2\),
\begin{equation}
\PP{\Svar>t}
\le
\exp\!\Bigl(-t\log(t/2)+t\Bigr)
=
\exp\!\Bigl(-t\log t+(1+\log 2)t\Bigr).
\end{equation}
Equivalently,
\begin{equation}
-\log \PP{\Svar>t}
\ge
t\log t-(1+\log 2)t,
\qquad t>2.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

