\end{align}
where $x^-=\max\{-x,0\}$ and $L_t^a(Z)$ denotes the local time of $Z$ at level $a$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:53:51.335083+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b9a8741cf527ed34e4f3ce6451007eb6fbc05a1770294d12dfe4d4210979adf4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:azgraph of arXiv:2605.03896, 'Dimer models on astroidal zig-zag graphs'] We call \(\mathsf G_{c, \mathsf f_0}\) an \emph{astroidal zig-zag graph} (AZ graph) if:
\begin{enumerate}
\item the medial cycle \(\partial \mathsf G_{c, \mathsf f_0}^\times\) is simple,
\item whenever a vertex of \({\mathsf{G}}\) is visited more than once as we go around \(\partial \mathsf G_{c, \mathsf f_0}\), all such visits occur consecutively along \(\partial \mathsf G_{c, \mathsf f_0}^\times\),
\item \(\mathsf G_{c, \mathsf f_0}\) is admissible.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

