{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.322002+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b9e5dc71bb709770eae21e9c31b78ad6526549950c9347376ef3c7453e1091a4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:higher_regularity of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] Suppose $f:[0,T]\times \mathbb T^3 \times \mathbb R^3 \to [0,1]$ is a weak solution to (equation e.LFD of the paper) with nonvacuum initial data in the sense of (d.nonvacuum of the paper) and an element of $L^\infty_m$ for some $m > 5$. Then, $f$ is a classical solution to (equation e.LFD of the paper). Moreover, for any fixed $k \in \mathbb N$, there is $m_0$ such that, if $m \geq m_k$, then
