    for any measurable function $f:[0,1]^2 \to \bbR_{>0}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.600737+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba20377f5a845c8d47ecb0bbc1578ba6d0b3aaf018856f1037f0f3a809140ca3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:homog of arXiv:2606.21049, '\textsc{Locality of rough path lifts}'] We say that an area process $\mathbb{A}$ on $P\subset C^\gamma \times C^\gamma$ is \emph{homogeneous}
