{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.970926+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba27997183a9b21160544cdfcd11434bbfb14135a5ec4997d142430550e80829","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lsdeter of arXiv:2606.15203, 'The existence of invariant sublinear expectations for $G\text{-}$SDEs'] Let $(P_{s,t}\varphi)(x)=E_P[\varphi( X_s^{t,x,\theta})]$. Then there exists a deterministic function  $\bar{\theta}_r$ and a diffusion process on $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, P)$,
