	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.132673+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba3a9fe83bc97732a4ed6706af9007abbce802d95ea5f4533e7a7ee675cb993e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2608.27500, 'Optimal Transport for Network Comparison: \\ A Review with Machine Learning Applications'] Let $G=(V,E)$ and $G'=(V,E')$ with $|V|=n$ be connected graphs. Then
    \begin{align*}
