{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.647268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba3d03c34d2364ae43d90c21df01ff6f25c4789b4c94f1890b5c4a56bfe41af8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-well-posedness of arXiv:2603.01823, 'on a fractional stochastic heat equation arising from the disordered pinning model'] Concerning the mild Skorohod solution to the SHE (equation e:she of the paper) in the sense of Definition~(def: solution of the paper), we have the following results:
\begin{enumerate}
\item When $\rho\in(0,2)$,  there exists no $L^p$-solution for any $p\ge2$; if  the solution to (equation e:she of the paper) is unique, then there exists no $L^p$-solution for any $p>1$.
\item When $\rho=2$, there exists a unique local $L^p$-solution but no global $L^p$-solution, for any $p>1$.
\item When $\rho\in(\frac{1}{2H-1},2]$, there exists a unique global $L^1$-solution.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.722592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba450563b3baf98ffc364c57dfe0b9cff940036b0b9f127cccbd4ab5b8064266","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2606.01944, 'Propagation of Chaos for Mean-field Mean Reflected Backward Stochastic Differential Equati'] For any $1\leq i\leq N$, set 
\begin{align*}
\hat{Y}^i:=Y^i-\bar{Y}^i, \ \hat{K}:=K^{(N)}-K,\ \hat{Z}^i:=Z^i-\bar{Z}^i.
