{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.339265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba7155e38e309972ad5f5f2915f4845dc6e73d1d52a4cd1827bce1fc846a4a2b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma I alpha elementary estimates of arXiv:2606.19207, 'Extrema of cooling branching Brownian motion and related Gaussian fields'] Fix $\alpha\in(0,1/2]$. For every $A>0$, there exists $C_A>0$
	such that, for every $t\geq1$,
	\begin{equation}
		I_\alpha(t)
		+
		A(1+\log(1+t))^{-2\alpha}
		\leq
		\int_0^{2\log(1+\sqrt{t})+C_A}
		(1+s)^{-2\alpha}\,\text{d} s .
	\end{equation}
	Moreover, for every $A>0$, there exist constants $C_A>0$ and
	$t_A\geq1$ such that, for every $t\geq t_A$,
	\begin{equation}
		I_\alpha(t)
		-
		A(1+\log(1+t))^{-2\alpha}
		\geq
		\int_0^{2\log(1+\sqrt{t})-C_A}
		(1+s)^{-2\alpha}\,\text{d} s .
	\end{equation}
	Finally, there exists $C>0$ such that
	\begin{equation}
		\int_0^L t\,I_\alpha'(t)\,\text{d} t
		\leq
		C\,L\,(1+\log(1+L))^{-2\alpha},
		\qquad L\geq1.
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.756167+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba72ef2879f7d533698d94907ff607b55bf20e155010c27a55cacd7692944c86","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 54 ({\cite{C70}*{Theorem 2}}) of arXiv:2609.03836, 'Koszul Orlik--Solomon Algebras from Non-supersolvable Arrangements'] A collection $\Fc$ of subsets (called ``blocks'') of the ground set of a matroid $M$ of rank $r$ is the set of rank $r$ flats of an erection of $M$ if and only if 
    \begin{enumerate}
