{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.816935+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baa6b7e2976d97982125d83ce18b0449377b47fd35f450fdb759787f159a907e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cond-lem of arXiv:2411.09516, 'Sharp Matrix Empirical Bernstein Inequalities\footnote{NeurIPS 2025 Poster}'] Let $\{ \mathbf{X} _n\}$ be an adapted sequence of $\mathcal{S}_d$-valued random matrices with conditional means $ \mathbb E  ( \mathbf{X} _n | \mathcal{F}_{n-1}) =  \mathbf{M} _n$. Further, suppose there is a predictable and integrable sequence of $\mathcal{S}_d$-valued random matrices $\{ \widehat  \mathbf{X} _n \}$ such that $\lambda_{\min}( \mathbf{X} _n - \widehat  \mathbf{X} _n ) \geqslant -1$. Let
