where $\mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_1$ and $\mathbb{B}^{\mathrm{br}}_2$ are correlated Brownian bridges given by (equation eq:defcd of the paper). (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.797716+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bab00033031286cf9f58ce379033c76d0650a35aa301e4fc0f77669e691a4a47","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:physical-coagulation-equation of arXiv:2608.05105, 'Cluster-Cluster model in $\mathbb{Z}^d$'] For \(\alpha\ge-1\) and every \(k\ge1\),
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
    c_k'(t)
    =\frac{1}{2d(t)}
      \sum_{i=1}^{k-1}K_\alpha(i,k-i)c_i(t)c_{k-i}(t) -\frac{c_k(t)}{d(t)}
      \sum_{j\ge1}K_\alpha(k,j)c_j(t),
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
with \(c_1(0)=1\) and \(c_k(0)=0\) for \(k\ge2\). Moreover,
\begin{equation}

    d'(t)=-\sum_{k\ge1}k^{-\alpha}c_k(t).
\end{equation}
Equivalently, the particle densities satisfy

\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
    V_k'(t)
    &=\frac{k}{2d(t)}\sum_{i=1}^{k-1}
      \frac{K_\alpha(i,k-i)}{i(k-i)}V_i(t)V_{k-i}(t) 
      -\frac{kV_k(t)}{d(t)}\sum_{j\ge1}  \frac{K_\alpha(k,j)}{k j} V_j(t).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.483138+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bab871297b6483a1039cd6158e0c27ff82eb22cbe094b3c544357a38adda12bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 39 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Fix $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$ and $z\in D$.
On the event $\{\ell_{0,b}(z) = b,\, 2\pi V_{A_{0,b}}(z)<\vert \log\varepsilon\vert\}$,
\begin{displaymath}
\PP(z\in \Ns_{\varepsilon}(A)\vert A_{0,b},\ell_{0,b}) =
\sum_{k=0}^{+\infty} (-1)^{k}
\dfrac{1}{2^{k} k! (k+1/2)}
\dfrac{\E[\psi_{2k+1, A} \vert A_{0,b},\ell_{0,b}](z)}{\big(\frac{1}{2\pi}\vert\log \varepsilon\vert\big)^{k + 1/2}}.
\end{displaymath}
On the event $\{\ell_{0,b}(z) = b, \CR(z,D\setminus A_{0,b})\in (\varepsilon,\varepsilon^{-1})\}$,
\begin{displaymath}
\PP(z\in \widetilde{\Ns}_{\varepsilon}(A)\vert A_{0,b},\ell_{0,b}) =
\sum_{k=0}^{+\infty} (-1)^{k}
\dfrac{1}{2^{k} k! (k+1/2)}
\dfrac{\E[\tilde{\psi}_{2k+1, A} \vert A_{0,b},\ell_{0,b}](z)}{\big(\frac{1}{2\pi}\vert\log \varepsilon\vert\big)^{k + 1/2}}.
\end{displaymath} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.571891+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bab8b7ddd67d18521f6f9ba9ee41a8599bf5adc6ff598dd23e108126a2240fba","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2606.14443, 'SEMICLASSICAL LIMIT OF POLYAKOV-LIOUVILLE MEASURE and Q-Curvature Uniformization ON EVEN-D'] Let $0<\gamma<\sqrt{2n}$. Then
