{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.812499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bad4f90c4b13f38d14e03ec9a4690b6616bdb4d45050ad1f1564d14fdc884699","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma mmn-variance-bound-light-traffic of arXiv:2504.02207, 'Finite-Time behaviors of M/M/$n$ Queue: Mixing Time, Mean Queue Length and Tail Bounds'] Let $\nu_n$ be the stationary distribution of the $M/M/n$ queue with arrival rate $\lambda_n \in (0,n)$ such that $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{\lambda_n}{n} = c$ for $c \in [0,1)$ and unit service rate, and let $X$ be a random variable that admits $\nu_n$ as the distribution, we have
