with our convention $z:=\frakm^k(x)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.861969+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baeac9e887e4ae49585c0ff2072e3a916a9be28333af059847f0f14e2b29e17e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $f$ be three times weakly differentiable with derivatives of polynomial growth. Let $\sigma$ and $\xi$ satisfy Assumption \ref{Aspt_new}. Let Assumption \ref{Ass:Half_Step} hold and let $\delta,h \in (0,1/2)$ such that $\frac Th \in \mathbb{N}$. Then there is a constant $C>0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
         \Bigl|\E\bigl[ f(Y_T)\bigr]-\E\bigl[f\bigl(\tiX_T^{h,(1),N,\delta}\bigr)\bigr]\Bigr|
        \lesssim 
        h + \delta^{1-}
        + \frac1{\sqrt{N}} \delta^{-1} 
        \exp\Bigl(\frac T2
        h^{-1} \log\bigl( C  \delta^{-1}h^{-1/2}\bigr)\Bigr).
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.439532+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baeb33216ae934d7b811d5f49b6b385e611d967d79c8208d563a9f2036d75922","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 21 of arXiv:2604.07370, 'Probabilistic Weyl law for twisted Toeplitz matrices with rough symbols'] Let $0<\A{1}\leq \A{2}\ll 1$ be such that there exists $\omega\in \hspace{0.1cm} ]0,1[$ such that 
    \begin{equation}
        N^{-\omega}\leq \pr{\alpha_1\alpha_2}^{1/2}.
    \end{equation}
    Let $p\in S(1,\A{1},\A{2})$. Then, as $N\to +\infty$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \norme{p_{N,\A{1},\A{2}}}\leq \sup_{\rho\in \mc{T}_{\A{1},\A{2}}}\bb{p(\rho)}+o(1).
    \end{equation*}
    In particular, there exists a constant $C>0$ independent of $N$, $\alpha_1$ and $\A{2}$ such that 
    \begin{equation*}
        \norme{p_{N,\A{1},\A{2}}}\leq C.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.029001+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baed613e33033ac3923abd0a098ab6ea962de804b8d6d678f1a69cf04c8bb279","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma untied-truncation-stability of arXiv:2609.03858, 'High-Dimensional Learning Dynamics of \\ Attention-Indexed Models'] Let \(\bar\mu\) be the admissible slow trajectory in
