{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.075395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb2772fa1de5df953e22a35f04f61cdb8ef4c0846c9b453446b798dff53db1c8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:bound-T_n-non-optimal of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Assume that all the variances in $\Lambda_n$ are unitary and all the other variances vanish. Then there exist some small enough universal constant $c_{1,2}>0$ such that
