    where $t_{\textup{mix}}^{(n),1}$ denotes the cutoff time for the corresponding $k = 1$ chain. Furthermore, for $k$ satisfying $\Omega(n) = k = n - \Omega(n)$, the chain exhibits cutoff around its mixing time $t_{\textup{mix}}^{(n),k}$, which is of the same order as the expressions in (equation eq:OrderkSteps of the paper). (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.868069+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb336c3d85a6258d29a12c1937314d497364e70bcc1c29c0be2f1de8df3952b9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2608.21255, 'Laws of the iterated logarithm for random Dirichlet series with general weights'] As $n\to\infty$,
