{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.322213+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb85ca62588c54cfd3b6cb5b0e9aa69198ef78dc359a8cedca9f337885215d22","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l.transformed_coefficients of arXiv:2608.31071, 'Global smooth solutions to the inhomogeneous Landau--Fermi--Dirac equation'] Consider any coefficients $\mathcal A$, $\mathcal B$, and $\mathcal C$ on $[0,T] \times \Omega \times \mathbb R^3$ satisfying~(equation defn:coercivity_assumption of the paper)-(equation defn:bounded_coefficient_assumption of the paper), and fix any $z_0 = (t_0,x_0,v_0) \in (0,T]\times B_1\times \mathbb R^3$. Then, $\overline \mathcal A$, $\overline \mathcal B$, and $\overline \mathcal C$, defined by~(equation eq:new_coefficients of the paper), satisfy~(equation eq:uniform_ellipticity of the paper) in $Q_2$ and, for any $m\geq 0$ and $z\in Q_2$,
