{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.432684+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bbd6fa2bf12eef161284bf0f2b388b7616c7eb27b09ba15f3b57380db8e744ba","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma threeeventsnsigma of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Let $A_n$ be as in Lemma (corollary3.6chap9 of the paper). Let $\Delta>0,\kappa>0$ and $\sigma\in(0,1)$ be fixed constants. Fix any $\lambda_1,\lambda_2\in[-(2-\kappa)\sqrt{n},(2-\kappa)\sqrt{n}]$ satisfying $|\lambda_1-\lambda_2|\geq\Delta n^{\sigma-\frac{1}{2}}$. Then \begin{enumerate}
