    Then, for all $n\in\N$, there exists a unique $p_{X_n}\in\pols_n(\C)$ satisfying \eqref{eq:poyperp} with $\kappa_n=\kappa$ and $p_{X_n}$ has only real, non-negative roots. 

    Moreover, the sequence $(\meas{p_{X_n}})_n$ converges weakly to some $\mu_{\X}\in\mathcal{M}(\R_{\ge0})$, which is uniquely determined by the free perpetuity fixed-point equation \eqref{eq:free_perp_admis}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

