{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.936712+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc8940e95b9b5b238e1788ab09a3e3e234978fab5d65568372b7f8221161bf6e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2607.17396, '2607.17396'] Let $\left\{X_{k},k\geq 0 \right\}$ be the critical branching processes with strictly stationary immigration. If $\mathbf{E}X_{0}^{2}<\infty$, $\sigma^{2}<\infty$ and $b^{2}<\infty$, then for all $k\geq 1$, we have
