{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.775920+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bcceae0a7456ec31f77109c6044746ee0ef3f42a0ccd87b4f16043a122d1b49d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:finiteLE of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] For any $\lambda > 0$, let $\mathcal{L}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},\lambda}_{n,\ell,r}$ denote the probability distribution
