{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.359852+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd256a12f9bdf7d07755ba956dbd52eda57a5d00a014cdab54ebcbe886c754f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem mainthm of arXiv:2605.16244, 'Analysis of a twisted Bose--Einstein Markov chain with applications to sampling Catalan st'] Fix $n \geq 2$. 
Let $K_{\mathrm{PF}}$ be the transition kernel of the Burnside process on $\mathrm{PF}_n$ and let $\pi_{\mathrm{PF}}$ be its stationary distribution. 
Then $\lambda_{2,\mathrm{PF}} = \lambda_2(K_{\mathrm{PF}}) = \frac{n}{2(n+1)}$, and for all $t\ge1$, 
