{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.705008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd403df260102355c3e0e3395bbd1e29a27d8a643302e8fab2f9a944c9d99c5d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 (Reference-compatible state lift) of arXiv:2609.02196, 'Schr\"odinger Bridges on Lie Group Manifolds for Probabilistic Intrinsic Generation'] If \(Q_i(\dd g\dd\bm\xi)=Q_i^\G(\dd g)Q_i(\dd\bm\xi\mid g)\) and \(\rho\ll Q_i^\G\), then the unique state law with group marginal \(\rho\) minimizing \(\KL(\cdot\|Q_i)\) is
