{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.440171+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd4d512b6f75759edfb52c8caf040e0f3d18a4b119da88975cec8dfa2787c49b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:Ucap of arXiv:2509.04155, 'An Approach to Sub-Gaussian Heat Kernel Estimates via Analysis on Metric Spaces'] Fix $p \geq 1$ let $\mathcal{F}_p$ and $\Gamma_p$ be as in (1)-(2) of Definition (def:SSS of the paper).
    For a given scale function $\Psi$, we say that the pair $(\mathcal{F}_p,\Gamma_p)$ satisfies the \emph{upper capacity estimate} (eq:UCap of the paper) if there are constants $C,\kappa > 1$ satisfying the following condition.
    For every $x \in X$ and $r \in (0,\diam(X))$ there is a cutoff function $\varphi \in \mathcal{F}_p$ for $B(x,r) \subseteq B(x,\kappa r)$ satisfying 
    \begin{equation}
        \tag{$\textup{Cap}_{p,\leq}(\Psi)$}
        \int_X \, d\Gamma_p\Span{\varphi} \leq C \frac{\mu(B(x,r))}{\Psi(x,r)}.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

