{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.317497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd6f007b9660026bd7aa8c45215810ffb9c87479adf408e599238dc8ede230d3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 ($L^r-$moment bound) of arXiv:2506.20789, 'Central limit theory for Peaks-over-Threshold partial sums of long memory linear time seri'] Let Assumptions~\ref{asu:coef},~\ref{asu:G_n} and~\ref{asu:f} hold. Then
  \[
  G_{\infty,n}'(0)
  \ := \
  \left.
  \frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}x}
  \EE[G_n(X_0+x)]
  \right|_{x=0}
  \]
is well-defined. Moreover, if $\gamma_G$ is such that there are $\gamma,r\in\RR$ satisfying
       \begin{align}

         \gamma_G
         \ < \
         \gamma
         \ < \
  \min \left\{
  \frac{d}{1-d}
  \,,
         1
          -
         \frac{1}{r(1-d)}
         \,,
         \frac{\alpha}{r}
