and
\[
g\in C_x^{1+\alpha}(\bar Q_T^+;L_\omega^\gamma(\elltwo)),
\qquad
g|_{\Sigma_T} = 0.
\]
Then
\begin{align}
|D_x^2u|_{(\alpha,\alpha/2);Q_T^+}^{L_\omega^\gamma}
\le C\Bigl(
|u|_{0;Q_T^+}^{L_\omega^\gamma}
+|f|_{\alpha;Q_T^+}^{L_\omega^\gamma}
+|f|_{(\alpha,\alpha/2);\Sigma_T}^{L_\omega^\gamma}
+|g|_{1+\alpha;Q_T^+}^{L_\omega^\gamma(\elltwo)}
\Bigr),
\end{align}
where $C$ depends only on $n$, $\alpha$, $\gamma$, $\kappa$, and $K$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.618792+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd94f217119bc47174aa77e6dde00f45e8804f11860c20c6091adc1c85a30818","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 163 (Differential and integral identities involving $\doublenulltoritwoarg{\ubar}{u}$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $f$ be a scalar function,
	and for 
