{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.853616+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bda909f91e6f6c6501b304d7077443ebd7299da44a3bdcfb0b7e70d7e83e6ad7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:approxmeasx_unif_bounded of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] The family $(\mu^{(a,\varepsilon)})_{\varepsilon>0}$ of measures on $(L, \mathcal{B}(L))$ is uniformly bounded for any $a\in (0,1)$. More precisely, it holds for all $\varepsilon>0$ that
