{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.963590+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bdb5797a6d415c35db14660cd6e598d4e7f8cbf0ee8b317adc5f17a80140cc70","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:perturbation-mat-bound of arXiv:2506.23062, 'Shifted Composition IV\@: \\ Toward Ballistic Acceleration for Log-Concave Sampling'] For any $c > 0$, if $h\lesssim \gamma^{-1} \wedge {\gamma/\beta}$ and $c_0\lesssim A$ for sufficiently small absolute constants depending only on $c$, then
