{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.726227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be397ad4ed06cc7982fde8c598faccd9f216adbbe6e1b7d2d9a92f9299521f72","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 (Compact reduction and path-law pushforward) of arXiv:2609.02196, 'Schr\"odinger Bridges on Lie Group Manifolds for Probabilistic Intrinsic Generation'] Under the reduced-representation assumption in Appendix~\ref{app:reduction-details}, the stochastic learning problem is an RCCBM problem on \(\G_{\rm red}\). If the reconstruction is a \(C^2\)-diffeomorphism onto the modeled conformation manifold, the induced path map preserves relative entropy,
