{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.903409+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be422282fc56a9c3d91c133f91fbe23eb758637007b183bcd5c9d81c8914960b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 55 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Suppose that Assumptions~\ref{Assumptions_Theta} and \ref{Assumptions_basic} hold.
 Then the equilibrium measure $\mu$ has a compact
 support, \textit{i.e.} its support is inside $[-D,D]$ with $D>0$ depending only on the constants in the assumptions. Moreover, there exists an $H$-tuple of constants $\boldsymbol{v}$ such that for any $h \in [H]$ and $x \in [\hat{a}'_h,\hat{b}_h']$, we have
