{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.023709+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be47cff8aefb4fc82cbc601f6d7ba3c761d523dcea5157d78e28b678fccf3d5f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:minimum of arXiv:2609.03858, 'High-Dimensional Learning Dynamics of \\ Attention-Indexed Models'] Let $\mathcal{K} \subseteq \{1, 2, \dots, K\}$ denote the index set of the learnable weights, while the remaining weights $\{S^k_{ij}\}_{k \notin \mathcal{K}}$ are fixed and satisfy the condition $\lim_{d\to\infty} \|S^k_{ij}\|_{\text{op}} / \|S^k_{ij}\|_F = 0$. Define the order parameter set $Q$ as
