{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.852120+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be5f1b37d1d2b92e6cfa124e7684a09ecca9c63d813d95d006079a29fb4f994a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 (Bulk, real Wishart) of arXiv:2511.12623, 'The eigenvector bead process'] We recall Convention~\ref{conv:inverse-stieltjes-branches}. 
Fix $E \in \bigl((1-\sqrt{q})^2,(1+\sqrt{q})^2\bigr)$ and define the anchor index
\[
i_N(E) \;:=\; \min\bigl\{\,k \in \{1,\dots,N\}\ :\ \lambda^{(N)}_{k} \ge E\,T\,\bigr\}.
\]
We recall the notation for the Marčenko–Pastur density $\rho_{\mathrm{MP}}$ (see Equation~\ref{eq:MP-law}).
Then the overlaps satisfy
\begin{equation}
\Omega^{(N)}_{\,i_N(E)+u,\;i_N(E)+v}
\;\mathrel{\underset{N\to\infty}{\overset{d}{\sim}}}\;
\frac{g_v}{\,S_{\mu,\,g^2}^{-1}(h)_u - \mu_v\,}\,
\sqrt{\bigl(S_{\mu,\,g^2}^{-1}\bigr)'(h)_u},
\qquad 
h
\;=\;
-\,\frac{E + q - 1}{2E}
\cdot
\frac{1}{2\pi\rho_{\mathrm{MP}}(E)}\,.
\end{equation}

\noindent
Here $(\mu_u)_{u \in \mathbb{Z}}$ follows the sine\(_1\) point process, 
and $(g_u)_{u \in \mathbb{Z}}$ are i.i.d.\ real Gaussian random variables 
$g_u \sim \mathcal{N}(0,1)$, independent of $(\mu_u)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.091762+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be631392b4aa11bd1cc31f6eaddbc1a417021a9e502efb38f0d5a748ab849ee1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm1.2 of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] Consider FBSDE (equation 2.1 of the paper)--(equation 2.2 of the paper) such that $b$ and $g$ satisfy Assumptions (assum2.1 of the paper) and the terminal value $\xi$ has the following structure
