{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:10.034583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be8c88480b0d2017a8db52f8544cc92925f214085b2f74f14f549d2e332faf1d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2506.09609, 'Schramm-Loewner evolution contains a topological Sierpi\'nski carpet when $\kappa$ is clos'] Suppose that all vertices $z \in a_{\mathsf m} \mathbb{Z}^2 \cap \mathscr{L}_R$ are nice $a_{\mathsf m}$-vertices. Then, we can find a sequence of vertex subsets $\{\mathcal{A}_m\}_{0 \leq m \leq \mathsf m - 1}$ satisfying:
    \begin{enumerate}[(I)]
