{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.499726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bee2d46e85bb2c88558afd2c0b4d603414e20e548b205d0e3d68f41ece308785","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 14 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $X \in C^1([0,T],V)$ be a smooth path. We consider $\mathbf{X} = (X,\bbx)$, where $\bbx : [0,T]^2 \to V \otimes V$ is defined as
