{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.638290+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf0f0e5021d871261b4437e98206210ab2e6e671779ccc4908c56839f207c3cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem Theorem:ProductRule of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] Let $L$ be the jump-diffusion operator defined in (equation ReferenceGenerator of the paper), $h$ be a non-negative function of class $C^{1,2}$ on $[0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^n$, and $\mathcal A_h$ be as in (equation definition_A_h of the paper). Define, for every $(t,x)\in \mathcal A_h$, 
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned} b^h(t,x):=b(t,x)& +\sigma\sigma^T\nabla
 \log h(t,x)+ \\
 & \int_{|z|\leq 1} \frac{h(t,x+\gamma(t,x,z))-h(t,x)}{h(t,x)}\gamma(t,x,z)\nu(dz),
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \nu^h(t,x;dz) :=  \frac{h(t,x+\gamma(t,x,z))}{h(t,x)}\nu(dz).
\end{equation}
Then for every $f\in C^{1,2}(\mathbb{R}^+\times \mathbb{R}^n)$, at $(t,x)\in \mathcal A_h$, \begin{equation*}
    L(hf)(t,x)=\left (h\tilde{L}f+fLh\right ) (t,x),
\end{equation*}
where $\tilde{L}$ is the operator defined in (equation ReferenceGenerator of the paper) with $b$ replaced by $b^h$, and $\nu$ replaced by $\nu^h$. 
Equivalently, writing $\tilde{{\mathfrak L}}:=\frac{\partial}{\partial t}+\tilde{L}$, at $(t,x)\in \mathcal A_h$, 
\begin{equation}
    {\mathfrak L}(hf) (t,x) =\left(h\tilde{{\mathfrak L}}f+f{\mathfrak L} h\right)(t,x).
\end{equation}
In particular, if $h$ is harmonic, then $$\tilde{{\mathfrak L}}f=\frac{1}{h}{\mathfrak L}(hf)={\mathfrak L}^hf\text{ and }L^hf=\tilde{L}f\text{ on }\mathcal A_h.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.284081+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf0fd0a2331ac9c362321127eeded9372784a3364277946e6aad017d89d2a641","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:good_approximation of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Suppose that we have the setup above where $\mathcal {L}$ is the outermost loop of $\Gamma_\mathbf{D}$ that surrounds~$0$. Suppose that $\metapprox{\epsilon}{\cdot}{\cdot}{\Gamma}$ is an approximate ${\rm CLE}_{\kappa'}${} metric for each $\epsilon \in {(0,1]}$ with respect to the same constants $c_{\mathrm{s}} \ge 0$, $c_{\mathrm{p}}(N) > 0$. We say that $(\metapprox{\epsilon}{\cdot}{\cdot}{\Gamma})_{\epsilon \in {(0,1]}}$ is a \emph{good approximation scheme} if there exists a constant $\mathbf{a}_{\epsilon} > 0$ for each $\epsilon \in {(0,1]}$ and a constant $a_0 > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \lim_{\epsilon \searrow 0} \frac{\mathbf{a}_{\epsilon}}{\epsilon^{a_0}\median{\epsilon}} = 0
\end{equation}
and for each $r>0$ we have
\begin{equation}
 \lim_{\epsilon \searrow 0} \mathbf{P}\left[ \sup_{V \in \metregions} \sup_{\substack{\dpath[\overline{V}](x,y) < \epsilon ,\\ \dpath(x, \Upsilon_\Gamma \setminus \overline{V}) \ge r}} \metapproxres{\epsilon}{V}{x}{y}{\Gamma} \le \mathbf{a}_{\epsilon} \right] = 1 .
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:15:46.817231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf114d9804be06220b8bc696bce8f5eca1afa40f9c5b0721d70ceb941cd43a2c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2609.02808 (conjecture environment labelled conjecture).] Let $k\ge2$ and let $g\in\overline{\Cc}$ minimize $f_k$. Let
