{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.238076+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf2956af4e517bbe20e2afc7c16d710b486720b0b418ff267b2682bdf148fd77","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:self_scaling_convergence of arXiv:2608.29448, '\method: Self-Scaled Adaptive Preconditioning for Physics-Informed Learning'] Let \(S_k=W_k-W_{k-1}\), \(Y_k=\nabla \mathcal{L}(W_k)-\nabla \mathcal{L}(W_{k-1})\), and let
\(K_k\succ 0\) denote the Kronecker metric whose quadratic form is $s_k^\top K_k s_k = \operatorname{Tr}\!\left(S_k^\top L_k^{-1}S_kR_k^{-1}\right)$, where \(s_k=\operatorname{vec}(S_k)\). Assume \(s_k\neq 0\) and
\(s_k^\top y_k>0\). Define $a_k=s_k^\top K_k s_k$ and $c_k=s_k^\top y_k$. Then the scaling factor
\begin{align*}
\tau_k
=
\min\left\{
1,
\frac{c_k}{a_k}
\right\}
=
\min\left\{
1,
\frac{s_k^\top y_k}{s_k^\top K_k s_k}
\right\}
\end{align*}
is the unique solution of the clipped one-dimensional log-secant matching
problem
\begin{align*}
\tau_k
=
\arg\min_{0<\tau\le 1}
\left[
\log
\frac{s_k^\top y_k}
{s_k^\top(\tau K_k)s_k}
\right]^2 .
\end{align*}

If \(y_k=H_ks_k+r_k\), then, whenever the unclipped solution is active,
the scaled Kronecker quadratic form satisfies $s_k^\top(\tau_kK_k)s_k = s_k^\top H_ks_k+s_k^\top r_k$. Thus the mismatch between the scaled Kronecker secant energy and the true
directional curvature is exactly the directional secant error \(s_k^\top r_k\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

