{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.907306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf7602743b13de456890c126685d5e7f193b58399fb4a89dcd1f7febf2c6594d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:powermean of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] For $-\infty \leq q \leq \infty$, the \emph{$q$-power mean} \\ $\mathcal{M}_{q}(a,b)$ of two numbers $a, b > 0$ is given by
	\begin{equation} 
		\mathcal{M}_{q}(a,b) = 
		\begin{cases}
			\min(a,b), & \text{ if } q = -\infty, \\
			\left(\frac{ a^q + b^q }{2}\right)^{\frac{1}{q}}, & \text{ if } q \in (-\infty,0) \cup (0,\infty), \\
			\sqrt{a b}, & \text{ if } q = 0, \\
			\max(a,b), & \text{ if } q = \infty. \\
		\end{cases}
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.711672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf7e633ae549c825c2e889c0530de6c7ec4ef64e482a609409c0d39045d40281","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 (Relaxation) of arXiv:2608.06317, 'Sharp Tail Bounds Beyond Twice the Mean'] For $n\in\N_0$ and $t\in\R$,
