{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.849058+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf89b191d9bfdb4da069927c73aa645d13499339fc61ca9f6485d7f06a8ff5e7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem burnIn:XtDtBoundedImpliesYtBounded of arXiv:2607.09841, 'Mixing and cutoff for the systematic scan dynamics of the mean-field ferromagnetic Potts m'] Suppose that for some integer $k\geq0$, a fixed constant $a \in (1/q, 1]$, and a sufficiently small $\varepsilon > 0$ that satisfies $G_{\beta,n}(a) + 2\varepsilon < a$, we have
