{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:14.935247+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf89e883cc685cc3ecb7e16a42d1107ebf0d6ab247abfbd4efece57beba42f9b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2607.11756, 'Full replica symmetry breaking in the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick model'] For every $\nu\in\Pr([0,1])$, the solution $u_\nu$ is even in $x$;
