{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.962588+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0090bc38f1c0d7327042a0c43397e77acb32d630e8a9ebbf6c0f005492b2360","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 (Uniform Smoluchowski--Kramers approximation) of arXiv:2604.00692, 'Uniform-in-time diffusion approximations for multiscale stochastic systems'] Assume {\bf (A$^\beta_{\rm SK}$)}. Let $\gamma\in(\beta,2)$, $\alpha\in(0,1]$, and let $(\rho_0,\omega_0)\in \sW_d\times \sW_d$. Then there exists a weight $\varrho\in \sW_{2d}$ such that, for every $\varphi\in \bC^\alpha_{\rho_0}\bC^\gamma_{\omega_0}$,   $\eps\in(0,1)$ and all $t\geq0$,
\begin{equation}
\Big|\mE\big[\varphi(Z_t^\eps(z))\big]-\bar\cT_t\bar\varphi(y)\Big|
\leq
\varrho(z)\Big(
\eps^\beta\|\varphi\|_{\bC^\alpha_{\rho_0}\bC^\gamma_{\omega_0}}
+
\e^{-\kappa_0 t/\eps^2}
\|\varphi-\bar\varphi\|_{\bC^0_{\rho_0}\bC^0_{\omega_0}}
\Big),
\end{equation}
where
\[
\bar\varphi(y):=\mu_y(\varphi(\cdot,y)),
\qquad
\bar\cT_t\bar\varphi(y):=\mE\big[\bar\varphi(\bar Y_t(y))\big],
\]
$\mu_y=\sN(0,\Sigma(y))$ is given by Lemma~\ref{lem:frozen-generalA}, and $\bar Y$ solves \eqref{eq:effective-SK-generalA}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.889831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c00f3b0d1eba249fd3d3175878fea9911b97a66453eca15295462154a04a8c51","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2608.29554, 'Limiting Behavior of a Class of Hermitian Yang--Mills Metrics, II: Exponential Approximati'] There exist constants $c>0$ and $\epsilon_0>0$, independent of
