{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.431311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c04196459bfa5d478c832bea708f3d9d3c6503eddae9df60191fcdb41958d8ab","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:sdp.factorized of arXiv:2604.22453, 'Adapted Wasserstein Barycenters of Gaussian Processes'] For every $t\in[T]$,
\begin{equation}

\min_{\mathbf P_t\in\mathscr{P}_+(K,d)}\Phi_t(\mathbf P_t)
=
\min
\left\{
\sum_{k=1}^K\lambda_k\bigl\|L_{\cdot,t}^k\mathbf M^k-\mathbf Y\bigr\|_F^2
\right\},
\end{equation}
where the minimum on the right-hand side is taken over
\[
\mathbf Y\in\mathbb{R}^{Td\times Kd},\qquad
\mathbf M^k\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times Kd},\qquad
\mathbf M^k(\mathbf M^k)^\intercal=I_d,\qquad k\in[K].
\]
The two problems are related by $\mathbf P_t=\mathbf M\mathbf M^\intercal$, where $\mathbf M\in\mathbb{R}^{Kd\times Kd}$ stacks the block rows $\mathbf M^1,\ldots,\mathbf M^K$; this correspondence is onto $\mathscr{P}_+(K,d)$.  For fixed $\mathbf M^1,\ldots,\mathbf M^K$, the inner minimum over $\mathbf Y$ is attained uniquely at
\begin{equation}

\mathbf Y=\sum_{k=1}^K\lambda_kL_{\cdot,t}^k\mathbf M^k=\mathbf L_{\cdot,t}\Lambda\mathbf M,
\end{equation}
which has zero block rows before time $t$.  Requiring in addition that the row spaces of $\mathbf M^1,\ldots,\mathbf M^K$ coincide with a fixed $d$-dimensional subspace, equivalently $\rank(\mathbf P_t)=d$, recovers the restricted local problem (equation eq:local.restricted.factor.problem of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

