{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.821059+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0474c1d5d7708b4bdafe84495d2ae91bc55bdb9d4fcb5d392ba957fa4d6c2b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2607.24640, 'The Yang-Mills measure on surfaces via Morse theory'] With the above conventions, one has, for every approximable currents $\mathbf{T}_1$ and $\mathbf{T}_2$ and for every $\psi\in L^\infty(\Sigma)$, 
