{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:54:27.994788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c07d414d6ca05ec43b5886f6a4a264591a59e1d315ad60a1c213271905790d7a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem k1k1LIinftythm of arXiv:2608.04730, 'A new look at some aspects of one-dimensional random sequential adsorption and its continu'] Let $m_{k_1,k_2;I}$ be as in Theorem (k1k2Ithm of the paper). Then for $L\in (1,2]$,
