{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.586424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0b4f4c1527dc2dff58027618402c9698f95ecd204920397f908ac463173a3d6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop intro-prop-1 of arXiv:2608.30518, 'Grow-up rates of inhomogeneous semilinear heat equations in the critical dimension'] Let $N\ge 3$ and $\lambda=\lambda^{*}$. Assume that (equation katei-f of the paper), $u_0\in C^{0}(\overline{B_1})$ and $\varphi_0\le u_0\le u^{*}$ in $B_1$. 
