{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.639467+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0d8fcf17eddc7b09cc30ec6f79f902468f3fba7d18e80a5ff4a7c2632430281","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Theorem:DualOperator-L* of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] Assume $L$ is a jump-diffusion operator given by (equation ReferenceGenerator of the paper) with coefficients satisfying the Assumptions \textup{(Assumptions-(C) of the paper)}. Then, the $L^2([0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^n)$-adjoint operator $L^*: C^{\infty}_0 \to C^{\infty}_b$ is well defined, and for every $f\in C_c^\infty([0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^n)$ and $(t,x)\in[0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^n$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
     L^*f(t,x)&:= -\nabla \cdot (bf) (t,x)+\frac{1}{2} \sum_{i,j}\frac{\partial^2[(\sigma\sigma^T)_{ij}f]}{\partial x_i \partial x_j}(t,x) \\
    &\;+\int_{\mathbb{R}^\ell} \left[\det \nabla\phi_{t,z}^{-1}(x)f(t,\phi_{t,z}^{-1}(x))-f(t,x) +\mathbbm{1}_{|z|\leq 1}\nabla\cdot (\gamma f)(t,x,z) \right]\nu(dz),
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where $\det \nabla\phi_{t,z}^{-1}$ is the Jacobian determinant of $\phi_{t,z}^{-1}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.266094+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0e50ff7149687ddd0aa5cfc7b33c6b07f0c38d596abdb15f4f1bab455bbcbd0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma S32L of arXiv:2410.23899, 'Tightness for interlacing geometric random walk bridges'] Fix $p, M\in (0, \infty)$. There exists $N_2 \in \mathbb{N}$, depending on $p$ and $M$, such that the following holds. If $M_1, M_2 \in \mathbb{R}$ are such that $|M_1 - M_2| \leq M$, $n \geq N_2$, $x, y \in \mathbb{Z}$ are such that $x \leq y$ and $x \geq M_1 n^{1/2}$, $y \geq pn + M_2 n^{1/2}$, $g: \llbracket 0, n \rrbracket \rightarrow [-\infty, \infty)$ is arbitrary such that $\Omega_{\mathsf{Inter}}(0,n,x,y, \infty, g) \neq \emptyset$, and $s \in [0, n]$, then we have
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{Inter}, \operatorname{Geom}}^{0,n, x, y, \infty, g} \left( Q_1(s) \geq \frac{n - s}{n} \cdot M_1 n^{1/2} + \frac{s}{n} \cdot (pn + M_2 n^{1/2}) - 3n^{1/4} \right) \geq \frac{1}{3}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

