{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.465777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c14944f7f9d248aaa33b9a4ea91138bb7a02c61f98be0b6a00fff60808e60a0c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3G of arXiv:2411.16572, 'Optimal decay of eigenvector overlap for non-Hermitian random matrices'] Fix small constants $\epsilon,\tau>0$. For any deterministic matrices $\|A_1\|+\|A_2\| \lesssim 1$ and vectors $\|{\bm x}\|, \|{\bm y}\| \lesssim 1$, the following holds
