			addition $w \in C^{k}$ and $f \in C^{k}$ then
			$\rho_{w}[f] \in C^{k}$, and if $w(1-z) = w(z)$ and $f$ is symmetric
			about $m$ then so is $\rho_{w}[f]$; in particular
			$\rho_{w}(\mathcal{D}_{+}) \subseteq \mathcal{D}_{+}$ for the three
			type kernels;
