{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.185417+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c184a3d3ca828177bb71026d065c03ee0ffb8042d30300541873b08ce3814ede","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ExitCentre of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Let $k \geqslant 2$, and suppose that the chain starts from a configuration $\eta \in {\mathrm{Centre}((k-1)C)}$. Let $\tau_{{\mathrm{Centre}(kC)}^{\mathsf{c}}}$ be the time it takes to exit ${\mathrm{Centre}(kC)}$. Then there exist constants $c_1, C_1 > 0$, depending only on $d$ and $m$, such that for any fixed $C > 0$ and all $\varepsilon > 0$,
