{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.050765+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1e5245e215cb0e1f38d2b123efe63be00d6fbb6f54e3dd3528201a874f652cc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2606.16164, 'A Low-Regularity Semigroup Sewing Lemma via Quotient Structures'] Set $\gamma\in(0,1]$, $\alpha\in\mathbb{R}$, and $\tau\in[0,T]$. Let  $h\in Z\hat C^{\gamma}(\Delta_T^3;B_\alpha)$ and define $h^\tau$ by \eqref{eq:frozen-defect}. Then
\begin{equation}
h^\tau \in ZC^{\gamma}(\Delta_\tau^3;B_\alpha) \quad \text{and} \quad \|h^\tau\|_{\gamma,\alpha;\tau}
\le
M_{\alpha,T}\|h\|_{\gamma,\alpha}.
\end{equation}
Furthermore, if $\gamma\in(0,1)$ and $R\in E^{\gamma}(\Delta_T^2; B_\alpha)$, then $\Theta_\tau R \in F^{\gamma}(\Delta_\tau^2; B_\alpha)$
and for every $0<\varepsilon<\gamma$,
\[\|\Theta_\tau R\|_{\gamma-\varepsilon,\alpha+\varepsilon;\tau}\le M_{\alpha+\varepsilon,T}\|R\|_{\gamma-\varepsilon,\alpha+\varepsilon};\]
if $R\in E_{\log}^{1}(\Delta_T^2; B_\alpha)$, then $\Theta_\tau R \in F_{\log}^{1}(\Delta_\tau^2; B_\alpha)$ and for every $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$,
\[\|\Theta_\tau R\|_{1-\varepsilon,\alpha+\varepsilon;\tau}\le M_{\alpha+\varepsilon,T}\|R\|_{1-\varepsilon,\alpha+\varepsilon},\]
while $\|\Theta_\tau R\|_{1,\log;\tau,\alpha}\le M_{\alpha,T} \|R\|_{1,\log;\alpha}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.701404+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1e957290b0052869ec7f355fa5ce9389e2eaa4b28bbfd12f432cb26221222c0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:LTtoZhardcore of arXiv:2411.18563, 'Lower tails for triangles inside the critical window'] Suppose $p\in[0,1]$ and set $\lambda = p/(1-p)$. Then
