{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.580808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c22ba59e64ef0ad3a65404de9f94028c8561dfc46a754477092abde69fe498ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition propboundbdependent of arXiv:2608.30443, 'On smooth holosphere solutions to compressible Euler equation'] There exist universal constants $c_{\nu,a}>0$ and $0<b^*\ll 1$ such that the following holds for all $0<b<b^*$.
