{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.828827+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c25ed6ec0dd68f2c60761aae5c201c9ab9b005c41878a8eb3475337e519cc687","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop fD-L of arXiv:2609.01751, 'Orthogonal polynomials which are eigenfunctions of a partial differential operator'] An orthogonal basis of ${\mathcal V}_n\big({\mathbb R}_\Sigma^d, {\bm W}_{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}^\Sigma\big)$ is given by 
\begin{equation} 
  \hat {\bm L}_{{\bm j},m}^{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}({\bm y}) := 
      {\bm L}_{{\bm j},m}^{\boldsymbol{\kappa}} (y_1,\ldots, y_{d-1}, |{\bm y}|), \qquad |{\bm j}|= n.
\end{equation}
Moreover, the polynomials in ${\mathcal V}_n\big({\mathbb R}_\Sigma^d, {\bm W}_{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}^\Sigma\big)$ are eigenfunctions of ${\mathfrak D}_{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}^\Sigma$ defined by
\begin{align}
{\mathfrak D}_{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}^\Sigma = \sum_{i=1}^d \left(y_i \partial_i^2 + ({\kappa}_i + 1 - y_i) \partial_i \right)  \,& + 2|{\bm y}| \partial_{y_d}^2   - 2 {\langle} {\bm y}, \nabla_{\bm y} {\rangle} \partial_{y_d}\\
  & - (|{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}|-{\kappa}_d +d-1) \partial_{y_d},\notag
\end{align} 
and the eigen equation is given by 
\begin{equation}
   {\mathfrak D}_{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}^\Sigma \, u = - n u, \qquad \forall u \in {\mathcal V}_n\big({\mathbb R}_\Sigma^d, {\bm W}_{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}^\Sigma\big). 
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.854407+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c25f4c143eaed7363dcbd79bddf43c88010f2fbc04585c21334b793b021a65d5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_NN20 of arXiv:2607.11469, 'Breuer-Major-Donsker invariance principle'] Let $(Y_n)_{n\geq 1}$ be a sequence of random elements 
