{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:15:46.799091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c297506e97ef9ff4fcd39d04dc6494170c03e4900415f418a73dc0dd6616d3f7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2607.02406, 'On the range of competing random walks' (conjecture environment).] If $X^1,\dots,X^N$ are in the domain of attraction of a $\beta$-stable process $U$ with scale function $b(n)$ and that $d/\beta<1$, then 
