{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.898461+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2d45abe4c11db6f7a2cfd3885f4e95fa1ee12af8b808b86318189a33cf42163","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 11 of arXiv:2606.19925, 'Asymptotic properties for fully coupled delayed forward-backward stochastic differential e'] Assume that conditions $({\bf A1})$-$({\bf A3})$ are satisfied. Then, the family $(Y^{\varepsilon,t,x}(.))_{0<\varepsilon<1})$ satisfy, as $\varepsilon$ goes to $0$, a large deviation principle with a rate function
