{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.388303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c33fd1005f1281ff9c118ccfb65857a1649667f996d7cd7bc4c2b9d3263123c5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def-green of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] We define the \textbf{Green's function for random walk on $\mathcal G$ reflected off of $\infty$ and killed upon hitting $\mathcal A$} by 
