{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.325915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c36f6d2eb24a728313c023a818ceb6470209649a4bc2bb97a97ae9b2e18309b1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:LaCroix-Gaussian-realization of arXiv:2609.03532, 'Airy limit for the Jack process and topological expansion'] For every $N\in\mathbb Z_{\geq1}$ and $b>-1$,
