{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.238841+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c3b1c6d90530cebadcf875b07f1f2e26e3f0db324c4586628624bd3554d5d81c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: renormalized cost fcn of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] Let $T>0$. The \emph{renormalized cost function} is the map given, for every $u \in \mathbb H$, by
