{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.991821+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c3c9523b08f7baa25f8497302dc9b5dc8732c5cd26eb1b71cce5cffb2db4bac7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 114 (Bernstein's Inequality) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $X_1, \ldots, X_m$ be i.i.d.\ random variables with $|X_i| \leq K$ almost surely, mean $\xi$ and variance $\sigma^2$. Then for $S_m = \sum_{i=1}^n X_i$ and any $\delta > 0$, we have
