{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.414220+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c422acdea54f7548d4c50e94a6b7af8a1a373fdaaf616219bc423169c0e4baa8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma W_ratio_big_extraction of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] There exists an absolute constant $c_1=c_1(q,\kappa)>0$ not depending on the size of the hexagon, such that for all $T,S,N,t$ and points
