{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.025226+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4576cf814ab5f9abe1cc8f8c0b850374885fdf7bebe682fb3a83f4639efb754","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo thm:frostman-intro of arXiv:2512.06984, 'Infinite Dimensional Multifractal Analysis of the Wiener measure'] Let $ (X,d) $ be a $\sigma$-compact metric space and $ A \subset X$ a Borel subset. Then for every Hausdorff function $h$  such that $\mathcal{H}^h(A) > 0 $, there exist a compact set $K\subset A$,
