    \]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.635575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c45a3da32fb3a88d03bc05ea52f2fb29e1cdcac1bc36588d5aef719f7e0e877c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cluster size restricted of arXiv:2512.12124, 'A discontinuous percolation phase transition on the hierarchical lattice'] Let $J$ be an isometry-invariant, integrable, and regular kernel on $\mathbb{H}^1_L$. If the infinite cluster density $\theta \coloneqq \mathbb{P}_{J} \left( |K_0| = \infty \right)$ is positive then 
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathbb{P}_{J} \left( |K_{\max}(\Lambda_n)| \geq (\theta -\varepsilon)|\Lambda_n| \right) \underset{n\to \infty}{\longrightarrow} 1 
