{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.446806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c45ee132cc96e95845e48a66d0f8d31639e675f84db7e0df1cb3ef124c09e680","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:g-fun of arXiv:2601.10568, 'Hydrodynamic Limit with a Weierstrass-type result'] For each $x\in\mathbb{T}_N$ fixed and every $t\in [0,T]$, let $\varphi:[0,T]\times \mathbb{T}_N\to\mathbb{R}$ be such that $M_{t,\varphi}\equiv\int_0^t\norm{\varphi(s,\cdot)}_{\infty}\mathrm{d} s<\infty$. It holds that
