{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.309082+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4750d273544f603b37db81e59ec4ea933245a99d21ff5530e05ce761e4983c0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:generatorXt of arXiv:2411.14876, 'Limit theorems for stochastic exponentials of matrix-valued L\'evy processes \\'] Let $L=(L_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a Lévy process in $\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$ with characteristics $(\Sigma_L,\gamma_L,  \nu_L)$ fulfilling (equation eq-nonsingular of the paper), and let $X=(X_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be its stochastic exponential. Then $X$ is a rich Feller process in $\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$ and  its extended generator is given by
		\begin{align*}\mathcal{A}_{X} f(x) &= \sum_{i,j=1}^d \ell(x)^{(i,j)} \frac{\partial}{\partial x^{(i,j)}} f(x) + \frac12 \sum_{i,j, k,l=1}^{d} Q(x)^{(i,j,k,l)} \frac{\partial}{\partial x^{(i,j)}}\frac{\partial}{\partial x^{(k,l)}} f(x) \\
			&\quad  + \int_{y\in \mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\setminus \{0\}} \Big( f(x+y) - f(x) -  \sum_{i,j=1}^d y^{(i,j)} \frac{\partial}{\partial x^{(i,j)}} f(x)\mathds{1}_{\{\|y \|\leq 1\}}  \Big) N(x, dy), \end{align*}
		for all $f\in C_c^2(\mathbb{R}^{d\times d})\subseteq D(\mathcal{A}_{X})$, the latter denoting the domain of $\mathcal{A}_X$. For any $x\in \mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$, the triplet $(\ell(x), Q(x), N(x,dy))$ is given by
		\begin{align*}
			\ell(x)&=  x \gamma_L +  \int_{y\in \mathbb{R}^{d\times d}\setminus\{0\}}  x y  \left(  \mathds{1}_{\{ \| x y  \| \leq 1\}}- \mathds{1}_{\{ \|y \| \leq 1\}} \right) \nu_L(dy),  \\
			Q(x)^{(i,j,k,l)} &= \sum_{n,m=1}^{d} 	x^{(i,m)} \sigma_{(m,j),(n,l)} x^{(k,n)} , \, i,j,k,l=1,\ldots, d,\quad \text{and} \\
			N(x,dy)&= \nu_L(T_x^{-1}(dy)),
		\end{align*}
		being the image measure of $\nu_L$ under the transform $T_x$ defined by
		$$T_x(y): \mathbb{R}^{d\times d} \to \mathbb{R}^{d\times d} , y\mapsto x y, \quad x\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

