{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.200833+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c478688ea6efae000bb36745f68a1f7016cd019b7c493f0a88862929f6de2f89","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:MLSI-MF of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Let $h\in{\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} ^{Nn}$, let \(J\in{\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} ^{n\times n}\) be a nonnegative definite matrix with largest eigenvalue \(\lambda(J) < 1/2\), and let  
\(\overline{J}=\max_{i\in [n]} \sum_{j\in [n]}|J_{i,j}|\), \(\overline{h}=\max_{\ell\in [n], i\in[N]}|h_\ell(i)|\). 

For any $N\ge 2$, and $\r\in \ensuremath{\mathcal D}_{\ensuremath{\mathcal A},N}$, 
\begin{equation}
\bar{\mathcal{E}}_{N, J,h,\r}(F, \log F) \ge \a\operatorname{Ent}_{\mu_{N,J,h,\r}}(F),
\end{equation}
for all $F\ge 0$, with constant  $\a$ such that  
  \begin{equation}
        \alpha \ge \tfrac14(1 - 2\lambda(J))\,e^{-8(\overline{J}+\overline{h})}.
   \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.745171+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4787d1962662503bb62442cba25d45f7bd8f7e6d8dc5da9eaa84a376d1c9f6a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 ({\cite[Theorem~4.19) of arXiv:2506.10511, '2506.10511'] {Morters_Peres_2010}}]
Recall \eqref{hausdorff}. Suppose that $(E,\widehat{D})$ is a metric space and $\Delta\geq 0$. If there exists a mass distribution $\zeta$ on $E$ along with constants $C <\infty$ and $\delta > 0$ such that
\begin{equation*}
	\zeta(V)\leq C\left({\rm diam}(V;\widehat{D})\right)^\Delta,
\end{equation*}
for all closed sets $V$ with ${\rm diam}(V;\widehat{D})\leq \delta$, then
\begin{equation*}
	C_\Delta(E,\widehat{D})\geq C^{-1}\zeta(E)>0
\end{equation*}
and hence $\mathrm{dim}_{\mathrm{H}}(E;\widehat{D})\geq \Delta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

