{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.598011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c47974f629e50e32239b42da0e83183d5d528c657f99af09485411cebd7fa8c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Let $\Lambda$ be a compact subset of $\Delta_I$ and let $k_t:\Lambda\to\N^d$ be Borel and satisfy

\begin{equation*}
\sup_{\lambda\in\Lambda}|k_t(\lambda)-t\lambda|_1=o(\sqrt t).
\end{equation*}

If $\Ee_{\mathfrak a}[L_1^2]<\infty$, then

\begin{equation*}
\sup_{\lambda\in\Lambda}
\frac{|N(k_t(\lambda))-D_{\mathfrak N(k_t(\lambda))}|}{\sqrt t}
\xrightarrow[t\to\infty]{\mathbb P}0.
\end{equation*}

If, in addition, $\Ee_{\mathfrak a}[(R_1^*(g))^2]<\infty$, then the reward accumulated in the incomplete cycle which intersects the boundary is $o_{\Pp}(\sqrt t)$ uniformly over $\lambda\in\Lambda$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.575678+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c47c17b3dc54ac271691d601c764823c90d5c3cfcc2b09f952faba870513ca80","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Theor-probIntUN-002 of arXiv:2412.08932, 'Gaussian heat kernel asymptotics for conditioned random walks'] Assume that $\bb E (X_1) = 0$, $\bb E (X^2_1)= \sigma^2  > 0$  and that there exists $\delta > 0$ 
