{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.562884+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c47e57124b77b9ea0bf5d07dedf9fae95e70d0069164af644c6e06d8450d903d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm h-continuous of arXiv:2605.21366, 'The Martin boundary of the Directed Landscape'] The following holds on a full probability event. For any $t>s$ and any function $\mathfrak h:\mathbb{R}\to[-\infty,\infty)$ satisfying 
