almost surely.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.662853+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4f4f3c175cbac90d3c2d3eb46d12802ccb4cfb85212cb6520894561214db8b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 (\cite{S11}) of arXiv:2604.23656, 'Doubly Reflected Backward SDEs Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Quadratic Generator'] For any $\alpha\geq 1$ and $\delta>0$, $L_G^{\alpha+\delta}(\Omega_T)\subset L_{\mathcal{E}}^{\alpha}(\Omega_T)$. More precisely, for any $1<\gamma<\beta:=(\alpha+\delta)/\alpha$ and $\gamma\leq 2$, we have
