{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.700442+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4fb5716861227301b5a78e48b10c27a85f4ddfb46f9f9ca44e216938140360a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def 34 (Approximation by subsets) of arXiv:2608.30990, 'Convergence of symmetries: nilpotency, dimension, and perfectness'] Let $\phi_i : G_i \to G$ be a sequence of local good approximations with regular neighborhoods $A_i \subset G_i$ and $A \subset G$. We say a sequence of open subsets $B_i \subset A_i $ \emph{approximates} an open set $B \subset A$ if the following holds: 
    \begin{itemize}
        \item  For all $U \subset B $ open nonempty, one has $\phi_i (B_i) \cap U \neq \emptyset$ for $i$ large enough. 
        \item  For all $V \subset G$ open with $\overline{B} \subset V$, one has $\phi_i (B_i) \subset V$ for $i$ large enough.
        \item For each compact $K\subset B$, there is $i_0 \in \mathbb{N}$  such that if $i \geq i_0$, and $g \in A_i^8$ satisfies  $\phi_i (g) \in K $,  then $g \in B_i$.
    \end{itemize}
    In particular, if $G$ is metrizable,  $\phi_i (B_i)$ converges in the Hausdorff topology to $B$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.773737+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4fb6386297846d47aaf6f4541afac1f150ca349256f57d909b7b70605806281","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:double-well of arXiv:2411.01364, 'Global Dynamics of Granular Media Equations via Stochastic Order'] Consider the following one-dimensional McKean-Vlasov SDE,
\begin{equation}
\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} X_t=-\left[X_t(X_t-1)(X_t+1)+\theta\left(X_t-\mathbf E [X_t]\right)\right]\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} t+\sigma(X_t)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} B_t.
\end{equation}
If the parameter $\theta$ and the Lipschitz function $\sigma\colon\mathbb R\to\mathbb R$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
    \theta\geq\frac{27(9+\sqrt{17})}{128},\quad 0<\inf_{x\in\mathbb R}\sigma^2(x)\leq \sup_{x\in\mathbb R}\sigma^2(x)<\frac{51\sqrt{17}-107}{256},
\end{equation}
and let $r=\frac{9-\sqrt{17}}{8}$, then
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textnormal{(\roman*)}]
\item There are exactly three invariant measures, $\nu_{-1}, \nu_0, \nu_1\in\mathcal P_{\8}(\mathbb R)$ with $\nu_{-1}<_{\mathrm{st}}\nu_0<_{\mathrm{st}}\nu_1$;
\item For all bounded sets $B\subset\mathcal P_2(\mathbb R)$, $\mathcal W_2(P_t^*B,[\nu_{-1},\nu_1])\to0$ as $t\to\8$;
\item There are a decreasing connecting orbit from $\nu_0$ to $\nu_{-1}$ and an increasing connecting orbit from $\nu_0$ to $\nu_1$;
\item There hold $\nu_{-1}\in B(\delta_{-1},r)$, $\nu_1\in B(\delta_1,r)$, and
\[
\mathcal W_2(P_t^*\mu,\nu_{-1})\to0\ \text{ as $t\to\8$ for all $\mu\in\bigcup_{a\leq0}B(\delta_{-1+a},r)$},
\]
\[
\mathcal W_2(P_t^*\mu,\nu_1)\to0\ \text{ as $t\to\8$ for all $\mu\in\bigcup_{a\geq0}B(\delta_{1+a},r)$}.
\]
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

