{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.383963+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c511b8c286dc570f27220cd8dabb47a79c305660f3878006edf6d9324d4825d7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:moderate.dev.FPP of arXiv:2411.02046, 'Speed of Convergence and Moderate Deviations of FPP on Random Geometric Graphs'] Consider first-passage percolation as in Theorem~(thm:speed.FPP of the paper), under the same assumptions as in that theorem. There exist finite constants~$\upvarphi > 0$ and~$C > 0$ such that, for~$x \in \R^d$ with~$\|x\|$ large enough,
