{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:44:12.631888+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c54276f50de6c2965ef37ec114eee455a41ebe03f91522f528aff259f51fc1b6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:subexp-informal of arXiv:2512.04371, 'Constructive Approximation under Carleman's Condition, \\ with Applications to Smoothed An'] Let $\mu$ be a sub-exponential distribution, i.e., the moment generating function of $\mu$ exists in a neighborhood of zero. 
