{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.257163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5541eb63927bebf8296de1e810dd721af90072c95e054bdcc7533c7e25a1b50","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:shift_blocks of arXiv:2607.08914, 'Linear spreading speed in non-monotone population models'] Let $\ell, \rho \in \mathbb{N}$ and $\emptyset \neq A\subseteq B_{\ell}^\mathrm{bl}(0)$. If
  $(z,t)\in \mathbb{L}$ with $t\ge T_\mathrm{bl} (\abs{z}L_\mathrm{bl}^{-1}+\rho+\ell)/\tilde v$, then
  \begin{equation}

    \mathbb{P}( B_{\rho}^\mathrm{bl}(z) \nsubseteq \tilde K_t^A)
