{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.387644+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c55aacdecd0156d06c9a7ad60aff685256fd0846f2145276cd6c91db12328f9d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3_integ of arXiv:2411.02156, 'Martin boundary of a degenerate Reflected Brownian Motion in a wedge'] Denote by $z_0=(a_0,b_0)$ the starting point of the process. Then, for any $(a,b)\in \mathbb{R}_+^2$ satisfying $a > 0$ or $b>0$,
