{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.614166+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c599e4aff201f21098c3cb77724d777e331fc2787c4a5d501fbf22daa44b90a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] Fix $\beta\in (0,1/2)$ and $\delta>0$. There exists a constant $C$ such that for all $m\in [\![\beta n,(1-\beta)n]\!]$, all $\ell\in [n^\delta,n]$, and all $n$ large enough, we have
