{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.878058+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5c9e88bbd1d202e21eb7abaa1ae30d5b083581374fd358a737c71f44d6e1a15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop|IdempotentFixedPoints of arXiv:2504.08935, 'Higher-Order Derivatives of First-Passage Percolation with Respect to the Environment'] If $\psi:R\to R$ is an idempotent function, then the set of its fixed points is equal to its range, i.e. \begin{align}
