{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:59.503580+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5ea17ad7bc9d591cdf9a8831190e64ef5a588cfd52bed5945bf9b04360cabcf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 66 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] For each $p \geq 2$ there is a constant $C_p > 0$ such that
