{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.026207+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5ebe5f9b1ddac82b3b5136cf340e1f0359a9949bd38ba3343bd3e4080d05be1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Level sets and multifractal spectrum relative at scale $ \Scl$ of arXiv:2512.06984, 'Infinite Dimensional Multifractal Analysis of the Wiener measure'] The \emph{level sets} of a measure \( \mu \) at scale $ \mathsf{scl}$  are given for $ \alpha > 0 $ by
    \begin{equation*}
    \underline{E}_\mu^\mathsf{scl} ( \alpha) := \left\{ x \in X :   \underline{\mathsf{scl}}_{ \mathrm{loc}} \mu ( x) = \alpha \right\}  \ , \quad 
    \overline{E}_\mu^\mathsf{scl}  ( \alpha) := \left\{ x \in X :   \overline{\mathsf{scl}}_{ \mathrm{loc}} \mu ( x) = \alpha \right\} \;  
    \end{equation*}
    and 
    \begin{equation*} 
    E_\mu^\mathsf{scl}  ( \alpha) := \underline{E}_\mu^\mathsf{scl} (\alpha) \cap \overline{E}_\mu^\mathsf{scl} (\alpha)
    =\left\{ x \in X :   \mathsf{scl}_{\mathrm{loc}} \mu ( x) = \alpha \right\} \; . 
    \end{equation*}
    Then, the (fine) \emph{multifractal spectra} of the measure \( \mu \) at scale $ \mathsf{scl}$ are defined by the functions
    \[ 
     \underline{f}_\mu^\mathsf{scl} ( \alpha)  := \mathsf{scl}_H \underline{E} ( \alpha) 
    \, , \quad 
    \overline{f}_\mu^\mathsf{scl} ( \alpha)  :=  \overline{E} ( \alpha)   \quad \text{and}\quad 
   f_\mu^\mathsf{scl} ( \alpha) := \mathsf{scl}_H  E ( \alpha)    \; .  \]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.237229+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5ebf9683be8350111aa1a6719531343c79986affd71ec4e212292bafd2747c5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 104 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] If $n\ge k|F|$, then the following hold:
