{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.359010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5f0374c69e6683e3203b1a03bbe16fd241d179d8fb69ea1985c2d9f17043bef","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor one-environment-lemma of arXiv:2507.09421, 'Stability of randomly switching stochastic reaction networks with asymptotically linear tr'] Suppose that $M$ is a $d\times d$ matrix which is associated to a mass-action CRN in the sense of equation (equation eq:associated CRN of the paper); suppose further that the CRN has at-most-monomolecular reactions. Suppose that there exists a vector $v\in\mathbb R_{\ge0}^d$ such that $(vM)_m>0$ for each $m$ such that $v_m>0$, where as above $(vM)_m$ is the $m$-th entry of the vector $vM$. Then for each constant $C\in\mathbb R$ and each $x\in\mathbb Z^d_{\ge0}$ such that $\operatorname{supp}(v)\cap\operatorname{supp}(x)\ne\varnothing$, there exists an $x^0\in\mathbb Z^d_{\ge0}$ such that $x^0$ is reachable from $x$ and $v\cdot x^0>C$.
\begin{proof}
We can view this as a switched process in one environment with $M_1=M$ and switching matrix $Q=(0)$. Applying Lemma (lem:v cdot x^0>C of the paper), the result is immediate.
\end{proof}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.081932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5f0437936ee20833e4643ec27eb93cce2fae9ddb7f207826aa3d942efd3899a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition CanoncialSpaceProperties of arXiv:2411.12522, 'Canonical insurance models: stochastic equations and comparison theorems'] For  $s \in [0,\infty)$ and $i \in \mathcal{Z}$, let $Y$ be  a $\mathbb{P}_s^i$-integrable random variable. Then
	\begin{itemize}
