{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.532754+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c60b5c94ec70d855db2f994cfa78bfc05b13ccaeee264107c7c3bb7eb7b74908","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Deff def:invasion-rates of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Fix $\mu \in P_{inv}(\mathcal{M}_0)$ (see (inv-meas of the paper)), $k \in \{1,\dots,m\}$, and suppose $\mu(\{x_k = 0\}) = 1$ 
    Let $\tilde{x}$ be a process satisfying
    \begin{align*}
        d\tilde x_k &= [d_k\Delta \tilde x_k + \tilde x_k(m_k -\sum_{j\neq k}a_{kj}\tilde x_j)]dt + \sigma_k'(0)\tilde x_kdW_k(t) \\
        d\tilde x_i &= [d_i\Delta \tilde x_i + \tilde x_i(m_i - a_{ii}\tilde x_i -\sum_{j \neq i,k}a_{ij} \tilde x_j)]dt + \sigma_i(\tilde x_i)dW_i(t) \qquad i \neq k \,. 
    \end{align*}
    Define 
    \begin{equation}
        r_k(\mu) \coloneqq \inf_{\nu \in P_k(\mu)} \nu\Big(\int_D v_k\Big(m_k - \sum_{j\neq k} a_{kj}\tilde x_j\Big) - \frac{1}{2} \sigma_k'(0)^2\sum_{i=1}^\infty \lambda_{ki}^2\Big(\int_D e_{ki} v_k\Big)^2\Big) \,,
    \end{equation}
    where $P_k(\mu)$ denotes the set of all invariant measures (see  (inv-meas of the paper)) $\nu$ for the process $(v_k,\tilde x_{-k}) \coloneqq (\tilde x_k/\|\tilde x_k\|_{L^1}, \tilde x_{-k})$ satisfying $\phi^*\nu = \mu$. Here, $\phi$ is given by $\phi(v,x_{-k}) = (x_1,\dots,x_{k-1},0,x_{k+1},\dots,x_m)$, $\phi^*\nu(A) = \nu(\phi^{-1}(A))$, and  $x_{-k} = ( x_1,\dots, x_{k-1}, x_{k+1},\dots, x_m)$.

    For a general $\mu \in P_{inv}(\mathcal{M}_0)$, by invariance there is $p \in [0,1]$ and $\mu_1, \mu_2 \in P_{inv}(\mathcal{M}_0)$ such that $\mu_1(\{x_k = 0\}) = 1$, $\mu_2(\{x_k = 0\}) = 0$, and $\mu = p\mu_1 + (1-p)\mu_2$. Then we 
    we define $r_k(\mu) = pr_k(\mu_1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.257035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c60da31dc98b899c37816118a55ac2462f0219f7fbac0f61c8a5cf48dc0c0973","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 58 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Let $x\in F,x_n\in F_n,\kappa\in [1/2,1],p\in [1,\infty],\alpha\in (0,\alpha_n),t>0$ and $f\in\BL^{\kappa}(M)$.
Then, under the condition $1_{\kappa,p}$,
we have that
\begin{align*}
  |P_t(G^{\alpha})^{\circ 2}f(x)-P_t^n(G^{\alpha,n})^{\circ 2}f(x_n)|
  \lesssim&\g{c}{sg1,n}
    \Bigl\{ \|f\|_{K_n}(d_{\rm{H}}(F,F_n)+d_{\rm{H}}(F,F_n)^{\kappa}+d(x,x_n))\\
    &\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\qquad\qquad\qquad\qquad +\|f\|_{\BL^{\kappa}(K_n)}d_{\BL^{\kappa}}(\mu,\mu_n)\Bigr\}\\
    \leq&\g{c}{sg1,n}\|f\|_{\BL^{\kappa}(K_n)}( d_{\rm{H}}(F,F_n)+d_{\rm{H}}(F,F_n)^{\kappa}+d(x,x_n)+d_{\BL^{\kappa}}(\mu,\mu_n) ),
\end{align*}
where 
\begin{align*}
  \g{c}{sg1,n}:=\g{c}{estres,n}(t+\alpha^{-1}+\alpha^{-1}c_1(t,\kappa,p)\mu(F)^{1/p})+\alpha^{-1}\mu(F)^{1/p}( c_1(t,\kappa,p)+c_1([0,t],\kappa,p)).
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.540779+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c60de240aab9cb6493183c430484958ff9729a24502eb6888e664611f1909e9c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem IP-limit of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Let $(X,d)$ be a compact metric space and $\{a_{n}\}_{n\geq
1}$ a sequence in $X$. Then there exist a strictly increasing sequence of
integers $q_{1}<q_{2}<\cdots $ and a point $a^{\ast }\in X$ such that for
every $\varepsilon >0$ there exists $L$ with 
\begin{equation}
d(a_{n},a^{\ast })<\varepsilon \qquad \text{for every }n\in \mathrm{FS}
(q_{L},q_{L+1},q_{L+2},\dots ).  
\end{equation}
Equivalently, the restricted sequence $\{a_{n}\}_{n\in \mathrm{FS}
(q_{1},q_{2},\dots )}$ IP-converges to $a^{\ast }$ (in either the
neighborhood form ((1007.1 of the paper)) or the metric form ((1007 of the paper)).","status":"unverified"}

