{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.548266+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6534655f1fa0de3150e28f3b1fd47ad975e8b0da8d0387b4d717a5c8f70dbd7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 20 (Discrepancy~\citep{marx2020predictive}) of arXiv:2609.01397, 'Measuring consistency via ensemble margin and local prediction variability: Auditing decis'] The discrepancy of $\emprashomonset$, at a test instance x, is the fraction of conflicting predictions of models in $\emprashomonset$ w.r.t. a reference model and is defined as,
