{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.855391+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c69d4b06dae97edf80f4b6e3cf3dc97e6ea0a58266cdc58b0f892856e36e6028","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:NS of arXiv:2411.06838, 'Generalized Wasserstein Barycenters'] A sequence $(\gamma_n)_{n\in \mathbb{N}} \subset \mathcal{P}_2^{sw}(Z)$ and a measure $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_2^{sw}(Z)$ satisfy
\begin{itemize}
