{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.801619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6a6631ae4592a6dbd3777844a10515bdad5d36053b819402b68a99bed91f48d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Thick quantum disk of arXiv:2510.05850, 'Three-point connectivity constant for $q$-state Potts spin clusters'] For $W \ge \frac{\gamma^2}{2}$, we define the measure $\mathcal{M}_2^{\rm disk}(W)$ as follows. Write $\beta=\gamma+\frac{2-W}{\gamma}$ and let $(B_t)_{t \ge 0}$ be a standard Brownian motion conditioned on $B_{2t}-(Q-\beta)t<0$ for all $t>0$, and $(\widetilde B_t)_{t \ge 0}$ be its independent copy. Let
    \begin{equation*}
        Y_t=
        \begin{cases}
            B_{2t}-(Q-\beta) t, & \mbox{ for }\,t \ge 0, \\
            \widetilde B_{-2t}+(Q-\beta)t, & \mbox{ for }\,t<0,
        \end{cases}
    \end{equation*}
    and set $h_1(z)=Y_{\mathrm{Re} z}$ for each $z \in \mathcal{S}$. Let $h_2$ be a random generalized function with the same law as $h_\mathcal{S}^2$ defined above and independent from $h_1$.
    Sample $\mathbf{c} \in \mathbb{R}$ independently from the measure $\frac{\gamma}{2} e^{(\beta-Q)c} \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d} c$, and set $\phi(z)=h_1(z)+h_2(z)+\mathbf{c}$. The infinite measure $\mathcal{M}_2^{\rm disk}(W)$ is defined as the law of $(\mathcal{S},\phi,-\infty,+\infty)/{\sim_\gamma}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:27:14.893698+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6a68ce7d0f9367d435b41335f0957f10abdf78796fdc6ca64d5ca12d3d87459","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 (Near-critical convergence to Feller diffusion) of arXiv:2608.23491, 'Stochastic Dynamics of Low Earth Orbit Near Full Capacity'] Under (A1), (A2'), and (A3), define the branching-scale fragment process
