{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.720396+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6ab7cc36655e6703e4252f68450124e7d8c05ebdcc3ad57dc4ea74a45c899ec","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2511.13404, 'Asymptotic stability and mean ergodicity of Feller processes on Polish spaces'] Under the above settings, the Feller process $\Xi$ admits a unique invariant probability measure $\mu=\delta_0\times\leb(\T)$. Moreover, for any $V:\R_+\times\T\rightarrow[0,\infty)$ that is continuous,
