  \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.574572+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7616e99113aa8a29e0096a3206c8dcafba4684c673b599d0bba0592b3c5d3a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 50 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:basic} and~\ref{ass:rand_ent}, suppose that $E_{+,0}$ is a regular right edge for $\Pi_0$ in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. With high probability, the critical point $\zeta_{t,N}$ exists uniquely in the $t^2$-neighbourhood of $E_{+,0}$. Moreover,
