{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.828612+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7639126d52e60acfc71d43ba24e219f449fda7dac023607e50316275b6fe4ac","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: bound_int_t-harmonic_by_distance of arXiv:2609.00257, 'Stability estimates for the initial-to-final-state inverse problem'] Let $n\geq2$ and $V_1, V_2\in L^1(\mathbb{R}^n)\cap L^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)$ with $\|V_j\|_{w_\delta} < \infty$, for $j\in \{1, 2\}$. Let also $\psi_1\equiv \psi_\lambda^{V_1}$ and $\psi_2 \equiv \psi_\lambda^{V_2}$ be the time-harmonic solutions (equation eq: time-harmonic solutions of the paper) to the Schr\"odinger equation, as constructed in subsection (sec: stationary states of the paper) for potentials $V_1$ and $V_2$ respectively. Then, there holds

\begin{equation}
