{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.362334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c767b4540f6b3e4abba1248f0ccd1dc6fe5e6743b9c966bdb809ceb474e1f08f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:carpet-information of arXiv:2607.24705, 'Derangetropy Operators'] For every $f \in \mathcal{D}_{+}$:
		\begin{enumerate}[label=\normalfont(\roman*), leftmargin=*]
			\item the time-averaged carpet is the tent modulation,
			\begin{equation}
				2\pi\int_{0}^{1/2\pi} f_{\tau}\,d\tau
				= \rho_{\Lambda}[f],
				\qquad
				\Lambda(z) = 4\min(z,\,1-z);

			\end{equation}
			\item the time-averaged chi-square divergence from the base law is
			universal,
			\begin{equation}
				2\pi\int_{0}^{1/2\pi}
				\chi^{2}\big(f_{\tau}\,\|\,f\big)\,d\tau
				= \frac{2}{3},
				\qquad
				\chi^{2}\big(f_{\tau}\|f\big)
				= \int_{0}^{1}\big(w_{s} - 1\big)^{2}dz;

			\end{equation}
			\item information breathes but never grows:
			$D(f_{\tau}\,\|\,f) \le \log\big(1 + \chi^{2}(f_{\tau}\|f)\big)$,
			and $\sup_{\tau}\chi^{2}(f_{\tau}\|f)$ is a finite absolute
			constant.
		\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.585884+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c76878d7463ffc61f70d4739210f9f58dc103661d7649983a6ed9367b04b0526","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 (Closed-form gradient refinement) of arXiv:2608.25116, '\method: Gradient Refinement and Progress-Aware Exploitation for Query-Efficient High-Dime'] Let $k_\calD(\cdot,\cdot)$ denote the GP posterior kernel after observing
$\calD$. Then $\alpha_{\mathrm{ref}}(\bz)$ is independent of the unobserved
value $y_\bz$ and equals
