     (N)} \varrho (\lambda) \frac{\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\chi}}^{\lambda} (u_1,
     \ldots, u_N)}{\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\chi}}^{\lambda} (1^N)} . \]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.678308+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c76d3874d8da2630269adadaddc4a8a6733a3b9e5b580b68a644074755ea2ffc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.30898, 'Necessity of Ladyzhenskaya \& Ural'tseva's sufficient conditions in nonuniform ellipticity'] Let $n\ge 2$ and $2<p<\infty$. There exists a bounded domain $\Omega\subset \mathbb{R}^{n}$ with smooth boundary, and a function $v_{0}\in C^{\infty}(\bar{\Omega})$ such that the unique solution $v\in v_{0}+W^{1,1}_{0}(\Omega)$ to Dirichlet problem
\eqn{pd}
$$
v_{0}+W^{1,1}_{0}(\Omega)\ni v\mapsto \min_{w\in v_{0}+W^{1,1}_{0}(\Omega)}\mathcal{A}_{p}(w;\Omega),
$$
and unique generalized minimizer of $\mathcal{A}_{p}$ in class $v_{0}+W^{1,1}_{0}(\Omega)$, satisfies $v\in C^{0,1-\frac{2}{p}}(\bar{\Omega})\cap W^{1;\frac{p}{2},\infty}(\Omega)\setminus W^{1,\infty}_{\loc}(\Omega)$. In particular, the set of non-Lebesgue points of $Dv$ has positive $\mathcal{H}^{n-1}$-measure. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.658201+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c76ec71f544f9a73c4a02579cca09175c698e05316e6f06c13fc84a765598a15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 (Exact distribution) of arXiv:2605.08629, 'Moderate deviations for the Maki--Thompson rumour model'] For $j = 1,\ldots,n$,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}(V_n = j) = \frac{(n-1)!}{(n-j)!} \frac{d_j}{n^{2j}},
    \end{equation}
    where the sequence $\{d_j\}_{j\ge 1}$ is defined recursively by $d_1=1$ and for $j\ge 2$,
    \begin{equation}
        d_j = \frac{j^{2j}}{(j-1)!} - \sum_{i=1}^{j-1} \frac{j^{2(j-i)}}{(j-i)!} d_i.
    \end{equation}
    Consequently, for $k = 0,\ldots,n-1$,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}(X_n = k) = \frac{(n-1)!}{k!} \frac{d_{n-k}}{n^{2(n-k)}}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.996696+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7759c4bc9e2cc2a646902543f81af873d1cbe5d3acefbb528430467c2a1670f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lm 44 of arXiv:2512.02286, 'Pfaffian Transition Probability and Correlation Kernel of TASEP in Half-space'] Let us denote, by $\Theta_i$, the polynomials from \eqref{eq:pre phi contour virtual} so that for a fixed integer $N$
\begin{equation}
   \Theta_i(x) := \phi_{[N-i+1,N]}(\virst_i,x) = \oint_{\gamma} \frac{\dd z}{2\pi\ii} \frac{1}{z^i} \left(\frac{1}{1-z}\right)^x = \binom{x+i-2}{x-1},
\end{equation}
where the contour surrounds $z=0$ while omitting all other singularities of the integrand. Then the following holds for all $1\leq i,j\leq N$:
\begin{equation}

    \sum_{x=1}^\infty \sum_{y=1}^\infty \Theta_i(x) Q_{1,1}(x,y) \Theta_j(y) =  Q_{i+1,j+1}(1,1).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.792139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7797d04535444931b0f7276c9210964209d886fbaa80c92ee109071c524905d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:usefuldecomp of arXiv:2411.08295, 'Improving the convergence of Markov chains via permutations and projections'] Let $l,m,n \in \mathbb{N}\cup \{0\}$ with $l > n \geq 0$ and $m \geq 1$. Let $P \in \mathcal{L}(\pi)$ and $Q_i \in \mathcal{I}(\pi) \cap \mathcal{L}$ for $i \in \llbracket 0,m-1 \rrbracket$ be a sequence of isometric involution transition matrices. Define $R_n$ as in (equation eq:Rndef of the paper). 
	\begin{itemize}
		\item For $E \in \mathcal{E}$, we have
		\begin{align*}
			D^\pi_{KL}(R_n \| E) 
			&= \sum_{j=n}^{l-1} D^\pi_{KL}(R_j \| R_{j+1}) + D^\pi_{KL}(R_{l} \| E).
		\end{align*}

		\item For $E \in \mathcal{E}$, we have
		\begin{align*}
			\left\lVertR_n - E\right\rVert_F^2 
			&= \sum_{j=n}^{l-1} \norm{R_j - R_{j+1}}_F^2 + \norm{R_{l} - E}_F^2.
		\end{align*}

		\item  We have
		\begin{align*}
			R_\infty(Q_0,\ldots,Q_{m-1},P) = R_\infty(Q_0,\ldots,Q_{m-1},R_l).
		\end{align*}

		\item(Projection is trace-preserving)
		\begin{align*}
			\mathrm{Tr}(R_n) = \mathrm{Tr}(P).
		\end{align*}
	\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

