{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.318307+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7f16b20a32b13e8dd7f286e993808f4694c8155f94e150b05cdec41f5df496b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] A map $f\colon X\to Y$ of closed orthogonal $G$-spaces is called a \emph{$G$-global ${\mathcal{F}}$-weak equivalence} if $f({\mathcal{U}}_H)\colon X({\mathcal{U}}_H)\to Y({\mathcal{U}}_H)$ is a $\mathcal G_{H,G}$-weak equivalence for every $H\in{\mathcal{F}}$ and some (hence any) complete $H$-universe ${\mathcal{U}}_H$. 

