 &\textnormal{(iv)}\quad
 &\Pp\{M>u\}>0\quad\text{for every }u\in\mathbb R.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.636157+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8745fe4aa91c5bcce50bd13bc64ed500b587520da1228201ab419661acbef15","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2512.12124, 'A discontinuous percolation phase transition on the hierarchical lattice'] We say that a set $U \subset \Lambda_{M_g+jr,\infty}$ is non-bad if all its elements are either good or mediocre. For a good or mediocre block $\varphi \in \Lambda_{M_g+jr,\infty}$, we define
    \begin{equation*}
        S(\varphi) = \begin{cases}
