{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.426443+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c88452a576bcf75d27867db2e4b959bdb2fae747c795e5fea08a7730c9d00b85","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma CountingConnectedSets of arXiv:2605.18744, 'Lattice random-field Widom--Rowlinson models'] For every $m\in \mathbb{N}$, there is a $C>0$ such that for all $n\in \mathbb{N}$ and $x\in \mathbb{Z}^d $ 
