{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.436728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c893fe7b49a5ad7286edf6aa5178f4b4e69aa41cb768d81996fc14ed3287f3d7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mec of arXiv:2508.09291, '1+O(1) asymptotics for loop percolation in five and higher dimensions'] If $\eta$ is sampled from $\mathbb{P}$, a Poisson point process with intensity measure $\mu$, then for $f\ge 0$ measurable
