{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.185507+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c89fb384aa22cb7a006ebc5fdc64ea74547e0c7b6148b263e3ce15caf3686bf8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$ with $d\neq 6$, there exist constants $\Cl(d),\cl(d)>0$ such that  the following hold for all $N\ge \Cref{const_four_point_1}$, $v,v'\in \widetilde{B}(\cref{const_four_point_2}N)$, and $w,w'\in \widetilde{B}(10N)\setminus \widetilde{B}(N)$ with $|w-w'|\ge N$: 
