{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.723324+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8a2fde294ebc7ec4e53584693809de659cc74fd63bad4598e82222927c50531","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2511.13559, 'Asymptotic analysis of rare events in high dimensions'] Suppose $D$ satisfies Assumption~\ref{assume:D} and let $D_\la$ be as in~\eqref{D-Dla}. Let $R=24+6(\log\la)/d$, fix an arbitrary constant $c_{\psi}$, and suppose
