{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.618189+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8a95b664b765536096b77fabe189717fc7cb229cf199b494811383646fa4220","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 37 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] For all~$\delta\in(0,1)$ there exist~$c>c'>0$ and $u_0>0$ such that for all~$n\ge1$ and all~$u\ge u_0$ with~$u \le n^{1-\delta}$,
