{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.265042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8cc0620369530d4b0ef437ece1e4038175914f2214070b7c0d6160aeab52aba","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2604.19924, 'Fluctuation theory for spectrally negative Lévy processes killed by additive functionals'] The scale functions $W^{(q,p_1,\dots,p_n)}_{(a_1,\dots,a_n)}$  and $Z^{(q,p_1,\dots,p_n)}_{(a_1,\dots,a_n)}$ defined in \eqref{volterra_lt}, are the unique solutions to the following integral equations
