{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.333027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8d8e7699a005a7083c75a2daf71f1e959286f8d5e783e19f841e2f6341cb14d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2607.14718, 'Anchored Nash inequalities and heat kernel bounds for a class of random conductance models'] Suppose that \eqref{a2-2-1} holds and there exist $m_{0} > d$ and $p, q \in (1, \infty]$ satisfying

