{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.395314+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c908cd9c976ce32f754f4281c057c8db790bebae6b492394ef4a1b457a0a86c9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2507.19554, 'Full extremal process in four-dimensional membrane model'] For $i=1,...,K^4$, let $z_i$ be as in (prop:aux of the paper) and $z_i' \in V_{N}^{K, \delta, i}$ be measurable with respect to $\{h_x^f: x \in V_N^{K, i}\}$ such that $\lv z_i - z_i'\rv = o(N/K)$ as $N,K \rightarrow \infty$. Then for any $A \subset [0,1]^4$ open and non-empty 
