{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.706290+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c9508485312a68863abc7fe8bdf6844d4b0b61ea8cf188817d9c1802560a4637","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition PROP:regular of arXiv:2411.07840, 'Central limit theorem for the focusing $Φ^4$-measure in the infinite volume limit'] Let $L \ge 1$. There exists a constant $C>0$, independent of $L$, such that for $i=1,2$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{x\in \mathbb{T}_{L^2}} |G_{i,x_0}(x,y)-G_{i,x_0}(x,z)|&\le C|y-z| \notag \\
