{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.203649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c98c5099e230973a8a36a6e36b8f4df7ca3f975d16633c43b9ce0f542fa49aea","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] For the equation given by \eqref{eq NS},\eqref{eq eta}, assume that the sequence $\{b_j\}_{j\in\N^+}$ satisfies $\sum_{j\in\N^+}b_j^2<\infty$. Then there exist constants $c,C,\gamma_0>0$ such that the solution $U_t=U(t,U_0)=(u_t,\eta_t)$ satisfies the following estimates.  
