{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.192063+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c9bb89dbbad5c2aa4478318e677c873fa56d40bdfe1d193d599353129434b585","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 9 of arXiv:2605.03528, '\bf Kolmogorov-Smirnov distance and discrepancies {\em versus} Wasserstein distances'] Let $p\!\in (0, +\infty)$ and let $d\ge1$.  There exists a positive constant $K_{p,d}$ such that for every pair   $(\mu,\nu)\in{\cal P}_p(\R^d)^2$,
\begin{equation}
{\cal W}_p^p(\mu,\nu) \le K_{p,d} \sum_{n\ge 0}2^{pn} \sum_{\ell\ge 0}2^{-p\ell}\sum_{F\in {\cal P}_{\ell}}\big| \mu(2^nF\cap \B_n)�- \nu(2^nF\cap \B_n)�\big|,
\end{equation}
where $2^nF = \{2^nx, \; x\!\in F\}$, ${\cal P}_0= \{ (-1,1]^d\}$ and, for every $\ell\ge 1$,  
$$
{\cal P}_\ell= \Big\{a+(-2^{-\ell}, 2^{-\ell}]^d,\; a = \frac{2{\bf k}+\mbox{\bf 1}}{2^{\ell}},\,{\bf k}\in\{-2^{\ell-1},\ldots-1,0,1,\ldots, 2^{\ell-1}-1\}^d  \Big\}.
$$
 Note that   ${\rm card}({\cal P}_\ell)= 2^{d\ell}$ and (with obvious notation)  ${\rm card}(2^n{\cal P}_\ell\cap  {\cal B}_n)= 2^{d(\ell-1)^+}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.853084+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c9bd0aa76618a393482270e8164ddc248dcbfc5ac03b988339579594bfee60f4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition explicit.V of arXiv:2607.10708, 'A class of Markov processes with resetting and applications to cybersecurity'] Under Assumption~(ass_ex of the paper), with  $\alpha = 1/\theta$ and $\eta(A) = c/A$, the value function is equal to 

