{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:07.918719+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca520418719a6809c53536a3775d5d749ea53a9ae627cebd664296fbe2022d37","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2608.12147, 'The Average Singular Value of a Complex Gaussian Random Matrix Strictly Decreases with Dim'] The average singular value of a normalized complex Gaussian random matrix strictly decreases with the dimension, i.e., for every $N\geqslant1$,
