{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.722449+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca5f667be54b67b21112c578cf4a7993ed3ef7b654bd69c6119929d7c5228b2c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2511.13559, 'Asymptotic analysis of rare events in high dimensions'] Let $N\geq1$, $\sup_{u\in D}|g(u)|\leq1$, and suppose Assumptions~\ref{assume1},~\ref{assume:global2} are satisfied. Suppose there is $R \geq 12/\cmin + 2(1+2N)(\log\la)/d$ and constants $\CR$, $C_{\g,\ell}$, $\ell=0,\dots,2N$, $C_{\z,\ell}$, $\ell=0,\dots,2N+2$ 
such that $\g\in C^{2N}(\us(R\e)\times[0,(R\e)^2))$, $\z\in C^{2N+2}(\us(R\e)\times[0,(R\e)^2))$, and
\begingroup
\addtolength{\jot}{0.3em}
\begin{align}
&\e\leq s,\qquad R\e\leq\min(1,\rho_0,2\rho_1, 2/\delta_2(\rho_1)),\\
&R\e\leq1/(2C_{\z,0}+2C_{\z,1}),\qquad R^4d^2/\la\leq \CR,\\
\begin{split}
&\max_{j=0,\dots,N}\g_{0,j}(R\e,(R\e)^2)\leq C_{\g,0}, \\
&\max_{j=0,\dots,\lfloor N-\frac\ell2\rfloor}\g_{\ell,j}(R\e,0)\leq C_{\g,\ell} \,d^{\lceil\frac\ell2\rceil},\quad\ell=1,\dots,2N,
\end{split}\\
\begin{split}
&\omega_{0,2}(R\e,R\e)\vee \max_{j=3,\dots,N+1}\omega_{0,j}(R\e,(R\e)^2)\leq C_{\z,0},\\
&\max_{j=j_\ell,\dots,\lfloor N+1-\frac\ell2\rfloor}\omega_{\ell,j}(R\e,0)\leq C_{\z,\ell} \,d^{(\lceil\frac\ell2\rceil-2)_+},\quad\ell=1,\dots,2N+2.
\end{split}
\end{align}
\endgroup
Here, $j_1=j_2=1$, $j_\ell=0$ for $\ell\geq3$, and $(\cdot)_+=\max(\cdot, 0)$.  Then
\bs
\int_{D}g(u)e^{-\la z(u)}\dd u =  \frac{(2\pi/\la)^{d/2}e^{-\la z(0_{d+1})}}{\la(\det H)^{1/2}}\left(g(0_{d+1})+\sum_{m=1}^{N-1}a_m\left(\frac{d^2}{\la}\right)^{m}+ \Rem_N\right),
\es where
\begin{align}

\max_{m=1,\dots,N-1}|a_m|&\leq C_{\g,\z,N},\qquad |\Rem_N|\leq C_{\g,\z,N,R} (d^2/\la)^{N}.
\end{align}
The constant $C_{\g,\z,N}$ depends on $N$, $C_{\g,\ell}$, $\ell=0,\dots,2N$, and $C_{\z,\ell}$, $\ell=0,\dots,2N+2$. The constant $C_{\g,\z,N,R}$ depends on these same constants and also on $\CR$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.526485+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca5f881da190c5bc721b1592f664e12b3611f5a1211e4705ea2ae272910c7634","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Def: identically distributed of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] Let $X_1$ and $X_2$ be two n-dimensional random vectors defined respectively in sublinear expectation spaces $(\Omega_1, \mathcal{H}_1, \hat{\mathbb{E}}_1)$ and $(\Omega_2, \mathcal{H}_2, \hat{\mathbb{E}}_2)$. They are called identically distributed, denoted by $X_1\stackrel{d}{=} X_2$, if
        \begin{equation}
            \hat{\mathbb{E}}_1[\phi(X_1)]=\hat{\mathbb{E}}_2[\phi(X_2)], \text{ for all } \phi \in C_{lip}(\mathbb{R}^n).
        \end{equation}
		It is clear that $X_1\stackrel{d}{=}X_2$ if and only if their distributions coincide.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.983221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca653a75c7794263c126982083aff6f0cfd5e8e59fee4266b5962f9ccd0b051c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 39 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $G_n = (V_n, E_n)$, with $|V_n|=n$, be a sequence of $b$-expander graphs with minimum and maximum degree $\deg_{\mathrm{min}}(n) = \deg_{\mathrm{min}}$ and $\deg_{\max}(n) = \deg_{\max(n)}$, such that for some fixed $\Delta > 0$ we have $\deg_{\max}/\deg_{\mathrm{min}} \leq \Delta$ for all $n$. Suppose that $\mu$ satisfies Assumption \ref{as:mu_tail}. Then there exists constants $C_1 = C_1(b,\Delta, \mu), C_2(\mu)$ such that if $\deg_{\mathrm{min}} \geq C_2 \log n$, then we have for $\beta \leq C_1 (\deg_{\mathrm{min}}/ \log n)^{1/\alpha}$ and any $\delta > 0$ that
	\begin{equation*}
		\widehat \P \left( C_3^{-1} \sqrt{n} \leq \diam(\cT) \leq C_3  \sqrt{n}  \right) \geq 1-\delta,
	\end{equation*}
	for some $C_3 = C_2(\delta, b, \Delta) > 0$ and all $n = n(\delta)$ large enough. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.242084+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca6568642bfdfcfffa8bbd22b37af7be70e6625bc895bd123c56313bd31eeb13","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm aggregated of arXiv:2608.20635, 'Minimax Optimality of Score-Entropy Discrete Diffusion'] Consider a discretization scheme $0 = t_0 < t_1 < \cdots < t_N = T - \delta$. For $k \in \{0, 1, \cdots, N - 1\}$, denote by $s_{T - t_k}$ the output of Algorithm (alg:thresholding of the paper) constructed using $n$ samples from $p_{T- t_k}$, then there exists a positive numerical constant $C_2$, such that 
	\begin{align*}
		& \sum_{k = 0}^{N - 1} (t_{k + 1} - t_k) \cdot \mathbb{E}[ \mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{SE}}(s_{T - t_k}, p_{T - t_k}, T - t_k) ] \\
        & \leq \frac{ C_2\, v |\mathcal{X}| \log_v |\mathcal{X}| (\log n)^2}{n} \cdot \Big(T + \log\frac{1}{\delta}\Big) \cdot  \Big(1 + \log v + \log\Big(1 + \frac{1}{\delta}\Big)\Big). 
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.356388+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca666dbd21eae9a55b59a1562b7ef5c3c282d91fe7f9e9c7df21f791488ea213","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:lm of arXiv:2607.20956, 'Sharp moduli of continuity for Gaussian fields and stochastic PDEs via correlation bounds'] Fix $t_0 \in I$. Suppose $\mathbb{E}[(X(t)-X(s))^2]^{1/2} \asymp \varphi(|t-s|)$ for all $t,s \in I$, where $\varphi$ is non-decreasing, continuous and regularly varying at 0 of index $\theta \in [0\,,1]$ with
    \begin{align}
        \int_0^1 \frac{\varphi(hr) \, {\rm d} r}{r\sqrt{\log(2/r)}} \lesssim \varphi(h)\sqrt{\log\log(1/h)}=o(1) \quad \text{as $h\to0^+$.}
    \end{align}
    If there is a sequence $(t_n)_{n=n_0}^\infty$ in $I$ with $|t_n-t_0| = a^{-n}$ for some $a>1$, and there exists $C_0>0$ such that
    \begin{align}
        \Var(X(t_n)-X(t_0)|X(t_m)-X(t_0))
        \ge C_0 \Var(X(t_n)-X(t_0))
    \end{align}
    uniformly for all $m>n\ge n_0$, then
    \begin{align}
        \lim_{h \to 0^+} \sup_{t \in I: 0<|t-t_0|\le h} \frac{|X(t)-X(t_0)|}{\varphi(|t-t_0|) \sqrt{\log\log(1/|t-t_0|)}} = K_2 \quad \text{a.s.}
    \end{align}
    where $0<K_2<\infty$ is a non-random number possibly depending on $t_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.547704+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca6adb545e85222125665b4158e80dc9a934eb24d851d396b9165ea5f9fcf675","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2603.29473, '$\chi^2$--cut-off phenomenon for Galerkin projections of Fokker--Planck equations with mon'] [No cut-off phenomenon for Galerkin projection, $\gamma>1$]\hfill

	\noindent
	Assume that $\gamma \in (1,\infty)$, $x_0 \in \R$ and $\delta(\varepsilon) = 1$. Then for any fixed $n\in \mathbb{N}$ there is no cut-off in the sense of \cref{eq:cutdef}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.279480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca6e423673a6e1c872babd5141c185943e5c0cd900c0a6c40518cf4474c9985a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi eq:assumptioninticonditionK of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] Let $R_{0} \in [0,R_{\max}]$ be a random variable. Let $(\nu^{K}_{0})_{K \geq 1}$ be a sequence of random variables in $\mathcal{M}_{P}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})$, such that
    \begin{align}
    \underset{K \geq 1}{\mathrm{sup}} \bigg( \dfrac{1}{K} \hspace{0.1 cm} \mathbb{E}\left(\langle \nu^{K}_{0},1+\mathrm{Id}+\omega \rangle\right) \bigg) < + \infty.

    \end{align}
We use the Poisson point measures $\mathcal{N}$ and $\mathcal{N}'$ of Section~(sec:construction of the paper), independent from $R_{0}$ and $(\nu^{K}_{0})_{K \geq 1}$. For every $K \geq 1$, the renormalized process $(\mu^{K}_{t},R^{K}_{t})_{t \geq 0}$ with initial condition $(\mu^{K}_{0},R_{0})$, is given for every $t \geq 0$ by $\mu^{K}_{t} := \dfrac{\nu^{K}_{t}}{K}$ and

\begin{align*}
    (\nu^{K}_{t},R^{K}_{t}) = &  \hspace{0.1 cm}X^{K}_{t}(\nu^{K}_{0},R_{0})  \\  & +  \displaystyle{\int_{0}^{t}\int_{\mathcal{U} \times \mathbb{R}^{*}_{+} } \mathbb{1}_{\{u \in V^{K}_{s-} \}} \mathbb{1}_{\{h \leq b\left(\xi^{u,K}_{s-}\right)\}}}  [ X^{K}_{t-s}(\nu^{K}_{s-} + \delta_{x_{0}} + \delta_{\xi^{u,K}_{s-}-x_{0}} -\delta_{\xi^{u,K}_{s-}},R^{K}_{s})  \\
    &  \hspace{3 cm} - X^{K}_{t-s}(\nu^{K}_{s-},R^{K}_{s}) ] \mathcal{N}(\mathrm{d}s,\mathrm{d}u,\mathrm{d}h)  \\
     & + 
    \displaystyle{\int_{0}^{t}\int_{\mathcal{U} \times \mathbb{R}^{*}_{+} } \mathbb{1}_{\{ u \in V^{K}_{s-}\}} \mathbb{1}_{\{h \leq d\left(\xi^{u,K}_{s-}\right)\}} [X^{K}_{t-s}(\nu^{K}_{s-} - \delta_{\xi^{u,K}_{s-}},R^{K}_{s})}  \\ 
    & \hspace{3 cm} - X^{K}_{t-s}(\nu^{K}_{s-},R^{K}_{s}) ] \mathcal{N}'(\mathrm{d}s,\mathrm{d}u,\mathrm{d}h), 
