where for all $t \geq 0$, $V^{K}_{t}$ is the set containing alive individuals at time $t$, and $\xi^{u,K}_{t}$ are individual energies, defined and actualized over time with the same conventions as in Section~(sec:construction of the paper), simply replacing the flow $X$ by $X^{K}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.639221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca70fbf4efba17a26cd370e2ded9b882cef4c6aea487ea8314b0bbbfbe1ae4ad","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm P^hk strong conv to hatP of arXiv:2411.13765, 'Schr\"odinger Bridge Problem for Jump Diffusions'] Suppose that Assumption \textup{(Assumption:Hypo of the paper)} holds for $\set{P_{s,t}(x,\cdot):0\leq s\leq t\leq T,x\in\mathbb{R}^n}$ the transition distribution  under the strong Markov reference measure $\mathbf{R}$. Let $\mathbf{P},\hat\mathbf{P}$ be the same as in Lemma (lem:from bR to bP of the paper) and $g_k,f_k$, $k\geq1$ be as in Lemma (lem:f_k,g_k approximation convergence of the paper). For every $k\geq 1$, we define 
\begin{equation}
    h_k(t,x):=\int_{\mathbb{R}^n}g_k(y)P_{t,T}(x,dy)\text{ for }(t,x)\in[0,T]\times\mathbb{R}^n,
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
    \mathbf{P}^{h_k}:=\frac{\mathbbm{1}_{\left\{ X_0\in A_k \right\}}}{r_k}\frac{h_k(T,X_T)}{h_k(0,X_0)}\mathbf{P},
\end{equation}
where $A_k:=\set{x\in\mathbb{R}^n:h_k(0,x)>0}$ and $r_k:=\rho_0(A_k)$. 
Then $\set{\mathbf{P}^{h_k}}_{k \geq 1}$ is a sequence of $h$-transforms by harmonic functions, and  $\mathbf{P}^{h_k}$ converges to $\hat\mathbf{P}$ in the strong topology in the sense that \[\lim_{k\to\infty}\sup_{A\in\mathcal F}|\mathbf{P}^{h_k}(A)-\hat{\mathbf{P}}(A)|=0.\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.309814+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca737046f4013ac6931c1720047c41a961b7ed8b9824a2cd573faced6b8aa7e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:covindfn of arXiv:2411.08848, 'Stationary random measures: Covariance asymptotics, variance bounds and central limit theo'] Let ${\mathcal X}$ be a stationary random measure whose truncated correlation measure ${\bf K}$ has finite total variation. Assume that $A$ and $B$ are bounded open sets with $C^1$-smooth boundaries.  Let ${\mathcal X}_L$ be the scaled random measure defined by ${\mathcal X}_L(A) := {\mathcal X}(LA)$,  $L \geq 1$.  Then

\begin{enumerate}
\item $L^{-d}\mathrm{Cov}({\mathcal X}_L(A),{\mathcal X}_L(B)) \to Q_0^{{\bf K}}(f,g) = (\lambda_D + \int {\bf K} ) \, |A \cap B|, $ where $| \cdot |$ is the Lebesgue measure. 
\item If $\lambda_D + \int {\bf K} = 0$ and further $\int |z||{\bf K}|(\mathrm{d} z)<\infty$, then it holds that

\begin{equation}

L^{-d+1}\mathrm{Cov}({\mathcal X}_L(A),{\mathcal X}_L(B))  \to  -\frac12 \int_{\partial A\cap \partial B} \varepsilon(x) \left[\int |z\cdot N_A(x)| \ {\bf K}(\mathrm{d} z) \, \right] \, \sigma_A(\mathrm{d} x),
\end{equation}

where $N_A(x)$ is the exterior normal to $A$ at $x$ and $\sigma_A$ is the surface area measure of $\partial A$. Further, $\varepsilon(x) \in \{+1,0,-1\}$ is defined as follows: $\varepsilon(x) = +1$ (resp. $-1$) if $N_A(x)$ is the exterior (resp. interior) normal to $B$ at $x$, and $0$ otherwise. 
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.062026+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca7b832be2bc82876b0893f426b28589358d5472de5e9e6b5453e1147b8b5190","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 10 of arXiv:2606.27078, 'Semimartingale Optimal Transport with Jumps: A General Framework and Equivalent Formulatio'] Let $\Theta$ be measurable. Moreover, let the cost function $\ell$ satisfy Assumption~\ref{L}. Then, for any probability measure $\mu$ on $\bigl([0,1]\times\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{R}^{d^2}\times\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{N}},
