{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.525239+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca8a9afb36c8ba8e6cd07d119cae38f660616ecc909f7d8469ec7c9631bc8465","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma frechet of arXiv:2507.01406, '{\Large On Iterated Lorenz Curves with Applications: The Multivariate Case }'] Let $A\in \mathcal{A}$ and $h\in C([0,1])$. Then 
\begin{equation}
DT_{A}[h](x)=\frac{-\int_{0}^{q(x)}(2-2t)\,h(t)\,dt+\tau
(x)\int_{0}^{1}(2-2t)\,h(t)\,dt}{M}.  
\end{equation}
Consequently, 
\begin{equation}
