{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.520624+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_caf85aec40007de080bafc2889a0a9897df3c867017482f3313d214de2cb617f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 (Pointwise minimal radial envelope) of arXiv:2609.02595, 'Minimal Radial Sub-Gamma Envelopes for Infinitely Divisible Random Vectors'] The function \(C_X\) is admissible. If \(q\) is any admissible radial denominator, then
