{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.529440+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cafb3688f1b6fd89178afd1046433517aaa8ac8ebeff7fd467b9efa61d2a34ae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq.tailWellConnected of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For every $\mathfrak{p} \in (\mathfrak{p}_c, 1]$, there exist two finite positive constants $C(d,\mathfrak{p})$ and $c(d,\mathfrak{p}) \in (0, \frac{1}{2}]$ such that 
