{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.876553+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbca456dc612a95f47db629b505614b60d72f7b7b71102c04fe222fc53e6ed6d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Thomeo of arXiv:2605.07920, 'Primitive Sequences for Probability Measures on Compact Intervals'] Equip $\pazocal{P}_{[a,b]}$ with the weak topology and $\pazocal{S}^{\mathrm{adm}}_{[a,b]}$ with the subspace topology inherited from the product topology on $\prod_{n = 0}^\infty [0, (b-a)^n/n!]$. Then the primitive sequence map $S$ is a homeomorphism between $\pazocal{P}_{[a,b]}$ and $\pazocal{S}^{\mathrm{adm}}_{[a,b]}$; in particular, for $\mu_k, \mu \in \pazocal{P}_{[a,b]}$ with $k \geq 1$, 
