The same estimates hold in the non-weighted case $\rho = 1$, in which case, in the last estimate, one has simply $\|v\|_{L^\infty([0,T],\mathbb R^d)}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.250962+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cc088ce4f0da74cb9676ba084e0b613b0e2937a7249a49cb0fab88f569340fe1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:bounded-X-gambles of arXiv:2512.21026, 'Minimax Duality in Game-Theoretic Probability\thanks{Work in progress: mistakes are likely'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{Z})$ be a gamble space, and $X:\Omega\to\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ a variable.
