{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:16:46.105608+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cc168c92cbe2841c0eedd1eae4b404160f0059e58f290956eafdcd43f0caae08","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lm:shockasymorder of arXiv:2604.12963, 'Shocks, instability, and the twenty networks\\ of infinite geodesics in the Directed Lands'] For all $\omega\in\Omega_0$, $s$, $\theta$, and $x<y$ in $\mathbb{R}$, and any $\theta+$ shock interface $\tau^+$ from $(x,s)$ and $\theta-$ shock interface $\tau^-$ from $(y,s)$, 
