{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.947654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cc23925b82bb14bc05d7d8f49cde557c2c2c2b51c51c125176c317c2678800ef","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 (Weighted core balls) of arXiv:2607.13183, '2607.13183'] Let $k=\lfloor\eps^{-1}\rfloor$.  There are absolute constants
