{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.683833+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cc5aabcbdd51e380dc3b794d5917d4523e6519fbfd060a8948ccf652397d2999","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 21 of arXiv:2609.03777, '2609.03777'] Let $k,k_1,k_2\in\ZZ_{\geq3}$ and $r\geq0$. There exists a real number $M\geq0$ such that for $\tau\in C$ and $N\in\ZZ_{>0}$, we have
