{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.988140+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cce8b115aa3bb31de04e939bdbcaa449de427869b55ffb992e365544c4ea8f16","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 62 (cf. {\cite[Lemma 3.2) of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] {Mak24}}] 
    Suppose $ \log n \ll np \ll \sqrt{n}$ and let $\epsilon = \epsilon(n) > 0$ be such that $\sqrt{\log n/ np} \ll \epsilon < 1/2$. There exists some universal constant $C > 0$ such that for any $K > 0$ the following holds with probability at least $1 - O(n^{-K})$: 
