{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.624103+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd6108ae005cf29d7cfd9b28620a606670f142b90e911e02a048369569f8c082","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Definition of mixing of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] A sublinear expectation system $(\Omega, \mathcal{H}, (U_t)_{t\in \mathbb T}, \hat{\mathbb{E}})$ ($\mathbb T=\mathbb N, \mathbb Z, \mathbb R_+, \mathbb R$) is called mixing if for any $X\in \mathcal{H}^{d_1},Y \in \mathcal{H}^{d_2}$ and $\phi \in C_{lip}(\mathbb{R}^{d_1+d_2})$, we have
