{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.812540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd88d4f127fbd7aa9cf58437030cd5f2f0d2450e62cc4d67d0e80489513cb12a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:bd_It of arXiv:2411.09482, 'Anomalous Regularization in Kazantsev-Kraichnan Model'] Take $s\in (0,d/2)$ and $\alpha\in (0,1)$. Then we have, as $|n|\to\infty$,
