{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.313235+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cde66eb2219d0178a69b321401fec47d73bb7e7dac82351425e27d43d7e66a47","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2607.23305, 'On extremes of a random walk with positive drift\\ over an intermediate regularly varying '] Assume that $a:=\E\xi>0$ and that the distribution of $\tau$ is intermediate regularly varying at infinity.
If
\begin{eqnarray}
x \P\{\xi>x\} &=& o(\P\{\tau>x\})\quad\mbox{as }x\to\infty,
\end{eqnarray}
then 
\begin{eqnarray}
\P\{M_\tau>x\} &\le& (1+o(1))\P\{\tau>x/a\}\quad\mbox{as  } x\to\infty.
\end{eqnarray}
If
\begin{eqnarray}
\int_x^\infty \P\{\xi<-y\}dy &=& o(\P\{\tau>x\})\quad\mbox{as }x\to\infty,
\end{eqnarray}
then 
\begin{eqnarray}
\P\{S_\tau>x\} &\ge& (1+o(1))\P\{\tau>x/a\}\quad\mbox{as  } x\to\infty.
