If both conditions, \eqref{F.tau.cond.sstar.upper} and \eqref{F.tau.cond.sstar.lower}, hold true then 
\begin{eqnarray}
\P\{M_\tau>x\}\ \sim\ \P\{S_\tau>x\} &\sim& \P\{\tau>x/a\}\quad\mbox{as  } x\to\infty.
\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.781824+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdeaabada1425ff8810bedf34c328c9218784640d098ab18e4892a0fe91c12e1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 34 (Multiplication between the $n$th and first chaos) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] Assume $f\in\H^{\otimes n}$ and $g\in\H$. Then 
