	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:05:57.807692+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce0d8d843980d6b7c763bffc4324e183569eb229917636bb01c6dcdfd214905c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2608.30570, '2608.30570'] (\cite{HL2})
		On a 2 dimensional translating soliton $\Sigma$ in ${\mathbb R}^4$, the following identity holds:


