{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.723252+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce103e3b92c9fea1ba521b9a6d1863e5068523a422f4a34e264f105fe0e97c2e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 33 (Scaling law, mixed-damping regime) of arXiv:2609.02728, 'Momentum in large-batch training: Polyak enlarges the critical batch size, Nesterov improv'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:diagonal-covariance} and~\ref{ass:power-law}, assuming the stability condition \(\eta\lesssim\min\{1, B^\beta(1-\rho)\}\), for the mixed-damping regime $\eta\gtrsim(1-\rho)^2$ with $k \gtrsim \max\left\{\frac{1}{1-\rho}, \frac{1-\rho}{\eta}\right\}$, the expected excess risk satisfies:
