{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:06.978771+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce1cb04d9f402d251ef4e07facf73b4c5abc264fd1f7332f350c27cdb016805e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:scaling-form of arXiv:2607.26169, 'Scaling and partial universality of the height zero probability in the 2D Abelian sandpile'] Let $\mathcal{G}$ satisfy Assumption (a:graph of the paper).  
Suppose that $U \subsetneq \mathbb{C}$ satisfies Assumption (a:U of the paper). \\
(i) There is a constant $c_\mathcal{G}$, only depending on $\mathcal{G}$, and a real-valued function $f_U(z)$, only depending on $U$, such that
\eqn{e:asymp-formula}
{ p_{U,\varepsilon}(0;z)
  = p_\mathcal{G}(0) + c_\mathcal{G} f_U(z) \varepsilon^2 + \mathcal{O}(\varepsilon^3), \quad \text{as $\varepsilon \to 0$.} }
(ii) The function $f_U(z)$ is conformally covariant with scale dimension $2$. \\
(iii) If $U$ is simply-connected, then
