{ f_U(z)
  = 2 |\phi'_U(z)|^{2}, }
where $\phi_U : U \to \mathbb{D}$ is (any) conformal map such that $\phi_U(z) = o$. \\
(iv) We have $f_U > 0$ and $c_G > 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.328570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce1e9faf51d0e61da4014b46eea2d76accff6c6ddb43aed6f4a509f37f77e8d8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma ev_V-cc of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] In the situation of the previous corollary, both the functor $\ev_V\colon{\mathfrak d\kern-.25pt}{\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_\textup{$G$-lvl}\to{{\mathfrak S\kern-.4pt}}_{\textup{$({\textup{O}}(V)\times G)$-gl},*}$ and the composite $((eq:semifree-corep of the paper))$ are cocontinuous.
    \begin{proof}
        In light of Lemma (lemma:id-g-fixed-points-vs-ev of the paper), it suffices to prove the first statement. For this it is in turn enough to verify preservation of coproducts and pushouts.

        For coproducts, let $(X_i)_{i\in I}$ be any family of cofibrant objects of $\cat{$\bm G$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Sp}$. By Corollary~(cor:SpL-level-hcof of the paper), each $X_i(V)$ is well-based, so that the inclusions $X_i(V)\to\bigvee_{i\in I}X_i(V)=\big(\bigvee_{i\in I}X_i\big)(V)$ exhibit the latter as a coproduct in the underlying $\infty$-category of $\cat{$\bm{({\textup{O}}(V)\times G)}$-$\textbf{\textup{L}}$-Top}_*$ by Lemma~(lemma:coprod-well-based of the paper), as desired.

        The statement about pushouts follows in the same way from Corollary~(cor:SpL-level-hcof of the paper) together with Lemma~(lemma:h-cof-compute-po of the paper)(2).
    \end{proof}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.369992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce1ec3a455102d14f0f73e0c7187fa7e92b10fa42400ab8808a8fcef2a6cf635","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Propo pro:aprioriestim of arXiv:2412.01673, 'Spatial SIR epidemic model with varying infectivity without movement of individuals'] Let $T>0$, and let $(\overline{\mu}^S,\overline{\mu}^{\mathfrak{F}} )$  be a solution of the first two equations of (equation syst of the paper). Then there exists  positive constants $C$ 	
