{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:32:58.301585+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce461d67fbbe1dadcdca334acb4fdb55cf30e192fa136ac0c7138d4d68d93f91","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:HDL_volume of arXiv:2505.10256, 'Stochastic Oscillators out of equilibrium:\\ scaling limits and correlation estimates'] Let $v_0$ be a bounded real-valued measurable function on $\mathbb T$ and let $\{\mu_N\}_{N\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence of probability measures on $\Omega_N$ associated to $v_0$ and assume that $\{\mu_N\}_{N\in\mathbb N}$ satisfies Assumption (assump:initial_measure of the paper).  
