{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.054663+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce4d9f229463b8108d60da879c87d3d82423e7e8801f4be45c30d88f85c24fde","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 (Lipschitz continuity of $\psi_\circ$) of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] For every $q, q' \in \mcl Q$ taking a finite number of values, we have
