{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.958189+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce52078efd93bc22042426b3b859f157d850b827b34308eb96ae623134f16faa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Uniform Malliavin--Sobolev approximation) of arXiv:2608.08177, 'Uniform-in-Time Smoluchowski--Kramers Approximation\\ in Total Variation for Fractional SD'] Suppose \Cref{ass:smooth,ass:dissipative} hold.  Let $p\ge2$ and
$\rho<2H-1$.  Then there exist $\mu_0\in(0,1]$ and $C<\infty$ such that
\begin{equation}
