where $L=\floor{\frac{\log n}{100}}.$ The estimate is uniform in the $\mathcal{F}_{k_*}$-measurable choice of $A_*$ and in $\lambda>0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.931667+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce5be7b8e88be1a4344d6d2559f544beeba8216ac78fb1ed1c8122f02bc93cb0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 20 (Control on the negative moments of $\sttm_k$) of arXiv:2506.19123, 'The longest increasing subsequence of Brownian separable permutons'] Let $0<\xi < \alpha$. Then we have
