{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.988628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce99f56a928bcf1729079b85d47da2d2f986a0b75bdc5f48bcc04751a0e9e16a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop thm:herm_pieri of arXiv:2412.05999, 'Non-Archimedean GUE corners and Hecke modules'] For any $\nu \in \Sig_n, \mu \in \Sig_{n-1}$ and $D$ large enough so that all $n$-tuples below are valid signatures, 
