{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:24:45.891385+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ceb7c4d6d46c3c93316f660ce1137a32e9ca8d75b0cb21554760bcd2b2dcb6ba","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2509.02996, 'Group-averaged Markov chains: mixing improvement'] Let $G$ be a locally compact topological group with Haar measure $\mu$ that acts on $\mathcal{X}$, and assume that $\pi$ is $G$-invariant. For $P \in \mathcal{L}(\pi)$, we have
