{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.353669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cee4100f2a16c0e185c6e29a822647a68a3e81930b6b85d0a930a16eeabf46c2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop.vnupperbound of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] For each $p > 4$, there is a constant $C_p > 0$ such that for all $n \in {\mathbb N}$, $k_0 \in \{0,1,\dots,n\}$, and $\bm{x} \in {\mathbb R}^n$, we have
