{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.724482+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ceec619eec494f12508d7b39682e8b5fe7a9db012a1d5d05e3bf8bb9fc95fd47","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem4new of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] Fix $T >0$,  $\lambda=(\lambda_k)_{k \in \mathbb{N}_0}$, and  $\mu\in \mathcal B$ such that
$$(\lambda_0\mu_0,\lambda_1\mu_1,\lambda_2\mu_2,\ldots)\in \mathcal{S}^*.$$
Assume that
$$\mathcal A (\lambda_k\frac{(\cdot)^k}{k!})(x)=\sum_{j=0}^\infty \beta_{kj}(\lambda_j\frac{x^j}{j!}-\lambda_k\frac{x^k}{k!})+\beta_k\lambda_k\frac {x^k}{k!}$$
for some $\beta_{kj}\in \mathbb R_+$ and $\beta_k\in \mathbb R$ such that $\sup_{k\geq 0}\beta_k^+<\infty$ and $\lim_{j\to\infty}\beta_{kj}=0$ for each $k\in \mathbb{N}_0$. 
If for all $x\in (-\epsilon,1+\epsilon)$ the sequence 
\begin{equation}
\Big(\lambda_k\frac{x^k}{k!},\sum_{j=0}^\infty \beta_{kj}(\lambda_j\frac{x^j}{j!}-\lambda_k\frac{x^k}{k!})\Big)_{k\in\mathbb{N}_0}
\end{equation}
lies in the bounded pointwise closure of 
\begin{equation*}
\Big\{\Big(\mathbf{a}_k,\sum_{j=0}^\infty \beta_{kj}(\mathbf{a}_j-\mathbf{a}_k)\Big)_{k\in \mathbb{N}_0}\colon \mathbf{a}=(\mathbf{a}_k)_{k=0}^N,\quad N\in \mathbb{N}\Big\},
\end{equation*}
then the linear ODE given by (equation eq:ODE sequence space holomorphic of the paper) admits a solution $({\bf c}(t))_{t\in[0,T]}$ satisfying (equation eq: ODE pointwise of the paper) for each $x\in S$ of the form  ${\bf c}_k(t)=\lambda_k\mu_k(t)$ for some $\mu_k(t)\geq0$. If $\beta_k\leq 0$ for each $k$, then  $\sum_{k=0}^\infty\mu_k(t)\leq \sum_{k=0}^\infty\mu_k$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.563685+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ceefcaf4a54c0b4498ac0fbd6ec8e31d53bf639007c566c9cf6c7e7453c71ab3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 (The $m$th-order Santal\'o inequality on $\R^n$) of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Fix $Q\in\conbodo[m].$ Let $K\subset \R^n$ be a compact set of positive volume such that $K$ or $K^\circ$ has center of mass at the origin. Then,
