{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.980206+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cef0c7d8e07cb6fc9759bcfeb4272fe79a5ccd070635881dfd512a862da6927c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eqn|CatsAndDogs of arXiv:2504.08938, 'Fourier Levels and Almost Sure Bounds on Higher-Order Derivatives in First-Passage Percola'] If $n$ and $k$ are non-negative integers, and $A$ an integer such that $n+A\in[0,k+n]$, the following holds
