{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.525109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cef83ac024c3d535151e163b0941c5fa7faaef4091b62c88b24918b2787d2343","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor Lp_concentration of arXiv:2411.03482, 'Ergodicity of 2D singular stochastic Navier--Stokes equations'] There exists some constant $C$ such that for any $t \in [0, 1]$, $N\in \mathbf{N}^*$ and $\gamma > 0$, we have 
