{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.086098+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ceff5a9d1464289ccd830066f8d3ca25911bf4b4427254ffa18f21fbf88787da","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 15 of arXiv:2607.13849, 'Rearranged Stochastic Heat Equation with an Entropy Gradient Structure'] Let $h \in {T/{\mathbb N}^*}$
and $\varphi \in {\mathcal C}^1({\mathbb S}) \cap {\mathcal U}^2({\mathbb S})$ such that $\varphi'({\mathbf x})=0$ if,  for some $\varsigma \in (0,1/4)$, ${\mathbf x} 
\in \cup_{k \in {\mathbb Z}/2}
(k-\varsigma,k+\varsigma)$. For a given $\varepsilon >0$, let 
\begin{equation}
   E_\varepsilon(\mathbf{x}) := {\varepsilon}\begin{cases} 1& \,\,{x}\in [0,1/2)+{\mathbb Z},
