\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.855015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf02479d561a738327b377ca336c805060a5bca015e58266154ab201cb24dea0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem RLD_rec of arXiv:2607.12061, 'Models for species evolution with random deaths'] Let $f^\ddagger_c = \frac{qr}{p-q(1-r)}$ and suppose $p>q$. 
