{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.182882+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf035ecee912d172d6ee6d2003b3d01fce23a04f6c3814acf2e4bd551b6be6f3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:HittingTimesGeneralCheeger of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Let $\varepsilon \in (0,1]$, and let $C$ be as in Lemma~(lem:revprelim of the paper). Suppose that the single ball chains are reversible and $\Phi_{\ast}^{(n)} = \Omega(n^{\alpha - 1})$ for some $\alpha \in (0,1]$. Let $k = \floor{\frac{1}{\alpha}}$. Further, let
    \begin{equation*}
        t_n = \frac{mn}{\gamma_n} \brac{\frac{1}{2} \log n + (k+1)\log(2dm)}, \text{ and } t_n' = \frac{mn}{\gamma_n} \brac{\frac{1}{2} \log n - \log(2C)},
    \end{equation*}
    for $n \in \mathbb{N}$. Then for all $\mathbf{x} \in \Omega_n$ and $n$ large enough, we have
