{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:14:37.619033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf06598a305a079faa7613af0279649bbe6b87ceb714b8b697a16d0ad382fe7f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2608.19065, 'Boundedly exchangeable graphs'] For any $B \in \widehat{\Bcal}(S)$ with $\pbb(\nu(B) = 0) < 1$, let $W_B$ and $W'_B$ be two local graphons for $\xi$ on $B$. Then there exist $\lambda\vert_{[0,1]}$-preserving transformations $T, T' : [0,1] \to [0,1]$ such that
