{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.901478+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf14a23e65f69c098e5c9dfa36a834e2be08664623e334443fc4d9f7f2b1738d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 (Differentiation in the Cameron--Martin space directions) of arXiv:2608.02417, 'A Bismut--Elworthy--Li formula for linear stochastic evolution equations in Banach spaces'] Let \(R\in \gamma(\scrH,E)\), and let \(g:E\to\R\) be bounded and Borel measurable. Then for every \(h\in \scrH\) the map
