{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.190833+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf4cf6a909c2139a560a54ac85b3d2c99650ec13d92655cffe26cd14022214aa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 25 of arXiv:2604.19200, 'Stochastic $\Sigma$-convergence in Orlicz setting and Applications'] The $H$-algebra $A$ (of class $\mathcal{C}^{\infty}$) on $\mathbb{R}^{d}_{y}$ is said to be stochastic $\Phi$-proper (resp. stochastic $\Phi$-pseudoproper) if the following two conditions are satisfied: 
