    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.999812+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf583ac78485e55ad8427748d9383d816bda1c0535868378e24091b583ac2054","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 1 (Indistinguishability) of arXiv:2512.02766, 'Fine-Graining and Continuous Space Scaling Limit of the $H^{2|2}$ Model on the Hierarchica'] Given a finite weighted graph $\mathcal{G}=(V,E,W)$, we say that a subset $U\subset V$ is \emph{indistinguishable from outside} if
\begin{equation*}
    \forall i,j\in U, \forall k\notin U,\quad W_{ki}=W_{kj}.
\end{equation*}
If additionally a boundary condition $\eta\in \mathbb{R}_{+}^{V}$ is given, $U$ is indistinguishable from outside if additionally
$$\forall i,j\in U,\ \eta_{i}=\eta_{j}.$$
In words, for a given vertex $k$ not in $U$, it is connected to all vertices in $U$ with the same weight.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.572074+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf5f9849a82cbc0ce122995119e1e5a0cf47ca0a40dda07548e5d5f9edf224f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:HAtInfty of arXiv:2602.05317, 'Strong local nondeterminism for stochastic time-fractional\\ slow and fast diffusion equat'] Suppose $\alpha>0$, $\beta\in(0,2]$, $\gamma \ge 0$, and $d \in \mathbb{N}$.
  Denote the following cases:
  \begin{multicols}{2}
    \begin{itemize}

