{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.220730+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf8f49368b6f04cfb6339e62bcd6f2bb6bfc5b90f8442caf8838b910202e0a7d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma intrep of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] Let $\varepsilon = - \log q$. Then for every $x\in \mathbb{C}\backslash\{0\}$ and $t\ge 0$
