{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.192276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cfccaf441dca0394055729231f7de40d92cf537462ce6b9d92516b383c595b53","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 12 (Bounding  star discrepancy discrepancy by $L^1$-Wasserstein distance) of arXiv:2605.03528, '\bf Kolmogorov-Smirnov distance and discrepancies {\em versus} Wasserstein distances'] Let $\nu $ be an absolutely  continuous distribution on $\R^d$
with density $g\!\in {\cal L}^{\frac{r}{r-1}}(\R^d, \lambda_d)$ for some $r\!\in (1,+\infty]$ and finite first moment. Then, for every probability distribution  $\mu$ on $\R^d$with  finite first moment,
\begin{equation}
D^\star(\mu,\nu)\le C_{r,d}{\cal W}^{\ell^\infty}_1(\mu,\nu)^{\frac{d}{r+d}} \big \| g\big\|^{\frac{r}{r+d}}_{{\cal L}^{\frac{r}{r-1}}(\lambda_d)}.
\end{equation}
with $C_{r,d} =  \begin{pmatrix}r+d \\ r \end{pmatrix}^{-\frac{1}{r+d}}\bigg( \Big(\frac dr\Big)^{\frac{r}{r+d}} + \Big(\frac rd\Big)^{\frac{d}{r+d}} \bigg)$ for $r\ge 1$.

If $g$ is bounded, one has:
\[
D^\star(\mu,\nu)\le C_{1,d}{\cal W}^{\ell^\infty}_1(\mu,\nu)^{\frac{d}{d+1}} \big\| g\big\|^{\frac{1}{d+1}}_{\infty}.

\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

