 \quad\text{for each } x \in \Upsilon_\Gamma \quad\text{as } t \searrow 0 .
 \]
 That is, the spectral dimension of the \clekp{} Brownian motion is $2\dcle/(\dcle+\resexp)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.076174+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cffe4bb056fb696abff094a413e6f2f65dca3e664c62cc0572d3815d2b8af959","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi eq:fegee of arXiv:2507.00737, 'Dispersion models on a circle: universal properties and asymptotic results'] Define the ``collecting path'' process $S:=(S_x,0\leq x \leq 1)$ by 
	\begin{equation} S_x =  -x + \sum_{j=0}^{k-1} m_j \1_{u_j\leq x},~~~\textrm{for }x \in[0,1].\end{equation}
