{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.657636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0449145880219ad03671ea13dc785415bddd8e1be5e428fee3daf04c734c2c8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn \cite{JamneshanMachado} of arXiv:2605.16921, '${\ASL_n}(\mathbb Z)$ invariant random subsets of $\mathbb Z^n$'] We call a \emph{bundle of nilsystems (of dimension $\leq k$) over $\Omega$} any $\mathbb{Z}^d$-system constructed from the following data:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item a standard Borel probability space $(\Omega, \nu)$;
    \item a countable Borel partition $(\Omega_n)_{n \geq 0}$ of $\Omega$ and a countable family of nilmanifolds $(N_n/\Gamma_n)_{n \geq 0}$ of dimension $\leq k$;
    \item Borel maps $\rho_n: \Omega_n \to \Hom(\mathbb{Z}^d, N_n)$ such that for $\nu$-a.e. $\omega \in \Omega_n$, the action of $\rho_n(\omega)$ on $N_n/\Gamma_n$ is ergodic.
\end{enumerate}
The space
$$ X := \bigsqcup_{n \geq 0} \Omega_n \times N_n/\Gamma_n,$$
equipped with the measure
$$\sum_{n \geq 0} \nu_{|\Omega_n} \otimes \mu_{N_n/\Gamma_n}$$
and the $\mathbb{Z}^d$-action defined for $(\omega, \overline{n}) \in \Omega_n \times (N_n/\Gamma_n)$ and $t \in \mathbb{Z}^d$ by
$$ t \cdot (\omega, \overline{n}) = (\omega, \rho_n(\omega)(t) \cdot \overline{n}),$$
is denoted
$$ \bigsqcup_{n \geq 0} \Omega_n \rtimes_{\rho_n} N_n/\Gamma_n.$$
The natural map $\bigsqcup_{n \geq 0} \Omega_n \rtimes_{\rho_n} N_n/\Gamma_n \to \Omega$ is called the \emph{bundle projection}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.337858+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0461721b6731ee003338d32510267db379bd51271cad19678f364bd9bb6f2a7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 1 of arXiv:2512.05687, '$L^p$-Boltzmann-Gibbs principle \\ via Littlewood-Paley-Stein inequality'] For functions $F=F(\phi)$ and $G=G(\phi) \in C^2(\R^N)$, if all integrals
in the following converge, we have
\begin{align*} 
& \int_{\R^N} GL_0F d\hat\mu_{N,m} = \int_{\R^N} FL_0G d\hat\mu_{N,m}
= -\frac12 \int_{\R^N} \sum_{x\in \T_N} \partial_{\phi(x)} F \cdot \partial_{\phi(x)} G \, d\hat\mu_{N,m}, \\
& \int_{\R^N} G L_1 F d\hat\mu_{N,m} = -\int_{\R^N} F L_1 G d\hat\mu_{N,m},
\intertext{and}
& \Ga(F) = \sum_{x\in \T_N} \big(\partial_{\phi(x)} F\big)^2 =: |D_\phi F|^2,
\end{align*}
where $D_\phi F = (\partial_{\phi(x)} F)_{x\in \T_N}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.607414+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d046f84179841aab8e4c62bc55b9902f72b82acf7e705788454a8463e824eb84","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2506.08775, 'Markovian multivariate Hawkes population processes: Efficient evaluation of moments'] If $\bm{C}_{i}^{m_{i}\times m_{i}}$ is invertible for all $i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}$,
then 
\begin{align} 
\begin{split}
\begin{bmatrix} \bm{\Psi}^{(0,1)}_t \\ 
    \vdots \\
    \bm{\Psi}^{(0,n)}_t\end{bmatrix}
    &= e^{\bm{A}_{n}^{\mathfrak{m}_{n}\times\mathfrak{m}_{n}}t}
    \begin{bmatrix} \bm{\Psi}^{(0,1)}_0 \\ 
    \vdots \\
    \bm{\Psi}^{(0,n)}_0\end{bmatrix}
    -\left(\bm{A}_{n}^{\mathfrak{m}_{n}\times\mathfrak{m}_{n}}\right)^{-1}\left(\bm{I}^{\mathfrak{m}_{n}\times\mathfrak{m}_{n}} - e^{\bm{A}_{n}^{\mathfrak{m}_{n}\times\mathfrak{m}_{n}}t}\right)\begin{bmatrix}
    \bm{b}^{2\times 1}  \\
    \bm{0}^{(\mathfrak{m}_{n}-m_{1})\times 1}
    \end{bmatrix}.
\end{split}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.017838+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d047292eb4c1dbfd61300fa1227bc51da922cf30d38da7744dd42e6177c7bf0c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2608.26288, 'Muon with Finite Newton--Schulz: The Smoothing Benefit in Nonsmooth Nonconvex Optimization'] Suppose~\cref{ass:general-spectral-link} holds and let $(C_t)_{t\geq1}$ be a positive sequence.
For any $t\geq1$, the action~\cref{eq:general-spectral-action} is the FTRL update
\begin{equation}
  X_t^h
  =-D\nabla\widetilde\Phi_{h,C_t}(M_{t-1})
  \in\argmin_{\lVert X\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leq D}
  \left\{
    \inpr*{\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\beta^{-s}G_s,X}
    +\frac{R_{h,C_t}(X)}{(1-\beta)\beta^{t-1}}
  \right\},

\end{equation}
where the regularizer $R_{h,C}$ is given by
\begin{equation}
  R_{h,C}(X)
  \coloneqq D\widetilde\Phi_{h,C}^*(X/D)
  =DC\sum_{i=1}^r
  \phi_h^*\left(\frac{\sigma_i(X)}{D}\right).

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.714000+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d047d19a7ad48576774e4dba7e19b92ea9b9501db98c585967f07891dfa215ba","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:1103.7 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Fix $u \geq 0$ and, for each $n \geq 1$, some deterministic subset $\widetilde{{\rm D}}_n \subseteq \mathbb{Z}^2$. In addition, let us set
	\begin{equation}
		{\rm W}^{\widetilde{{\rm D}}_n}_n(u) = {\rm W}_n(u) \cap \widetilde{{\rm D}}_n
		\quad ; \qquad 
		{\mathbf W}^{\widetilde{{\rm D}}_n}_n(u) := \big\{ z \in \mathbb{X}_{n-r_n} :\: {\rm W}^{\widetilde{{\rm D}}_n} \cap {\rm Q}(z;n-r_n) \neq \emptyset\} \,.
	\end{equation}
	Then,
	\begin{equation}
		\lim_{\delta \downarrow 0} \limsup_{n \to \infty}
		\mathbb{P} \bigg( \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}|{\mathbf W}^{\widetilde{{\rm D}}_n}_n(u)| > \delta^{-1} \sqrt{|{\rm D}_n^\circ \cap \widetilde{{\rm D}}_n|/|{\rm D}_n|} \bigg) = 0 \,.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.319687+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d04941ea4eda0c7478197b647fb02aa92679917019b3bf78e09242a2e70019c7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:one_step_improvement_intro of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] There exists $\gamma_0>0$, a spatial scale $\eta\in (0,1/4]$ and a frequency $L_0\geq 1$ such that for every $N\geq L_0$, it holds that
\begin{align}

\Big({\mathbf E}\Big\|v^N-\fint_{\eta B} v^N\Big\|_{\underline{L}^2(\eta Q)}^r \Big)^{1/r}
&
\leq \eta^{\gamma_0}\Big({\mathbf E}\Big\|v^N-\fint_{B} v^N\Big\|_{\underline{L}^2( Q)}^r \Big)^{1/r}\\ 
\nonumber
&+ \mathscr{C}_Q[\pi^N,(\widetilde{\pi}^N_{k,\alpha})_{k,\alpha},F,G],
\end{align}
where the last term collects the contributions of pressures and forcing at the scale $Q$ (see Subsection (ss:role_pressure_intro of the paper) for details on the former). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.068262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d04bf4c6bd63900a747bab0ae51926fd339773282cd63cb61d9e8b59a0bbe7cc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2606.00945, 'Ising model and percolation: from hexagonal lattice to 3-12 lattice'] For a general polygon $(\Omega;y_1,\ldots,y_{2N})$, the pure partition functions for multiple $\SLE_{\kappa}$ are defined as 
\begin{align*}
    \LZ_{\alpha}^{(\kappa)}(\Omega;y_1,\ldots,y_{2N}):=\prod_{i=1}^{2N}|\varphi'(y_i)|^h\times \LZ_{\alpha}^{(\kappa)}(\varphi(y_1),\ldots,\varphi(y_{2N})), \qquad\text{for }\alpha\in\LP_N, 
\end{align*}
where $\varphi:\Omega\to \HH$ is a conformal mapping such that $\varphi(y_1)<\cdots<\varphi(y_{2N})$. By M\"obius covariance~\eqref{eqn::COV}, this definition is independent of the choice of $\varphi$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.593333+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d04ce00762dc116757a3036e86009c8967f7c406b46c049fbaf6e9cd06944192","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-5 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] Suppose Assumption~(ass-1 of the paper) holds. For each~$b\ge2$ there exists~$\epsilon>0$ and, for all~$\beta>0$ with~$1<b\theta<1+\epsilon$, there exist $\eta>0$, $C>0$ and a sequence $\{\lambda_\star(q)\}_{q\in\mathbb Z}$ with $\lambda_\star(0)=1$, $\lambda_\star(q)\le\theta^{q^2}$ for~$q\in\mathbb Z$ and
\begin{equation}

0<\lambda_\star(q)=\lambda_\star(-q)\le \bigl(2b^{1/2}\sqrt{b\theta-1}\,\bigr)^{|q|},\quad q\in\mathbb Z,
\end{equation}
for which the following is true: For all initial~$\nu$ subject to Assumption~(ass-2 of the paper) there exists~$k_0\ge0$ such that for all integer $n$ and~$k$ with $\min\{k,n-k\}\ge k_0$ and all~$q\in\mathbb Z$,
\begin{equation}

a_k(q)\le a_k(0) \bigl(2b^{1/2}\sqrt{b\theta-1}\,\bigr)^{|q|}
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}

\biggl|\frac{a_k(q)}{a_k(0)}-\lambda_\star(q)\biggr|\le C^{|q|}\biggl[\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{-\eta k}+\sum_{j=0}^k\text{\rm  e}\mkern0.7mu^{-\eta(k-j)}\,\fraktura d_{\min\{j,n-j\}}\biggr]
\end{equation}
 hold  with~$\{\fraktura d_j\}_{j\ge0}$ denoting the sequence from Assumption~(ass-1 of the paper). Moreover, each $v_k$ is a $C^\infty$ function with   with~$\{v_k'\}_{k\ge0}$ and~$\{v_k''\}_{k\ge0}$ uniformly bounded and, defining $v_\star\colon\mathbb R\to\mathbb R$ by 
