		Then
		\begin{equation}
			\lim_{\varepsilon\to 0}\lim_{N\to\infty}
			\frac{1}{N}\log\mathbb{E}\bigl[\mathcal{N}_\varepsilon(f,\zeta)\bigr]
			\;\geq\;
			\zeta(\{0\})\,\bigl(\mathcal{P}\mathrm{arisi}(\zeta)-f\bigr).
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.748792+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0b2937b6641fa8e0e19ef4cf849a2f17d0d5e5547e8f750053ba5fbb103c255","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 21 (Crossing count) of arXiv:2607.28865, 'First-Passage Percolation on Spread-out line graphs: Microscopic Regime'] Let
