{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.127622+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0c93e7b5d0655cb6264ad278334d0688242aca87d9d5e2b31808b828bcfaa04","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def B of arXiv:2411.15954, 'A gradient model for the Bernstein polynomial basis'] For each $ n,L\in\mathbb{N}$ fixed with $n\leq L$, define the constraint $\mathbf{b}_{n,L}:\Omega_N\to[0,1]$ as 
