{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.279781+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0d2aa8fbcfa18f7a992e99258269243133f403e9df7e295638e6b7bae88e6fb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 (subgaussian maximal inequality) of arXiv:2606.22611, 'Upper and Lower Bounds on Expected Soft Maxima\\of Gaussian Processes'] If $X_1,\ldots,X_n$ are $\sigma$-subgaussian random variables defined on a common probability space, then 
