{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.831323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d17daefa419d04e038b0ea6a5154a3b833467249b1f37181bda6fc6f9cd8e6fd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:upper_bounds of arXiv:2607.22908, 'Epidemic Phase Transitions in the Zero-Range Process'] For any relative deviation $\delta > 0$ and corresponding absolute deviation $\varepsilon = \rho\delta > 0$:
  \begin{equation}
  \begin{gathered}
    \mathbb{P}(\bar{X} \ge \rho(1+\delta)) \le \exp\braces*{ -n \frac{\rho}{\Gamma} \frac{\delta^2}{2 + 2\delta/3} }, \\
    \mathbb{P}(\bar{X} \ge \rho + \varepsilon) \le \exp\braces*{ -\frac{n}{\Gamma} \frac{\varepsilon^2}{2 \rho + 2\varepsilon/3} }.
  \end{gathered}
  \end{equation}
  If restricted to $\delta \in (0, 1]$ (or $\varepsilon \le \rho$), the bounds simplify to the sub-Gaussian forms $\exp\braces{ -n \frac{\rho \delta^2}{3\Gamma} }$ and $\exp\braces{ -n \frac{\varepsilon^2}{3 \Gamma \rho} }$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:35:04.213285+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1805c875563d1341b3b3bf2dc78d570db2364a9453d2f3bff200874202d2ee6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 6 of arXiv:2608.03956, 'From Triangular Array Progression\\ to Near-Log-Concave State Transitions'] Let $\eta = [\eta_1,\ldots,\eta_{n+1}]$ for $n\geq 2$ be a sequence, where $\min(\eta) > 0$. Define 
\begin{align}
\Theta_{i}(\eta) = \max\left( \log(\eta_{i-1}) + \log(\eta_{i+1}) - 2\log(\eta_i) \,,\, 0 \right), 
\end{align}
for every $i\in\{2,\ldots,n\}$. Then,
\begin{align}
\Theta(\eta) = \sum_{i=2}^{n} \Theta_{i}(\eta), 
\end{align}
is called the \emph{log-concavity deviation} of $\eta$ under logarithmic scaling.","status":"unverified"}

