{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.632268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d199ea7e0650d7c88edcc8c6adbb0d624846620dfc61d9894b59682c28118eea","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 29 (Trutschnig et al. (2016)) of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\vartheta \in \mathcal{P}_\mathcal{A}$, $A$ be its corresponding Pickands dependence function, $C_{A} \in \mathcal{C}_{ev}$ and $L$, $R$ be defined as in eq. \eqref{eq:definition_L_R} with $L<R$. Then,
