{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.055375+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1c8c07616d15e71eec5cc91a6505c4a92886de31108e0e53670bb1d2b5aa76a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem fundamental_solution of arXiv:2506.10623, 'Polynomial slowdown in an angle-dependent 2d branching Brownian motion'] Assume $k \leq 0$ and $k$ is Hölder continuous on any compact subset of $[0,T] \times \mathbb{R}$.
	For any $0 \leq \tau < t \leq T$ and any $\xi,x\in\mathbb{R}$, let
	\begin{align*}
	\Gamma(\tau,\xi;t,x)
	& \coloneqq \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi \sigma^2 (t-\tau)}} 
	\exp \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft( - \frac{(\xi-x)^2}{2 \sigma^2 (t-\tau)} \aftergroup\egroup\originalright) \\
        & \hspace{2cm}\times 
	\mathbb{E}_{(\tau,\frac{x}{\sigma})} \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft[ \exp \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft( \int_\tau^t k(t+\tau-r,\sigma B_r) \mathop{}\mathopen{}\mathrm{d} r \aftergroup\egroup\originalright) \middle| \sigma B_t = \xi \aftergroup\egroup\originalright] \\
	& = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi \sigma^2 (t-\tau)}} 
