    & \hspace{2cm}\times 
	\mathbb{E}_{(\tau,\frac{\xi}{\sigma})} \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft[ \exp \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft( \int_\tau^t k(r,\sigma B_r) \mathop{}\mathopen{}\mathrm{d} r \aftergroup\egroup\originalright) \middle| \sigma B_t = x \aftergroup\egroup\originalright].
	\end{align*}
	Then, $\Gamma$ is a fundamental solution of the PDE (equation eq:PDE_k of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.241571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1cf0dfd1b4149b5cd1782aa030b2c40cefc8226e4f4aa1daeaff656c6c0b8f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:eprocess-retention of arXiv:2608.20295, 'Physical-Support Confidence Sets for Highly Coherent Dictionaries'] Suppose the candidate laws, data split, proposal construction, and evaluation
