}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.049273+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1d3ee0adab8a1e7dcc5dfcf5033f966ce8f4528947de0e785749a1f2710e4cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 (Stationary singularity in the supercritical regime) of arXiv:2608.15914, 'Absorption cutoff and stationary singularities for rounded Gaussian random dynamical syste'] Fix $N\geq1$ and assume $A>A_c(N)$. Let $\pi_{A,N}$ be the nonzero invariant
  law of $X^{(N)}$. Let $\beta_{A,N}\in(0,N)$ be the unique
  positive solution of
  \begin{equation*}
    A^{-\beta}N^{\beta/2}2^{-\beta/2}
    \frac{\Gamma((N-\beta)/2)}{\Gamma(N/2)}
    =
    1.
  \end{equation*}
  Here $\bar\sigma_N$ denotes normalized surface measure on
  $\mathbb S^{N-1}$. Then there is a constant $c_{A,N}>0$ such that, for every
  Borel set
  $B\subseteq\mathbb S^{N-1}$ satisfying $\bar\sigma_N(\partial B)=0$,
  \begin{equation*}
    s^{-\beta_{A,N}}\pi_{A,N}\left(
