{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.650851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1e7a48128c6ab1e984f42b4aa5df8f7a13b0081afcfc0552d6b1a75e567b1e3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn pure partition function of arXiv:2506.01306, 'Asymptotic of Coulomb gas integral, Temperley-Lieb type algebras and pure partition functi'] The functions $\mathcal{Z}_\alpha: \mathfrak{X}_n \rightarrow \mathbb{R}^+$, indexed by link patterns $\alpha \in \mathrm{LP}(n,m)$, are called \emph{pure partition functions}. They are a collection of positive solutions to the null vector equations, subject to boundary conditions specified by their asymptotic behavior, which is determined by the link pattern $\alpha$
\begin{itemize}
    \item[\textnormal{(ASY)}] \textbf{Asymptotics:} For all $\alpha \in \mathrm{LP}_(n,m)$, $j \in \{1, \ldots, n\}$, and $\xi \in (x_{j-1}, x_{j+2})$, the following limit exists:
    \[
    \lim_{x_j, x_{j+1} \rightarrow \xi} \frac{\mathcal{Z}_\alpha\left(x_1, \ldots, x_n\right)}{(x_{j+1} - x_j)^{\frac{6 - \kappa}{\kappa}}}
    =
    \begin{cases}
        0, & \text{if } \{j, j+1\} \notin \alpha, \\
        \mathcal{Z}_{\hat{\alpha}}\left(x_1, \ldots, x_{j-1}, x_{j+2}, \ldots, x_n\right), & \text{if } \{j, j+1\} \in \alpha,
    \end{cases}
    \]
\end{itemize}
where $\hat{\alpha} = \alpha / \{j, j+1\} \in \mathrm{LP}(n-2,m-1)$ denotes the link pattern obtained from $\alpha$ by removing the link $\{j, j+1\}$ and relabeling the remaining indices as $1, 2, \ldots, n-2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.115042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d1e803634a5be96fc5070cfd575e9ea656b2aa431d0f7f01c276bd997aa1f992","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-sum-prod-L-x-j-delta of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $0 < \alpha < 1$. There exists a constant $C>0$ depending on $D$ only such that for any $k \in \mathbb{N}$,
