{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.750358+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d203ce3c38d7c6f2c62d8d4ca9bbd4d447a8f2f7e956786e51f246d2f6d8e44c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma decouple_label_degree_multiple_vertices of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Suppose that Assumption~$\hyperref[ass:A]{\mathbf{x}}$(item:geq1 of the paper) is satisfied. Fix $k\in\mathbb{N}$ and consider any truncation sequence $(t_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ such that $t_n\leq n$ for all $n\in\mathbb{N}$. Let $n\in\mathbb{N}$ and, for $v\in [k]$, let $u_v,d_v\in\mathbb{N}_0$, $\ell_v\in\Omega_1$. Furthermore, let $\overline{J^-},\overline{J^+}\in{\mathcal{P}(\Omega_1)}^k$ such that $J^-_v\cup J^+_v$ and $J^-_w\cup J^+_w$ are disjoint for $v\neq w\in[k]$. Then,
