{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.018013+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d21802a4edf85ecdee942fe4950dc3ad91be2c0757d4b47b63d8afceb2c1a348","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:xi2-chi-ratio of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $d\ge 1$ and $\delta >0$.
Suppose that Assumptions~(ass:Omega of the paper) and~(ass:J of the paper) hold for $S_z$ for each $z\in [z_c-\delta,z_c)$, suppose that $m_z \to 0$ as $z \to z_c$,
and suppose that there are constants $M,K_{\mathrm{IR}},\zeta$ such that
$(J_z^{(\mu)},h_z^{(\mu)}) \in \mathcal{Q}_{M,K_{\mathrm{IR}},\zeta}$
and $\hat h_z^{(\mu)} (0)  \ge M^{-1} > 0$
uniformly in $\mu\in \overline\Omega_z$ and in $z \in [z_c-\delta,z_c)$.
Then
\begin{equation} 
\frac{\xi_2(z)^2}{\chi(z)}
	= \frac{\sigma_{z}^2}{\hat h_z(0)}
