{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.806014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d243523c71268effb30af260ae2a7641986782c035f8e649707743a2689676bd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 67 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] Let $(\delta_n)_{n\in \mathbb{N}}\subset (0,1)$ such that $\delta_n \to 0$ as $n \to \infty$. Assume Assumption \ref{ass-A3} holds. Suppose that $\bu_n \to \bu$ in $L^2([0,T] \times \domO)$. Then, we have
