{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.438222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2479d93daf586ff2530153cc993f4160799a0ffc4209497999bc3e3967a8dc5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary CLT in diffusive regime of arXiv:2505.05921, 'Limit Theorems for step reinforced random walks\\ with regularly varying memory'] {}
    Let $\{S_n\}_{n\geq 0}$ be the SRRW-RVM with the zero mean innovation sequence $\{\xi_n\}_{n\ge 1}$ satisfying $\mathbb{E}\xi_1^2=1$. Then, for all $p\in [0,p_c)$ and $\gamma>-1/{2}$, $S_n/\sqrt{n}$ converges weakly to a centered normal distribution with limiting variance $\varsigma^2$ given by:
    \begin{equation} 
        \varsigma^2=
        \begin{cases}
            \frac{2\gamma+1-p}{(1-p)(2(1-p)(\gamma+1)-1)}, & \text{for } p\neq \widehat{p},\\
            2\gamma^2+2\gamma+1, & \text{for } p=\widehat{p}.
        \end{cases}
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.762183+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d24900fde96c55622333d669b691c2f919598b1f169d6533aedf72aa05ef375b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:lbm-cluster-response of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] For these branches, the response operator has matrix
\begin{equation}
 \left(\inner{B_f^\Lambda(M_x)\phi_j}{\phi_i}
              _{L^2(M_x)}\right)_{i,j=1}^r
 =-\gamma\Lambda
 \left(\int_Df\phi_i\phi_j\,dM_x\right)_{i,j=1}^r,

