{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:03:35.745756+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d26def905746bcdfbb4825d5f4c95fa8c8e383e6da7e202a7ff69c46f367cbcb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor entropicCommutatorTemperatureInterpolation of arXiv:2609.02743, 'Sharp mean-field estimates for diffusive log/Riesz gases in the Hilbert--Schmidt regime'] Assume the hypotheses of (thm:entropicCommutator of the paper) and moreover that the sharp pointwise commutator bound holds with the scale $a_{N,\mathsf{s}}$ from (equation eq:temperatureInterpolationScale of the paper): there are constants $C_{\mathrm{pw}}(\mu,v,n),C_{\mathrm{pt}}(\mu)<\infty$ such that, for every $N\ge1$ and every configuration $X_N$,
