{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.456806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d2715f9040627539dd19e7fb5fab54848355bfd71f716041c85751426e64cc6f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:maint of arXiv:2411.16572, 'Optimal decay of eigenvector overlap for non-Hermitian random matrices'] Assume that $X$ is a real or complex i.i.d. matrix satisfying Assumption~(ass:mainass of the paper) and that, for simplicity, its spectrum is simple (see Remark~(rem:nonsimpspec of the paper)). Let $\mathcal{O}_{ij}$ be the overlaps defined in (equation eq:defover of the paper). Then, with very high probability, for any small $\xi>0$, we have
