{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.412858+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d34b6e8b0603dc79d2abc5c3691e31e3dbb538b3d8fccf82657c8365a8969d1e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop P: contractive of arXiv:2511.11036, 'Analysis of a class of Recursive Distributional Equations Including the Resistance of the '] Suppose that $T$ is an operator on $CDF(\overline{\mathbb{R}})$ satisfying the following two properties:
		\begin{itemize}
			\item[(i)] \emph{Monotonicity:} If $F \leq G$ pointwise in $\mathbb{R}$, then $TF\leq TG$ also holds.
		\item[(ii)] \emph{Discrete-Time Reaction-Diffusion Equation:} There is a function $\mathcal{L}$ defined on $CDF(\overline{\mathbb{R}})$ and a function $Q$ defined on $[0,1]$ such that
			\begin{align*}
				TF - F = \mathcal{L}F - Q(F) \quad \text{for each} \, \, F \in CDF(\overline{\mathbb{R}}).
			\end{align*}
		\item[(iii)] \emph{Commutation with Constants:} Given $F,G \in CDF(\overline{\mathbb{R}})$, if the difference $F - G$ is a constant function, then $\mathcal{L}F = \mathcal{L}G$.

		\end{itemize}
		If there is a constant $L > 0$ such that $|Q(q) - Q(q')| \leq L|q - q'|$ for each $q,q' \in [0,1]$, then
		\begin{align*}
			\| T^{n}F - T^{n}G \|_{\sup} \leq (1 + L )^{n} \| F - G \|_{\sup} \quad \text{for any} \, \, F,G \in CDF(\overline{\mathbb{R}}), \, \, n \in \mathbb{N}.
		\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:56:00.651234+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d34cc0c0d050e221f7b374da57a72a4af1be168ba9b7d307e6fa3a1f47b1cc4e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_stop_markov of arXiv:2603.29442, 'A compact support property for infinite-dimensional SDEs with Hölder continuous coefficien'] Suppose $0 \leq a \leq x \leq w \leq y \leq b$ with $x < y$ and let $\mathbb{P}_w \in \mathscr{M}_{\gamma,\delta}(w)$. Then provided $\mathbb{P}_w(\tau_x < \tau_y) >0$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}_w(\tau_x < \tau_y, \tau_a < \tau_b) = \mathbb{P}_w(\tau_x < \tau_y) \mathbb{P}_x'(\tau_a < \tau_b),
\end{equation}
for some $\mathbb{P}_x' \in \mathscr{M}_{\gamma,\delta}(x)$. Moreover, the analogous inequality holds for all variations of the ordering of the stopping times, i.e.\ exchanging $\tau_x < \tau_y$ for $\tau_y < \tau_x$, and similarly for $\tau_a$ and $\tau_b$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.817208+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d34eed23bcfe4e6eccb8e96e4d2f7cf9ebb2e1bccaa7fe8d5d826774bb457107","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:divergence-pullback of arXiv:2607.24640, 'The Yang-Mills measure on surfaces via Morse theory'] Let $\mathrm{v}$ be a volume form on a compact manifold $M$ of dimension $n$. Let $V$ be a smooth vector field with $(\varphi^t)_{t\in \mathbb{R}}:M\mapsto M$ the corresponding flow. Then we have the exact identity
