{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.490636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3848f9a63b589cedf57ce3388b18079e26d49f7096b3e347b64c02483dc524d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 (Definition and triangularity of $\Gamma$) of arXiv:2605.28677, 'Weak universality for stochastic reaction-diffusion models\\ with long-range correlated no'] Let $ (\pi^{(\n)} )_{\n\in\NN^{1+d}} \subset \RR [\![ z_{k}, z_{\n} ]\!]$ such that for all $\beta$ and $\n$ it holds that $\pi^{(\n)}_{ \beta} \neq 0$ implies $ |\n| < | \beta| $.
