{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.619112+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3c86db10df3ac482b03d89fc7169fa3bf18e18b1a2524aa9614d3337efaf98e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 87 of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] There is a constant $\alpha$ such that for any interval $[a,b]\subseteq [-1,1]$ and $t\leq n^\alpha$, we have
