{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.775328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d40c9369be24f75f1258af3b2428b259a2fa7675cf24bfa2e84073a418ba9060","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:confinement of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] {For any $\lambda > 1$} there is some $M > 0$ such that for the $\lambda$-tilted line ensemble $\mathbf{X}$, we have
