The expression in \eqref{eq:occupation-closed-form} is independent of the chosen solution, and every entry of $\vect m_\ell(y)$ grows at most linearly in $y$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.955602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d416f6b93c0f1fe83127f18db459231979dcbe2cbd106923bd3a313347ac8612","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition EstimImpo of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] We have, for all integers $k \leqslant n \leqslant m \leqslant l$,
    \begin{align*}
        &\mathbb{E}\Big[
            \big|
                A_N(k2^{-N} \xrightarrow{m2^{-N}} l2^{-N})
                - A_N(k2^{-N} \xrightarrow{n2^{-N}} l2^{-N})
            \big|^p
        \Big] \\
        &\qquad\leqslant
        \sup_{\substack{k \leqslant j \leqslant l \\ n \leqslant i \leqslant m}}
        \sigma\big(\square(i2^{-N},(i+1)2^{-N},j2^{-N},(j+1)2^{-N})\big)^{\beta}
        (l-k)^{\beta}(m-n)^{\beta} \\
        &\qquad\quad+
        \sup_{\substack{k \leqslant j \leqslant l \\ n \leqslant i \leqslant m}}
        \sigma\big(\square(i2^{-N},(i+1)2^{-N},j2^{-N},(j+1)2^{-N})\big)^{2\beta}
        (l-k)^{\beta} n^{2\beta}.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.364281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d417790a5a1457eb99de720083d931e9b929c9024de3d609f0c05edcd6e79ee3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:centear of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] If $T$ is a $(K,\delta,c_1)$-good tree on $\{0,\ldots, n\}$ with centrality sets denoted by $A_r$, $r=1,\ldots, n$, then
