{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.424550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4445d5de54691a439815aaef0f20f10de65255f8a2faa31e9458446f5624a4d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary thm.mtg2 of arXiv:2605.17725, 'Limit theorems for random walks with spatio-temporal drift'] Let $(M_n)$ be an $\mathbb{R}^d$-valued martingale such that
        $$\Lambda_n := \sum_{k=1}^n \mathbb{E}[\Delta_k \Delta_k^\top] = \mathbb{E}[M_n M_n^\top] \to \infty$$ and $\Lambda_n$ is eventually positive definite.
