{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.413592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d44f08f0ea162f6ba7ef13b130a54225d2dd42cc9c1022f6e5f62d38e876710b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:nf of arXiv:2608.27771, 'A normal form for the Thin Flat Surfaces category'] Let $f \colon n \to m$ be a connected viewable tf-cobordism with interval cycles
$\lambda_1, \ldots, \lambda_p$, where $\lambda_k$ involves $a_k$ incoming and $a'_k$
outgoing intervals, genus $g \geq 0$, and $c \geq 0$ holes.  Fix an ordering of the
cycles as in Section~(sec:ordering of the paper).  The \emph{normal form} of $f$ is the
tf-cobordism
\begin{equation}

  \mathrm{NF}(f)
  \;:=\;
  \Gamma(c,\, g)
  \;\circ\;
  \bar\rho(f)
  \;\circ\;
  K_p\!\bigl(\lambda_1, \ldots, \lambda_p\bigr)
  \;\circ\;
  \bar\sigma(f).
\end{equation}
For a general (not necessarily connected) viewable tf-cobordism $f = f_1 \otimes
\cdots \otimes f_c$ decomposed into connected components, the normal form is the
monoidal product
\[
  \mathrm{NF}(f) \;:=\; \mathrm{NF}(f_1) \otimes \cdots \otimes \mathrm{NF}(f_c).
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.067152+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d45204f266e80cbf4b028839f19b3f0686076caebfd05e59ca7754e789c1450b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-orbit-expectation of arXiv:2506.12752, 'Strong Detection Threshold for Correlated \ER Graphs with Constant Average Degree'] {}
Recall (equation eq-def-p-rho of the paper). For any $\sigma\in\mathfrak S_n$, let $\pi = \pi^* \circ \sigma$ and let $\Pi,\Sigma$ be the bijection on $\operatorname{U}_n$ induced by $\pi,\sigma$, respectively. Then for any legal realization $J$ of $\mathcal J_{\sigma}$ and any orbit $O \in \mathcal O_{\sigma}, O \not \subset J$, we have
\begin{equation}{}
    \mathbb{E}_{(A,B) \sim \mathbb P(\cdot \mid \pi_*)} \Big[ \prod_{e \in O} \ell(A_e, B_{\Pi(e)}) \mid \mathcal J_{\sigma}=J \Big] = \frac{ 1+\rho^{2|O|}-s^{2|O|} }{ 1-(ps^2)^{|O|} } \,.
\end{equation}
In particular, we have
\begin{equation}{}
    \mathbb{E}_{(A,B) \sim \mathbb P(\cdot \mid \pi_*)} \Big[ \prod_{e \in O} \ell(A_e, B_{\Pi(e)}) \mid \mathcal J_{\sigma}=J \Big] \leq 
    \begin{cases}
        1+O(n^{-2}) \,, & |O| \geq 2 \,; \\
        1+\frac{\lambda s^2(2s-1)}{n} + O(n^{-2}) \,, & |O|=1 \,.
    \end{cases}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.662064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d4534251b20aee9a0c9d9ba8e27b2f01985b8d3412e6fa75601b19602812fad6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local-set-1 of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $D$ and $\mathbb P_\delta$ be as in Lemma (lem:conv-fields-fractal of the paper). Let $\ell_\delta$ be an inner boundary of the boundary cluster of $\hat\mathbf{n}_\delta$ on $D_\delta$, with parity label $c_\delta$. Let $\mathcal O(\ell_\delta)$ be the induced subgraph of $D_\delta$ whose vertices are enclosed by $\ell_\delta$, and let $\mathcal{O}(\ell_\delta)^*$ be its \emph{strong} dual graph, where all vertices of $D_\delta^\dagger$ belonging to $\ell_\delta$ are identified. Then,
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[$\bullet$]  the law of the restriction of $\tau_\delta$ to $\mathcal O(\ell_\delta)$ is that of $-c_\delta$ times a XOR-Ising model $\tau_\delta^{\ell_\delta}$ with free boundary conditions, 
        \item[$\bullet$]  the law of the restriction of $\tau_\delta^\dagger$ to $\mathcal O(\ell_\delta)^*$ is that of $c_\delta$ times a XOR-Ising model  $(\tau_\delta^{\ell_\delta})^\dagger$  with $+$ boundary conditions.
    \end{enumerate}
    Moreover, every subsequential limit as $\delta\to0$ of the joint law
    \begin{equation}
        \left( h_\delta,\ \ell_\delta,\ c_\delta,\ \tau_\delta,\ \tau_\delta^\dagger,\ \tau_\delta^{\ell_\delta},\ (\tau_\delta^{\ell_\delta})^\dagger \right) 
    \end{equation}
    is given by 
    \begin{equation}
        \left(\frac{1}{2\sqrt{2}\lambda}\ h,\ \ell,\ c,\ \field{\cos(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi)},\ \field{\sin(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi)},\ \field{\sin(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi^\ell)},\ \field{\cos(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi^\ell)} \right),
    \end{equation}
    where 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[$\bullet$] the loop $\ell$ is a loop of the two-valued set $\mathds A_{-\sqrt{2}\lambda, \sqrt{2}\lambda}$ of $h$,
        \item[$\bullet$] the label $c$ is the label of the above two-valued set,
        \item[$\bullet$] given $\ell$, the conditional law of $\phi^\ell$ is that of a GFF with zero boundary conditions in $\mathcal O(\ell)$,
        \item[$\bullet$] given $\ell$, the label $c$ and the pair $\big(\field{\cos(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi^\ell)}, \ \field{\sin(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi^\ell)} \big)$ are conditionally independent.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.388345+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d453da6d97f1d0315c6310f3ca6c811f007b2c4a046111ba80199a2f56c0fb7d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 of arXiv:2609.04139, 'The conformally invariant metric on CLE$_4$ II:\\ existence of geodesics'] Let $U\subset \BC$ be a domain. Let $z \in U$. Let $(U_n)_{n\ge 0}$ be a sequence of domains in $\BC$. The sequence $(U_n)_{n\ge 0}$ converges in the sense of Carath\'eodory toward $U$ relative to $z$ if 
	\begin{itemize}
		\item For each compact set $K\subset U$, we have $K\subset U_n$ for all $n$ large enough;
