{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:52.204351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d53677eabbaf912aa0033e54d22b1e86c1bc9f7bb0522bc82456379ca448e02a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 of arXiv:2512.08745, 'Variance strikes back: sub-game--perfect Nash equilibria in time‑inconsistent $N$‑player g'] Let {\rm\Cref{assumpDPP}} hold. Given the set-up introduced so far, let $\alpha^\star \in \widetilde{\cA}$ be a sub-game--perfect equilibrium. Then, for any $(t,\tilde{t}) \in [0,T] \times [t,T]$, it holds that
