{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.820943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d55d9271104993114c1dd79c972dadeec1c444e0d228eb63e708c6f85206705d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:integration-connection of arXiv:2607.24640, 'The Yang-Mills measure on surfaces via Morse theory'] With the above conventions, one has, for every two admissible curves $\gamma$ and $\tilde{\gamma}$ and every $\psi$ and $\tilde{\psi}$ in $L^\infty(\Sigma)$,
