{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:43:43.468261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d56be82321526d0d2db5821c7934f23962d17af538399e988d91c626e92447a9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:PI(Dir) of arXiv:2509.04155, 'An Approach to Sub-Gaussian Heat Kernel Estimates via Analysis on Metric Spaces'] We say that $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ satisfies the \emph{Poincar\'e inequality} (eq:PI(Dir) of the paper) if there are constants $C,\sigma \geq 1$ satisfying the following condition.
    For all $x \in X$, $r > 0$ and $f \in \mathcal{F}$,
    \begin{equation}
        \tag{$\textup{PI}(\Psi)$}
        \int_{B(x,r)} (f - f_{B(x,r)})^2 \, d\mu \leq C \Psi(r) \int_{B(x,\sigma r)} \, d\Gamma\Span{f}.
    \end{equation}
    We also say that $(\mathcal{E},\mathcal{F})$ satisfies the \emph{upper capacity estimate} (eq:Ucap(Dir) of the paper) if there is a constant $C \geq 1$ satisfying the following condition. For all $x \in X$ and $r > 0$ there is a cutoff function $\varphi \in \mathcal{F}$ for $B(x,r) \subseteq B(x,2r)$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \tag{$\textup{Cap}_\leq(\Psi)$}
        \mathcal{E}(\varphi) \leq C \frac{\mu(B(x,r))}{\Psi(r)}.
    \end{equation}
    If $\Psi(r) = r^\beta$ for some $\beta \geq 2$, we write \hyperref[eq:PI(Dir)]{$\textup{PI}(\beta)$} and \hyperref[eq:Ucap(Dir)]{$\textup{Cap}_\leq(\beta)$} instead.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.315918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d56bf28d80822730ee9cc9bc1f833deb4d96933b3b7c700ba108629442a62fe6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem ;lpre2 of arXiv:2604.12462, 'Stochastic analysis of Beckner's and related functional inequalities'] Let $\Phi \colon (0,\infty )\to \mathbb{R} $ be as above. Then, for every $0\le s\le t\le 1$, 
