{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:38.632195+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5acaadb7acb4330cb6516d7f5e3746cde7f6b763421f9a9f4c5877864d94e14","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 28 of arXiv:2506.17045, '\LARGE{On bivariate Archimax copulas: Level sets, mass distributions and related results}'] Let $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_\mathcal{W}$ with $\mathrm{supp}(\gamma) = \left[\frac{1}{\varphi(0)},\infty\right)$, $\vartheta\in\mathcal{P}_\mathcal{A}$ and $C$ be the corresponding Archimax copula. Moreover, let $L$, $R$ be defined as in eq. \eqref{eq:definition_L_R_measure} with $L < R$. Then the following assertions hold:
