{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.580244+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5bb18514ace5e3734b9106a164bae778ccba22b82b5d6eaeaf25b246e05dcaa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:nSD[a,b] of arXiv:2411.15401, 'The reference interval in higher-order stochastic dominance'] [{\color{black}[J80]}]
Let $a,b\in[-\infty,\infty]$ with $a<b$ and $n\in\mathbb{N}$. For $X,Y\in\mathcal X_{[a,b]}$, we say that $X$ dominates $Y$ in the sense of $n$th-order stochastic dominance on $[a,b]$ ($n{\rm SD}_{[a,b]}$), denoted by $X\ge_{n}^{[a,b]} Y$ or $F_X\ge_{n}^{[a,b]} F_Y$ if 
\begin{align*}
F_X^{[n]}(\eta)\le F_Y^{[n]}(\eta),~\forall \eta\in[a,b]~{\rm and}~F_X^{[k]}(b)\le F_Y^{[k]}(b)~{\rm for}~ k\in[n]
\end{align*}
or equivalently,
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}[(\eta-X)_+^{n-1}]\le \mathbb{E}[(\eta-Y)_+^{n-1}],~\forall \eta\in[a,b]~{\rm and}~\mathbb{E}[(b-X)^{k-1}]\le \mathbb{E}[(b-Y)^{k-1}]~{\rm for}~ k\in[n].
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.573585+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5be73f4a2839ac2d20ef27d19338ffeb14d0c5f6dc47019d061c73bc52f38ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 30 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 4$. There exists $C_{\textup{mag}}=C_{\textup{mag}}(d)\geq 1$ such that, for every $h\geq0$,
