{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.036759+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5c7fea9bfb739fd8a342e34e1a16bcf3a2d2a6cd49e4ef16e63b803b2c0608b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2-l10 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Fix a function $G\colon {\mathbb R}_+ \times {\mathbb T}^{d}_N \to {\mathbb R}$ and a
cylinder function $f$. Then, there exists a finite constant
${\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N)$, depending only on ${\boldsymbol u}^N$, $f$ and $d$, uniformly
bounded in $N$, such that
\begin{align*}
& {\mathbb E}_{\nu^N} \Big[\, \Big|\,
\int_0^t \, 
\sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N} G (s, x)\,
(\Xi^{\rm c}_{{\boldsymbol u}^N (\cdot), x}  f) (\eta (s))
\, ds \, \Big| \,\Big]
\\ 
&\quad \;\le \;
{\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N) \, \Big\{ \frac{1}{K_N} \;+\;
K_N\,  \int_0^t (\, 1 + \Vert G(s)\Vert^2_\infty\,)\, \big[ \,
H_N(f^N_s)  + (N/\ell_N)^d \,\big] \, ds\; \Big\}
\\
& \quad \; + \;
\int_0^t \frac{1}{\gamma_s}  \big\{\, H_N(f^N_s) +
\log 2 \, \big\} \; ds
\;+\; {\mathfrak c} ({\boldsymbol u}^N) \,  K\, N^{d-2}\, \int_0^t   \gamma_s \,  {\mathfrak n}_K (G_s)^2\,
\, e^{c ({\boldsymbol u}^N) \, \gamma_s\,  {\mathfrak n}_K (G_s) \, \epsilon_N }\; ds 
\end{align*}
for all $t>0$, $\gamma\colon [0,t] \to (0,\infty)$.  In this equation,
$f^N_s$ is given by (equation 2-34c of the paper), $(\ell_N : N\ge 1)$ is the sequence
introduced in the statement of Theorem (mt1 of the paper), and
$\epsilon_N = K^{1/2}/N$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:03:59.345382+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5ca73bbabce18a1304758f457a0f091042199fe8f6157e6362cf633aa2ce1a4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Korollar cortb of arXiv:2507.08692, 'Some notes on higher order concentration of measure'] Let $F\in L^1(\mathbb{P}_\eta)$. If $\mathbb{P}$-almost surely $V^+ \le L$ or $V^- \le L$ for some $L > 0$, we have that
