{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.609017+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5fd453144411b93df0f322fe7ac77a142ca3f6e599f6ca30a0380f908cc0164","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-5.7 of arXiv:2412.08964, 'Phase transition and critical behavior in hierarchical\\integer-valued Gaussian and Coulom'] For all~$\alpha\in(-\ffrac12,\ffrac12)$ and~$\delta\in(0,1-2|\alpha|)$ there exist~$\epsilon>0$ and $C'>0$ and, for all~$\beta>\beta_\text{\rm c}$ with~$1/\beta>1/\beta_\text{\rm c}-\epsilon$, there exist $C>0$  and  $\eta>0$ such that
