{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:24:25.989110+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d60d2f207570507728169a3214363ca6638f4f5a0690a3359ed8394b86e55cf0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 76 of arXiv:2507.07702, 'Observables of random spanning trees in random environment'] Let $(G, \weight)$ be a finite connected weighted graph and let $\mathcal{K}$ be the kernel of $G$. Assign each edge $(U,V) \in E(\mathcal{K})$ the weight
