$$
is an element of $\Lc$. 
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.333773+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d63b194f32ff3754334a0b3b115267fd8edafb9c71bcf19db2546d6e4ab0cd8a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2511.06196, 'Central limit theorem for high temperature spin models via martingale embedding'] Let $p_d$, $d=0,1,2,\dots$, denote the probability mass function of $D_\infty$. We have, for some $d_1$ depending only on $\alpha$ and any $d_2\geq 1$,
