{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:05:52.431918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d66173f47120be871fe3336bb8f12ff6fa3324b32487f2c411b5f3526af3ac1f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma singularvalueproduct of arXiv:2504.15992, 'Repeated singular values of a random symmetric matrix and decoupled singular value estimat'] Fix some constants $\sigma>0,c>0,C>0$ and $\tau\in(0,1].$ Let $M_1,M_2$ be two $n\times n$ random matrices (not necessarily independent) that satisfy, for any $\delta_1,\delta_2>0$,
