{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.656218+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d70a09b726ae17ae00abacc0d843b9cb3946f7cbb964ea82ac9d7f915888bd80","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2609.03726, 'Inverse Scattering for Single Photons in Quantum Optics'] Let $k_\rho$ be the threshold from Lemma \ref{lem_LAP} with $l=[n/2]+1$ and $\delta=3/4$. Let $k>k_\rho$ and let $\alpha,\theta\in\mathbb S^{n-1}$ satisfy
