{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.286263+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d728c1f67ffc1c9971114f9873c59cc8755628985df0b9d9f510c531a3772380","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2606.22964, 'Signature McKean--Vlasov stochastic differential equations'] Let $(p,\alpha)\in(1,\infty)\times(0,1)$ with $p\alpha<1$. We define $C^{\alpha,p}_o([0,T],G^{\lfloor 1/\alpha\rfloor}(\mathbb{R}^k))$ as the set of continuous paths $\mathbf{x}:[0,T]\rightarrow G^{\lfloor 1/\alpha\rfloor}(\mathbb{R}^k)$ such that $\mathbf{x}_0=(1,0,\dots,0)$ and
