{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.847061+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d72e9fc6d4894e89d5fc42a8949032c3bc4371a24273c755a5cbc192205fe85a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:GaussianEigenvalues2 of arXiv:2410.23915, 'Asymptotic Bounds and Online Algorithms for Average-Case Matrix Discrepancy'] Let $X,Y$ be two $m \times m$ GOE matrices with correlation $\rho \in (-1,1)$. The joint probability density function of their ordered eigenvalues $\lambda_1(X) \leq \ldots \leq \lambda_m(X)$ and $\mu_1(X) \leq \ldots \leq \mu_m(X)$ is bounded above by
