            (\lambda,\mu) \mapsto C_m^2 (1 - \rho^2)^{-m(m+1)/4} \exp{-\frac{\left\lVert\ifblank{\lambda}{\:\cdot\:}{\lambda}\right\rVert_2^2 - 2\rho\inp{\lambda}{\mu} + \left\lVert\ifblank{\mu}{\:\cdot\:}{\mu}\right\rVert_2^2}{4(1 - \rho^2)}} \Delta(\lambda)\Delta(\mu)
        \end{equation}
        on $\mathbb{R}^m_\geq \times \mathbb{R}^m_\geq$, where the constant $C_m$ is defined as in (equation eq:NormalizationConstant2 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:13:21.310264+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d73428868018378fb38460fbf77bfdd57823079c67f9a8d9a4dc73ca81e62288","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2609.01485, 'On the Ramification of Quadratic Fields where the Torsion of a Rational Elliptic Curve Gro'] Let $E/\mathbb{Q}$ be an elliptic curve. Assume $K$ is a quadratic number field such that there exists $P\in E(K)[\ell]\setminus E(\mathbb{Q})$, with $\ell\geq 3$ prime.
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item For every prime $p\neq \ell$ that ramifies in $K$, $E$ has additive reduction at $p$, i.e. $p^2|N_E$.
        \item If $p=\ell>3$  ramifies in $K$, $E$ has additive reduction at $p$, i.e. $p^2|N_E$.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

