{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.384850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d749c3f8122c143ffc67e0381acc8d020159b5e8ba27155da7228a7d4bdb9c02","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 1 of arXiv:2607.28004, 'Folding representations of reflected diffusions'] Let $\sigma:I \to (0,\infty)$ be a locally absolutely continuous function with $\int_0^\infty \frac{1}{\sigma(u)}du = \infty$.  
    Then the unique solution $f$ to equation \eqref{eq:nonlinear_ODE} with initial condition $f(0) = 0$ is given by the inverse function $f = g^{-1}$ of 
     \begin{equation} 
        g(\xi) := \int_0^\xi \frac{1}{\sigma(u)}du, \qquad \forall\,  \xi \in I.
    \end{equation}
 Moreover, this solution satisfies 
    \begin{enumerate}[label = (\roman*),noitemsep]
        \item  $f \geq 0$ and $f\in W^{2,1}_{\mathrm{loc}}(I)$;
        \item  $f$ is strictly increasing with $f'(0) = \sigma(0)$;
        \item  $f''(y) = \sigma'(f(y))f'(y)$ for a.e.\ $y \in I$;
        \item  $\lim_{y \to \infty} f(y) = \infty$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.353312+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d74b6a63e9a7e1a1241584b613a656959ae23f6362774ef6f6607b837da23e86","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L3 of arXiv:2608.22945, 'A Momentum-Based Variance-Reduced Algorithm for Federated Multiobjective Optimization'] Suppose that Assumptions (A1 of the paper)--(A2 of the paper) hold. If $\gamma L\leq\sqrt{\frac{\beta KM}{54}}$, then, for all $t\ge1$,
