{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.695109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d757ce230372127061869c3f271ce3678d90abce24b9bcba268899dbc293c9ed","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem prop:alpha_llt of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] Let $p_n(x,y)$ denote the $n$-step transition probability associated with the transition matrix $P_N$ from Definition~(defmodel of the paper), with profile $f_\alpha(x)$, where $N=L^d$.
