{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:02:34.839542+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d81d27588a42fde339665b29758e9299118c8147645695eea7c022dc86c3267e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 (Characterization of the shape-$k$ Gamma case and a concentration bound) of arXiv:2607.20680, 'Exact Scale--Shape Factorization of the Typical Poisson--Voronoi Cell Volume in Arbitrary '] Fix $k$ with $p_{d,k}>0$.  The conditional law $Y_d\mid K=k$ is Gamma distributed with shape $k$ if and only if $A_k$ is almost surely constant.  More precisely, for $a>0$,
  \begin{equation}

