then $Z$ is said to have a regularly varying tail with index $\alpha$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.914191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d84eed1799766f72f84d9983445963500bd6da273e00703ca2615e8d5ef758f0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:set_hitting_animals of arXiv:2505.07145, 'Nonamenable Poisson zoo'] For any $K \subset \subset V(G)$, let us introduce the notation
