\sigma(\phi_I^M)^2:=\fint_M{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}}\left\{ \phi_I^M(x)\right\} dx,
\quad
\lambda(\phi_I^M)^2:=\frac{1}{\sigma(\phi_I^M)^2}\fint_M\mathbb{E}\left\{ \|d_x\phi_I\|^2 \right\} dx.
\end{gather}
and call them \emph{average variance} and \emph{average frequency} (consistently with the terminology introduced in [cgv2025StecconiTodino]). If $\sigma(\phi^M_I)=0$, we set $\lambda(\phi^M_I)=0$. We extend such notation to any setting in which the integrands in (eq:sigmalambdaRW of the paper) are constant, including non-compact manifolds $M$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.629711+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d883be45e3bcd91b5dec9b07da0cbb5bad24f1a802224a1b0dd2963249a311ca","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] A spin model $\left< \cdot \right>_{G}$ satisfies Pfaffian relations 
