{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:28:34.971874+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d88c6e83f2147b6bbeeac92fefd53c30fff6f6692c653533207cf737d39cf9d3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def:skew_signature_functions of arXiv:2412.05999, 'Non-Archimedean GUE corners and Hecke modules'] For any $n \geq 0, k \geq 1$ and $\lambda \in \Sig_{n+k}, \mu \in \Sig_{n}$, we let 
