{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.198011+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d8d4e4465a7ab2f9028a79c1a44fd4fe6f453a0db817575f9cee0deb709d5f5b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2604.26549, 'Existence and uniqueness results of a stochastic nonlinear heat equation with a constraint'] Let $(\wtilde{\Omega},\wtilde{\Fn},\wtilde{\Fb},\wtilde{\Pr},\wtilde{W},u)$ be a solution, obtained in Proposition \ref{Prop-pre-martingale}, of \eqref{eqn-main-prob-Ito} on $[0, T]$ such that $u(t) \in\bM$, for $t\in [0, T]$, and
		\begin{equation}
			\wtilde{\E} \Big[\sup_{t\in[0,T]} \big(\|u(t)\|_{H_0^1(\bO)}^{4} + \|u(t)\|_{L^p(\bO)}^{2p}\big)\Big] + \wtilde{\E}\Big[\int_0^T\big(\|\Delta u(t)\|_{L^2(\bO)}^2+ \|u(t)\|_{L^{2p-2}(\bO)}^{2p-2}\big)dt\Big]<\infty.
