{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.335438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d93b50bd805811f595205fe19971fecf1849144a5958205ac84856aea50f8254","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2511.06414, 'Non-uniform Edgeworth expansions for weakly dependent random variables and their applicati'] There are polynomials $\tilde H_j$ whose coefficients are polynomial functions of $q_k$ and $p_k$ for $k\leq 3j$ so that
