{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.201496+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d96bec7fb668c9a3b111d51ca1e783e89caf82c62e45ce0e7e3a3f7bf11c120a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem MLSI DOWN UP MC of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Let $\ensuremath{\mathcal B}$ be a fixed partition of $[L]$. Suppose that \(\Lambda\) is a nonnegative definite $L\times L$ matrix with largest eigenvalue \(\lambda(\Lambda) < 1/2\). Then 
