	\end{equation}
	where $\gamma_j = m_j(k+1)$, $\delta_j = \nu(N(k+1)-j)+1$, $E_{\nu, \delta_j}^{\gamma_1, \dots, \gamma_M}$ is the multivariate Mittag-Leffler function defined by \eqref{multML}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.969409+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9a662547a1c72ee40c1559f46230d72844e78f428530d17cf9dc4d125e62cd9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 35 of arXiv:2606.09904, 'Non-explosion principles for branched rough differential equations with unbounded coeffici'] For any \(\delta \le \frac{\gamma}{N}\), we denote
