\end{equation}
In particular, one has $\boldsymbol{\tau}^{L,M}(\beta)\geq 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:05.622310+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9afa386667f3cae99af319aa5ad2c113911ab855e79c51ee1b6273a7821c98e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2608.22112, '2608.22112'] \textbf{(Control of $\ell^2$ trajectory error via norm equivalence)}
Define $\tilde \f_H$ as in \cref{fH}, and let $\tilde \S_H$ be the corresponding learned stroboscopic map. Assume that the true and predicted trajectories remain uniformly bounded over the training horizon, i.e., there exists constants $M > 0$ and $\tilde{M} > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\|\S^h(\x[0])\|_2 \le M,
\qquad
\|\tilde \S_H^h(\x[0])\|_2 \le \tilde{M}
\end{equation}
for all $\x[0] \in \X_0$ and $h = 1,\dots,H$. Such bounds are natural when trajectories remain in a compact region of state space over the training horizon. Then there exists a constant $C = (M + \tilde{M}) > 0$, such that
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{mH}
\sum_{h=1}^H
\sum_{\x[0] \in \X_0}
\|\tilde \S_H^h(\x[0]) - \S^h(\x[0])\|_2^2
\;\le\;
C \cdot \mathrm{Loss}_H(\tilde \f_H).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:40:22.370141+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9b16852a4ca7ff285c1dfa869a17fff24e60266c38d080ff4aafda1d3821dad","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def-harmonic of arXiv:2506.18827, 'Random walk reflected off of infinity, with applications to uniform spanning forests and s'] We say that $h : \mathcal V\mathcal G \to \mathbbm R$ is \textbf{discrete harmonic at $x$} if\footnote{If $\mathcal G$ is not locally finite, the relation~(equation eqn-harmonic of the paper) implicitly requires that the sum is convergent, i.e., $\sum_{y\sim x} \mathfrak c(x,y) |h(y) - h(x)|< \infty$.}
\begin{equation}   
\sum_{y\sim x} \mathfrak c(x,y) (h(y) - h(x)) = 0   .
\end{equation}  
For $f : \mathcal V\mathcal G\to\mathbbm R$, we define its \textbf{Dirichlet energy} by
\begin{equation} 
\operatorname{Energy}(f) :=  \sum_{(x,y) \in \mathcal E \mathcal G} \mathfrak c(x,y)  |f(y) - f(x)|^2  .
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.645583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9b6eb3e04d8fe9ee21337117e786e8593eba8d38ea5b5ace070cdb2f64da859","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (KL telescoping bound) of arXiv:2605.24937, '2605.24937'] Let $(Y_n')_{n=0}^N$ and $(\widetilde Y_n)_{n=0}^{N-1}$ be defined
by~\eqref{eq:tildeY-def}--\eqref{eq:aux-update}. Then
\begin{equation}
  \KL\!\bigl(\widehat\mu_N\,\|\,\nu_N\bigr)
  \;\le\;
  \sum_{n=0}^{N-1}
  \E\!\left[
    \KL\!\bigl(Q_n(\widetilde Y_n,\cdot)\,\big\|\,P(Y_n',\cdot)\bigr)
  \right].
\end{equation}
If~\eqref{eq:reg-framework}--\eqref{eq:crossreg-framework} hold, then
\begin{equation}
  \KL\!\bigl(\widehat\mu_N\,\|\,\nu_N\bigr)
  \;\le\;
  c\,\sum_{n=0}^{N-2}\eta_n^{2}\,\E\|\widehat X_n-Y_n'\|^{2}
  +c'\,\E\|\widehat X_{N-1}-Y_{N-1}'\|^{2}
  +\bar b^{\,2},
\end{equation}
where $\bar b^{\,2}:=\|b\|_{L^2(\widehat\mu_{N-1})}^{2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

