{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.548726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9ba542b4bf1462571379dcdc159b58941424e042251b217c3ef6ba5dcbf8560","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 24 (Margin) of arXiv:2609.01397, 'Measuring consistency via ensemble margin and local prediction variability: Auditing decis'] Given a Rashomon \smallset{} set $\retailset = \{f_k :  k \in [\Nretail]\}$, the ensemble model $\ensmretset(\retailset,x)$ of size $\Nretail$, we define the margin of  $\ensmretset(\retailset,x)$ at a fixed instance $x$ as, 
