{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.077033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9e34ee3fad9a79b37e71aa21f2d7a1cbe3610db2937cdcae74c2e7bd57e7f55","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro disc of arXiv:2507.00737, 'Dispersion models on a circle: universal properties and asymptotic results'] In the discrete parking,
	\begin{equation} 
	{{\bf N}_{t_n}^{(n)}}/{\sqrt{n}} \xrightarrow[n]{(proba.)} \lambda (1-e^{-1})\end{equation}
	while, in the continuous parking
	\begin{equation}  {{\bf N}_{t_n} }/{\sqrt{n}} \xrightarrow[n]{(proba.)} \lambda.\end{equation}
	For any $k$, the following convergence in distribution holds in $\mathbb{R}^k$,
	\begin{eqnarray} 
	n^{-1}\,L^{(n), \downarrow}[t_n(\lambda),k] &\xrightarrow[n]{(d)}&(\ell_i^{\downarrow}(\lambda,{\sf e}),1\leq i \leq k)\\
	 n^{-1}\,L^{\downarrow}[t_n(\lambda),k] &\xrightarrow[n]{(d)}&(\ell_i^{\downarrow}(\lambda,{\sf e}),1\leq i \leq k)
	\end{eqnarray}
	where $(\ell_i^{\downarrow}(\lambda,{\sf e}),1\leq i \leq k)$ is the (random) vector formed by the $k$ largest excursion sizes of the process $t\mapsto ({\sf e}_t -\lambda_t)-\min_{s\leq t} ({\sf e}_s -\lambda s)$, sorted in descending order (where ${\sf e}$ is a normalized Brownian excursion). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

