		&	\mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \Bigg[ \Bigg\{ \widehat{b}_n \int_s^t \dd r \sum_{x}   \nabla H ( \tfrac{ \lfloor x - r v_n \rfloor }{n}  )    \Psi_{x,L_n}^{\alpha,\beta}(\eta_r^n)  \Bigg\}^{2} \Bigg] \leq  2 \chi(\rho_{\alpha}) \chi(\rho_{\beta}) (t-s)^{2} n \frac{(\widehat{b}_n)^2 }{L_n} \| \nabla H \|^{2}_{2,n}.
	\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.309546+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da2e9960e93a04bc0808d82a8bf09dbc8c0d9e099d605f063ad059a4992d85f1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop_irreducible:CPPdrift of arXiv:2411.14876, 'Limit theorems for stochastic exponentials of matrix-valued L\'evy processes \\'] Assume $L$ is a Lévy process in $\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$ fulfilling (equation eq-nonsingular of the paper) with characteristic triplet $(\Sigma_L, \gamma_L, \nu_L)$ such that $\Sigma_L=0$ and $\nu_L$ has finite total mass, i.e. $L$ is a compound Poisson process, possibly with drift $\gamma_L^0 \in \mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$. Assume that the closed semigroup generated by
	\begin{equation}
		\big\{ e^{t \gamma_L^0} \, : \, t >0 \big\} \cup \big(\Id+\mathrm{supp}(\nu_L)\big)
	\end{equation}
	satisfies condition (i-p). Then the same holds true for $G_X$.

	In particular,  if the closed semigroup generated by $\big(\Id+\mathrm{supp}(\nu_L)\big)$ satisfies condition (i-p), then so does $G_X$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:04:55.811669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da2f21cf8e204f8d8e05ec348df625c321ae6440219482900c2eec198a1d8171","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm t:main of arXiv:2607.18194, 'Temperature chaos in directed polymers'] Let $(\mathfrak{H}^{\xi}_{\beta_1}, \mathfrak{H}^{\xi}_{\beta_2})$ be as in (d:narrow-wedge of the paper), coupled through a shared space-time white noise $\xi$.
