{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.199699+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da67bc8c0b24e938f499ef6cc0d71146bc44a5269cab0eff78ef407d9f547159","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] For the equation \eqref{eq dual}, there exist constants $\widehat s,\widehat\lambda,C>0$, depending only on $D$, $\omega$ and $\nu$, such that the following holds. For any $g$ satisfying \eqref{eq g} and $ w\in \mathcal H$, the solution $\varphi$ of \eqref{eq dual} satisfies that
