{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:07.876528+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da69ed2f97dc91e984fcef7447f8d5ae56fe852450ce80538fb0959651fd2d4b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def_good of arXiv:2608.09105, 'Longest convex chains with i.i.d.\ points'] Given $\eta>0$ and $\delta>0$, we say the sample set $\mathcal{S}_n$ is \textit{$(\eta,\delta)$-good} if
\eeq{ 
\#\big(\mathcal{S}_n\cap([1-\eta,1]\times[0,1])\big)\leqslant\delta n \qquad \text{and} \qquad
\#\big(\mathcal{S}_n\cap([0,1]\times[0,\eta])\big)\leqslant\delta n.
}
Otherwise we say $\mathcal{S}_n$ is \textit{$(\eta,\delta)$-bad}.
\hfill\ensuremath{\square}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.617468+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da6aa5eeecadea8b825256f6aaac22149f1d049cb5ac5f0dcf624eb82e20b7f4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 63 ({\cite[Lemma 3.5) of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] {Dau23}}]

  For every $k\in \NN$, there exist constants $c_k,c_k'$ such that the following holds. For all $t,s$ satisfying $2\leq 2t< s< n^{1/3}/4$ and all $a$ satisfying $a\sqrt{s}< n^{2/3}/4$, we have
