 \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:35:56.960500+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da6c1bf44810813928953e05008eefdde5623414eec58cba4e29003c45ef3f63","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma E[sl]_asymp of arXiv:2604.05921, 'Simplicity of random hypergraphs'] If $\forall e \in E: \delta_e^{\textnormal{tail}} = \delta_e^{\textnormal{head}} = \delta \in O(1)$ and
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mathds{E}[(d_U^{\textnormal{in}}d_U^{\textnormal{out}})^{\delta}] \in o(n)$
    \item $\exists c>0: \mathds{P}(d_U^{\textnormal{out}},d_U^{\textnormal{in}} \geq \delta) \geq c$
\end{enumerate}
then
\begin{align*}
    \mathds{E}[S_n] = (\delta-1)! n \mathds{E}[d_U^{\textnormal{in}}] \Bigg( \frac{\mathds{E}[d_U^{\textnormal{in}}d_U^{\textnormal{out}}]}{n\mathds{E}[d_U^{\textnormal{in}}]^2} \Bigg)^{\delta} (1+o(1)).
