{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.613511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da857b26322ed95e1c296fceb277ad2a626f0c20c439ffb225d3c591dba804cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 ({\cite[Corollary 1.5) of arXiv:2510.27589, 'Geodesic switches and exceptional times in dynamical Brownian last passage percolation'] {GH20}}]

 There exist constants $C,c$ such that for all $n$ and all $\alpha\leq n^{1/10}$, we have
  \begin{equation}

