{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.221578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_db2b7b836521410fd914722a5f552a4c3081cc9e7553a2d13ccc8d40febafedb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Codim2 13 of arXiv:2609.00483, 'On Embedding Hamming Spheres with Applications to Positive Curvature'] Let $M^{n+2}$ be a closed, positively curved Riemannian manifold. Suppose $N^n$ is a closed, totally geodesic submanifold of $M$.
