{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:27:11.400591+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_db65c68b06143cd8ad0ff37708923f06af7c43a9792280afadadde7905025b1f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Splitting distribution of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Let $\cK^d_1:=\{B\in\cB^d: B \textnormal{ convex}, \lambda_d(B)=1\}$ and 
    \begin{equation}
        \cF^d_1:=\{(\phi,\tau): (\phi,\tau) \textnormal{ is a fair partition of } \R^d, C(x)\in\cK^d_1 \text{ for } x\in\phi\}.
    \end{equation}
