{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:38:17.791628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_db900347efba4dbff1529b9069e56eac13cca2aba0f17b5e38b291291444d1d1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition $\mathcal{S}$-condition of arXiv:2509.20779, 'Diffusive Scaling limit of stochastic Box-Ball systems and P\MakeLowercase{ush}TASEP'] Let $S$ be the convex polyhedron in (equation eq:def_polyhedron of the paper). We say a $d \times m$ matrix $R$ satisfies the \textit{$\mathcal S$-condition} with respect to  $S$ if and only if one of the following conditions, which are equivalent, holds: 
