{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.611946+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_db970ba5385b49d8bc2018221d6d949164564f214f165acf067a0130368d83e4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2510.27451, 'Bi-martingale optimal transport and its applications'] Let us be given two measures $\mu,\nu \in \mathcal{P}_1(\R)$ on the real line with the same barycentre, $[\mu] = [\nu]$. Then, 
