{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.709761+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dba2ee3d416378901e9edd5b02fd0a5dc16e0bca88f6e7fdb352b0f14f4ca59d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 (Structure of the scaled NP operator) of arXiv:2608.30991, 'A block-Toeplitz approach to the spectrum of the Neumann-Poincaré operator on self-similar'] The scaled Neumann-Poincaré operator $\widetilde{\mathbb{K}}^*_\alpha$ admits the explicit block-Toeplitz representation:
	\begin{equation*}
		\widetilde{\mathbb{K}}^*_\alpha = \begin{pmatrix} \tilde{K}^*_0 & r^{-\alpha} \tilde{K}^*_{-1} & r^{-2\alpha} \tilde{K}^*_{-2} & \cdots \\ r^\alpha \tilde{K}^*_1 & \tilde{K}^*_0 & r^{-\alpha} \tilde{K}^*_{-1} & \cdots \\ r^{2\alpha} \tilde{K}^*_2 & r^\alpha \tilde{K}^*_1 & \tilde{K}^*_0 & \cdots \\ \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \ddots \end{pmatrix}. 
	\end{equation*}
	The blocks are defined by $(\widetilde{\mathbb{K}}^*_\alpha)_{j,k} = r^{(j-k)\alpha} \tilde{K}^*_{j-k}$ for $j, k \ge 0$. The reference operator $\tilde{K}^*_m : W_0^{s,p}(\Gamma_0) \to W_0^{s,p}(\Gamma_0)$ is given by:
	\begin{equation*}
		(\tilde{K}^*_m \psi)(\tilde{x}) = P_{0,0} \left( \mathrm{} \int_{\Gamma_0} \frac{\partial G}{\partial \nu_{\tilde{x}}}(\eta_m(\tilde{x}), \tilde{y}) \psi(\tilde{y}) \, d\sigma_0(\tilde{y}) \right).
	\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.148313+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dba38f3c192305bec049437e61bcc877a6de8a1c828e713befcc6d00c9c4dd0a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma claim:S over 64v of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] There exists a  constant $C>0$ such that for any $n\geq 1$, and $t \leq n/16$,
