{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.008075+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dbd8fc93b27ce19252c88072c8a8e11376c7b28ae8703533e1fce71245a48515","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:D-Xt of arXiv:2608.21805, 'Logarithmic derivatives of variational and singular stochastic partial differential equati'] Under Assumptions (ass:LR of the paper), (ass:diff2 of the paper), and~(ass:SC of the paper), the solution $X(t)$ belongs to $\mathbb{D}^{1,2}(H)$ for each $t \in [0, T]$, and its Malliavin derivative at time $r \in [0, t]$ is given by
