{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.179848+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dbe4be24860b1378253afed6c01d2a8a6a638c290e5cbc530c341ff4882cd5da","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 (Endpoint leading term) of arXiv:2606.29635, 'Extremality and Limit Laws for the Siblings of the Coupon Collector'] Assume Hypothesis~\ref{hyp:endpoint}. Then for every fixed $j\ge2$,
