{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.967128+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc01b0597216962a655e7b41db1ca31f04be08c481aec94c92194b0dc8e360e1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 37 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Hellinger Integrals for Zero-Mean Gaussians}


    Let $\mathcal N_1$ and $\mathcal N_2$ on $\R^n$ be zero-mean Gaussians with covariances matrices $\Sigma_1, \Sigma_2$. Assume that $M := \alpha \Sigma_1\inv + (1-\alpha) \Sigma_2\inv \succeq 0$. Then, the Hellinger integrals of order $\alpha > 1$ have the form
    \begin{align*}
