{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.061433+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc4c30458e060faf00013cf06ce1b5b2c5bed376b3117c706bcc4eab87fdb2bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem many_to_one of arXiv:2506.10623, 'Polynomial slowdown in an angle-dependent 2d branching Brownian motion'] Let $t \geq s_0 \geq 0$ and $f \colon \mathcal{C}([s_0,t],\mathbb{R}^2) \to [0,\infty)$ be a measurable functional. Then, for any $x,y \in \mathbb{R}^2$,
	\begin{align*}
	    & \mathbb{E}_{(s_0,x,y)} \mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft[\sum_{u \in \mathcal{N}(t)} f\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft((X_u(s),Y_u(s))_{s\in [s_0,t]} \aftergroup\egroup\originalright) \aftergroup\egroup\originalright] \\
