{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.662169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dcf3d77afe8f939a4d3718ca601b5efba0f0b7b47a868d847dfe6a6c7cc254ed","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem The01 of arXiv:2604.06012, 'Large fringe trees for random trees with given vertex degrees'] Assume Condition~(Condition1 of the paper) and assume that the limit distribution $\mathbf{p}$
is not concentrated at $0$ or at $1$, i.e., $p_0,p_1<1$.
For $\kappa \geq 1$, let $T_{\kappa} \in \mathbb{T}$ be such that
$m_{\kappa} := |T_{\kappa}| \rightarrow \infty$
as \ensuremath{{\kappa\to\infty}}.
Then, as $\kappa \rightarrow \infty$:
\begin{romenumerate}[-20pt]  
\par
 \refstepcounter{thmenumerate}\textup{(\roman{thmenumerate})\enspace}  
If\/ $|{\mathbf{n}}_{\kappa}| \pi_{\mathbf{p}({\mathbf{n}}_{\kappa})}(T_{\kappa}) \rightarrow \lambda$, 
for some $\lambda \in [0,\infty)$, then 
\begin{align} 
N_{T_\kappa}({\mathcal T}_{{\mathbf{n}_\kappa}}) \overset{\mathrm{d}}{\longrightarrow}\operatorname{Po}\bigl(\lambda\bigr)
\end{align} 
with convergence of all moments.

\par
 \refstepcounter{thmenumerate}\textup{(\roman{thmenumerate})\enspace}  
If\/ $|{\mathbf{n}}_{\kappa}| \pi_{\mathbf{p}({\mathbf{n}}_{\kappa})}(T_{\kappa}) \rightarrow \infty$, then 
\begin{align}
\frac{N_{T_\kappa}({\mathcal T}_{{\mathbf{n}_\kappa}})- |{\mathbf{n}}_{\kappa}| \pi_{\mathbf{p}({\mathbf{n}}_{\kappa})}(T_{\kappa})}{\sqrt{|{\mathbf{n}}_{\kappa}| \pi_{\mathbf{p}({\mathbf{n}}_{\kappa})}(T_{\kappa})}} \overset{\mathrm{d}}{\longrightarrow}\mathrm{N}\bigl(0,1\bigr),
\end{align}
\end{romenumerate}  
with convergence of mean and variance.

Thus, in both cases,
\begin{align}
\operatorname{\mathbb E{}}\bigsqpar{N_{T_\kappa}({\mathcal T}_{{\mathbf{n}_\kappa}})}
\sim
\operatorname{Var}\bigsqpar{N_{T_\kappa}({\mathcal T}_{{\mathbf{n}_\kappa}})}
\sim
|{\mathbf{n}}_{\kappa}| \pi_{\mathbf{p}({\mathbf{n}}_{\kappa})}(T_{\kappa}).   
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.786819+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dcf963d5552997e232a33dbb8d700810dd024dd0a13277f93d1cb2f38b2636f0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem thm:5.1-replacement of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists a $C$ (independent of $\beta$) such that if we consider the infinite strip  $S$ of width $\ell$ with boundary conditions $\eta$, and let $\lambda = \lambda(\sigma)$ be its interface, the following holds. For $i \in \mathbb Z$, let $H_i^* = \{ \frac{1}{2},...,\ell + \frac{1}{2}\}\times \{i+\frac{1}{2}\}$. For every $\ell \ge e^{ \beta/5}$,  
