{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.777014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dd034033caacccc741fe1aee105864fde989c6bdcb6e88762704def94e048038","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2608.17493, 'Integrals of some compound processes'] Let $n\in\mathbb{N}$ and $t>0$. Let $\Lambda_1,\dots,\Lambda_n$ i.i.d. r.v.s taking values in $[0,t]$ a.s., $X_1,\dots,X_n$ independent copies of a real r.v. $X$ and $f:\mathcal{R}\times [0,t] \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}$ measurable. Then,
