{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.751862+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dd0fa4b9c4e46da5a39af33fec621e089fae7fd2031edaff6da78e2fc29b636c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2604.11682, 'Semilocalization for inhomogeneous random graphs'] Let $\nu > 0$ be a constant. An event $E \equiv E_N$ holds with \emph{$\nu$-high probability} if there exists a constant $C > 0$ such that, for all $N$,
