{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.532852+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dd1a967608f2b567326f593791ac324f284659cd464762d55a0babb2401fe228","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.maximalCluster of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Every ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}} \in \mathcal{G}^{(N)}_k$ is $N$-$\mathsf{stable}$ for the following property: for every ${\scaleobj{1}{\square}}', {\scaleobj{1}{\square}}'' \in \mathcal{S}^{loc}_{\mathcal{G}^{(N)}_{k-1}}({\scaleobj{1}{\square}})$ with ${\dist({\scaleobj{1}{\square}}',{\scaleobj{1}{\square}}'')\leqslant 1}$, there exists a cluster $\mathscr{C}^\#$ such that
