{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.374475+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ddc4d94ab662bd2243b06d8a79cc2490cbd11e7967ebcaaf6156d85d7fc7ad5b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: ModuleRephrasingWalkDet of arXiv:2603.26932, 'On the satisfaction frequency of spectral characterization conditions'] It holds that $p^2 \nmid \det(\bW)$ if and only if one of the following two events occurs: 
    \begin{enumerate}[leftmargin = 1.6em]
        \item It holds that $\coker\bigl(\bM - x\bI,\, \zeta\bigr)_{p,\beta} \cong 0$ for all monic $\beta(x) \in \bbZ[x]$ with irreducible reduction in $\bbF_p[x]$.
        \item Or, there exists $a\in \bbZ$ such that one has an isomorphism of $\bbZ[x]$-modules 
        \begin{align}
            \coker\bigl(\bM - x\bI,\, \zeta\bigr)_{p, x-a} \cong \bbF_{p}[x]/(x-a)\bbF_{p}[x],
        \end{align}
        and it holds that $\coker\bigl(\bM - x\bI,\, \zeta\bigr)_{p,\beta} \cong 0$ for every $\beta \not\equiv x-a \bmod p$.     
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}
